window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 101","paragraphs":["Firewood (4)","I was stunned by the shocking news, but only for a moment. I immediately left a comment.","The comment section was already a complete mess, but I couldn’t suppress my curiosity.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s that supposed to mean? Are they saying they’ll send survivors in there for me?","└ The man himself has arrived.","└ Grylls, you won’t have to be lonely anymore.","└ The Holy Kingdom is sending a search party just for you. Kekekeke.","└ The Holy Kingdom accomplishes what no one else could!","└ Wild Grylls: I can just dismiss that as bullshit, right? Damn it, they’re getting my hopes up for nothing.","└ Normally, you’d be terrified, but Grylls is actually looking forward to it. Kekekeke.","└ Considering he’s in the Forest of Four Seasons, that’s understandable. Kekeke.","└ But who exactly are they planning to send?","└ Rumor has it they’re sending people who oppose the current Pope’s regime.","└ So they’re just using this to eliminate their political enemies. Kek.","└ Do they even have the ability to find the head mod?","└ Absolutely not. Kekekeke. Unless the head mod openly gives them his location, it’s impossible.","└ Didn’t the head mod once tell them where the person planning to assassinate the emperor was?","└ Even then, the head mod only gave them the culprit’s location in real time. He didn’t reveal his own address.","└ And that head mod got his eyes gouged out for stalking someone. Kekekeke.","└ So they can send messages to the moderators?","└ Yeah, they can. Those bastards will definitely send one.","So it was all for show.","I had a rough idea of what they were trying to do.","I thought this sort of thing only happened on Earth, but since this world had the Gallery, events seemed to follow a similar pattern.","It was what people called a battle for public opinion. After all, the Gallery was practically the only place where public sentiment could be gauged.","’They just keep stepping on land mines.’","Naturally, public opinion toward the Holy Kingdom was as bad as it could possibly get.","There were occasionally people who defended or made excuses for it, but they were an exceedingly tiny minority.","All I had to do was sit back and enjoy the spectacle. The Holy Kingdom might declare the Gallery evil, but I wasn’t so sure that would work.","’Wasn’t the Emperor of the Central Plains beheaded after he tried to stop people from using the Gallery?’","It was a fairly famous incident—the assassination of the Emperor of the Central Plains.","It occasionally resurfaced as a hot topic, so I knew the story well.","The emperor tried to ban people from using the Gallery, only to be assassinated one day.","The imperial family officially announced that he had died of illness, while the people of the Central Plains assumed that he had fallen victim to an internal power struggle.","However, considering how ominously the Gallery users from the Central Plains had been behaving, most people on the Gallery didn’t believe either explanation.","’I’m sure they’ll handle it somehow.’","Whether Eldorado made another blunder or entered the Forest of Four Seasons was none of my concern.","The key was how the head mod—Don’tAbandonTheHero—would respond.","He could reveal my location in real time, and he could even impose penalties on them.","’The head mod told me not to worry, but judging from the Holy Kingdom’s behavior...’","Moreover, the head mod was presumed to be from the Holy Kingdom himself.","The fact that he was a devout apostle who worshiped the goddess Ares provided a clue to his origins.","Still, considering what a mess his country had become, hadn’t he probably lost whatever patriotism he once possessed?","The head mod worshiped his goddess. That didn’t necessarily mean he felt any loyalty toward Eldorado.","’I’ll have to wait and see how things unfold.’","It seemed the small ball I had set rolling had transformed into a massive meteor before crashing down.","Cleaning up the aftermath would take time. But if the Holy Kingdom continued stepping on land mines, the fire would never go out.","Until then, I could simply go about my business.","Title: I Made an Oven","Wild Grylls","(A photograph of a fairly well-made oven)","I made an oven out of bricks and clay. What do you think?","└ Heavenly Demon: That is quite a decent-looking oven. Are you planning to bake bread?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s meant for fish rather than bread. I think this will save me time.","└ Heavenly Demon: I wonder what oven-roasted fish tastes like.","└ Wild Grylls: Would you like me to give you some later?","└ Heavenly Demon: If you can spare a single piece.","└ SwordMaster: Weren’t you the one who said taking anything from him would be like squeezing blood from a stone? Kekekeke.","└ Heavenly Demon: I have realized that he is no stone.","└ SwordMaster: That excuse is pathetic. Kek.","└ Heavenly Demon: I can do something even more pathetic, if you wish.","└ SwordMaster: Ah. Come on, man...","└ Instantly subdued. Kekekeke.","└ Master, you know what to do if you think it’s unfair, right?","└ You merely need to turn blue as well.","└ SwordMaster: I’d rather die than become a junior mod.","└ Starlight Princess: Did you make that yourself? You did a wonderful job!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you, hehe.","└ Starlight Princess: Now that you have an oven, you’ll be able to prepare many different dishes. Is there anything you have in mind?","└ Wild Grylls: I only have fish, though.","└ Starlight Princess: I could give you some flour. Would you like to try baking bread?","└ Wild Grylls: No, thank you. I don’t need to go that far.","Bread was a luxury.","Unless I grew wheat myself, it would be absurdly extravagant.","At most, I could use the oven to warm up smoked meat. That was essentially the extent of its usefulness.","As I had said earlier, the only reason I made the oven was to save time.","’Though even that will be difficult until the dwarf gives me the iron plate.’","He had said he would give it to me at lunchtime along with the barricade.","I could train until then.","This morning’s training would be swordsmanship practice.","Ding!","Just as I was about to close the Gallery, a notification sounded.","Gallery notifications appeared whenever someone commented on one of my posts or sent me a message.","If it had been a comment, I would have merely checked who had left it. This time, however, it was a message.","Thinking it might have come from the head mod, I immediately checked it.","[NecromancyIsLove: Are you the one who uploaded the final record of Rice Kraone?]","It was a username I had never seen before.","I raised an eyebrow as I read the message.","Come to think of it, if this person possessed authority similar to that of the head mod, there was no reason they would only be capable of messaging him.","They could send messages to me as well.","’The username is a little strange, though...’","At present, the Holy Kingdom was the only party likely to send me a message like this.","Curious about what kind of bullshit they would spout, I greeted them politely.","[Wild Grylls: If you’re asking whether I uploaded the book about the Immortal King, then yes.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Then you must also be the one who gave the book to Kadir.]","[Wild Grylls: Kadir? The Sorcerer King?]","Kadir, the Sorcerer King.","I had vaguely heard about him on the Gallery.","He was said to have gone beyond merely mastering every form of magic in the world and reached an understanding of the fundamental principles behind it.","He had joined the previous Hero in subjugating the Immortal King and had slain a dragon driven mad.","He was a truly legendary figure.","Some people said he had an eccentric side, though I didn’t know anything about that. In any case, he was famous.","’But the person I gave the book to was Allfather. No, before that...’","How did this person know that I had given the book to someone?","There were many things I didn’t understand, and the entire situation seemed suspicious.","Perhaps this user was merely fishing for information.","There was no need to answer carelessly.","[Wild Grylls: I’m afraid I don’t know what you mean.]","[NecromancyIsLove: There is no need to play dumb. We have already seen the book in Kadir’s hands.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you saying Allfather is Kadir?]","[NecromancyIsLove: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: Then who are you?]","[NecromancyIsLove: The Immortal King—no.]","NecromancyIsLove appeared to contemplate the matter for a moment before revealing his identity.","[NecromancyIsLove: We are Kazan Kraone III, the final king of the Kingdom of Balkan.]","[Wild Grylls: I heard the Immortal King was dead.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Our physical body has perished, but our soul remains. We are currently sealed inside Kadir’s refrigerator.]","[Wild Grylls: This is just role-playing, right?]","What kind of scam was he trying to—no, what kind of nonsense was he spouting?","The overwhelmingly powerful Immortal King had been sealed inside a refrigerator? Why didn’t he just say he was being aged in there like kimchi?","It seemed he had simply made a lucky guess about me giving the book to Allfather.","However, this user was apparently so committed to his role that he continued speaking without the slightest hesitation.","[NecromancyIsLove: Whether you believe us is your choice. That is not what matters to us.]","[Wild Grylls: Then what does?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We merely wished to express our gratitude. Whether you intended to or not, you vindicated our kingdom.]","It was rare for genuine emotion to come through in a message.","And right now, I could... not feel any sincerity at all.","I merely thought he had chosen an exceptionally strange role to play. Then again, there were plenty of strange people in the world.","Besides, I had heard that the Immortal King was undead. Could undead beings even use the Gallery?","Weren’t undead supposed to lack a sense of self?","Nothing about his story made any sense.","’It doesn’t matter even if Allfather really is Kadir.’","He was someone from a distant land who had nothing to do with me.","Even if I told anyone about this, no one would believe me.","He might as well have claimed that Heavenly Demon was the actual Heavenly Demon of the Central Plains.","It seemed best to humor him for now.","[NecromancyIsLove: Regrettably, that would be difficult, as we no longer possess a physical body.]","I knew it.","Not that I had expected anything from him.","I snorted and continued my conversation with NecromancyIsLove.","[Wild Grylls: Then tell me something that might help me. I’m curious how the person who wrote that book survived.]","[NecromancyIsLove: First, we shall tell you how our brother died.]","[Wild Grylls: You translated it?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We have not forgotten the kingdom from those impoverished yet joyful days. Nor could we forget its language.]","[Wild Grylls: I uploaded it because I wanted to obtain some information too, you know.]","[NecromancyIsLove: We see. Is there something you desire?]","[Wild Grylls: Come here and help me.]","Ah, yes. Of course.","What a unique character he was playing.","Still, it was fortunate that he claimed to know why the book’s owner had died.","Of course, there wasn’t the slightest shred of credibility to his story, so I intended to ask Allfather separately.","[NecromancyIsLove: Our brother, Rice Kraone, died from an infection.]","[Wild Grylls: An infection?]","[NecromancyIsLove: His wound gradually began to rot. Unable to endure the pain, he ultimately took his own life. That is what he wrote in his final entry.]","[Wild Grylls: What injured him?]","[NecromancyIsLove: He wrote that he was attacked by a group of gorilla-like apes.]","Gorillas...","Could they be the creatures living in that place?","I remembered hearing something resembling monkey cries when I traveled upriver.","It seemed Rice Kraone had encountered the creatures that lived there.","’That’s important information.’","I didn’t know how far he had explored, but it would probably be best to avoid that area if possible.","After all, I already suspected that there were several of those creatures rather than just one.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you for the useful information. That helped a little.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Ask us if there is anything else you wish to know. We shall take our leave now.]","[Wild Grylls: What are you going to do?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We intend to observe the world. Seeing it again after so long has left us with a peculiar feeling.]","He was just going to browse the Gallery. Did he really need to dress it up like that?","His commitment to the role was so unhinged that it nearly rivaled Heavenly Demon’s.","I ended the conversation there and immediately sent a message to another registered user.","[Wild Grylls: Allfather, may I ask you something?]","[Allfather: Go ahead.]","[Wild Grylls: A registered user told me earlier that you’re Kadir. You know, the Sorcerer King.]","[Allfather: Yes. That’s correct.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","Now I was the one caught off guard.","I had never expected him to admit it so readily.","[Allfather: Do you believe me?]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm... No?]","He had a point.","I accepted that answer immediately.","’I’ll just assume he’s another strange person.’","There was no reason to overcomplicate things.","***","Asella, the current Hero and head moderator of the Gallery, had found herself in a difficult situation.","It wasn’t because a search party was hot on her heels or because she had run out of money.","It was an extension of the enormous controversy that had spread beyond the Gallery and into the real world.","\"No message... has come at all.\"","Asella was waiting for a message from Eldorado, the Holy Kingdom.","Only registered users could send private messages.","Therefore, sending Asella a message would practically amount to admitting that they used the Gallery.","Fortunately, she hadn’t received any private messages so far...but that created a problem of its own.","’Does the Holy Kingdom... have no intention of resolving this?’","It would be a problem if a message arrived, but it would also be a problem if none came.","In the former case, they would be exposing their own guilt. In the latter, it would mean they had no intention of resolving the issue.","Either way, Asella couldn’t help but feel disappointed.","’If they do send me a message...’","Couldn’t she reveal that she was the Hero and gain an opportunity to clear up the misunderstanding?","The moment that thought occurred to her, Asella hurriedly shook her head.","As previously mentioned, she had a foolish side, but she wasn’t stupid.","Even if she cleared up the misunderstanding, Eldorado would undoubtedly attempt to exploit her position as the head moderator.","Among other things, they would pressure Grylls, the person who had released the information. In the worst-case scenario, they might even order her to permanently ban him.","That would be devastating for Grylls, whose chances of survival differed drastically depending on whether he had access to the Gallery.","’That... wouldn’t be right.’","The Gallery was a platform that everyone could use.","Even a nation had no right to regulate it recklessly. At least, that was what she believed.","However, the Holy Kingdom’s actions were completely at odds with Asella’s principles.","How could a nation blessed by the gods use those very blessings to commit such abuses?","’It would be better if...’","Asella closed the Gallery.","She could feel herself growing increasingly depressed.","’It would be better if they did nothing at all.’","Then, at least, she would be a little less disappointed."]},{"title":"Chapter 102","paragraphs":["Territory (1)","I set aside the rumor that Allfather was actually Kadir...and finished what I had to do.","The newbie(?) with the outrageous role-play had taken up some of my time, but it had only been ten minutes.","It hadn’t affected my overall schedule. It was no different from browsing the Gallery.","’Today is Day Thirteen. In two more days, it’ll be exactly half a month.’","Time seemed to pass slowly yet quickly at the same time.","It would have flown by if my daily routine had simply repeated itself, but I was currently going through all sorts of hardships.","’A little hardship is fine, but this is too much.’","Grumbling inwardly, I began my training.","After cultivating my internal energy, it was time for swordsmanship practice.","Two days from now, once I reached the half-month mark, I planned to consume the inner core.","I had already told Heavenly Demon about it, so she had given me a more in-depth explanation.","[Heavenly Demon: It seems you have laid a sufficient foundation. You truly possess extraordinary talent.]","[Wild Grylls: How long does it normally take to finish laying the foundation?]","[Heavenly Demon: The beginning is difficult in all things. The time required to sense the internal energy within one’s dantian differs from person to person. It takes between a week and half a month on average, yet you sensed it in only a single day. You can truly be called a genius.]","[Wild Grylls: You’re embarrassing me.]","[Heavenly Demon: This is not something to be embarrassed about, but something you should take pride in. This lady is also delighted to have the opportunity to teach someone as talented as you.]","Hmm. Now this was what a true adult looked like.","She didn’t envy the achievements of someone beneath her(?) and instead praised them sincerely.","This was why, even if I resented the heavens, I didn’t want to resent humanity.","There might be bad people in the world, but there were also kind people like Heavenly Demon.","Smiling happily, I sent Heavenly Demon another message.","[Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t have made it this far without you either, Heavenly Demon. The mnemonic chant you taught me has been especially helpful whenever I’ve been in danger.]","[Heavenly Demon: A carp living in a lake grows larger than one living in a pond. However, even a carp living in a lake gains nothing if it fails to survive.]","[Wild Grylls: You’re saying the Heavenly Demon Divine Art is the lake and I’m the carp, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: You understood immediately. How gratifying.]","The way she used poetic expressions confirmed that she was indeed fairly old.","She occasionally used strange expressions, but I could simply assume that the Gallery had corrupted her.","[Wild Grylls: When will you teach me the second mnemonic chant?]","[Heavenly Demon: You said you would consume the inner core soon, so I shall teach you then. If the first chant is about entrusting your body to the heavens, the second is about sensing the power of the heavens.]","[Wild Grylls: Entrusting myself to that power instead of controlling it?]","[Heavenly Demon: To control a power, you must first understand its true nature. Can you forcibly twist the course of a raging river?]","[Wild Grylls: That would be difficult.]","[Heavenly Demon: The heavens are no different. The closer you draw to them, the farther away they appear. This is a means of approaching the heavens, if only slightly.]","Her explanation was easy to understand.","I nodded as I listened to Heavenly Demon.","The eel I had eaten before.","I remembered all the side effects it had caused.","I had genuinely thought I was going to explode, but I had somehow managed to disperse its energy.","Perhaps consuming the inner core would proceed similarly.","It felt as though I had unintentionally studied the material in advance.","’That’s actually better.’","After receiving various pieces of fundamental knowledge from Heavenly Demon, I began circulating my internal energy.","As I gradually came to understand what the foundation entailed, the amount of time I spent cultivating also increased.","One might think the required time should decrease, but as Heavenly Demon had explained through her metaphor, the foundation was like a tree’s roots.","The deeper and wider the roots grew, the more water they required.","’The only way to increase its purity is to improve my lung capacity.’","That could only be achieved by continuously practicing my breathing.","My lung capacity would naturally increase while I cultivated my internal energy.","My goal was to breathe the same way I did while practicing my cultivation technique, even during my ordinary routine.","According to Heavenly Demon, this was less about laying a foundation and more about strengthening my roots.","In other words, I still had a very long way to go.","Nevertheless, it was entirely achievable if I put in the effort.","’Next is swordsmanship practice.’","Once I finished cultivating, it was time to practice swordsmanship.","I had been training step by step while following SwordMaster’s post, but there were parts where I had gotten stuck.","Other people claimed that merely reading the post was enough to turn anyone into a mass-produced(?) Swordmaster, but there was no one beside me to provide guidance.","Having a teacher was extremely important when learning something like martial arts. Since I was effectively trying to figure everything out from scratch, it was a little disheartening.","[SwordMaster: So, which part are you having trouble with?]","[Wild Grylls: It feels unstable. Like my sword keeps wavering?]","That was why I had decided to ask SwordMaster directly.","Previously, I could only ask questions by making a post, but now I could send private messages.","SwordMaster was just as excellent a teacher as Heavenly Demon, so I listened carefully.","[SwordMaster: I understand what you mean. However, that’s unavoidable as long as you wield your sword with one hand, Mr. Grylls. Naturally, using one hand is less stable than using both.]","[Wild Grylls: Is there no way to fix it?]","[SwordMaster: There are plenty of ways. One tip is to place the foot opposite your sword arm forward. Since you’re right-handed, Mr. Grylls, you should step forward with your left foot.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s what I’ve been doing.]","[SwordMaster: Were you doing it during training as well?]","[Wild Grylls: Oh.]","[SwordMaster: Here’s another tip: abandon the idea of cleaving your opponent in two. Stability is crucial when wielding a sword, but using it one-handed inevitably reduces stability while making you rely more heavily on brute force.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you saying I’ll eventually have to abandon my shield?]","[SwordMaster: That comes down to personal preference. You can compensate for the lack of cutting power with aura.]","[Wild Grylls: So practicing aura is ultimately my only path to survival.]","[SwordMaster: That’s right. If you work hard, your efforts will bear fruit someday. And one more tip—practice thrusting as much as possible!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you!]","[SwordMaster: Please hurry up, become a fine man, and marry me!]","[Wild Grylls: Teacher?]","Hearing a joke so completely at odds with her character left my mind reeling.","Come to think of it, I had been neglecting thrusts.","I had gained a great deal from this conversation.","Following SwordMaster’s advice, I began training my swordsmanship and aura.","The training focused on improving my lack of stability and compensating with aura for the weaknesses I couldn’t eliminate.","’I should practice thrusting too.’","In addition to practicing thrusts, I needed to gradually adjust my fighting style.","Until now, my strategy had been to wait for an opportunity, restrict my opponent’s mobility, and then slowly whittle away its stamina.","Since most of the monsters I encountered were enormous, the method had proven surprisingly effective.","However, it was only possible because I possessed the Heavenly Demon’s Sword, an absurdly overpowered item.","I also needed to consider how I would fight animals that weren’t particularly large.","’What would happen if a fight dragged on?’","That probably wouldn’t happen often, but who knew?","This was the Forest of Four Seasons.","I was probably vulnerable in prolonged battles. There weren’t exactly many opportunities to build endurance here.","My lung capacity had at least improved the more I practiced my cultivation technique, but I still couldn’t be certain.","There might be animals in the Forest of Four Seasons with greater lung capacity than mine.","\"...What are you doing?\"","\"Hoo.\"","When I asked Namu-Ppareumbo what it was doing, it exhaled deeply.","Rather than sighing, it seemed to be practicing its breathing.","The absurdity of it made me laugh.","Surely it wasn’t imitating the breathing method I had demonstrated before.","There was no way.","’I’d sooner believe that a gorilla had learned a breathing technique.’","A gorilla was an animal capable of literally tearing a person in half.","If an animal like that learned a breathing technique on top of its natural strength, it would be an unprecedented disaster.","Moreover, a breathing technique—or rather, an internal-energy cultivation technique—required a certain degree of intelligence.","Unless the Forest of Four Seasons had evolved its apes until they were as intelligent as humans, it would be difficult.","’Besides, no one would have taught them one in the first place.’","With that thought, I rose from my seat.","It was almost lunchtime.","Now that I had made the oven, I might as well use it. I could also collect the items from the dwarf.","\"Wonmo, let’s go.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","Wonmo happened to be awake, so I brought him along.","Naturally, I also carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back.","I headed toward the river, eagerly wondering how many fish had been caught in the trap.","Splash! Splash!","\"Now that’s what I’m talking about.\"","There were two again.","I couldn’t have been happier.","I pulled in the trap while imagining the feast I would have for lunch.","Rustle!","As I was dragging the trap back, I heard something brush against the undergrowth.","The moment I heard it, I assumed a defensive stance just as I had that morning.","However, no other sound followed.","’Am I overreacting?’","Perhaps I had suffered so many attacks lately that I was beginning to hear things.","I rubbed my face before glancing at Wonmo.","Wonmo was staring fixedly at something—specifically, the upper branches of a tree.","\"Wonmo, was something there?\"","\"Kkyuu?\"","\"Never mind. Let’s go.\"","Worrying about it unnecessarily would only give me a headache.","Even if something launched a surprise attack, Namu-Ppareumbo was with me, so I felt somewhat reassured.","I placed the two fish caught in the trap inside the iron container and began preparing lunch.","[Passing Dwarf: Here’s the barricade and the tray you wanted. The tray is pretty heavy, so be careful.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. I’ll give you some fish in a little while.]","[Passing Dwarf: My mouth is already watering. Kek.]","You too, huh?","Same here.","I installed the barricade I had received from the dwarf in the location I wanted.","Since my basic physical strength had increased tremendously, moving it wasn’t difficult.","Next was the appropriately sized steel tray.","I intended to place the fish on it before sliding it into the oven.","’He thoughtfully raised the edges so the oil wouldn’t spill.’","I repeatedly slid the tray into and out of the oven to test it.","Its weight was a slight drawback, but that was unavoidable.","Even so, it was excellent.","I could feel my quality of life gradually improving.","Crackle! Pop!","I lit a fire at the very bottom of the oven and slowly preheated it.","While the oven was heating, I prepared the fish. Using an oven didn’t change the preparation process itself.","However, I spread the fish open so it would cook evenly.","I didn’t forget to season it with salt either.","Slide—clunk!","Finally, all I had to do was place the fish inside the preheated oven.","The tray’s length and height fit perfectly.","The dwarf had given me an excellent gift.","’He said it would take around fifteen to twenty minutes, right?’","I could play with Wonmo until then.","It would also serve as training to improve Wonmo’s hunting skills.","Calling it training was a bit generous. All I had done was tie a rope to a branch and fasten a fish head to the other end.","It was more like playing with a cat.","The commonality was that they were both adorable.","This exercise might also help improve my reaction speed, even if only slightly.","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuuuu!\"","\"That’s it! Good job!\"","While the fish inside the oven cooked, Namu-Ppareumbo merely stared blankly at the trees.","Rustle!","Rustle! Swish!","Several beasts swiftly made their way through the trees.","Rather than traveling beneath them, they moved rapidly by lightly stepping from branch to branch.","At first glance, their bodies resembled those of humans. However, their long arms and the fur covering their entire bodies made it clear that they were not.","The beasts sped through the forest faster than any human could and eventually arrived in a particular area.","There, they found an ape lounging leisurely atop a tree.","Its overall appearance resembled a gorilla, but there was something unusual about its presence.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The group of gorillas that had gone out to scout(?) began hooting as though they were reporting something.","The gorilla that had been lounging in the tree slowly rose.","Unlike its previously relaxed demeanor, its expression had turned deathly serious.","\"Ooh?\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh...!\"","A subtle breeze began to blow through the forest."]},{"title":"Chapter 103","paragraphs":["Territory (2)","The oven was a cooking appliance with a remarkably long history.","One didn’t need to look far to understand its importance. Without ovens, Western civilization couldn’t even have produced bread, its staple food.","The oven was created to take fire-roasting to the next level.","Well, the true next step was probably putting food in a pot and boiling it, but that was beside the point.","What mattered was that possessing an oven had an enormous effect on my quality of life.","\"Wow.\"","I exclaimed in admiration as I looked at the deliciously cooked fish.","Even though it was a makeshift oven, it had cooked the fish evenly.","Whenever I grilled fish on the cast-iron pan, some parts ended up undercooked while others burned.","An oven, however, surrounded the food with heat from every direction, so it naturally cooked everything evenly.","’I might even be able to bake bread if I ever get the opportunity.’","I carefully carried the grilled fish, which made my mouth water just by looking at it.","I didn’t forget to wear gloves since I could easily burn myself.","I had even purchased a new pair of kitchen gloves from the auction house specifically for today.","Munch, munch.","\"Mm!\"","It tasted exactly as I had expected.","That was precisely why it was so delicious.","Even when I grilled it normally, the fish had tasted somewhat like meat. Now it tasted like actual meat.","It reminded me of the pork belly I used to splurge on while living alone and desperately saving every penny.","Of course, it wasn’t exactly the same. The texture was especially different.","Even so, its flavor was every bit as good as pork belly.","’Even the parts that look burned are tender inside.’","I would probably be using the oven often from now on.","I happily enjoyed my meal.","I didn’t forget to send a piece to each of the registered users who had helped me. This time, the recipients were Heavenly Demon and Passing Dwarf.","They also tasted the oven-roasted fish and praised it highly.","It was objectively delicious.","’How did people invent the oven?’","I gazed at the oven while eating the fish.","The firewood had burned away and was turning into charcoal, while thin wisps of smoke rose from the chimney.","The oven had made an enormous contribution to human cuisine.","Without ovens, there would be no bread.","’Could I make pizza with that?’","No.","That would be a luxury.","Unless I cultivated my own wheat and obtained eggs as well, it was nothing more than a pointless fantasy.","For now, I should be satisfied with oven-roasted fish.","The oven would be useful not only for cooking fish but also for reheating smoked meat.","\"La-la-la~\"","As my quality of life improved, my morale naturally rose with it.","An increase in morale also meant an increase in combat effectiveness.","While singing the oven’s praises, I planned my afternoon schedule.","’I should determine where the gorilla troop’s territory is.’","Rice Kraone, the final chronicler of the Kingdom of Balkan, had died by suicide.","However, the infection had already left him without hope of survival, meaning the gorilla troop was effectively responsible for his death.","I needed to determine the precise boundaries of the gorillas’ territory so they wouldn’t pose a threat to my safety.","’I’ll have to learn about gorilla behavior first...’","I didn’t know how gorillas had adapted to the Forest of Four Seasons.","In other words, I needed to consider the possibility that the behavior I already knew about had changed.","Still, knowing something was better than knowing nothing.","I sent a message to the person best suited to answer my questions.","[Allfather: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: I wanted to ask you about gorilla behavior.]","[Allfather: Gorillas? Ah. It seems you discovered how the book’s owner died.]","Apparently, the information NecromancyIsLove had given me was genuine.","Did that mean I accepted his claim that he was the Immortal King?","No.","I could simply assume that an intelligent person was engaging in elaborate role-play.","Even if he truly was the Immortal King, it didn’t particularly matter.","[Wild Grylls: Allfather? Are you still there?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I heard there’s a gorilla territory nearby. I also have a vague idea of where it is.]","[Allfather: Among primates, including humans, gorillas are exceptionally unaggressive and nonconfrontational. Naturally, this varies by subspecies, but that is generally the case.]","[Wild Grylls: Does that mean they’re safe?]","[Allfather: Not necessarily. If a gorilla reveals itself, it generally means you have intruded upon its territory. Furthermore, considering how the book’s owner died, you cannot afford to let your guard down.]","So I ultimately had no choice but to be careful.","I should avoid entering their territory if at all possible.","However, I had no idea where their territory began or ended.","Animals commonly marked their territory with excrement.","It seemed I would have to search carefully for their droppings.","’I’ll have to bring Wonmo.’","Wonmo possessed an excellent sense of smell, so finding the droppings should be easy.","He happened to be bouncing around energetically instead of taking a nap, so I could bring him along.","I began composing a message to thank Allfather.","[Wild Grylls: Like humans? What did they do, specifically?]","[Allfather: First, they reportedly used \"tools.\" They carried animal bones in their hands and wielded them like clubs.]","[Wild Grylls: ...]","[Allfather: Incidentally, there is one aspect of these gorillas that concerns me.]","[Wild Grylls: Something that concerns you?]","[Allfather: According to the book, the gorillas behaved almost like humans.]","What was this, Planet of the Apes ?","Could gorillas really be that intelligent?","It was a terrifying thought.","One careless mistake, and they could smash my skull open with those bones.","What if they were also aggressive?","The entire gorilla troop might gang up on me and beat me senseless.","’...Should I just not go?’","Allfather’s warning dampened my enthusiasm.","My resolve faltered briefly, but I soon shook my head vigorously.","This was precisely when taking a risk was necessary.","There was an enormous difference between possessing information and remaining ignorant.","’I’ll only determine the boundaries of their territory.’","For now, that would be my sole objective.","I would do exactly that and nothing more.","Even if the territory contained a legendary medicinal herb, I intended to ignore it.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you for the advice. I’ll have to be careful.]","[Allfather: I don’t think you should enter their territory, even out of curiosity.]","[Wild Grylls: I only intend to determine where the boundary lies and then return.]","[Allfather: I see. Understood.]","After ending my conversation with Allfather, I prepared for the expedition.","It would be wise to prepare for the possibility that I might accidentally enter the gorillas’ territory.","’Gorillas are herbivores, right?’","Allfather had told me that gorillas survived by eating things such as tree bark.","Despite living on tree bark, they possessed the greatest physical strength among all primates.","I felt an irrational stab of envy but quickly dismissed it.","Humans possessed far greater intelligence than they did.","I packed a few fasting pills as a gesture of goodwill.","If the situation became tense, I planned to offer them the pills and earn their favor.","’Namu-Ppareumbo eats them without any trouble, so gorillas should too, right?’","Or perhaps I should purchase a banana.","When people thought of gorillas, bananas were the first fruit that came to mind.","Entertaining such pointless thoughts, I completed my preparations.","Namu-Ppareumbo climbed onto my back, while Wonmo eagerly urged me to get moving.","All that remained was to depart, but...","Grrrrumble!","\"Ah.\"","It seemed I would have to delay my departure for a moment.","***","Grylls set out to explore only after thoroughly relieving himself.","The cave he left behind was silent, with no presence to be felt anywhere.","Only the occasional crackling of the campfire broke the stillness.","Rustle! Rustle!","Then it happened.","The bushes lining the path toward the river—the opposite direction from the one Grylls had taken—began to shake.","At first, they trembled only slightly, but the movement soon became noticeable.","Swish—","Eventually, something emerged through the bushes.","It did not fully reveal itself, instead cautiously poking out only its face.","Its overall features resembled a human’s, but it had a flat nose and pitch-black skin.","Most tellingly, the hair covering parts of its face revealed that it was an ape.","\"...Ooh! Ooh!\"","After surveying Grylls’s shelter for some time, the ape let out a quiet call.","In response, the bushes shook even more violently than before.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","A troop of apes emerged—the very gorillas Grylls had been wary of.","The gorillas appeared to communicate through their distinctive calls before cautiously entering the shelter.","At first glance, they looked like ordinary gorillas. Upon closer inspection, however, several details set them apart.","The gorilla presumed to be their leader carried nothing, but the gorillas following him were armed with clubs.","Their weapons varied considerably. Some wielded bones, others pieces of wood, and a few even carried crudely fashioned stone axes.","It was clear that these creatures were fundamentally different from ordinary apes.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh.\"","\"Ooh-ooh.\"","The apes meticulously inspected Grylls’s shelter.","They examined the iron container holding the fish, the container filled with charcoal, and finally the oven.","\"Oookyaaagh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh?!\"","Suddenly, one of the gorillas screamed.","The others hurried toward him at the sound.","The gorilla was rolling on the ground while clutching his hand. In front of him stood the oven Grylls had recently constructed.","Apparently, he had put his hand inside before it had fully cooled and burned himself.","It was an accident caused by curiosity.","The leader hurried over and examined his condition.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","After assessing the injury, the leader pointed toward the iron container holding the fish.","It was as though he were telling the injured gorilla that the container held water and that he should quickly cool his hand.","The burned gorilla immediately plunged his hand into it.","Splash!","As soon as his hand entered the water, the gorilla’s face filled with relief.","The fish inside were startled and began splashing wildly, but he didn’t seem to care.","After briefly showing his relief, the leader carefully examined the oven.","Perhaps he noticed the appetizing scent lingering inside.","He brought his nose close to the opening and sniffed repeatedly.","However, he apparently couldn’t determine the oven’s purpose and merely tilted his head.","Eventually, he lost interest and turned his attention elsewhere.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","One of the gorillas pointed toward the iron container holding the fish.","It was an important source of food for Grylls.","However, the leader shook his head in refusal.","He appeared to be indicating that it would be difficult to carry.","Although disappointed, the other gorilla accepted his decision.","The leader turned away and continued surveying the shelter.","He soon discovered the laundry hanging from the clothesline.","\"Ooh.\"","The leader stared at the laundry before slowly pulling on it.","The makeshift clothesline couldn’t withstand the gorilla’s immense strength and collapsed helplessly.","The leader carefully examined the uniform PrincessCheonggu had given Grylls, then tossed it onto the ground.","He didn’t seem particularly interested in it.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","Just then, the gorillas exploring the cave rushed outside.","Unlike the burned gorilla’s earlier scream, these were cries of celebration.","When the leader showed interest in what they had found, the gorillas placed their discovery on the ground.","They had brought out the sack of fasting pills that currently served as Namu-Ppareumbo’s staple food.","\"Hmm...\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The gorillas urged their leader to make a decision.","However, the leader remained cautious.","He took one fasting pill from the sack and placed it in his mouth.","Before long, he began chewing it thoroughly.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh?! Ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","The leader’s eyes widened as he cried out in astonishment.","Anyone could tell that his reaction meant, \"Delicious.\"","His expression made it seem as though he had discovered the greatest delicacy in the world.","The other gorillas each placed a fasting pill in their mouths.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","\"Oooook!\"","Like their leader, the other gorillas reacted with tremendous excitement.","To some, the pills were unbearably bitter emergency rations, but the gorillas apparently considered them an exquisite delicacy.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","After eating several more pills, the gorillas quietly lifted the sack.","We can’t keep something this delicious to ourselves. Let’s share it with the rest of our troop.","The leader apparently agreed, as he picked up the sack without hesitation.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The gorilla troop then departed Grylls’s shelter.","They had not stolen the elixir, inner core, or any of the other treasures Grylls cherished, but the loss was still devastating.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Oblivious to that fact, the gorilla troop happily returned home."]},{"title":"Chapter 104","paragraphs":["Territory (3)","Territory was an extremely sensitive matter, whether for animals or humans.","In the broadest sense, a human’s territory was their country and its borders. On a smaller scale, it was their home.","Food, clothing, and shelter were all essential, but shelter was the element responsible for providing safety.","Without a home, people could never be safe from natural disasters and all manner of other dangers.","Therefore, both humans and animals required territory to live safely.","Even humans became wary or confrontational when strangers entered their homes. Animals would naturally react even more strongly.","I hadn’t set out to explore the forest and identify the gorillas’ territory for no reason.","’But considering the Owlbear and Mad Dog, there must be territorial conflicts between the animals too.’","Although I had set out confidently, there were more than a few things that concerned me.","First, what would happen to the territories that had belonged to the now-deceased Owlbear and Mad Dog?","I had considered that question several times, but nothing noteworthy had happened so far.","There had been a kangaroo inside the Owlbear’s cave, but it had fled upon seeing me.","Only now was I truly beginning to understand that other animals might move in to claim the vacant territories.","The saber-toothed tiger was a monster I had barely defeated with Namu-Ppareumbo’s assistance.","Had I fought it alone, I would have died several times over.","’If something is powerful enough to force its way into a saber-toothed tiger’s territory...’","It might have challenged the saber-toothed tiger even while it was alive.","Alternatively, it might already have become the dominant predator of this entire region.","’I’ve been consistently marking my territory too.’","Of course, I wasn’t being entirely serious.","I had simply been relieving myself wherever I pleased.","Even so, I believed it must have served as a territorial marker to some extent.","’This is the Owlbear’s cave.’","Retracing yesterday’s route, I arrived at the Owlbear’s cave.","I had originally planned to use this location as the starting point of my search.","That was before Wonmo dashed inside.","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuu!\"","I urgently called out to him, but he had already disappeared into the cave.","Shaking my head, I followed him inside.","\"Кkyaaagh! Kkyaagh!\"","However, Wonmo came racing back out before I had gone very far.","Judging by his terrified expression, something was inside.","After barely managing to calm the trembling Wonmo, I cautiously peered into the cave.","\"Oh.\"","I could understand why Wonmo was frightened.","The creatures inside were anything but ordinary.","It was the kangaroo I had seen yesterday.","It was hopping around inside the cave.","The problem was that there wasn’t just one. There were several of them.","Apparently, they had claimed this place as their territory.","Exactly what I had feared had happened.","A mob of kangaroos had taken over after the Owlbear’s death.","’But can kangaroos even survive in this kind of environment?’","Perhaps it was merely a preconception, but on Earth, kangaroos usually lived in Australia.","As long as they had grass, trees, and other sources of food, there was no reason they couldn’t survive here.","Even so, their presence felt oddly out of place.","Regardless of how I felt about it, I decided to withdraw quietly.","Fighting them now would only disadvantage me, and there were still many places I needed to investigate.","’If I want to escape, I’ll have to pass through other animals’ territories...’","That also bothered me.","I would inevitably have to trespass into territories belonging to other animals.","If I was unlucky, I might be forced to fight a series of battles against the creatures ruling those territories.","That was precisely why I needed more information.","’Wait. Come to think of it...’","I turned and looked back at the entrance to the former Owlbear nest.","I was thinking about Rice Kraone, the owner of the book I had found there.","’How was he able to live inside the Owlbear’s nest? Did he live there before the Owlbear arrived?’","Allfather would probably be able to tell me later.","After one last look at what had now become the kangaroos’ cave, I continued onward.","I still had no way of estimating where the gorillas’ territory might be.","It would have been convenient to use the area upriver as a reference, but even that was uncertain.","’The river itself could be part of their territory.’","It would be easier to treat this as both exploration and an attempt to determine territorial boundaries.","If I discovered any droppings along the way, I could stop immediately.","After all, I had an excellent detection dog—no, a detection bear—with me, so finding them should be easy.","Sniff, sniff.","\"Hey, Wonmo. That’s dirty. Don’t touch it.\"","That didn’t mean I wanted him to search for mushrooms.","Worried that Wonmo might eat one, I hurriedly stopped him.","Afterward, I continued exploring while carefully marking my route so I wouldn’t get lost.","As I proceeded, I suddenly realized that the terrain was gradually changing.","’This is practically a jungle rather than a forest.’","The leaves were becoming a deeper shade of green, and moss was growing increasingly abundant.","Moreover, while the forest floor had often consisted of stone rather than soil, at some point it had become covered entirely in tree roots.","Even the air had changed noticeably, particularly the humidity.","It had been somewhat dry moments ago, but at some point, it had become humid.","’I didn’t feel myself crossing into a different space.’","It wasn’t anything like the alien sensation I had experienced when crossing the river.","It merely felt as though I had gradually entered a jungle without noticing.","I considered turning back but decided to explore just a little farther.","\"Good lord. What the fuck?\"","Not long after making that decision, I discovered a new species.","A creature of unknown origin was steadily crawling forward.","Its appearance was unmistakably that of a snail.","The problem was its size.","Its shell alone was much larger than I was, to say nothing of its actual body.","’Is this what the snails from Maple World would look like?’","The sight of a human-sized snail crawling along was utterly horrifying.","At the same time, however, it puzzled me.","Wouldn’t a creature that large be quickly devoured?","’There must be a reason it survives.’","I shouldn’t touch it merely to satisfy my curiosity.","The wisest course was to let it continue on its way.","I passed the snail, which was crawling even more slowly than a sloth.","Not long afterward, I discovered exactly how it had managed to survive.","Hissssss—","The grass along the snail’s trail had completely melted.","As if that weren’t enough, even the soil appeared to have dissolved, with smoke rising from the ground.","The substance was probably poisonous like the Golden Poison Frog’s toxin, or perhaps acidic.","Considering the nature of snails, its entire body might be poisonous or acidic.","Anything that tried to eat it would probably melt into liquid.","’...I should name it the Acid Snail.’","Surely it couldn’t spit acid from its mouth like the frog, could it?","Just in case, I moved far away from the snail.","I continued exploring various parts of the jungle, but after finding nothing unusual, I eventually turned back.","’Do the gorillas not live here?’","Either they lived deeper inside, or I had searched in the wrong direction.","Wonmo hadn’t found anything either, so it felt like the entire excursion had been a waste.","’There’s...still plenty of time.’","When I checked the Gallery clock, it was only two thirty.","I had planned to continue exploring until five at the latest, so I could afford to search a little longer.","However, as a precaution, I decided not to reenter the jungle.","It would be disastrous if I encountered the gorillas.","\"Hmm?\"","Just as I resolved to return, I discovered something strange.","It was a tree with a deep depression in the center of its trunk.","Since fights constantly broke out in the Forest of Four Seasons, finding a damaged tree wasn’t unusual.","However, the mark carved into this particular tree stood out.","’Could this be...a handprint?’","A distinct handprint had been imprinted on the trunk.","I couldn’t tell much about it, but it certainly didn’t appear to belong to a human.","I didn’t know what kind of ape had made it. I wasn’t an expert.","There were only two things I could determine.","It was much larger than my hand, and its proportions differed from those of a human hand.","The palm was much larger than the fingers, while the hand itself was more than twice the size of mine.","’...This might be a territorial marker.’","I examined the impression, which was large enough to engulf my entire hand.","If a gorilla had truly made this mark, it would be best to leave immediately.","If I wandered around unnecessarily, I might be ambushed.","’Are there any other marks?’","However, I felt the urge to determine the territorial boundary more precisely.","I couldn’t allow a single handprint to frighten me into doing nothing.","Just as I was about to turn my head—","\"Huh?\"","My fingertips brushed against another indentation.","There was a second mark beside the large handprint.","The tree was so thick that I had nearly overlooked it.","However, there was another reason I was surprised.","’This one...really looks like a human handprint.’","A much smaller handprint had been carved beside the larger one.","Although it was still bigger than mine, its size was within the limits of an ordinarily large human hand.","I wondered if it belonged to an adolescent gorilla, but that didn’t seem right either.","’The fingers are long.’","Its fingers were unusually long.","The difference became obvious when the two prints were compared.","Could it have belonged to Rice, who had been attacked by the gorilla troop?","That didn’t seem right either.","I didn’t know why, but the prints gave me a sense of companionship.","It was almost as though the two owners had made them to display their bond.","After carefully examining both handprints, I took a photograph.","I intended to upload it to the Gallery later.","\"They seem pretty old...but I don’t know.\"","I couldn’t tell whether the smaller print had been left by a survivor or a mutant.","Still pondering the mystery, I headed out of the jungle.","I couldn’t remain there any longer.","’I have something to think about, so I should return to the shelter.’","I wanted to continue exploring, but I changed my plans.","After all, I had discovered a mark that might have belonged to a survivor.","Furthermore, it belonged to a survivor other than Rice.","’Why would someone leave a handprint? And why beside a gorilla’s?’","Still contemplating that baffling question, I returned to the shelter.","The moment I arrived, all the tension drained from my body.","\"Hmm?\"","Something was strange.","I sensed an inexplicable incongruity.","What was causing it?","I couldn’t identify it at all.","Everything was familiar, yet something felt wrong. The positions of various objects seemed to have changed slightly.","\"Why has the laundry rack fallen over? Did I fail to secure it properly?\"","The first oddity was the laundry I had hung up, which was now scattered across the ground.","The iron container’s position seemed to have changed slightly, and something about the charcoal container also looked strange.","There were signs throughout the shelter that someone had visited, putting me on guard.","’There’s no one inside, though.’","I cautiously peered into the cave, but no one was there.","For a moment, I had thought an intruder might still be hiding inside.","I rubbed the back of my neck before lowering my weapons and entering the cave.","The instant I stepped inside, the feeling that something was wrong became far stronger.","No.","It wasn’t merely a feeling.","One of my belongings had completely disappeared.","\"Huh?\"","I usually kept everything neatly organized so that it would be easy to find.","Therefore, I immediately realized what was missing.","\"What the hell? Where are the fasting pills?\"","The fasting pills were gone.","The entire sack had disappeared.","Since Namu-Ppareumbo was the one who primarily ate them, I always kept them in one specific place.","If they had vanished, there could be only one explanation.","Someone had broken into my shelter and taken them.","The idea of a thief living in the forest seemed absurd, but it wasn’t unprecedented.","Hadn’t a raccoon stolen some fasting pills during the last torrential downpour?","Of course, Namu-Ppareumbo had taught that raccoon a painful lesson before it ended up inside Wonmo’s stomach.","\"...\"","Perhaps it was deeply shocked to hear that the fasting pills were gone.","Namu-Ppareumbo scrambled off my back at the fastest speed it could achieve outside combat.","It then stared blankly at the spot where the fasting pills had been.","I could vividly sense the devastation and fury radiating from it.","Who could have stolen the fasting pills?","Stranger still, the thief hadn’t touched anything else.","’Maybe they left footprints.’","Criminals always left traces behind.","Leaving the silently furious Namu-Ppareumbo inside, I stepped out of the cave.","When I carefully examined the ground, I discovered footprints that hadn’t been there before.","’I should upload these to the Gallery.’","I didn’t know who the culprit was, but...","’I’ve never seen Ppareumbo this angry before.’","It seemed the thief had nothing left to look forward to but death.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the jungle—","\"Ooh-ho-ho! Ooh-ho!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh! Ooh-hoo-hoo!\"","An impromptu gorilla feast was underway."]},{"title":"Chapter 105","paragraphs":["Hostage (1)","Whoever they were, they had seriously gotten on Namu-Ppareumbo’s bad side.","With that thought, I made a post on the gallery. This time, it wasn’t a handprint but footprints.","The handprint could wait. The urgent matter right now was identifying the culprit.","Aside from Namu-Ppareumbo’s staple food disappearing in its entirety, this was also a serious problem for me.","Whether they had deliberately waited until we were gone or it had simply been unfortunate timing, the incident had occurred during that brief window.","’At this rate, I won’t even be able to leave home whenever I want.’","Should I have installed an iron fence as well, knowing this might happen? I wasn’t sure.","Perhaps I should have built an actual door instead of a fence. It was something I needed to start considering.","Title: Anyone Know What Made These Footprints?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of animal footprints)","(Photo of animal footprints)","(Photo of Namu-Ppareumbo’s back, radiating emptiness and rage)","(Photo of Wonmo beside him, nervously watching his mood)","I went exploring today, and my fasting pills were gone when I returned.","These footprints seem to belong to the culprits. Does anyone recognize them? I’m asking because there seem to be several different kinds.","└ Heavenly Demon: They look more like handprints than footprints. More importantly, I can feel Namu-Ppareumbo’s fury through the photograph alone.","└ SwordMaster: I know, right? Wonmo cautiously watching him from the side is adorable too. Does he realize something terrible has happened?","└ Wild Grylls: Wonmo is surprisingly good at reading the room. By the way, Heavenly Demon, if it isn’t too much trouble, could I ask you for some more fasting pills?","└ Heavenly Demon: That itself is no problem, but it will take some time. The pills require rare medicinal herbs, so our supply is limited.","The moment I read that comment, I checked on Namu-Ppareumbo. He was still staring at the spot where the fasting pills had been.","For a person, would it feel like discovering that an entire pile of meat dishes had vanished?","And now he would have to eat nothing but vegetables and wild greens.","Thinking about it that way, I would be pissed too. Besides, this problem wasn’t limited to Namu-Ppareumbo.","’They trespassed into my territory and even stole my belongings.’","It was embarrassing to admit, but whenever nature called, I usually relieved myself nearby.","I wanted to mark my territory at least a little. Before that, I had always buried it with dirt.","However, since I would have to stay here for a long time, establishing territory of my own was unavoidable.","└ Starlight Princess: Stealing someone else’s food... What terrible creatures. What will you do if you find them?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t have enough time to search for them today. I’ll have to look tomorrow.","└ Cheonggu Princess: The uniform is safe, right?","└ Wild Grylls: It was lying on the ground.","└ Cheonggu Princess: ...","└ Even animals rejected it, hahahahaha.","└ Animals won’t even touch Cheonggu’s uniform, lololol.","└ The design is admittedly a little lame, lol.","└ Forget the design, that deer emblem is just... hahaha.","└ Allfather: Hmm. Judging from the prints alone, they appear to belong to primates.","└ Wild Grylls: Primates?","└ Allfather: Yes. I cannot determine the exact species, but they are definitely primate prints.","└ Wild Grylls: Then there’s a high chance they’re gorillas. Do gorillas invade other creatures’ territories?","└ Allfather: That rarely happens. As I mentioned before, they possess low aggression and seldom fight outsiders unless there is internal conflict among their own group.","In other words, there was a high probability that the gorillas had undergone some kind of change.","Whether it involved increased aggression or something else, it wasn’t good news for me.","’And it looks like there was more than one...’","There were many footprints. Looking at them closely, each had a slightly different shape.","After roughly distinguishing them, I estimated that there had been four or five.","Even one would have been overwhelming, yet an entire group had invaded.","This was not something I could overlook. I absolutely had to make an example of them.","’But how?’","I didn’t even know exactly where the gorillas lived, let alone when they would return.","They could raid the place every time my animal companions and I were away.","It seemed my only choice was to set a trap and wait. Entering their territory would be far too dangerous.","’I never expected them to strike first like this.’","I had imagined myself trespassing into other animals’ territories, but I had never dreamed that other animals would raid my home.","As I had said earlier, I should have realized it when that raccoon blatantly stole my fasting pills.","The animals in this forest seemed to be evolving in ways far beyond anything I could predict.","└ Praise the Sun: What are you going to do when you catch the thieves? Just kill them?","└ Wild Grylls: If they do it again, I won’t have any choice but to kill them. This is where I live.","└ Praise the Sun: You’ve gotten ruthless. Didn’t you agonize over Namu-Ppareumbo for ages?","└ Wild Grylls: It wasn’t that I spared him. I couldn’t kill him;;","└ Praise the Sun: Oh, right. I’d forgotten about that.","└ Looks like Ppareumbo is seriously pissed this time.","└ Whoever did it is definitely dead, hahaha.","└ Gorilla vs. Namu-Ppareumbo. My heart is already swelling with anticipation.","└ Passing Dwarf: What happened? Something got stolen?","└ Wild Grylls: My fasting pills. Ppareumbo eats them, but they’re also my emergency rations.","└ Passing Dwarf: Oh, really? You should install a door from now on, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m seriously considering it.","└ Passing Dwarf: Actually, forget it. Even if you install a door, they’ll just smash it apart.","└ Wild Grylls: You have a point. Ha. Damn it.","└ Destined to be robbed;;","└ Guess you have no choice but to keep it wide open, lol.","└ Grylls’s home gives everything away for free.","└ Wild Grylls: Shut up, you bastards.","└ Grylls, criminals always return to the scene of the crime.","└ The comment above is right. They might come back tomorrow.","└ Wild Grylls: So in the end, I just have to wait until tomorrow. Fine, okay.","After chatting about various things on the gallery, I looked around the shelter.","Aside from the cave, the surrounding area was generally wide open.","Although I had blocked it off with barricades, small animals could still enter easily.","’And like the dwarf said, they’d just destroy any door I built.’","An iron fence could keep out small animals, but even a door wouldn’t stop larger ones.","There were so many extreme creatures here that I couldn’t think of a suitable solution.","My best option was to claim the surrounding area as my territory and make sure nothing dared to enter without permission.","’Should I comfort Ppareumbo first?’","Namu-Ppareumbo was still staring blankly into space. He seemed more devastated than angry now.","I started to place a hand on his shoulder, then stopped.","Come to think of it, this bastard still hadn’t washed himself.","I quietly lowered my hand and offered him some words of comfort instead.","\"I’m angry too, Ppareumbo.\"","\"....\"","\"We still have something to eat today, so don’t worry too much. But I can’t promise that we’ll recover the stolen fasting pills.\"","I could obtain another supply through the Heavenly Demon.","However, it would be best to consider the stolen pills gone for good.","As Allfather had said, gorillas were herbivores. They might have already eaten all of them.","\"For now, just be patient. Those bastards might come back tomorrow. We can teach them a lesson then, okay?\"","\"Try to lighten up a little. Wonmo is scared of you.\"","Only then did Namu-Ppareumbo turn his head to the side, toward Wonmo.","Wonmo flinched when their eyes met, but soon began rubbing his cheek against him.","\"Kyuu. Kyuuu.\"","\"....\"","Had adorable Wonmo’s nuzzling softened his heart?","Namu-Ppareumbo slowly raised his hand and placed it atop Wonmo’s head.","It seemed that he also regarded Wonmo as either a pet or a member of the family.","I smiled warmly at the sight, but only briefly before considering how to handle the situation going forward.","’A trap... would be pointless. I wonder if there’s anything like CCTV?’","There was even an orichalcum vein nearby, so I wondered whether a similar type of magic existed.","If relay magic existed, there was no way they didn’t have something like CCTV.","If I couldn’t prevent my home from being robbed, I at least wanted to identify the culprits.","’Or I could scare them away with an alarm.’","It was a fairly decent idea. Wouldn’t Cheonggu Princess know something about that?","Just as I was about to log into the gallery with that thought—","Rustle—","\"....\"","I clearly heard something brushing against the grass outside.","The moment I heard it, I stopped trying to access the gallery.","Wonmo, who had been acting affectionate, seemed to sense something too. His eyes widened, and he froze in place.","As for Namu-Ppareumbo...","Swoosh—","He turned his head toward the cave entrance.","I did the same.","Silently and stealthily, I reached into my subspace bag.","What I pulled out was my crossbow. I always carried it with me, just in case.","Picking it up from the ground would have made at least some noise, but taking it from the subspace bag was completely silent.","Drawing the string wasn’t difficult either. I had grown stronger than before, so this much was a piece of cake.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Primate cries came from outside the cave.","I couldn’t tell whether they came from small monkeys or gorillas.","I would have to see them with my own eyes to find out.","Suppressing every trace of my presence, I crept forward.","And perhaps the anonymous commenter had been right when they said criminals always returned to the scene of the crime.","\"Ooh! Ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh.\"","Two monkeys—no, two gorillas—were talking to each other outside.","One of them beat its chest and gestured in apparent frustration, while the other made gestures as though trying to restrain it.","As expected of creatures that understood the concept of theft, they seemed more intelligent than ordinary gorillas.","Even so, to Namu-Ppareumbo and me, they were nothing more than thieves.","Bastards who stole food in the wild deserved to die.","They had stolen it knowing that could happen in the first place, hadn’t they?","Swoosh—","I slowly raised my crossbow and aimed it at the gorillas.","They were still chattering among themselves, apparently unaware that we had returned.","I wanted to pull the trigger immediately, but I suppressed the urge with superhuman patience.","My chances of hitting them would increase if they came a little closer. It was still too soon.","Splash!","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Had the fasting pills not been enough?","One of the gorillas pulled out the fish stored inside the metal barrel.","The fish was so enormous that even the gorilla had to wrap both arms around it.","The sight made me feel as though my rage meter had risen another notch.","The otters had all died after attempting to steal my fish.","That gorilla would meet the same fate.","Slowly—","As I silently took aim, Namu-Ppareumbo positioned himself beside me.","He wasn’t trying to charge forward. He stood right by my side.","He almost resembled a spotter assisting a sniper.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh.\"","Before long, the jubilant gorillas turned around and began to leave.","I aimed at the one that had greedily taken my fish.","Then, I stopped breathing altogether. Just as my sights settled perfectly on the target—","Shoot.","Perhaps it was my imagination, but a voice that seemed to belong to Namu-Ppareumbo echoed inside my head.","The instant I heard it, I pulled the trigger without hesitation.","Twang!","The moment the string was released, the bolt tore through the air.","Its tip flew directly toward the gorilla’s broad back.","Thud!","\"Gwooooooh!\"","\"Uooh?!\"","Flap-flap—","The bolt buried itself squarely in the gorilla’s back.","The gorilla immediately screamed in pain and let out a tremendous roar.","At the same time, the fish it had been carrying flew into the air and thrashed violently.","Creak—","I didn’t stop there. I immediately took out another bolt and loaded the crossbow.","Then I aimed at the gorilla once again. The other one had already fled into the undergrowth.","The gorilla struck by the bolt was also desperately trying to escape.","It apparently had no presence of mind to retrieve the fish that had fallen to the ground.","A human would have collapsed after taking a shot like that, but a beast was still a beast.","Yet even beasts could be deprived of their mobility.","Thud!","\"Uoooooh!\"","By targeting their legs.","The bolt lodged squarely in the gorilla’s calf.","I had fired immediately after loading, so I had been rather lucky.","Or perhaps my skill had improved. Either way, the situation was favorable.","The moment the gorilla collapsed, I took up my sword and shield and stepped outside.","Namu-Ppareumbo climbed onto my back as well, ready to join the fight at any moment.","\"Uooh....\"","The gorilla reached toward the bushes, desperately trying to escape.","But its companion had already abandoned it. There was no one left to help it.","I approached the gorilla as it clawed frantically along the ground.","The gorilla seemed to notice the shadow looming over it and slowly turned to look at me.","\"U... uoooh....\"","It stared at me with a terror-stricken expression.","Then it noticed Namu-Ppareumbo clinging to my back, and its eyes widened in shock.","Its reaction seemed to say, What are you doing here? It looked unable to believe the situation before it.","Whatever the circumstances were, the gorilla clearly knew Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Uh... ugh....\"","The gorilla pointed at Namu-Ppareumbo, then fainted.","Foam gathered around its mouth, as though it had been unable to withstand the physical and psychological shock.","The only difference was that it couldn’t speak. Its reactions otherwise seemed remarkably human.","Had its intelligence truly increased?","More importantly, however, its reaction puzzled me.","\"Ppareumbo.\"","’Judging by its behavior, it seems pretty similar to you.’","The fact that it had extorted food from me only made that possibility strangely more convincing.","\"What did you do to these guys?\"","Had he been the local bully around here?","I had no idea."]},{"title":"Chapter 106","paragraphs":["Hostage (2)","Two gorillas had broken into Grylls’s home again.","One of them had been subdued after Grylls shot it with a crossbow, but the other fled for its life.","It forced its way through dense bushes and thick trees, climbing trunks and leaping from branch to branch.","Its speed was remarkably agile for such a heavily built gorilla. That showed just how desperate it was.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","Before long, the fleeing gorilla reached the place where its troop lived.","The gorillas were currently enjoying an unexpected fasting-pill feast.","However, when their companion approached with such an urgent expression, they had no choice but to put the feast on hold.","\"Ooh?\"","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","Sensing that something serious had happened, the leader stepped forward.","The fleeing gorilla then explained everything that had happened.","After hearing the full story, the leader adopted a grave expression and issued an order.","\"Ooh-ooh. Ooh!\"","\"Ooh!\"","First, they would send out scouts and observe the situation. They had been the ones to trespass into another’s territory.","If the owner of that territory had killed their fellow gorilla, they could retaliate afterward.","When the leader conveyed something along those lines, the other gorillas nodded.","\"Ooh-hoo.\"","\"Hoo....\"","The leader handed the gorilla a fasting pill to calm it down.","It seemed a fight would break out before long.","That was the feeling they had.","***","After completely subduing the gorilla, what I did next was kill it...","No, I tied it up.","I wanted to cut off its head and put it on display, but that didn’t suit my nature.","More importantly, since these creatures possessed considerable intelligence, there were many factors I needed to consider.","’If they have any sense of camaraderie, they’ll definitely come back. It would be better to keep this one alive for then.’","Seeing their companion dead might only enrage them further.","One gorilla would be manageable, but if several of them attacked at once, it would be a difficult fight.","Even with Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo here, I had no idea how powerful the gorilla troop was.","What I needed was information.","It would be best to use the gorilla I had captured as a hostage and extract information from them.","’Let’s see. Tie its arms behind its back, then tie its legs... It must be incredibly strong, so I need to bind it tightly.’","Gorillas possessed tremendous strength even among primates.","And this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","It was a place where even ordinary-sized animals were terrifying.","Therefore, I thoroughly bound the unconscious gorilla with rope.","I tied it so securely that it would never be able to escape through brute strength alone.","What did I do about the bolts lodged in its body?","I administered some rough first aid.","The bolts had gone in so cleanly that I simply snapped off both ends.","An elixir?","I didn’t have any elixirs to waste on thieves.","I merely purchased the cheapest potion available at the auction house and wrapped the wounds in bandages.","└ Heavenly Demon: You have bound it securely. Since ancient times, those who stole food have been punished with flogging.","└ Wild Grylls: Food is directly tied to my survival, so I’m thinking of giving it an even harsher punishment.","└ Heavenly Demon: Cutting off its hands so that it can never steal again would not be a bad idea.","└ Wild Grylls: Whoa;; I’ll just stick with flogging.","└ SwordMaster: Just cut off its hands. As far as I know, repeat offenders have their hands cut off in my country too.","└ Wild Grylls: ;:;","Title: Captured the Thief Alive","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a gorilla tightly bound with rope)","Some anonymous commenter said that criminals always return to the scene of the crime.","Apparently, the fasting pills weren’t enough for these gorilla bastards, because they tried to steal my fish too.","There were two of them. I subdued one with my crossbow, but the other escaped.","For now, I’m planning to use this bastard as a hostage to obtain information.","It was the kind of extreme punishment that suited the era.","It seemed barbaric, yet also strangely reasonable.","└ Allfather: You have certainly bound it tightly. Judging from its appearance, it is definitely a gorilla.","└ Wild Grylls: Right? I thought these creatures were herbivores, but they tried to steal my fish too.","└ Allfather: It appears their diet has changed. Be careful. Its companions will certainly come.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve already taken that into account. I’m waiting for them.","└ Suspiciously: Is that one male or female?","└ Why are you asking?","└ Suspiciously: I heard gorillas live in matriarchal societies.","└ Aren’t you thinking of orangutans?","└ I heard male orangutans travel alone too.","└ What kind of beastkin doesn’t even know that? Lol.","└ Suspiciously: There are things even beastkin don’t know, damn it.","Lunatics were bound to appear on the gallery sooner or later.","I chuckled but didn’t respond. I simply let them entertain themselves.","If they crossed the line, the moderators would deal with them. There was no need for me to interfere.","’More importantly, when is this guy going to wake up?’","I stared at the still-unconscious gorilla.","It had foamed at the mouth and fainted the moment it saw Namu-Ppareumbo.","That made me curious about Namu-Ppareumbo’s past, but it wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","The important thing was obtaining information. It seemed best to leave the gorilla alone for the time being.","’It would be so convenient if I could talk to animals.’","The ability to communicate with animals.","In other words, the power of a druid.","Since this was a fantasy world, I had searched for such an ability, but apparently none existed.","There were occasionally people who claimed they could understand animals, but most of them were lying.","’Even humans speak different languages. How much worse must it be for animals?’","While entertaining those pointless thoughts, I carefully examined the gorilla.","It was much larger than me.","Aside from that, however, it seemed completely ordinary. I couldn’t find anything unusual about it.","\"Sniff, sniff.\"","\"Wonmo, that’s not food.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","I warned Wonmo in case he tried to eat the unconscious gorilla.","My job was to wait until this creature’s companions arrived.","If they didn’t come...","There was nothing else I could do. I would have to kill it.","Disposing of the body wouldn’t be a problem either. I could bury it or throw it into the river.","’Should I dig the hole in advance, just in case?’","I was thinking about that as I casually picked up a shovel.","\"Ugh....\"","The unconscious gorilla gradually began to regain its senses.","Seeing it wake up, I quietly put down the shovel.","\"Hey. You awake?\"","\"Uuugh...?\"","The gorilla stared at me in confusion, apparently still dazed.","It didn’t seem to recognize my face yet.","\"Ooh... ooh? Ooh?!\"","Then the gorilla suddenly began thrashing violently.","Judging by its bewildered expression, it had realized that its body was completely bound.","It was a good thing I had used several lengths of rope. Otherwise, it probably would have broken free in no time.","\"Awooh....\"","Of course, struggling wouldn’t make the wounds from the crossbow bolts disappear.","Unable to endure the pain, the thrashing gorilla soon became still.","Now that it had calmed down, it was time for us to have a conversation of sorts.","\"Hey. Look at me.\"","At my words, the gorilla slowly raised its head.","Its face had been twisted in pain moments ago, but now it looked stern and unyielding.","It seemed determined not to answer me, regardless of what I did.","It really was like a person.","’You couldn’t understand me anyway.’","There was no particular reason I had called out to it.","I merely wanted to observe its reaction.","I had intended to decide how to treat it based on that reaction, but it appeared to be remarkably stubborn.","’Then how will it react when it sees Namu-Ppareumbo?’","I brought over Namu-Ppareumbo, who had been standing silently and staring into the forest.","Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t resist at all, even as I carried him over.","I then placed him in front of the gorilla’s face where it could see him.","\"Do you know this—\"","\"Ookyaaaaak!\"","The instant it saw Namu-Ppareumbo, the gorilla reacted as though it were having a seizure.","Its violent force could be felt even though it was bound with rope. That was how terrified it was.","I stared blankly at the rampaging gorilla before turning toward Namu-Ppareumbo.","Namu-Ppareumbo looked at the thrashing gorilla and slowly raised his hand.","Just as I was about to stop him, thinking he might kill it—","Smack!","Ppareumbo delivered a resounding slap across its face.","The gorilla immediately became docile. Its dejected expression was an added bonus.","No. Rather than dejected, it seemed to have lost the will to live.","’What the hell has this bastard been doing?’","I knew what Namu-Ppareumbo was capable of. He possessed speed that the eye couldn’t follow and razor-sharp claws.","I couldn’t tell whether he was infamous among all the gorillas or if only this particular one feared him.","Either way, he had made it behave, so it was fine.","I rummaged through my bag and took out a fasting pill.","It was one of the pills I had brought as emergency food and as a gesture of goodwill.","I intended to show it to the gorilla.","\"Hey. Look at this.\"","\"...?\"","\"You know what this is, right?\"","The moment I showed it the fasting pill, the gorilla’s eyes trembled violently.","It clearly recognized the pill, which was practically a confession that they were the culprits.","There was nothing more to verify. I snorted and slowly conveyed my meaning.","\"Fasting pill.\"","First, the fasting pill.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","Next, Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Staple food. Okay?\"","Finally, I mimed eating it, and the gorilla’s face seemingly turned pale.","You might ask how I could tell when its entire body was covered in black skin and fur.","Would you believe me if I said that was simply how it felt?","Anyway, let’s just leave it at that.","’In the end, I’ll have to wait for this guy’s companions to arrive.’","I asked Namu-Ppareumbo to watch the gorilla.","Since I didn’t know when the troop would appear, I planned to inspect my weapons.","First was the crossbow that had proven so useful. I drew the string so it would be ready to fire at any moment.","Rustle, rustle—","\"Kyuu?\"","\"....\"","Speak of the tiger and it appears.","No, in this case, was it speak of the gorilla?","Holding the loaded crossbow, I turned toward the source of the noise.","Rustle!","Apparently having no intention of concealing themselves, gorillas began emerging from the bushes.","There weren’t just one or two, but exactly five.","An exceptionally large gorilla stood in the center.","Since it stood ahead of the others, it appeared to be their leader. More importantly, there was also a difference in their equipment.","’Just as Allfather said.’","The leader was barehanded, but each of the other gorillas held something.","One of them was even holding a stone axe. I couldn’t describe how shocked I was when I saw it.","The fact that they had made a stone axe meant that they understood the concept of crafting.","They seemed more intelligent than I had expected.","I needed to remain vigilant.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ugh...!\"","Upon seeing that its companions had arrived, the hostage gorilla cried out frantically.","But as I had mentioned, it had been shot with crossbow bolts. The movement made it grimace in pain.","The presumed leader glanced at the hostage before focusing its gaze on me.","I raised my sword and shield, prepared to fight if necessary.","\"Ooh! Ooh!\"","\"Uooh! Uooh!\"","Then the gorillas beside their leader began making a commotion.","Rather than a commotion, it was more like they had seen something horrifying.","\"....\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo.","At some point, Ppareumbo had approached my side.","Most of the gorillas began trembling in fear when they saw him.","The leader managed to remain calm, but its expression had stiffened considerably.","That meant Namu-Ppareumbo’s infamy among the gorillas was truly terrifying.","Thanks to that, the negotiation might be a little easier.","I immediately began communicating with them.","First, I showed them one of the fasting pills they had taken.","I was asking whether they had stolen something containing these.","The leader seemed to understand my intention and nodded.","\"Ooh.\"","The leader issued an order with a short grunt.","At its command, one of the gorillas brought over an object.","The leader took it and threw it toward me.","Flop—","However, apparently containing nothing, the object lost momentum and fell midway.","It was a pouch.","The pouch that had contained the fasting pills.","But there were no fasting pills left inside.","’They already ate all of them.’","I had suspected as much, but they had eaten everything in such a short time.","All I could do was sigh.","Would those bastards apologize?","Or would they shamelessly refuse to take responsibility?","Considering Namu-Ppareumbo’s infamy, they would probably apologize, but who knew?","First, it seemed best to observe Namu-Ppareumbo’s reaction.","\"What do you want to do?\"","\"....\"","Namu-Ppareumbo had been staring blankly at the empty pouch. At my question, he slowly began walking.","The gorilla troop made no move in response. They merely watched him with tense expressions.","Before long, Namu-Ppareumbo approached the fully restrained gorilla.","For a moment, I wondered whether he had partially given up and intended to release it.","Slash!","I was wrong.","Namu-Ppareumbo’s actions exceeded my imagination.","With his sharp claws, he sliced straight through the gorilla’s neck.","These were the same claws that had cut through a metal barrel—the claws I had personally maintained for him.","They could effortlessly sever the fragile flesh and bones of an animal.","Spurt!","Ignoring the blood gushing from the severed neck, Namu-Ppareumbo did what he intended to do.","He drove his claws into the gorilla’s head as it rolled across the ground like a ball.","It looked as though he had stabbed it with a fork.","Then, holding it that way, he slowly raised his arm and hurled the head toward the gorillas.","Thud! Bounce! Roll—","The severed gorilla head landed in front of the leader.","He hadn’t thrown it at me, but had tossed it upward instead.","What exactly was he trying to do?","Just in case, I placed my left foot forward so I could defend myself at any moment.","Whoosh—","As the gorilla’s head descended, the leader pulled back its right arm.","The moment the head reached eye level, the leader thrust its drawn-back fist forward.","Booooom!","A deafening impact erupted.","Whoooooosh!","The gorilla’s head flew toward us like a cannonball."]},{"title":"Chapter 107","paragraphs":["The Way of the Wild (1)","The wild is harsh.","And savage.","It would be foolish to demand \"reason\" from animals living in the wild.","It was a world governed by the law of the jungle, where the strong took everything from the weak.","At the same time, it was a world where those who survived were the strong.","Even if I wanted to treat them rationally, animals were not rational creatures.","Their instincts took precedence over reason, and that wouldn’t change even if their intelligence increased.","Those who invaded your territory were enemies.","Those who stole your food were enemies.","Those who went beyond stealing it and actually ate it were enemies too.","Either you killed your enemies, or they killed you.","That was the way of the wild and the law of nature.","Whoosh!","The gorilla’s head had been punched away by the leader.","It flew toward Namu-Ppareumbo like a cannonball, but who was Namu-Ppareumbo?","He could effortlessly dodge an arrow fired from point-blank range.","Avoiding a mere head propelled by a punch was nothing to him.","’But that thing was launched with a punch?’","Even so, I was astonished.","The punch I had just witnessed from the gorilla leader wasn’t merely powerful. What made it even more astonishing was the perfect control behind that strength.","If the leader had simply forced it forward with brute strength, the gorilla’s head would have exploded.","Yet through some unknown principle, it had been launched like a cannonball without bursting apart.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","Namu-Ppareumbo’s provocation had been answered by the leader’s attack.","When the leader began beating its chest, the other gorillas followed suit.","A gorilla beating its chest was unmistakably a threat.","In other words, this was a declaration of war.","\"Ha....\"","\"Grrrr...!\"","Unlike me, who let out a sigh, Namu-Ppareumbo wore his usual relaxed expression.","Wonmo seemed to sense the atmosphere too. His fur stood on end as he became alert.","’They were the ones in the wrong, though.’","The gorillas had poured the fuel, and Namu-Ppareumbo had thrown a match onto it.","The problem was that it was my house now going up in flames.","What a rotten situation.","Unless we dealt with those gorillas, there would be no extinguishing the fire consuming my home.","I steeled myself and prepared for an attack that could come at any moment.","’They’ll be incomparably stronger than those otters.’","These weren’t just any animals. They were gorillas, the primates with the greatest physical strength.","Moreover, as the clubs in their hands demonstrated, they could even use tools.","This would undoubtedly be a difficult fight.","Above all, the gorilla leader bothered me.","’What is that thing that it doesn’t need to carry anything?’","It had no weapon, yet somehow seemed even stronger.","It was a strange intuition.","While I narrowed my eyes and glared at the leader, the other gorillas began charging.","As expected of gorillas, they rushed forward with their long arms planted against the ground.","The leader, however, merely stood behind them and watched. It made no move to join the battle itself.","\"Ppareumbo, get on Wonmo’s back.\"","\"....\"","\"Wonmo, don’t start running yet. Stay close behind me.\"","After giving Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo their instructions, I slowly retreated.","My chances of victory would be low if I charged at the gorillas like this.","I had been able to defeat the otters because they were small and their tactics were simple.","But look at these bastards.","They weren’t merely charging blindly.","’They’re surrounding us.’","Instead of running straight at us, they scattered in every direction.","They spread out to the front, rear, and both sides, forming an encirclement.","They executed the maneuver the moment the battle began, suggesting they had done it many times before.","’As expected, these bastards know how to use their heads.’","Intelligence was the reason humanity had risen to the top of the food chain.","Even if their intellect fell far short of a human’s, that didn’t make them any less threatening.","\"Kwaaaaah!\"","Once the encirclement was complete, the gorilla whose gaze met mine swung down its weapon.","Of the three wielding a bone, a stone axe, and a wooden club, it was the one holding the stone axe.","I urgently raised my shield to defend myself.","Just in case, I even reinforced it with mana.","Claaaaang!","The stone axe collided with my shield, producing a deafening crash.","As expected of gorillas, reputed to be the strongest primates, the impact felt tremendously heavy.","If this had been before I ate the eel, every one of their attacks would have been lethal.","But I had no time to worry about the noise.","The gorilla wielding the wooden club was already approaching.","Without even thinking of counterattacking, I hurriedly pulled back my shield.","Whoosh!","The club narrowly swept past my face.","At the same time, the stone-axe-wielding gorilla roared and charged at me.","Its vicious teeth were slightly frightening, but I forced the fear aside.","Clang!","The stone axe struck my shield again.","However, counterattacking was difficult.","Just as before, the club-wielding gorilla immediately launched another attack.","Their attacks were wild and indiscriminate, yet that very recklessness allowed them to cover one another’s openings.","’At this rate, I’ll be at a disadvantage.’","I didn’t even have the freedom to check on Wonmo and Namu-Ppareumbo.","I was somehow managing to block and evade their attacks with the skills I had honed until now, but I was hopelessly outnumbered.","Unless I attacked, I would never escape the gorillas’ endless assault.","’Their attacks themselves are simple.’","After exchanging several rounds of attacks and defenses, I began to understand their pattern.","No, perhaps calling it a pattern was giving them too much credit.","Their attacks were closer to wild swings.","However, they were using \"tools.\"","They were trying to strike me with those tools.","I was looking for the inevitable openings created whenever someone grew careless while trying to use a weapon.","How ironic.","They had picked up weapons to become stronger, yet those weapons were instead creating openings.","Whoosh!","The stone axe narrowly passed in front of me.","I had watched the timing of its downward swing and stepped back.","’Now the other one will swing its club.’","I glanced to the side.","Just as I had expected, the gorilla was preparing to swing its club.","It wasn’t bringing the weapon straight down from above. It was swinging diagonally.","Having roughly predicted the direction of the attack, I raised my shield.","And the sword in my right hand—","Stab!","I thrust my sword toward the collarbone of the stone-axe-wielding gorilla.","Since it was the Heavenly Demon’s sword and was even enveloped in aura, the blade penetrated easily.","Moreover, given the gorilla’s posture, stabbing it in the shoulder was extremely easy.","\"Kuaaaaaah!\"","Booom!","Clutching the wounded area, the gorilla stumbled backward.","Meanwhile, my shield blocked the wooden club.","Now was my chance.","While one gorilla was reeling, I decided to eliminate the other one first.","’If it’s only one...’","The remaining gorilla continued attacking despite what had happened to its companion.","That was the mistake that would cost it the fight.","Its physical strength might have been immense, but it was slow.","Furthermore, this one’s weapon wasn’t a stone axe. It was merely a wooden club.","Crack!","No matter how sturdy the wood was, it would still break after colliding with an iron shield.","The instant I heard the club snap, I swung my sword diagonally.","Slash!","Rather than trying to cleave through the gorilla’s entire body, I focused on cutting only as deeply as necessary.","That was something SwordMaster had taught me.","Trying to cleave completely through a body inevitably required putting more strength into the attack.","Doing so significantly reduced stability.","A sword depended more on stability than strength.","SwordMaster had even advised me to use an axe instead if I wanted to rely on greater force.","’He also said that striking something too hard could damage my shoulder.’","Following his advice, I had slightly changed the way I fought.","Even when a perfect opportunity presented itself, I wouldn’t put excessive strength into my attack.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was so exceptional that I didn’t have to worry about its cutting power for the time being.","\"Krraaaaaah!\"","A diagonal wound appeared across the gorilla’s upper body, sending it crashing backward.","Blood didn’t spray immediately, but the wound was clearly deep.","\"Kuaaaaah! Kua! Kuaaaaah!\"","The gorilla thrashed and rolled across the ground.","Blood began gushing from the wound carved by my sword.","It wasn’t only blood. Its organs began spilling from its split abdomen.","Even though I had swung lightly, the power of the attack seemed to have torn open more than half its abdomen.","That took care of one.","The other was still clutching its shoulder.","When our eyes met, it looked at me in terror.","Perhaps the greater one’s intelligence became, the harder it was to escape the fear of death.","Stab!","\"Kuh... kua....\"","I immediately finished it by stabbing it through the heart.","Cutting its throat didn’t suit my nature, and more importantly, it would make cleaning up afterward troublesome.","Having killed both gorillas, I turned around to check on Wonmo and Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Kyuu... kyuu....\"","\"Wonmo?\"","As expected, the two gorillas they had faced had become cold corpses.","However, Wonmo was whimpering as though he had been injured.","I glanced at the gorilla leader before approaching Wonmo.","\"Kyuuu....\"","\"You broke a claw.\"","One of Wonmo’s claws had broken.","Fortunately, it wasn’t a serious injury.","It didn’t look as though a gorilla had struck him. He seemed to have made a mistake on his own.","I stroked Wonmo’s head and spoke to Namu-Ppareumbo, who was riding on his back.","\"Go to the cave and give Wonmo some elixir. You can do that, right?\"","\"....\"","Namu-Ppareumbo nodded.","He then patted Wonmo’s side a couple of times.","Wonmo glanced at me once before lumbering back into the cave.","’Now, all that remains is...’","The gorilla leader.","I turned and faced it.","The creature had continued observing from behind even as all its companions were killed.","Was it confident?","Or did it have some other reason?","’The fact that it isn’t carrying a weapon bothers me most.’","Unlike the other gorillas, which had wielded weapons, it stood completely barehanded.","What did it possess that allowed it to fight without a weapon?","I couldn’t help wondering.","But that didn’t change the fact that it was my enemy.","I spoke to the gorilla leader.","\"Do you still want to continue?\"","The gorilla leader didn’t answer.","Instead, it responded by slowly rising upright.","As it straightened its back, it lifted both hands from the ground.","Its two legs were short compared to its arms, like a sloth’s, but they were as thick as logs.","’So it intends to fight...’","Just as I thought that, the gorilla slowly began moving.","It placed its left foot forward and drew its right foot back.","It extended its left hand with its palm facing forward and positioned its right hand beside its waist.","Finally...","It slightly twisted its body.","When all those movements came together, they formed a complete stance.","’What the fuck am I looking at?’","No matter how I looked at it, that was a stance for performing martial arts.","And a gorilla was displaying it?","A martial art that could never be learned without a master’s instruction?","I wanted to deny everything I was seeing.","Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, this was...","This was going too far.","\"...Who taught you?\"","\"Who the hell taught you...?!\"","My voice was unconsciously beginning to rise when the gorilla leader leaned its upper body forward, as though it didn’t consider my question worth answering.","It was an obvious signal that it was about to charge.","I suppressed my agitation and assumed my stance.","Swoosh!","Its movements differed from those of the other gorillas.","The others had simply charged at me.","The leader, however, approached me as though it were gliding across the ground.","Whooom!","That wasn’t all.","The moment it arrived in front of me, the gorilla leader attacked.","Its enormous palm flew directly toward my face.","If that attack landed properly, my head would burst like a watermelon.","Bang!","I barely turned my head in time to evade the palm strike.","But I hadn’t avoided it completely.","The palm narrowly grazed my cheek.","I felt a stinging pain, as though my skin had been torn.","’Th-this is...’","As though time itself had slowed, I found myself staring directly at the gorilla leader.","Its eyes were perfectly calm, yet a faint anger smoldered within them.","Despite that anger, it maintained complete composure.","Seeing those eyes reminded me of the palmprints I had discovered during today’s exploration.","One palmprint that I had assumed belonged to a gorilla.","And beside it, another that appeared to belong to a human.","’Just who...?!’","There was only one possible explanation.","’Just who the hell taught it...?!’","Someone had taught this gorilla martial arts."]},{"title":"Chapter 108","paragraphs":["The Way of the Wild (3)","Martial arts had contributed greatly to human history.","From ancient times to the modern era, more than half of humanity’s history had been defined by war.","And martial arts had played a significant role in those wars.","Particularly in ancient times, the course of a war could often change depending on an individual’s skill.","As technology advanced, the greatest cheat item in history—the gun—eventually appeared. Even so, the importance of martial arts never diminished.","That was because martial arts weren’t limited to any particular tool.","They were techniques for wielding martial force more effectively.","That was the essence of martial arts, and even the accuracy and stability of a gun varied drastically depending on the person using it.","Furthermore, martial arts were difficult to master without someone teaching you directly. Learning them alone might technically be possible, but it was close to impossible.","The length of a person’s limbs, height, weight, and many other attributes were different. Even talent varied tremendously between individuals.","Someone needed to watch the learner in real time and correct them accordingly.","’Just who...?!’","I couldn’t hide my astonishment as I faced the gorilla leader that had launched the palm strike.","It had approached as though gliding across the ground, followed by an attack that flowed as naturally as water.","Every individual movement was astonishing.","But I had no time to think.","What mattered was that this gorilla leader was my enemy.","I had to defeat it at all costs.","Swoosh!","The moment I evaded the palm strike, I counterattacked.","Because it felt as though time were moving slowly, my counterattack was equally swift.","My sword descended from above.","At this rate, the blade would bury itself in the gorilla leader’s collarbone.","Yet the gorilla leader’s expression remained perfectly calm.","Instead of retreating, it moved even closer to me.","Grab!","Then it seized my arm with both hands.","Not only that, but it also turned its back toward me.","Just as before, every movement flowed seamlessly into the next.","And as that sequence of movements continued, something happened to my body.","Whoosh!","Without my consent, both my legs left the ground.","Booom!","The world spun once, and a tremendous impact struck my back.","My breath was violently knocked from my lungs, and my eyes widened in pain.","What the hell had it just done to me?","’Was that a shoulder throw...?!’","I had only a moment to be shocked that the gorilla leader could even use grappling techniques.","The sole of its foot appeared directly above my head.","If that stomp landed, I would die.","Booooom!","I narrowly avoided it by rolling aside.","Hurriedly steadying my breathing, I rose to my feet.","During the brief time it took me to stand, the gorilla leader approached.","It had no intention of giving me even a moment to recover.","One mistake and I would genuinely die.","I rapidly accelerated the mana flowing through my body.","If even one of its attacks struck me properly, it would undoubtedly inflict catastrophic damage.","Claaaang!","Another palm strike flew toward me.","I blocked it with my shield.","It was powerful, but not powerful enough to break through my shield.","If I could exploit an opening, this fight was manageable.","If my opponent had been an ordinary human, I could have created some distance, but...","’Its arms are so long that the difference in reach is meaningless.’","Since it was a gorilla, the length of its arms rendered distance management far less effective.","That meant I had to engage it in a battle of tactics on equal ground.","This was completely different from my previous fights.","Unlike the battles I had survived through improvisation, this was a contest of pure skill.","In other words, it might turn into the kind of prolonged battle of endurance I hated so much.","Booom!","Once again, the gorilla leader’s hand collided with my shield.","This time, it used a fist rather than its palm.","The impact transmitted through the shield made my shoulder tingle.","Its physical strength was on an entirely different level from the other gorillas.","Grimacing, I swung the sword in my right hand diagonally.","I didn’t forget to be careful so it couldn’t throw me over its shoulder again.","However, it evaded my attack with a simple backstep.","Its control of distance was exceptional too.","Who the hell had taught this creature martial arts?","Whoever it was, they had taught it something truly obnoxious.","’A weakness. I need to find a weakness.’","Its short legs?","Its much longer arms compensated for them.","Counterattack by exploiting its sluggish movements?","If it threw me again, I would die.","The difference between bare hands and a weapon?","That bastard’s entire body was a weapon.","No matter how hard I tried, I couldn’t find a weakness.","As I had said, this was a contest of pure skill.","’No. I do have an advantage.’","After thinking carefully, I realized I wasn’t entirely without an advantage.","That creature couldn’t defend against my attacks.","Its only option was to evade them.","The instant it tried to block, the Heavenly Demon’s sword would cut through it.","I decided to exploit that fact.","I would create a situation where it had no choice but to defend.","Then an opportunity would inevitably appear.","Swoosh!","I thrust into an opening, aiming for its shoulder.","However, the gorilla leader not only evaded effortlessly but also responded by lightly tapping the flat of my sword.","The tap diverted my blade to the side and slightly disrupted my balance.","In other words, it was now the gorilla leader’s turn.","Realizing that, it extended its palm toward me.","That was precisely what I had been waiting for.","I charged directly at the gorilla.","\"?!\"","The gorilla leader’s eyes widened, apparently not expecting me to charge.","But it was already too late to retract its outstretched arm.","Even if it somehow managed to pull it back, its posture would become awkward.","While the gorilla leader was caught off guard, I thrust my shield forward as though throwing a punch instead of swinging my sword.","My target was its face.","Startled, the gorilla leader hurriedly raised an arm to protect itself, but—","Cr-r-rack!","Its arm wasn’t enough to stop my mana-enhanced body or the shield surging with aura.","The unmistakable sound of breaking bones entered my ears.","The moment I heard it, I became certain of my victory.","Cr-runch!","\"Keugh?!\"","But perhaps that was the price of letting my guard down.","I felt something burst around my ribs.","It was accompanied by an ominous noise.","Not the sound of bones merely breaking, but of them being crushed into fragments.","At first, I felt nothing.","There was only a tingling sensation, as though lightning had passed through me.","Then, in an instant, excruciating pain struck and my vision went black.","I couldn’t breathe.","\"Kuh... kuh....\"","\"Kuaaaaah!\"","The gorilla leader and I both staggered backward.","We had each delivered a devastating blow to the other.","My ribs had been struck, while its arm had been destroyed.","When it came to continuing the fight, I still had the advantage.","The arm that had blocked my shield hung limply.","Its bones had been completely shattered.","’My ribs, though...’","Of course, I wasn’t unscathed either.","For one thing, I couldn’t breathe.","It was even worse than when I had been thrown over its shoulder.","As I remained unable to draw breath, my vision gradually began to fade.","\"Uuugh... Hah! Ugh!\"","Fortunately, I finally managed to suck in a breath.","Then an overwhelming wave of pain surged through me.","It hurt several times worse than when the orichalcum guardian had struck me.","It had only been one hit.","A single blow had inflicted enough damage to nearly incapacitate me.","I was fortunate it had struck my ribs. If it had hit another vital point, I would have died instantly.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Perhaps it had decided that it could no longer continue fighting.","Clutching its broken arm with its other hand, the gorilla leader turned and fled.","That was actually fortunate.","I wasn’t in any condition to continue fighting either.","’Elixir... I need to drink an elixir...!’","Clutching my ribs, I stumbled into the cave.","I couldn’t breathe properly.","I was worried that one of my broken ribs might have punctured a lung. Still, an elixir should heal it.","Once inside the cave, I hurriedly drank an elixir.","I emptied the entire bottle.","\"Hoo. Hoo. Hoo.\"","Cold sweat poured from my body as I struggled to steady my breathing.","Thanks to the elixir, I seemed to be doing a little better.","However, the excruciating pain remained, occasionally forcing me to grimace.","\"Haa....\"","Only after approximately five minutes did I finally manage to stabilize myself.","This situation was completely different from when the orichalcum guardian had struck me.","Injuring my ribs had made it difficult even to breathe.","\"Cough! Cough! Keugh!\"","As if that weren’t enough, blood sprayed from my mouth.","That had been dangerous.","I roughly wiped the blood from my hand and sank to the ground.","Things seemed to become more difficult with each passing day.","’Just what was that bastard...?’","A gorilla that used human martial arts.","I couldn’t understand it at all.","I wondered whether a survivor had taught it, but I wasn’t even sure that was possible.","The people on the gallery had said there had never been a case where someone taught martial arts or a breathing technique to a primate and achieved any remarkable results.","’Is the Forest of Four Seasons different?’","Perhaps it would be easier to simply accept that the gorilla had learned martial arts because it possessed enough intelligence to do so.","But I still wanted to know who had taught it.","A gorilla had learned martial arts.","Its teacher not only had to possess a high level of mastery but also needed exceptional teaching ability to pass martial arts on to a gorilla.","Most importantly, this was someone who had survived in the Forest of Four Seasons long enough to teach a gorilla martial arts.","Swoosh—","As my thoughts grew increasingly complicated, someone approached me.","It was Namu-Ppareumbo.","’What was that all about?’","I stared intently at him, then suddenly remembered what he had done.","He had decapitated the gorilla we had taken hostage and thrown its head at the others.","It had truly been the way of the wild.","It was also a side of Namu-Ppareumbo I had never seen before.","\"Hey.\"","\"....\"","\"Why did you spare me?\"","Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t answer.","However, he seemed to be saying:","Because you were so pathetic that there was no need to kill you.","’Hmm. That makes sense.’","I chuckled.","It was fortunate that I had been so weak back then.","If I had posed even the slightest threat to Namu-Ppareumbo, I probably wouldn’t be alive today.","\"Come to think of it, Ppareumbo, what are you going to eat?\"","\"....\"","Separate from everything else, I needed to consider his diet from now on.","Namu-Ppareumbo merely wore his usual relaxed expression.","Of course, it wasn’t difficult to interpret the meaning behind that expression.","\"There won’t be any fasting pills for a while. The Heavenly Demon said you’ll have to wait.\"","\"....\"","The corners of Ppareumbo’s mouth lowered slightly.","So even this guy could make an expression like that.","How fascinating.","***","The gorilla leader ran and continued running.","One of its arms had been completely destroyed, leaving it unable to climb trees.","All it could do was run.","Even so, it moved at an extraordinary speed. The surrounding scenery changed continuously with every stride it took.","Just like the technique it had used to close the distance with Grylls in an instant, even the way it ran differed from that of an ordinary animal.","Rustle!","Before long, the gorilla leader reached its main camp.","The other gorillas were going about their respective tasks.","One gorilla was gathering bananas hanging from a tree.","Another lay sprawled out, sleeping.","Others were splitting stones to make tools.","\"Awoooooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","The leader roared while clutching its limp, dangling arm.","At the sound of that roar, every gorilla stopped what it was doing.","An eerie silence instantly descended over the gorillas’ territory.","What had the leader told them?","Swoosh—","Then someone approached from behind the leader.","The leader turned around the moment it sensed the presence.","The newcomer was similar in size, but its posture was entirely different from that of the other gorillas.","Even the leader planted both hands on the ground when running.","This newly arrived gorilla, however, stood proudly upright on two legs.","More importantly, its appearance was markedly different.","The leader and the other gorillas all had their bodies exposed.","The newcomer, however, wore \"clothes\" like a human.","Although the clothing was worn, tattered, and practically reduced to rags...","It was still clothing.","It wore black garments that Grylls would have described as Eastern in style.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","The moment the leader saw that gorilla, it began explaining everything that had happened.","It even pointed at its broken, dangling arm.","The newly arrived gorilla silently listened to the leader’s account.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"....\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","The more it heard, the more serious its expression became.","Perhaps it was older than the other gorillas. Its face was lined with wrinkles and bore the unmistakable signs of age and experience.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"....\"","It also had a five-pronged scar slashed across one eye."]},{"title":"Chapter 109","paragraphs":["Welcome To (1)","I had been through a lot of hardships while living in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Whenever that happened, I would rest in my own way—collapsing from exhaustion and spending the entire day holed up in the cave, or occasionally practicing my breathing technique.","However, I rarely smoked.","I had decided only to smoke when both my body and mind were utterly exhausted.","And that perfectly described my current condition.","Sizzle!","I lit the tip of a cigar with a fire-starting stone.","Once smoke began curling from its tip, I placed it between my lips and took a long, refreshing drag.","The cool fragrance—without the slightest trace of harshness—filled my lungs and invigorated me.","\"Phew.\"","With the World Tree tobacco still between my lips, I exhaled. The smoke rose in wisps before gradually dispersing.","Smoking seemed to clear my head, at least a little.","Though my thoughts were still complicated.","I wanted to keep my distance from tobacco whenever possible, but that was difficult right now.","’I have to dispose of the gorilla corpses, and they might come back for revenge... Haah...’","Thanks to the elixir, my broken ribs had mostly healed.","My stamina hadn’t been depleted too severely either, so I still felt relatively energetic. My head, however, was a mess.","I had started smoking because I wanted to untangle those complicated thoughts somehow.","After all, there was simply far too much to consider regarding the gorillas.","’Who the hell taught them martial arts?’","I could overlook the gorillas using tools. Allfather had warned me about that in advance.","Besides, their obsession with using tools had actually made them easier to deal with in some respects.","But the gorilla that had used martial arts was a different matter. It had been an extremely difficult opponent.","The combination of a gorilla’s naturally powerful body and fluid techniques had made every one of its attacks dangerous.","If I hadn’t trained my reaction speed with Namu-Ppareumbo, my skull would have been smashed open.","’Considering the circumstances, the person who left that palm print on the tree must have taught them.’","With the cigar still between my lips, I organized my thoughts.","If I wanted to uncover the truth more precisely, I would need to enter their territory.","Even if I captured the leader gorilla, it wasn’t as though it could speak.","They might be incapable of speech, but they were remarkably intelligent creatures.","The fact that they had gone beyond using tools and learned martial arts was proof enough.","’Just how intelligent do they have to be to use martial arts?’","When it came to martial arts, the person being taught was just as important as the person doing the teaching.","There was a reason the word talent existed. Without talent, a person would simply remain stuck in place.","Perhaps that gorilla possessed more talent for martial arts than I did.","The thought suddenly occurred to me.","’...This forest is seriously insane.’","I couldn’t help but chuckle bitterly.","I took another deep drag of the cigar and exhaled the smoke.","For now, it seemed best to put the gorillas out of my mind and deal with the work in front of me.","\"Wonmo is... asleep.\"","Wonmo had been injured for the first time in his life. After receiving treatment, he was now sleeping soundly on the mat.","He normally slept sprawled out with all four limbs extended, but now he had curled himself into a ball.","Since intruders had entered his territory, he was probably remaining alert so that he could spring into action at any moment.","’Even our home isn’t safe anymore.’","There was no telling when the gorillas might return.","They had even raided our fasting pills. This wasn’t something I could take lightly.","Nor could I leave someone behind to guard this place. Even Namu-Ppareumbo would be in danger.","’In the end, I definitely need to install a door.’","And it would have to be an extremely sturdy one.","A door that even the gorillas couldn’t easily break down.","For that, it would have to be made of steel.","I had no choice but to ask the dwarf to make it. I would assemble it myself afterward.","’Wouldn’t a few lumps of orichalcon be enough?’","I took one final, refreshing drag before opening the wooden box.","Then I tapped the ash into the ashtray and cut off the burnt tip with my dagger.","I could still smoke it several more times. I didn’t have much tobacco left, so I needed to conserve it.","’It really is delicious, though.’","If I started running low later, I would have to ask Let’s Grow Trees for more.","I didn’t know what that person wanted in return, but I could at least hear them out.","I gathered a shovel and various other tools before heading outside.","The moment I stepped out, I was greeted by the sight of the dead gorilla troop.","The most gruesome of them all was the gorilla whose head had been severed—the one Namu-Ppareumbo had killed.","’First, I should take a few pictures to upload to the Gallery.’","I had a mountain of questions to ask, so documenting the scene was essential.","After photographing the tools the gorillas had used, I began cleaning everything up.","Considering the gorillas’ massive size, even disposing of them was inevitably difficult.","’Should I just bury them?’","The easiest method was to dig a hole, throw them inside, and bury them.","There was no need to carry every corpse all the way to the river and dump them there.","If I was attacked while heading toward the river, I would be in serious trouble.","In particular, the leader gorilla that had escaped might return with another troop to take revenge.","’Cutting them... into pieces would feel a little wrong.’","They were primates rather than ordinary beasts like the saber-toothed tiger, so I felt uncomfortable dismembering them.","Besides, some of the corpses were already badly mutilated.","It would be better to simply dig a pit.","I started by gathering all the corpses in one place. Incidentally, I had a hard time finding the severed head belonging to the decapitated corpse.","’I should dig the pit far away from here.’","I wasn’t insane enough to bury them inside my shelter.","I would bury them somewhere reasonably far away.","There was also a chance that other animals might come and dig them up, so I intended to bury them as deeply as possible.","’This should be good enough.’","It was behind the cave, in a reasonably spacious clearing.","The place could easily have been called my backyard, and I dug a deep pit there.","Moving each gorilla individually was tedious, but there was no avoiding it.","It was only after roughly an hour had passed that I finally managed to bury all the gorilla corpses.","If my strength and other physical abilities hadn’t improved, it would have taken me at least two hours.","Title: Gorilla Troop Eliminated","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a dead gorilla)","(Photo of a gorilla lying on the ground)","(Photo of a gorilla lying dead in a spray of blood)","(Photo of a gorilla cleverly positioned so its severed neck isn’t visible)","(Photo of the tools used by the gorillas)","(Photo of the gorilla corpses gathered together)","I wiped out all the gorillas that came to rescue the hostage I captured.","There was a leader gorilla, but it escaped.","Also, the leader gorilla used something resembling martial arts. Is that even possible? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: A gorilla used martial arts? What kind of martial art did it display?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s difficult to explain in detail, but I’ll start with its stance. It extended its left hand forward with the palm facing outward, while its right hand was clenched into a fist and held beside its waist.","└ Heavenly Demon: That alone is insufficient. Could you describe the martial art it demonstrated in a little more detail?","└ Wild Grylls: It used palm strikes frequently. They were incredibly fast too.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. There are far too many martial arts that employ palm strikes. We need a more distinctive feature...","└ SwordMaster: Before that, aren’t you surprised that a gorilla used martial arts? Something completely absurd just happened, you know? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: That is true. This lady has seen countless fools inferior to monkeys, but never imagined that an actual ape could practice martial arts.","└ SwordMaster: You do know the difference between apes and monkeys, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: Is it not simply the presence or absence of a tail? They are all the same monkeys to this lady.","└ SwordMaster: Fair enough. Anyway, were you injured anywhere?","└ Wild Grylls: I was struck in the ribs and nearly died, but fortunately, I survived. The leader gorilla broke its arm too.","└ Heavenly Demon: What a remarkable occurrence. However, it could not have cultivated martial arts on its own. This lady suspects that someone taught it.","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of the center of the tree bearing both a gorilla’s palm print and a human palm print) Looking at this, I’m certain someone taught it.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is a reasonable inference.","└ Allfather: There may still be another survivor alive. If someone taught martial arts to an entire gorilla troop, they must have defeated them in battle first.","└ Praise the Sun: I’m more surprised that they used tools. Aren’t they genuinely evolving into humans?","└ Allfather: That is a highly plausible hypothesis. Either they possess abnormally high intelligence, or the Forest of Four Seasons is accelerating their evolution.","└ That sounds terrifying just hearing about it. Shudder ;;","└ So that’s why the place is overflowing with miraculous herbs. Surviving there is just as difficult.","└ Grylls got lucky.","└ Forget all that. Doesn’t this mean Grylls is weaker than a gorilla?","└ Wild Grylls: Shut up. I didn’t lose.","└ If you lose, you’re officially worse than a gorilla. Lmao.","└ Lmao. A bastard inferior to an ape.","└ Wild Grylls: Don’t worry. I’m already a bastard inferior to a sloth.","└ Oh, right. Lmaoooo.","└ I forgot about that. Lmao.","Once I uploaded the post to the Gallery, everyone began chattering in their own way.","It was surprising enough that the gorilla had displayed martial arts, yet they had even used tools.","Why had humans risen to the top of the food chain?","It was precisely because they made extensive use of tools.","Fortunately, the gorillas had only used clubs. I would have struggled if they had wielded spears.","’And the person behind them...’","The \"master\" who had taught martial arts to the gorillas undoubtedly existed.","The question was whether that master was still alive.","The gorillas now recognized me as an enemy.","If they had a human master, that person should have shown at least some curiosity about me.","’Besides...’","I turned my head and looked at Namu-Ppareumbo.","Perhaps it was because his fasting pills had been stolen despite teaching the gorillas a proper lesson, but he seemed unusually dispirited today.","However, I couldn’t immediately produce fasting pills that I didn’t have.","There was also something I wanted to know.","Just what kind of creature was Namu-Ppareumbo for the gorilla troop to fear him?","That fear had allowed us to undermine the gorillas’ morale. That had been the greatest advantage of all.","\"Ppareumbo.\"","\"...\"","\"Just how strong are you for the gorillas to be so afraid of you?\"","I had become curious about Namu-Ppareumbo’s past.","Namu-Ppareumbo was strong—far stronger than I could imagine.","He had treated someone like me as insignificant, and even among the gorillas, he reigned as an object of terror.","What in the world had this creature done before I arrived?","I found myself more curious about it than usual today.","\"...\"","Instead of answering, Namu-Ppareumbo stared intently at me.","His expression seemed to ask whether I truly wanted to know.","I stared back at him for a moment before nodding.","Although it hadn’t even been a month, I could understand Namu-Ppareumbo’s intentions to some extent.","Scritch—scritch—","He began drawing on the ground.","I focused on the picture.","True to the nature of a sloth, he moved painfully slowly, but I waited patiently.","’No. Wait a minute. He’s drawing?’","I glanced at Namu-Ppareumbo.","He only looked like a sloth on the outside. I was beginning to suspect that there might be a human inside him.","Of course, like the evolved gorillas, perhaps he had simply evolved in a different direction.","Nothing that happened in the Forest of Four Seasons could be considered strange.","So I decided to let it go.","Thinking too deeply about every little thing would only give me a headache.","Scritch—scritch—","After ten minutes, the drawing gradually began to take shape.","The first thing Namu-Ppareumbo drew was himself.","Short legs compared to his long arms. Claws at the ends of his hands. Finally, even his perpetually peaceful expression.","Anyone could tell that it was Namu-Ppareumbo.","However, there wasn’t just one.","There were two, then three, then four, eventually reaching ten.","It looked like a picture of Namu-Ppareumbo’s \"family.\"","He pointed with one claw at the smallest Namu-Ppareumbo—or rather, the smallest sloth—among them.","Apparently, that one represented him.","I nodded to show that I understood.","’But there weren’t any other members of his family...’","Just as that thought crossed my mind—","Scrape—","He dragged his claw across one of the sloths in the group.","Anyone could tell that it meant the sloth had died.","Scrape—scrrrape—","One by one, Namu-Ppareumbo crossed out every member of the group except himself.","He didn’t stop until he had scratched out even the sloth standing directly beside him.","Based on this, I could form several hypotheses.","First, Namu-Ppareumbo had once belonged to a group of his own.","Second, that group had been massacred for some reason, leaving him as the sole survivor.","And lastly, the reason they had been massacred was...","\"Was it because of the gorillas?\"","Namu-Ppareumbo gave no answer.","He merely stared at the ground.","But that alone was answer enough.","Namu-Ppareumbo’s group had been defeated by the gorilla troop.","Only Namu-Ppareumbo, the sole survivor, had lived.","’They wiped out the entire group of someone this strong?’","It seemed that the gorilla troop was far stronger than I had imagined.","Either that, or—","’The person who taught them martial arts fought on their behalf.’","Neither possibility was particularly encouraging."]},{"title":"Chapter 110","paragraphs":["Welcome To (2)","The annihilation of an entire group, like what Namu-Ppareumbo had experienced, was a story that could be found not only in the wild but also throughout human civilization.","Foreigners would drive out the indigenous people who had originally occupied the land and claim it for themselves.","History contained many examples of indigenous people resisting to the bitter end, only to be forced to their knees by the foreigners’ overwhelming military power.","’So he really became stronger to survive too.’","After learning about Ppareumbo’s past, I began to see him differently.","He hadn’t been abnormally strong from the beginning. Like me, he had grown stronger in order to survive.","During that process, he must have repeatedly clashed with the gorilla troop that had seized his territory.","’...’","There was a high probability that he had single-handedly caused far more than mere chaos.","He certainly possessed enough strength to do so.","In any case, Namu-Ppareumbo was currently living with me. I couldn’t have asked for a more dependable companion.","Of course, that didn’t mean I could neglect defensive preparations.","An entire horde of gorillas might descend upon us as early as tomorrow.","’Should I move?’","The option of relocating occurred to me, but I quickly discarded it.","That was a last resort.","I would have to abandon the barricade and all the other tools I had prepared.","More importantly, with the river nearby, this base was something I absolutely needed to defend.","’I’m definitely holding this place.’","In that case, how could I defend it easily?","The best method would be to lure them toward the narrow cave entrance.","The gorillas were huge.","Even if they forced their way inside, no more than two could enter at once. That would make it easy to defeat them individually.","’But will they obediently fall for it?’","They were highly intelligent and even knew how to employ tactics.","I didn’t know whether they would behave exactly as I wanted.","Still, doing something was better than doing nothing, so I slowly began designing my defenses.","’If I want to take advantage of a confined space like I did when I killed the owlbear...’","Ultimately, I needed a door—and one sturdier than any wooden door.","The dwarf had once asked why I would bother installing a door when it would only be destroyed.","In that case, why not install a door sturdy enough that it couldn’t be destroyed?","It was an extremely simple solution.","Someone might suggest buying a safe instead, but if I was going to do that, I might as well place the entire safe in front of the entrance.","A small safe was out of the question because the gorillas might simply carry it away.","’There should be something like a CCTV camera, right?’","I would ask the dwarf to make the door and ask Cheonggu Princess about the CCTV.","Cheonggu Princess would probably give me one willingly, but I couldn’t be certain. Someone else might also have one.","Once I had roughly organized my ideas, I immediately uploaded a post to the Gallery.","***","Title: Does Anyone Here Have Something That Can Record Video? Besides the Gallery.","Wild Grylls","I’m thinking about installing a security system after the gorillas robbed my house.","Does anyone have an item that can record video while I’m away? I heard there are broadcast orbs. Can’t something be done with one of those?","I’m also planning to install a door, and I intend to make it extremely sturdy. Anyone have some advice?","└ Heavenly Demon: Would the gorillas not simply destroy the door?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll install a door sturdy enough that they can’t break it.","└ Heavenly Demon: A simple answer, but a reasonably good one.","└ SwordMaster: Why don’t you buy a safe instead? A door would probably break from a single body slam by an animal like an owlbear.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m considering a separate container. Besides, the gorillas might carry away the entire safe.","└ SwordMaster: Are those gorillas really that intelligent?","└ Wild Grylls: I think it would be easier to treat them as slightly dim-witted humans.","└ Passing Dwarf: An item like the one you described does exist. But it’s insanely expensive, so you’ll have trouble buying it.","└ Wild Grylls: How does one kilogram of orichalcon sound?","└ Passing Dwarf: This bastard was filthy rich.","└ Wild Grylls: Heh.","└ A man with an orichalcon vein in the cave outside his house. ;;","└ What if he finds adamantium later?","└ It’s not impossible. But isn’t adamantium found deep underground?","└ Who knows? Maybe Grylls will go mining later.","└ Wild Grylls: Why the hell would I go mining, you bastards?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I have the item you’re talking about, Mr. Grylls. Would you like one?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll trade with you tomorrow after visiting the orichalcon cave. Is it operated similarly to a crystal orb?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I don’t know which crystal orb you mean, but it should be similar. I can also use orichalcon to prevent it from overheating, so I’ll modify it for you.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you!","└ Cheonggu Princess: If you’re grateful, what should you do?","└ Wild Grylls: Chae-U is invincible, and Kone is a god.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Kyaa! Look at that wit! Absolutely splendid!","└ He’s seriously going to wear himself out doing this. Lmao.","└ At this point, isn’t he genuinely becoming a Cheonggu fan? Lmao.","└ Seems like he’s already been completely Cheonggu-fied. O_O","***","I used the collective intelligence of the Gallery to discuss how I should renovate my shelter.","The first task was to narrow the cave entrance.","I planned to use bricks for this, just as I had when constructing the oven.","’And the dwarf agreed to make the iron door.’","Incidentally, it would be an iron door made with orichalcon mixed into it.","The dwarf said he would modify it so that, just as orichalcon absorbed mana, it could also absorb physical impacts.","Of course, he explained that its impact-absorption rate would be far lower than that of a mineral called adamantium.","’Do I seriously have to go mining for it?’","Mining—the unavoidable chore in that blocky game.","Just thinking that I might have to do it made me dizzy.","However, the Forest of Four Seasons was a place where I had no choice but to do whatever became necessary.","I wrote my plans in my notebook and looked around.","’Fortunately, they only stole the fasting pills. If they’d stolen the elixirs...’","I needed to hide the important items in an obscure corner where they would be difficult to find.","As I continued making plans to renovate the shelter one feature at a time, evening eventually arrived.","I headed up to the river to collect the fish caught in the traps and cooked food in the oven.","I began preparing to bring today’s particularly grueling routine to an end.","Oh, and I fed Namu-Ppareumbo with the fasting pills that remained.","I had brought them as emergency rations, so there was enough to last until tomorrow morning.","’I wonder if the gorillas will come tomorrow.’","Even if they did, I had no intention of going down without a fight.","As I circulated my breathing technique, I recalled the leader gorilla I had fought earlier that day.","Normally, no distracting thoughts should enter one’s mind while practicing an internal energy cultivation technique.","Strangely, however, I felt as though I could concentrate even better this way.","My breathing continued unconsciously while the battle against the leader gorilla replayed inside my head.","’I couldn’t even see the attack that struck my ribs.’","It had been the price of letting my guard down, but I genuinely hadn’t seen the leader gorilla’s final attack.","It had come from outside my field of vision.","I needed to keep that in mind.","It would be nice if I could glimpse the future like in a certain pirate manga, but something like that was probably still beyond me.","I continued visualizing the battle little by little before eventually focusing solely on the breathing technique.","\"Phew...\"","I finished circulating the technique and slowly opened my eyes.","Tomorrow would mark exactly two weeks since I had fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","It felt as though well over a month had passed, yet it had only been two weeks.","That probably meant I had been living every day in a frenzy.","It was also because I had considered every minute and second precious and tried to use my time as efficiently as possible.","’Still, it’s surprisingly manageable.’","The owlbear, the saber-toothed tiger, the orichalcon guardian, and finally, the leader gorilla.","Every one of them had been difficult to face, but I had somehow endured.","Of course, I couldn’t deny that Namu-Ppareumbo’s assistance had played the largest role.","Still, what mattered was that I had survived.","I would continue surviving, no matter what.","\"No matter what.\"","I would escape this hell.","***","The next day arrived.","As soon as dawn broke, I began my daily routine.","My shelter had been raided yesterday, but that didn’t mean I could postpone the things I needed to do.","Moreover, I planned to renovate the shelter today, so I needed to move quickly.","\"Ppareumbo, this is the last one.\"","\"...\"","\"I’ll find more somehow, so survive on grass for the time being.\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo’s final fasting pill.","He stared at it with a sorrowful expression before placing it in his mouth.","He looked rather pitiful, but I had mixed feelings when I remembered that I was the one paying tribute to him.","Still, every tribute I gave this creature increased my chances of survival, so it was well worth it.","’The Heavenly Demon said it would take time to make more fasting pills.’","I had heard that fasting pills were made using expensive medicinal herbs.","She said they would take at least a week to prepare. I wasn’t sure whether Namu-Ppareumbo could hold out until then.","If necessary, I would have no choice but to explore and gather medicinal herbs myself.","Since there was an entire colony of mature Mandrakes, a field of medicinal herbs likely existed somewhere too.","’Let’s see... Should I narrow the cave entrance this much?’","I began working on narrowing the entrance.","The owlbear had widened it when it forcibly squeezed inside.","Narrow terrain provided a natural advantage for me.","’Exploring will probably be difficult today. I should only visit the orichalcon cave.’","There was no telling when the gorillas might attack again.","Of course, now that we had clearly demonstrated that this was our territory, there was also a chance they wouldn’t return.","More importantly, Namu-Ppareumbo was here.","Unless they came as an entire horde...","Rustle—rustle—","I was examining the cave entrance when a rustling sound reached my ears.","Wondering if it could possibly be what I feared, I turned my head.","The rustling gradually grew louder.","\"...\"","Without saying a word, I armed myself as the sound drew closer.","Namu-Ppareumbo seemed to sense something as well and climbed onto my back. Wonmo also approached my side.","Eventually, the rustling became considerably louder.","\"...Huff.\"","A gorilla emerged.","It was every bit as massive as the leader gorilla, but everything about it—from its posture to its appearance—was different.","The gorillas flanking it supported themselves with both arms against the ground, while the one leading them stood upright on two legs.","More importantly...","\"Clothes?\"","It was wearing clothes.","They were old and tattered, practically no different from rags, but they were unmistakably clothes.","They were yellowed with grime, and the dye had faded until the fabric was nearly white, though traces of black could still be seen here and there.","Then there was its appearance.","Five distinct claw marks ran across its left eye.","Compared to its healthy eye, the injured one had turned cloudy white, making it easy to guess that it was blind.","It wasn’t merely unusual. There was something extraordinary about it.","That was my impression of the newly arrived gorilla.","’Did it inherit those clothes from a human?’","That was certainly how it appeared.","Judging by how old and tattered the clothes were, they looked as though they had been worn for at least ten years.","Normally, that would mean they were a deceased person’s belongings...","But did a gorilla even understand such a concept?","’And they’re carrying spears too? What the hell are they?’","As if that weren’t enough, the gorillas flanking their leader were carrying spears rather than clubs.","They were crudely crafted wooden spears, but they were still spears.","Their evolution was approaching the level of humans.","I assumed a defensive stance as I watched them.","Squeeze!","A powerful pressure gripped my shoulder.","Ppareumbo had seized it with one hand.","I turned my head and looked at Namu-Ppareumbo.","He was frowning slightly.","Since he normally maintained an expressionless face, such a clear display of emotion was highly unusual.","’Could those scars around its eye be...?’","The pieces of the puzzle were gradually clicking into place.","The gorilla I presumed to be the leader glanced to one side and jerked its head.","One of the spear-wielding gorillas then headed somewhere.","It soon returned carrying something and handed it to the leader.","Whoosh!","The leader threw the object toward me.","It didn’t feel like a declaration of war. It seemed more like it was simply giving the object to me.","Thud!","The object landed on the ground shortly afterward.","I stared at it.","It was a long, yellow fruit.","Not just one, but an entire bunch.","\"...Bananas?\"","The gorilla leader had thrown me a bunch of bananas.","At first, I had no idea what it meant.","But considering what had happened yesterday, I interpreted it this way:","I apologize for what happened yesterday. In exchange, I offer you these bananas.","In other words, it was a peace offering.","I stared blankly at the gorilla leader.","And then...","\"Ddui-bbu-chi.\"","The gorilla spoke a human \"language.\"","I couldn’t even begin to understand what it had said, but it had undoubtedly spoken.","A gorilla capable only of bestial cries couldn’t produce \"words\" like that.","’...Fuck. This really is Planet of the Apes .’","A rough voice shouting \"NO!\" echoed inside my head."]},{"title":"Chapter 111","paragraphs":["Welcome To (3)","Language.","The alpha and omega of civilization.","If human standards were applied directly to animals, one could argue that animals possessed no language.","But what if communication itself was considered a language?","Could one truly say that animals had none?","Their linguistic systems were simply less complex and less segmented than those of humans.","However, the greatest difference between humans and animals was intelligence, and that gap was clearly reflected in their use of language.","That difference gave rise to many things.","Even when humans encountered a foreign language, they could understand it to some extent as long as they made an effort to learn it.","Animals could not.","Language wasn’t something that merely needed to be memorized. Its true value could only be realized through complete comprehension.","In that sense, one could say that animals had failed to grasp the ultimate essence of language.","And right now, all that common sense came crashing down through the mouth of the gorilla chief.","Was this what it felt like to have the entire universe unfold inside one’s head?","Human words had emerged from the chief’s mouth—a language completely removed from an animal’s cries.","Could the person who had taught the gorillas martial arts have taught them language as well?","However, separate from the act of teaching them language, the important point was that they had acquired human methods of communication.","The chief had given me bananas as an apology and even bowed politely.","It undoubtedly possessed intelligence comparable to that of a human.","’Now that I look closely, it has a lot of wrinkles too.’","Its face was far more wrinkled than those of the other gorillas, giving it an air of considerable age and experience.","Then who in the world was the person who had taught it language?","After thinking for a moment, I decided to pick up the bananas first.","Judging by its polite manner and the overall atmosphere, it had clearly offered them as an apology.","Even if it launched a surprise attack, I had Namu-Ppareumbo with me, so I wasn’t worried.","\"Ni chou narira?\"","\"...What the hell are you saying?\"","When I picked up the bananas, the gorilla chief spoke again.","However, I didn’t know any of this world’s languages, so I couldn’t understand it.","’Judging by the intonation, it sounds somewhat similar to Chinese...’","This world had a place called the Central Plains, a nation resembling those found in martial arts stories.","If it was anything like the martial worlds I knew, it wouldn’t be strange for its people to speak a language resembling Chinese.","That didn’t change the fact that I had no idea what the words meant.","This was precisely when I needed the Gallery.","I opened the Gallery and began recording a video. I planned to upload it.","\"Could you... say that again?\"","I made a circular gesture with my hand to indicate that I wanted it to repeat itself.","I had unconsciously spoken politely, but I didn’t bother worrying about that.","Fortunately, it seemed to understand my gesture.","The chief stared at me before repeating the same words.","\"Ni chou narira?\"","\"Just a moment, please.\"","I immediately uploaded the recorded video to the Gallery.","I desperately hoped it was the language of the Central Plains.","If so, the Heavenly Demon could translate it immediately.","***","Title: Emergeeeency!!! The Gorilla Can Speak!!!","Wild Grylls","(Video of the gorilla chief speaking a human language)","I’m starting to get really scared. Does anyone know what it’s saying?","Gorillas in the Forest of Four Seasons can speak human languages. Can anyone translate this?","└ Heavenly Demon: ??? Why is a gorilla speaking the language of the Central Plains? Is this truly happening?","└ Wild Grylls: I’d broadcast it live if I could, but that isn’t possible right now. This is really happening.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm... I do not know where that gorilla learned it, but it is indeed speaking the language of the Central Plains. It is even using an archaic form of the language.","└ Wild Grylls: An archaic form?","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady means that it speaks as the elders do.","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t you an old fossil yourself?","└ Heavenly Demon: Did this lady not say that she only recently entered the prime of her youth?","└ SwordMaster: How can you say that while talking like some ancient relic? ;;","└ Allfather: Oh. My. God. By Aragorn, what am I looking at?","└ Wild Grylls: A video of a gorilla speaking a human language.","└ Allfather: Oh. Fuck. This must be an omen of the world’s destruction.","└ Wild Grylls: Are you okay? ;;","└ Allfather: I shall go relieve my urges for a moment.","└ Wild Grylls: Dude... ;;","└ Wait, can that gorilla seriously speak?","└ Monsters capable of human speech appear occasionally. Orc shamans and goblin sorcerers, for example.","└ Sure, but have you ever seen a gorilla speaking a human language?","└ Of course not. Lmao. What the hell is that? Lmao.","└ It even seems to have learned the language of the Central Plains. Lmao.","└ Who the hell taught it?","└ Judging by the way it speaks, that dialect is ancient as hell. It sounds like something people would’ve used during the Righteous-Blood War.","└ When did the Righteous-Blood War happen?","└ About sixty years ago, I think.","└ Why is it wearing clothes too? Lmao.","└ Looks like it’s wearing a dead person’s clothes.","└ Gorilla fashion. Lmao.","***","Countless comments appeared in less than a minute.","Most people said it was unbelievable or accused me of using ventriloquism.","They offered all sorts of wild theories, but this was the reality in front of me.","’Anyway, it asked where I came from, right?’","It was time to answer.","If I kept it waiting, I might ruin its first impression of me.","However, I didn’t know a single word that it could understand.","[Heavenly Demon: Do you wish for this lady to teach you what to say?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? How did you know?]","[Heavenly Demon: Considering the situation, that much is easy to deduce. However, although the Gallery can convey written words, it cannot transmit spoken language. Unless this lady knew your native tongue, it would likely be difficult.]","[Wild Grylls: Then could you show me how to write \"Republic of Korea\" in the language of the Central Plains?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is easily done. Wait a moment.]","While the Heavenly Demon wrote down the words, I attempted to converse with the gorilla chief.","Of course, the chief merely reacted as though it had no idea what I was saying, so I accomplished nothing.","It had only been an attempt to buy time, so I waited patiently.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon. Heavenly Demon. Could you help me?]","[Heavenly Demon: (Photo of \"Republic of Korea\" written in the language of the Central Plains on a sheet of paper) Will this suffice?]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you!]","[Heavenly Demon: Ask whenever you require assistance. From what this lady can see, you will continue to need her.]","I copied the characters from the Heavenly Demon’s photograph onto the ground.","I would have preferred to write them in the notebook inside the cave, but I didn’t know what might happen while I went to retrieve it.","When I began writing on the ground, the gorilla chief shifted its gaze toward the characters.","It tilted its head before looking back up at me and speaking.","\"Buchidao.\"","I recorded it and immediately sent the video to the Heavenly Demon.","According to her, it had answered, \"I don’t know.\"","Naturally, it couldn’t have known.","The Republic of Korea was a country from another world.","\"Yao. Shabi?\"","\"Bu.\"","\"Kai. Zama. Jubeo?\"","\"Junja tungpeo.\"","The chief then began conversing with one of the spear-wielding gorillas beside it.","Judging by their behavior, the spear-wielders seemed to be something like its personal guards.","Unlike the gorilla chief, who spoke fluently, the guards spoke in short, broken phrases.","I recorded their conversation and sent it to the Heavenly Demon.","[Heavenly Demon: That ape is asking whether they may kill you. It says you are the enemy who slew its kin.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Heavenly Demon: The chief says there is no need. Finding the bodies of their kin takes priority.]","The bodies of their kin.","They seemed to be referring to the gorillas I had killed yesterday.","Still, perhaps an ape remained an ape even after learning a language, because they openly discussed killing me while I stood right in front of them.","Or perhaps they had deliberately spoken where I could hear them.","I waited for their response.","\"Ssŭchi dorenma?\"","According to the Heavenly Demon, it was asking where its dead kin were.","Since they were the bastards who had stolen my food, I didn’t want to tell them so readily.","Moreover, if I conceded too easily, they might look down on me. I needed to proceed cautiously.","Scritch—scritch—","I wrote some characters on the ground.","They roughly meant:","What if I don’t want to tell you?","The chief carefully examined what I had written before responding.","\"Hwiurulseda.\"","According to the translation, it meant:","There will be blood.","I could tell from its half-threatening tone even before receiving the translation.","’It can even use figurative expressions?’","The figurative expression was surprising enough, but the fact that it could convey nuance through its tone was even more astonishing.","Just how intelligent was this creature?","I narrowed my eyes and stared back at the chief’s ferocious gaze before glancing at the gorillas beside it.","’Assuming the chief is as strong as Namu-Ppareumbo...’","There were approximately five other gorillas, including the guards.","We were at a numerical disadvantage.","If we fought, we would inevitably lose.","It was best to avoid battles with such poor odds whenever possible.","In particular, the fact that the chief had offered me bananas meant that it was willing to resolve the situation peacefully.","’Let’s avoid fighting.’","I imposed a condition.","I would show them where their kin were buried, but they had to leave immediately afterward.","When I wrote the condition on the ground, the chief nodded.","I didn’t know whether it would honor its promise, but reaching an agreement was still the best choice available.","\"They’re here.\"","When I showed them where the gorillas had been buried, the chief jerked its head.","One of the gorillas—an ordinary soldier rather than a personal guard—stepped forward and began digging.","It dug with its bare hands.","However, given a gorilla’s physical capabilities, it excavated the ground as rapidly as a mechanical digger.","Before long, it began pulling out the buried corpses one by one.","Since I had only buried them yesterday, they were still intact, without any signs of decomposition.","’Will this satisfy them?’","I watched the gorillas carry away the bodies before glancing at the chief.","It remained standing in place, silently observing until the other gorillas disappeared into the forest.","Once every one of its subordinates had vanished, the chief addressed me.","\"Shincha.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Shishin pangeol laotera.\"","As expected, I had no idea what it was saying.","However, I always kept the Gallery open.","I sent the recording to the Heavenly Demon.","[Heavenly Demon: It says that it is time to discuss a personal matter.]","[Wild Grylls: A personal matter?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is not a particularly good sign. In the murim, when someone distinguishes between public and personal affairs, a fight usually follows.]","Was I going to have to fight this creature?","I slowly retreated.","The chief saw my reaction and spoke impassively.","\"Chinpalli lyushi eomeon kwoeo.\"","\"...\"","\"Sunzŭ shi billa. Ni shie jeungpandeo.\"","Invading your territory was our fault.","My grandson was discourteous. Your actions were justified.","\"Keoshi baenzhu join shien shin. Haio sso kong.\"","However, this Sovereign is the leader of the troop—and the boy’s grandfather.","The moment I heard the translation this Sovereign , I couldn’t help but stare dumbfounded.","The Heavenly Demon seemed equally astonished, immediately revealing her feelings after translating it.","[Heavenly Demon: How arrogant. A mere ape dares to call itself \"this Sovereign.\" Who in the world taught it that?]","[Wild Grylls: Maybe the person who taught it used that expression?]","[Heavenly Demon: Whoever it was taught the creature improperly. None but the greatest under heaven may refer to themselves by that title.]","More importantly, the chief’s aura was becoming increasingly ominous.","Even its personal guards gradually retreated, creating the unmistakable atmosphere of an imminent fight.","I slowly circulated the mana within my body and infused the Heavenly Demon’s sword with aura.","Unless I took it by surprise, defeating the chief seemed impossible.","\"Ssuai.\"","Therefore...","\"Na joi ikeubeo.\"","I shall take one of your arms.","The instant the Heavenly Demon finished translating, I charged.","Aura shimmered around the Heavenly Demon’s sword like a heat haze.","No—it had far surpassed the level of an ordinary heat haze.","Flames.","The sword’s aura surged like raging flames.","If I struck the gorilla chief with it, its body would be cleaved in two.","Don’t call me a coward.","This was the best I could do.","What wouldn’t I do to survive?","This was a place where the one who survived was the strong one.","’Good. I caught it completely off guard!’","The chief didn’t react even when the sword entered striking distance.","Perhaps it had failed to respond in time.","This was my chance.","If I continued forward and cleaved through its torso—","That never happened.","Instead, an unbelievable sight unfolded before my eyes.","Aura blazed like fire around the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","It was a strike capable of effortlessly slicing through an animal’s flesh and bones with the slightest contact.","Yet the gorilla chief casually caught it.","Not with one hand.","With only three fingers—its thumb, index finger, and middle finger.","As I stared in disbelief, the chief spoke with a serene expression.","\"Hao chil reo.\"","I didn’t know what it meant.","Even so, I was now certain of one thing.","The gorilla chief was far stronger than I had ever imagined."]},{"title":"Chapter 112","paragraphs":["Welcome To (4)","If I had to choose the most difficult opponent among all the creatures I had fought to the death, it would undoubtedly be the saber-toothed tiger.","A tiger’s natural ferocity. Its terrifying size. Its absurd regenerative ability.","Without Namu-Ppareumbo’s timely assistance, I would have died several times over.","That ordeal had allowed me to achieve tremendous growth. Without the saber-toothed tiger, I probably couldn’t have defeated the guardian either.","I had encountered all sorts of bizarre creatures since then, but I had never been defeated.","Whenever a beast that seemed likely to beat me appeared, I fled immediately rather than fighting it.","Fwoosh!","Aura surged around the Heavenly Demon’s sword like blazing flames.","I stared blankly at the gorilla chief holding the sword between its fingers.","Even though I had swung with all my strength, it had caught the blade effortlessly.","I might have understood if it had caught it with its entire hand.","But it had used only its fingers.","The fundamental strength I had gained from eating the eel and the additional strength I had acquired through cultivating internal energy—","Even with all of that combined, I had been stopped by three fingers.","\"Urgh...!\"","I couldn’t even pull the sword free.","No matter how much strength I exerted, it wouldn’t budge.","While I desperately struggled, the chief remained perfectly calm.","It was silently demonstrating just how vast the gap between us was.","There was a reason it had confidently declared that it would take one of my arms.","Release!","\"Whoa!\"","While I was desperately pulling on the sword, the chief suddenly relaxed its grip.","The resulting recoil nearly sent me tumbling backward in an embarrassing heap.","I barely regained my balance and faced the chief again.","It had even folded its massive arms across its chest.","\"Bugou.\"","I had no time to access the Gallery in this situation.","Still, one thing was obvious.","It was looking down on me.","Realizing that, I decided to attack more carefully.","\"Kyuu! Kyuu!\"","At that moment, Wonmo, who had remained still until now, suddenly charged into the fight.","Apparently, he had identified the chief as an enemy.","Just as I was about to order Wonmo to stay back, someone else intervened first.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"...\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo, who had climbed down from my back at some point.","Ppareumbo stepped in front of Wonmo and gestured for him to retreat.","Wonmo initially looked confused before turning his head toward me.","\"Wonmo, do as Ppareumbo says.\"","\"Kyuu...\"","Only then did Wonmo retreat.","Ppareumbo went so far as to push him all the way into the cave.","Afterward, Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t climb back onto my back. Instead, he moved some distance away and began watching.","Observing from there would make it easier for him to intervene than if he were clinging to my back.","’Looks like he understands the situation.’","The chief’s personal guards were also standing still and watching.","This meant that it was a fight between the chief and me.","Ppareumbo seemed to have understood that as well.","Or perhaps, as always, he intended to intervene if I found myself in danger.","It seemed I could trust him a little.","I gripped my sword and shield and glared at the chief.","It remained motionless with its arms folded.","It didn’t even have a prominent nose, yet it still managed to look unbearably arrogant.","\"Hmph!\"","Then I would make it pay for letting its guard down.","I kicked off the ground and thrust my sword.","The attack came without warning.","Moreover, it was a thrust rather than a slash.","It utilized the exceptional sharpness of the Heavenly Demon’s sword to its absolute limit.","If it chose to block the attack as it had before, it would be severely injured.","Swoosh!","My sword pierced the chief directly in the abdomen.","At least, that was how it looked.","’What?’","But the sensation was strange.","I was certain I had stabbed it, yet it didn’t feel as though I had pierced anything.","It felt like thrusting into empty air.","The discrepancy between what I saw and what I felt was deeply unsettling.","Shimmer—","Shortly after that thought crossed my mind, a change occurred in the chief.","Its figure wavered like a mirage before vanishing entirely.","Startled, I hurriedly pulled back my sword and looked around.","’Where is it—?!’","A chill!","An ominous instinct sent a chill through the back of my head.","I had only lived in the Forest of Four Seasons for two weeks, but I had already learned something important.","I must never ignore an ominous feeling—my instincts.","This time, I chose to trust them.","Slash!","I spun around and swung my sword horizontally.","The flame-like aura swept violently through the air.","\"Hmm.\"","The chief was standing behind me.","Unlike before, its arms were no longer folded.","Apparently, it had attempted to ambush me but failed.","I didn’t let the opportunity pass.","It was still underestimating me.","\"Huaah!\"","With a fierce shout, I slashed, thrust, and slashed again.","The chief must have been surprised by my ferocity because it made no attempt to counterattack and focused solely on evading.","Slash!","Again.","I had definitely cut it, yet I felt no resistance.","At the same time, the chief’s figure faded like a mirage.","What in the world was this technique?","Could Namu-Ppareumbo use it as well?","I hurriedly turned around, remembering to slash with my sword as a precaution.","Slash!","The gorilla wasn’t behind me.","There was nothing but empty air.","At that exact moment, the back of my head began to tingle.","It had completely fooled me.","However, I couldn’t simply turn around and slash again.","That would be impossible unless my waist could rotate a full three hundred and sixty degrees.","Therefore, I chose the next-best option.","’I have to block with my shield!’","I twisted my waist back into its original position and raised my shield.","Fortunately, my decision seemed correct because the chief’s fist was heading directly toward it.","Just how powerful was that fist?","It belonged to a creature that had effortlessly caught my sword.","I might be sent flying backward, so I should also prepare to break my fall—","\"...\"","Yet contrary to all my expectations, the chief’s attack was anticlimactic.","No impact traveled through the shield.","It merely felt as though the chief had gently placed its fist against it.","The chief pressed its fist against my shield.","That was all.","Confused, I looked into its eyes.","Its expression was perfectly serene.","’Why?’","Before that question could even fade—","Thump!","A strange sensation traveled through the shield.","Crack!","A sound like a snapping branch reached my ears.","At the same time, the shield slipped downward.","Even though I was gripping it firmly, it fell limply from my grasp.","Wondering what had happened, I lowered my gaze toward the shield.","Then I realized why the shield had fallen.","It hadn’t disobeyed my will.","Dangle—dangle—","My arm had broken, leaving it incapable of carrying out my commands.","I stared blankly at the arm hanging limply by my side.","But only for a moment.","The pain that my adrenaline had barely suppressed came surging in.","\"Aaaaaaargh!\"","The agony of a broken bone was beyond imagination.","Hadn’t I suffered from broken ribs only yesterday?","I even dropped my sword as I grabbed my dangling arm.","It felt as though someone were stabbing needles directly into my brain.","’H-How? It only touched its fist against my shield...!’","Its body dispersing like a mirage, and now this attack—","Everything about it defied comprehension.","The chief’s abilities completely surpassed my common sense.","\"Urgh...! Haaah...!\"","\"...\"","While I gritted my teeth and endured the pain, the chief silently stared at me.","Its expression seemed to ask:","Do you wish to continue?","I answered through my actions.","Swoop—","I picked up the Heavenly Demon’s sword from the ground.","One arm was broken, but the other remained intact.","I wrung out every last bit of mana I possessed and concentrated it into the sword.","Hummm—","Perhaps I had instinctively sensed the danger.","The aura that had previously billowed like flames gradually began condensing.","I couldn’t die here.","My desperate desire to survive pushed my concentration to its absolute limit.","Just as the flame-like aura began assuming a definite shape, the chief moved.","At first, it merely appeared to bend its knees slightly.","I reacted the instant I saw the movement, but—","Swoosh!","Before I could even register what had happened, the chief was standing directly before me.","Its speed equaled Namu-Ppareumbo’s—perhaps even surpassed it.","I slowly looked up at the chief standing proudly on two legs.","Had I ever been overwhelmed so completely before?","Its presence erased even the faintest desire to resist.","The feeling resembled what I had experienced while confronting the saber-toothed tiger, yet it was also fundamentally different.","Swoosh—","The chief pulled its right arm back.","Its hand wasn’t clenched into a fist.","It appeared to be preparing a palm strike.","The instant that palm struck me directly, I would die.","I had to move my body somehow if I wanted to survive.","Yet perhaps because I had already been utterly overwhelmed, my legs refused to move.","’I can’t die like this...!’","I struggled desperately.","I even bit my tongue as I forced myself to move.","Fortunately, that desperate resistance seemed to work, and I barely managed to move my legs.","Next came my arm.","Under the illusion that time itself had slowed, I tried to raise it.","Whoosh!","The problem was that the chief could also act within that fleeting moment.","The arm it had drawn back shot forward like a bullet.","Its enormous gorilla palm completely filled my vision.","Just as I resigned myself to dying—","Baaaaang!","The chief’s palm swept past the side of my face.","The explosive burst of air left my ears ringing, while my hair whipped violently in the wind.","Craaaaaash!","My one relatively functional ear allowed me to guess what had happened behind me.","The noise wasn’t merely something collapsing.","It sounded as though everything had been completely obliterated.","I desperately hoped the cave hadn’t been behind me.","\"...\"","I froze in place.","Only my eyes could move.","Slowly, I shifted my trembling gaze toward the chief.","For some reason, it was smiling.","The chief lowered the hand that had passed beside my face and placed it on my shoulder.","Even though it had merely rested its hand there, it felt unbearably heavy.","Pat, pat—","The chief patted my shoulder several times as though telling me to relax.","It had truthfully said that it would take one of my arms.","But it had never said that it would take my life.","The chief removed its hand from my shoulder and spoke in the language of the Central Plains.","\"Wai wonni.\"","Welcome to the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Shinshou.\"","Youngster.","For some reason, I felt certain that was what it was saying.","\"Zheoba.\"","The chief turned around and issued an order to its personal guards.","The spear-wielding guards merely glanced at me once before following it.","I remained rooted in place until the chief and its party disappeared.","\"Phew...\"","Only after they had been gone for some time did I finally manage to exhale.","I paid no attention to my broken arm dangling at my side.","More precisely, I was incapable of doing so.","My pounding heart felt as though it might burst at any moment.","It was like someone was forcibly pressing down upon my entire body.","The saber-toothed tiger had inspired an instinctive, primal fear.","The chief’s pressure, however, had felt almost deliberately manufactured.","’Who in the world...?’","At the same time, I became curious about the person who had taught the chief martial arts.","Just who was its master to have trained a gorilla into such an extraordinary expert?","I gradually organized my chaotic thoughts and came back to my senses.","My immediate priority was treating my broken arm.","Leaving it in this condition could result in severe lasting complications.","’Will an elixir even heal this...?’","I was carefully holding my arm to prevent the broken bones from twisting when I turned around and froze.","The chief had launched a palm strike beside my face.","I had clearly heard something being destroyed behind me.","I had assumed that a tree had simply fallen, but the reality far exceeded my expectations.","A \"road\" had appeared.","The area had originally been filled with densely packed trees.","But a single palm strike from the chief had sent trees crashing down or torn them out by their roots.","The unexpected road left me feeling faint.","’...Even Sun Wukong couldn’t do something like this.’","Then again, Sun Wukong wasn’t a gorilla. He was a monkey with a tail.","Whatever.","’Can I really survive here?’","Either way, my resolve had been shaken."]},{"title":"Chapter 113","paragraphs":["Welcome To (5)","I barely managed to immobilize my dangling arm before returning to the cave.","When I arrived, I found Wonmo pacing back and forth.","It seemed he had been beside himself with worry while I was gone.","\"Kyuu! Kyuu!\"","Wonmo gave me an enthusiastic welcome when he saw me return injured.","I would have loved to hug him with both arms, but that was rather difficult with one arm in this state.","\"Wonmo, wait just a moment. Let me fix my arm first.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","Wonmo answered energetically and took a small step back. Good little Wonmo was such a good listener.","I chuckled and carefully lowered my arm. First, I needed to remove the shield.","I had suffered plenty of injuries before, but this was my first time breaking an arm, so I wasn’t sure what to do.","’What if I pour the elixir on it without knowing what I’m doing and the bone heals crooked?’","That was my greatest concern.","My ribs hadn’t been shattered as badly as my arm.","It seemed best to immobilize it with a splint first.","Using my good arm, I found a suitable plank of wood.","All I had to do was cut one of the logs I had split for the campfire down to an appropriate size.","’And buy some cloth from the Gallery.’","Then I simply had to place the splint against my arm and tie it in place. The problem was that doing so with only one usable arm was difficult.","\"Hey, Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","Hold this for me, will you? My arm’s in a bit of a state.\"","I asked Namu-Ppareumbo for help. He might not be able to tie it, but he should at least be able to hold the cloth.","Namu-Ppareumbo stared silently at me before holding the cloth as I had asked.","With that, I managed to fashion a splint using the piece of wood and cloth.","This was only a temporary measure, however. Pouring elixir on it would be the real treatment.","Title: My Arm Got Wrecked","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an arm in a splint)","Fought the leader gorilla and got my arm wrecked. Good thing the leader gorilla spared me. Otherwise, I’d be dead, lol.","Anyway, can I just pour elixir over my arm like this? I was worried the bone might heal out of alignment, so I only immobilized it with a splint for now.","└ Heavenly Demon: Was the monkey strong?","└ Wild Grylls: Absurdly strong. My arm broke even though I blocked it with my shield. It didn’t even punch the shield. It just placed its fist against it.","└ Heavenly Demon: Your arm broke merely from it touching the shield?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It literally just tapped it.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think it can even use Penetrating Force. Its cultivation must be remarkably advanced. I did not anticipate this.","└ Wild Grylls: And when I swung my sword at it, its body vanished like a mirage before it reappeared directly behind me.","└ Heavenly Demon: Even Shifting Form and Position? How astonishing. It appears the creature showed you mercy.","└ SwordMaster: You’re really lucky to be alive. If that gorilla had gone all out, you would’ve died in less than a second.","└ Wild Grylls: I even launched a surprise attack, but it stopped my sword with nothing but its fingers. That was when I knew it was over.","└ SwordMaster: How many fingers did it use?","└ Wild Grylls: Three.","└ SwordMaster: It must have used three because it was you, Mr. Grylls. It probably would’ve used only one against most people.","└ Wild Grylls: It probably also sensed the power of the sword the Heavenly Demon gave me.","└ What kind of gorilla uses Penetrating Force and Shifting Form and Position? I won’t believe it until I see it myself;;","└ It can speak a human language, so why wouldn’t it be possible?","└ Honestly, this sounds like a lie. You might as well say it can fire palm blasts.","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t know about palm blasts, but it did destroy the entire forest. I’ll show you later.","└ What the hell? Did it actually fire a palm blast? Lol.","└ Not even the monkeys from mythology were like that, lol.","└ Monkeys appear in mythology?","└ It’s a story from the Central Plains. A monkey became a mystical creature by imitating human behavior.","└ Oh. Sounds interesting.","└ Starlight Princess: Is your arm completely broken?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It’s dangling loosely. I can pour elixir on it as it is, right? I was worried the bone might heal incorrectly, so I immobilized it with a splint first.","└ Starlight Princess: You made the right choice. Bones actually do heal out of alignment fairly often. Parts of the torso are strongly affected just by drinking elixir, but that isn’t the case with the limbs.","└ Wild Grylls: Would it heal quickly if I cut my arm open with a knife and poured the elixir inside?","└ Starlight Princess: I’ll just give you a syringe. I used to be ill, so I had to use syringes frequently.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Is there anything you want in return? I don’t think I’ll be able to go outside today, but I should be able to give it to you tomorrow.","└ Starlight Princess: Just stay alive and in one piece. You’re really starting to seem like you could drop dead at any moment.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes, ma’am.","└ But his life really is hanging by a thread, isn’t it?","└ Honestly, I don’t think he’ll last a month.","└ Hasn’t it only been exactly two weeks?","└ I wonder what’ll appear after the gorilla, lol.","└ Good thing the gorilla showed him mercy. Otherwise, everything could’ve ended today, lol.","└ PraiseTheSun: Should I try raising a gorilla too? I wonder whether I could teach it martial arts.","└ Wild Grylls: Try teaching it to speak first. I’m curious whether it’s possible too.","└ PraiseTheSun: Wouldn’t simple sign language be possible? A chimpanzee I raised before could do it.","└ Wild Grylls: You raised a chimpanzee?;;","└ PraiseTheSun: Yeah. But it eventually died because of its limited lifespan. I doted on that little guy.","└ Upvote if you think that chimp lived better than you, lol.","└ Lol, they say that even if you become a slave, you should become a nobleman’s slave~","└ I’d rather become a chimpanzee, lol.","└ My intelligence is lower than a chimp’s. Could you raise me?","└ Then share some of your intelligence with me. You’re no different from a chimpanzee or monkey anyway.","└ Instead of becoming my pet, just become my slave. I’ll take good care of you.","└ You bastards, lol.","While the people in the Gallery continued their chatter, I received the syringe from Starlight Princess.","[Starlight Princess: I gave you a new one just in case, so you can use it without worrying.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I just fill this with elixir and inject it into my arm, right?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Please use it carefully.]","The syringe looked both similar to and different from the ones I knew.","Its basic shape was identical, but its material and size were completely different.","It was especially large. The barrel was thick, though the needle was relatively small.","\"If even the needle had been huge... Ugh.\"","I filled the syringe with elixir and checked whether it flowed properly.","Golden liquid trickled from the tip of the needle. This should be enough.","I then inserted the needle into the spot where my arm had broken and slowly injected the elixir.","’I look like some drug addict shooting up.’","The elixir’s distinctive cooling sensation spread through my arm, and the pain gradually subsided.","I could even feel the bones knitting together, so it seemed to have mostly healed.","Nevertheless, I planned to keep the splint on for the rest of the day if possible.","I had heard that broken bones could leave some fairly serious aftereffects.","’At least I survived.’","I took a sip of elixir and stared up at the ceiling.","Despite the Forest of Four Seasons’ notoriety, I had thought it was surprisingly easy to survive here. That had been a grave miscalculation.","I simply hadn’t encountered an irregular existence like the leader gorilla until now.","Even the saber-toothed tiger would be nothing more than a house cat before that gorilla.","’So there are creatures as powerful as that gorilla?’","Just how strong were they?","The thought frightened me a little.","After all, I didn’t even have to travel far to find those monstrous crabs and crayfish that looked as though they had stepped straight out of a kaiju movie.","However, their habitats were different, and their enormous size made them easy to avoid.","The real problem was creatures like the leader gorilla—small enough to be difficult to spot and living nearby.","As I brooded over the situation, my gaze suddenly fell upon Namu-Ppareumbo.","He had merely watched without intervening even though I had nearly died.","Had he refrained because the gorilla’s royal guards would have joined the fight the moment he interfered?","Or had he already known that the leader gorilla would show me mercy?","I wasn’t sure of the details, but it was obvious that Namu-Ppareumbo had some sort of history with the leader gorilla.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","\"Can you use that Shifting Form and Position thing too? You know, where you disappear and then reappear somewhere else.\"","Nod—","Namu-Ppareumbo answered by nodding.","Seeing that, I nodded as well. Offering tribute to this guy had definitely been the right decision.","’Come to think of it...’","After Namu-Ppareumbo, my gaze fell upon the bananas.","It was the bunch of bananas the leader gorilla had thrown to me as an apology.","To be precise, it was three clusters of bananas bound together, practically an entire set.","This would be enough to keep me from worrying about food for a while. Or I could eat them as snacks.","’Let’s try one.’","I was feeling gloomy, so I might as well eat something sweet.","I plucked off a banana.","I didn’t take only one for myself. I also picked one each for Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo.","\"Here. Eat up.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"...\"","My animal companions began eating the bananas in their own ways.","Wonmo, who had an insatiable weakness for sweets, practically buried his face in his banana, while Namu-Ppareumbo simply stared at his.","He probably felt reluctant to eat a banana given to him by his enemy. Still, judging by the way he peeled it, he didn’t seem completely opposed to the idea.","’It’s been a long time since I ate a banana.’","I struggled to peel it with one hand.","I wanted to use my left hand, but I intended to rest it just to be safe.","Munch, munch—","\"...Oh?\"","The moment I took a bite, a honey-like sweetness filled my mouth.","It even possessed the distinctive fragrance of a banana. It was literally a banana as sweet as honey.","No wonder Wonmo had buried his entire face in his. It was a flavor that filled you with joy.","’Can a banana really have such a high sugar content?’","These bananas had grown while absorbing an abundance of mana. Even Southeast Asian bananas probably weren’t this sweet.","They were enormous too. A single banana was as large as my forearm.","I devoured the banana ravenously, gradually calming my troubled mind.","’He really did give me something good.’","Of course, it was still far inferior to the fasting pills.","At first, I had even thought he was telling me to take these and get lost.","But considering how delicious they were, it seemed he had done his best in his own way.","How could he possibly obtain something as nutritious as a fasting pill in this place?","Simple medicinal herbs were one thing, but fasting pills were man-made food created by combining various herbs.","\"Nom, nom, nom.\"","Wonmo even ate all the banana peels. They were delicious, but I worried they might give him diarrhea.","I leaned against the cave wall and glanced at my broken arm.","No matter how many times I thought about it, it was astonishing. The gorilla had merely placed its fist against my shield, yet my arm had broken.","Would I ever be able to perform a feat like that?","It seemed difficult to learn something like that solely through posts on the Gallery.","’Wait. Come to think of it...’","It had happened just before the leader gorilla delivered its final strike.","When my survival instincts had surged and my concentration had reached its absolute limit.","I remembered how the aura that had billowed like flames gradually condensed and began taking shape.","’I need to practice before I forget that feeling.’","The sensation still lingered within me. The impact it had left was simply that profound.","I immediately brought over the Heavenly Demon’s sword and manifested my aura.","When I infused it with a small amount of mana, aura rose from it like a heat haze.","If I infused it with just a little more power, it surged like flames.","’Let’s slowly recall what I felt back then.’","The sensation of that formless energy crushing my entire body.","How I had even bitten my tongue in my desperate attempt to escape that pressure.","Although I hadn’t completed it, merely grasping the first clue was enough.","Woooong—woong—woooong—","Nevertheless, it was still difficult. The aura refused to condense properly.","Even so, I occasionally saw parts of the flame-like aura diminish.","It wasn’t because I had stopped supplying it with mana. If anything, I was forcibly pumping more and more mana into it, yet its volume still decreased.","It hadn’t taken on a complete form, but even this alone was remarkable progress.","’The problem is that there’s so much aura that it’s difficult to control.’","I would eventually achieve results if I continued practicing slowly.","I put down the sword and accessed the Gallery.","The moment I logged in, I saw everyone talking about me.","They were saying that a talking gorilla was obviously fiction and that I had made the whole thing up.","’This is why I recorded it, you bastards.’","So I uploaded all the footage of the gorilla speaking to the Gallery.","The Heavenly Demon had translated everything it said, but far too many people still refused to believe me.","’They probably don’t have things like video editing or AI here.’","Then again, if they did, that would be fascinating in its own way.","I quietly checked the Gallery’s comments.","└ What kind of fabricated translation is this?","└ Damn.","└ Bull.","└ Shit.","\"...\"","Or maybe not.","Perhaps people were the same everywhere."]},{"title":"Chapter 114","paragraphs":["Mining (1)","Title: Come See a Talking Gorilla","Wild Grylls","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the royal guards and leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla threatening me)","Too many people refused to believe me, so I’m uploading these.","Watch them and decide for yourselves whether I’m lying.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is fascinating no matter how many times I see it. Even its manner of speech sounds like something from ancient times.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t know the language of the Central Plains very well. What is it saying?","└ Heavenly Demon: It says SwordMaster is a liar and that only the Heavenly Demon is great.","└ SwordMaster: There you go, lying every time you open your mouth again;;","└ What’s with the fake translation?","└ F—","└ U—","└ Cker.","└ What the hell is this? Lmao.","└ Look at that teamwork, lol.","└ Allfather: By Aragon! Not only the leader, but even the gorillas beside it can speak. This will send shock waves through academia...!","└ Professor, won’t those gorillas pose a threat to us?","└ Allfather: That is unlikely. It might be a different story if they developed the Forest of Four Seasons into a civilization of their own.","└ A civilization in the Forest of Four Seasons, damn.","└ I heard those bastards are strong, lol. They even know how to use tools.","└ Once they start farming, the second human race will be complete.","└ Then should we classify them as beastmen? What exactly are they?","└ Wouldn’t we have to classify them as beastmen?","└ Suspiciously: It’s hard to call them beastmen. Their limb proportions aren’t right.","└ Allfather: The commenter above is correct. To be classified as beastmen, they must possess bodily proportions similar to humans.","└ Clever Main: By the way, do you know that guy’s name? If they have a language, they must have names too.","└ Wouldn’t whoever taught it to speak have given it a name? Does Grylls know?","└ Looks like he went off to do something else. He isn’t replying to any comments.","└ Clever Main: Then we’ll have to name it ourselves. How about Sun Wukong-plus-one?","└ What the hell is Sun Wukong-plus-one? Lol.","└ Clever Main: Sun Wukong is the name of a monkey from the mythology of the Central Plains. That guy isn’t a monkey but a gorilla, so he’s Sun Wukong-plus-one. Isn’t it fucking brilliant?","└ Holy shit, are you a genius? Your IQ must be over 150!","└ Clever Main: I am pretty smart, lol.","└ And yet a guy like you wastes his time on the Gallery, lol.","It was the Gallery, all right. Toss them one juicy topic, and they would happily entertain themselves.","Some of their speculation was occasionally meaningful, so browsing through it was quite useful.","’If everyone thinks they speak in an archaic manner, someone from the old days must have taught them.’","The most noteworthy detail was the leader gorilla’s archaic speech.","Languages naturally changed over time.","Even without looking far back, there were plenty of differences between the Korean spoken fifty years ago and the Korean spoken today.","Moreover, I had heard that the Jeonghyeol War, which occurred approximately sixty years ago, had brought significant changes to the language of the Central Plains.","In other words, the leader gorilla was speaking the language as it would have been spoken by someone from that era.","’All sorts of things really have happened.’","From the Immortal King to the Jeonghyeol War.","Such was human history. Roughly half of it inevitably ended up being marked by war and bloodshed.","People beating and fighting one another day after day was practically normal.","’It’s the same here.’","The wilderness was no different. It was a place where battles for survival took place every single day.","Hadn’t the leader gorilla nearly killed me just moments ago?","I was in no position to criticize anyone. As I had repeatedly said, I had more than enough problems of my own.","I considered how I should spend the rest of the day.","The leader gorilla had completely disrupted my plans, so I needed to revise them.","’Should I... build the door and wall?’","One slap from the leader gorilla would bring down any door or wall I constructed.","Even in The Three Little Pigs , the house built from bricks had remained standing.","The leader gorilla, however, rendered all of that meaningless.","’At least it apologized, so it probably won’t invade my territory again.’","Still, I had no idea when another creature as powerful as the leader gorilla might appear.","That meant any structure I painstakingly built could collapse with a single flick.","And it might not stop at the structures. The entire cave could collapse just like my heart.","’Let’s give up on the door and wall. I’ll only install CCTV cameras.’","Thanks to that realization, I could abandon the idea without hesitation. I should consider myself lucky to have realized it early.","If I had finished building everything only for the leader gorilla to appear and destroy it, my despair would have been twice as great.","That didn’t mean I could simply stand by and let someone steal my possessions from right under my nose.","Losing the fasting pills would be manageable, but if someone stole the elixir, even my life would be endangered.","’Should I hide the important items underground?’","I could dig into the floor and cleverly conceal the spot beneath the tiger hide.","As an additional precaution, I should place charcoal inside for its moisture-absorbing properties.","To do that, I would need to dig through a portion of the cave’s solid floor.","’Will a pickaxe be enough?’","The cave floor contained some soil, but most of it was stone.","It would probably be difficult to excavate unless I used a hammer or pickaxe.","Besides, I couldn’t use my left arm immediately, so for now, I only intended to inspect the area.","\"This should be a decent place to hide them.\"","I found a relatively soft spot and marked it.","I could begin modifying it once I decided that my left arm had fully recovered—probably sometime after lunch.","\"Chomp! Chomp, chomp!\"","\"Good grief, Wonmo.\"","You can’t eat that many bananas. You’ll give yourself diarrhea.","Just how delicious did he find them to be that he was even eating the peels? He had already eaten four bananas by himself.","In the end, I had no choice but to hide the bananas somewhere else too. Wonmo flailed in protest, but it couldn’t be helped.","’Does that... more or less settle everything?’","It seemed I had finished organizing everything that needed attention.","I planned to start digging into the floor around lunchtime.","It was currently approximately eleven in the morning.","Since the leader gorilla had visited early in the morning, I still had plenty of time.","’I should light the oven first. Then I’ll head up to the river and check the fish trap.’","My left hand might be in a splint, but I still had work to do.","I stood up.","Then I began wondering what I should feed Namu-Ppareumbo.","He had only eaten fasting pills until now, so I had no idea what his staple diet was.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo, what do you eat? We don’t have any fasting pills left.\"","Namu-Ppareumbo raised a claw and pointed somewhere.","I turned toward the direction he indicated.","Splash! Splash!","He was pointing at the metal bucket containing the fish.","Was he saying that he ate fish?","When I looked at him questioningly, he nodded.","’Come to think of it, didn’t he try to steal my fish when we first met?’","I still remembered it vividly.","He had slowly crept toward the fish to steal one, only to be caught red-handed.","I couldn’t even describe how dumbfounded I had been at the time. Of course, in hindsight, Namu-Ppareumbo had been showing me mercy.","’Considering both the gorillas and Namu-Ppareumbo like fish...’","Was fish something like gukbap to them?","Delicious gukbap, the so-called commoner’s meal—even though it had recently become expensive enough to make that label sound ridiculous.","It seemed quite likely, since catching fish would be difficult for both the gorillas and Namu-Ppareumbo.","After all, a Golden Poison Frog was sitting right beside the water. Without a fish trap, fishing would be dangerous.","\"All right. I’ll give you fish for the time being. You eat it raw like Wonmo, right?\"","\"...\"","He nodded again.","With this, I wouldn’t have to worry about his meals for a while.","I carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and brought Wonmo along with me.","When we eventually reached the river, I found two fish caught in the trap.","’Three in the morning and two at noon. Not bad.’","I still had plenty in reserve. There should have been three or four left.","Now that I also had to account for Namu-Ppareumbo’s meals, I needed to conserve them.","If necessary, we would have to eat smoked meat instead.","’The time is gradually coming when I’ll have to earn everything for myself.’","With one unexpected incident occurring after another, it seemed my reliance on the Gallery was gradually decreasing.","No. I had only survived this long because the Gallery existed in the first place.","As I cleaned the fish, I removed the inner cores from their entrails.","Slide—","\"Hmm?\"","However, the moment I removed one of the inner cores, Namu-Ppareumbo extended his hand beside me.","The gesture made it look as though he wanted me to give it to him.","I alternated my gaze between Namu-Ppareumbo’s face and his outstretched hand before asking uncertainly,","\"You want the inner core?\"","He answered with a nod.","I was slightly dumbfounded but soon gave it some thought.","To be honest, I had an abundance of inner cores.","Every time I cleaned a fish, another inner core was added to my stockpile.","It might actually be better to give one to Namu-Ppareumbo every now and then.","\"Here. Take it.\"","\"...\"","When I handed him the round inner core, Namu-Ppareumbo immediately placed it in his mouth.","Apparently, he ate them as a substitute for fasting pills.","However, they must not have tasted as good as the fasting pills because he frowned slightly.","Even so, one should be enough for a meal. After all, it probably contained far more mana than a fasting pill.","’But he eats inner cores like ordinary food?’","That was fascinating in its own way.","Just how strong was this guy?","I continued stealing glances at Namu-Ppareumbo as I finished preparing the fish.","My left arm was slightly uncomfortable, but cleaning the fish and placing them in the oven wasn’t difficult.","’I’m glad the gorillas didn’t destroy the oven.’","Now that I had filled my stomach, it was time to circulate my inner cultivation technique.","Under normal circumstances, I would have begun consuming the inner cores today, but I postponed it because of the condition of my arm.","I would probably start eating them around the evening. The day I became stronger wasn’t far away.","’My arm... seems to have mostly healed.’","The arm into which I had injected the elixir appeared to be almost completely healed.","Of course, I had no intention of going out to explore. I planned to remain holed up at home all day.","I tapped my left arm in several places before nodding. It felt sturdier than before.","’Let’s start by digging into the cave floor.’","I needed somewhere to hide the elixir and my other valuables.","The gorillas probably wouldn’t invade again, but there was always a chance something might happen.","Since they were highly intelligent, there were bound to be a few with thieving tendencies.","I purchased a suitably sized pickaxe from the Gallery.","’When I think about it, I learned all sorts of things in the military.’","I had learned how to use both a shovel and a pickaxe during my military service.","Back then, I had grumbled about when I would ever need such skills, but now they were proving extremely useful.","Life really was unpredictable.","I let out a hollow laugh and moved into position.","’Swing it in a full circle to build centrifugal force. And instead of relying on my strength, let the weight of the pickaxe itself do the work.’","If I recklessly swung it with brute force, I would only injure my back and hands.","I had learned that lesson the hard way in the military.","Granted, the injury had allowed me to take it easy for a while, but they hadn’t shown me any mercy afterward.","Distracted by those pointless thoughts, I swung the pickaxe in a full circle.","Then I added a little force and brought it down upon my chosen spot.","Clang! Clang! Clank!","Worried that the floor might not break easily, I even infused the pickaxe with aura as I began digging.","Fortunately, the cave floor wasn’t particularly hard, so it broke apart easily.","’Since I’m putting an entire box inside, I should dig fairly deep.’","Not only did it need to be deep, but it also needed to be wide.","I might eventually have to store various supplies there in addition to my valuables.","I enthusiastically swung the pickaxe to a steady rhythm. Little by little, the floor began to give way.","Clang! Clank! Clank!","However, at some point, it stopped breaking so easily.","It seemed I had reached a different type of rock.","Still, it would eventually break if I kept at it.","With that thought, I continued patiently.","Clang!","\"No.\"","Clank!","\"Why!\"","CLAAAAANG!","\"WON’T YOU BREAK?!\"","In the end, I lost my temper and hurled the pickaxe away.","Just how hard was this rock that even an aura-infused pickaxe couldn’t break it?","Irritated, I stared at the hole, which was only about half as deep as I had intended.","A pile of loose stones surrounded it, so I cleared them away one by one with my hands.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","Once I removed the rubble, a stone with a striking green glow was revealed beneath it.","No. This was closer to an ore than an ordinary stone.","I could tell because I had seen orichalcum before.","\"What the hell is this now?\"","As if everything else weren’t enough, now I couldn’t even dig into the ground.","It felt as though God himself were deliberately screwing me over.","Setting that aside, what kind of ore was so hard that even my pickaxe couldn’t break it?","I immediately took a photograph and uploaded it to the Gallery.","Title: Does Anyone Know What This Is?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a green, glowing mineral)","I was digging into the ground to make a place to store my valuables, and this crap showed up.","What the hell is it? Is it that mithril stuff someone mentioned before?","It’s so fucking hard that my hands are killing me.","└ Passing Dwarf: Uh... I think that really is mithril.","└ Wild Grylls: ?","It was real?"]},{"title":"Chapter 115","paragraphs":["Mining (2)","There was a saying:","Try digging in the ground all day and see if you find even a single ten-won coin.","It meant that instead of dreaming about making money through pointless schemes, you should find yourself a proper job.","In reality, however, you could uncover all sorts of things by digging, and the greatest prize of all was oil.","The moment you struck oil, becoming rich was only a matter of time.","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. I think that really is mithril.","└ Wild Grylls: ?","But I didn’t need money.","I needed something immediately useful more than I needed wealth.","Even if oil had erupted from the ground, I was in a situation where a single lump of steel would have been more valuable.","Naturally, I couldn’t help feeling bewildered by the sudden appearance of mithril, which was said to be even rarer than steel.","’You find something bizarre every time you dig into the ground in this damn forest, don’t you?’","I had no idea how this place was structured.","As if having an orichalcum cave nearby weren’t enough, now mithril had appeared when I dug into the ground.","Of course, I needed to verify rigorously whether this truly was mithril.","Moreover, all kinds of theories had begun flying around the Gallery, so I needed to be cautious.","└ You’re just going to run off and get drunk again after saying that, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: You caught me, lol.","└ What do you mean, \"caught me,\" you dwarven bastard? Lmao.","└ A race that drinks whenever they get a break, lol.","└ That’s mithril? Isn’t it too bright for mithril?","└ It isn’t even mixed with rock. It looks like a solid mass of pure mithril.","└ The entire orichalcum cave was made of orichalcum, so it isn’t impossible.","└ Be precise. It would be impossible anywhere outside the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ Ah, I think I understand. Just as all the animals grew larger, the minerals must have grown too! That’s why it looks like that even before being refined!","└ That sounds pretty convincing. Then why are the gorillas normal-sized?","└ Dunno.","└ Passing Dwarf: Whatever. Break off a small piece and send it to me. I’ll examine it for you.","One comment among the countless replies caught my attention.","Was this truly mithril in its natural, unrefined state?","Not only mithril, but most minerals were found mixed with rock.","Pure substances were obtained by placing the ore inside a furnace and processing it through a method known as smelting.","What I had discovered, however, appeared to be a pure material that required no smelting whatsoever. That was why it was difficult to believe.","There were exceptions, such as diamonds, but mithril was not normally one of them.","’Everyone seems willing to accept it because I’ve already discovered an orichalcum cave, though.’","Orichalcum was originally a mineral as well. Nevertheless, I had discovered a cave made entirely of orichalcum.","There was no reason mithril couldn’t be the same.","The only problem was that this one happened to be beneath my home.","Either way, I needed to give at least a small piece to the dwarf.","I stared at the green-glowing mithril.","’A guardian isn’t suddenly going to rise out of the ground, is it?’","If that happened, the entire cave—including the floor—would collapse.","My heart would collapse along with it.","Unlike the orichalcum cave, however, there wasn’t any empty space beneath this ore.","Moreover, there was an even greater problem.","’Why won’t this damn thing break?’","Mining it was incredibly difficult.","No matter how many times I struck it with the pickaxe, I couldn’t leave even a single scratch.","If I remembered correctly, mithril was supposed to possess strength similar to steel while being far lighter.","It might have been different if it were mixed with ordinary rock, but most mithril was notoriously difficult to mine.","Clang! Clang! Clank!","Still, what else could I do?","I had no choice but to keep mining.","They said no tree could withstand ten swings of an axe, and mithril should be no different.","More importantly, I had aura.","I continued mining while infusing the pickaxe with aura.","Clang! Scrape!","After some time, I finally managed to extract a tiny piece of mithril.","I had been mining for so long that sweat streamed down my body.","’I only extracted a little, but the pickaxe is already almost completely blunt.’","Even though I had used aura, I couldn’t prevent the pickaxe from being damaged.","Aura might enhance a tool’s performance, but it wasn’t omnipotent.","Using aura didn’t increase the durability of the weapon itself.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was sturdy only because it had been forged from something called Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron.","I examined the thumb-sized piece of green ore before accessing the Gallery.","If possible, I also wanted to get a high-quality pickaxe from the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls: I managed to mine this, so please examine it for me.]","[Passing Dwarf: Okay.]","[Wild Grylls: If you say you’re going drinking again, I’m never giving you anything else.]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s too harsh;; Fine, I understand. It’s easy to examine, so I’ll let you know soon.]","Since the dwarf said he would post his findings, I inspected the remaining mithril ore.","I wasn’t sure whether I should even call it ore, but for now, that was what I would call it.","Unlike orichalcum, mithril could be fashioned into weapons and all kinds of equipment.","It would undoubtedly be of immense help to me.","Before that, however, there was something I needed to do.","’I should give some to the Heavenly Demon and PraiseTheSun.’","If this truly was mithril, there were two people I wanted to repay immediately.","The Heavenly Demon had given me an absurdly overpowered weapon, while PraiseTheSun had continuously provided me with shields.","I had believed that even a fully mature Mandrake wouldn’t be enough to repay their kindness.","’And I broke the shield PraiseTheSun gave me.’","Like orichalcum, mithril was a mineral that was difficult to obtain even with money.","Wouldn’t PraiseTheSun, who loved rare things, be delighted to receive it?","’First, I should determine how far this deposit extends.’","If the entire cave floor was made of mithril, that would create its own set of problems.","I couldn’t simply leave the mithril untouched, but I couldn’t destroy the entire cave floor either.","After considering the matter, I decided to proceed with my original plan.","I still needed a hidden storage space, so I could simply continue digging in the same spot.","’Even this much is enormous.’","I wasn’t asking for an entire suit of armor.","I only needed some spare tools.","I vigorously swung the pickaxe to create the storage space.","’Damn it. Should I just ask him to make me a mithril pickaxe?’","After five minutes of mining, I was already sick of it.","I wiped away the sweat and accessed the Gallery.","The dwarf should have finished examining it by now.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hey, hey! Read this quickly. It’s urgent.]","[Passing Dwarf: You’re always gone at times like this, damn it. This is really fucking urgent, so hurry up and read this.]","The moment I entered the Gallery, I saw the dwarf’s messages, which sounded rather urgent.","They had arrived only a minute ago.","I stared at them in confusion.","’Is it a different mineral rather than mithril?’","This was the same dwarf who had drunkenly responded far too late with, \"Yeah, that’s orichalcum.\"","It was strange for someone like him to send messages in such a frantic manner.","[Wild Grylls: Yeah;; Why are you in such a hurry?]","[Passing Dwarf: This really is mithril. But it’s completely different from what I expected.]","[Wild Grylls: What’s different about it?]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s practically a solid mass of pure mithril that barely needs any refining;;]","A solid mass?","I tilted my head when I read that. Wasn’t that a good thing?","[Wild Grylls: What’s wrong? Is it not mithril? Or are you upset because you can’t go drinking?]","[Passing Dwarf: I’m being serious, so stop making jokes about alcohol.]","[Wild Grylls: Isn’t this good? It means we can skip all the annoying steps.]","[Passing Dwarf: Do you have absolutely no idea what you’ve discovered?]","[Wild Grylls: Nope. No idea whatsoever. Isn’t it just something good?]","[Passing Dwarf: Good grief. Fuck, is your head an anvil or did someone smash it with a hammer?;;]","[Wild Grylls: Stop insulting me and explain. I came from another world, so I don’t know any of this.]","[Passing Dwarf: Fine. I’ll explain it while assuming your head really is an anvil.]","Passing Dwarf’s explanation went as follows.","Minerals were ordinarily found inside rock, and their purity could be increased through the refining process.","The same applied to mithril.","Moreover, mithril occurred less frequently and in smaller quantities than other ores, so its higher value was unavoidable.","Even if what I had discovered had been ordinary mithril ore, the sheer size of the deposit would already have been absurd.","[Wild Grylls: Are you worried you’ll get caught browsing the Gallery?]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s a separate issue. This is going to make my real life a huuuuge pain in the ass.]","If he needed permission from his superiors, mithril must ordinarily require a fairly complicated refining process.","Well, it was supposed to be a rare mineral, so that much made sense.","Fortunately, mine was a solid mass of mithril, so simply melting it would be enough.","[Passing Dwarf: The so-called mithril weapons out there are actually all alloys. There isn’t a single tool in the world made entirely from pure mithril. Not even the wealthiest people in Setan could do something like that.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. But you’re saying I can?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. If it had been ordinary ore, I was going to send it back.]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Why? Didn’t you say you were a dwarf?]","[Passing Dwarf: I am a dwarf, but ordinary mithril has to undergo a special refining process. The furnace required for it can only be used with permission from the higher-ups.]","[Passing Dwarf: How did you mine this? More importantly, are you sure you actually mined it? Considering mithril’s hardness, I could only understand this if you said you found a loose piece lying around.]","[Wild Grylls: What are you talking about? It was hard, but it broke apart like stone.]","[Passing Dwarf: What are you talking about? The piece you gave me is a solid mass. Solid mithril. It’s basically a lump of metal.]","What was this guy talking about now?","I furrowed my brow.","The mithril vein was certainly hard, but based on my experience, it definitely wasn’t as tough as metal.","If it had been, I wouldn’t have been able to mine it with a pickaxe at all.","It was rock that could be broken with enough effort.","That was the mithril I was currently mining.","[Wild Grylls: That’s strange. I mined it just like ordinary stone. Isn’t that normal?]","[Passing Dwarf: Don’t talk nonsense. You’d have trouble cutting it even with a saw, so how could you possibly—;;]","[Wild Grylls: No, I’m serious;; I’ll record a video and show you. Before that, give me a pickaxe.]","[Passing Dwarf: I have no idea what kind of nonsense you’re spouting, but fine. I’ll give you one. I made it as a spare for myself, so it should be good.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, and make me a mithril pickaxe. Digging this stuff is difficult.]","[Passing Dwarf: Holy shit, lol. The first pure-mithril tool in the world is going to be a pickaxe? Lmao.]","[Wild Grylls: I’m serious. It’ll make mining easier, won’t it?]","[Passing Dwarf: It would make things slightly easier, but the difference wouldn’t be dramatic;;]","Reality really was different from a game.","In games, tools made from the same material made mining that material far easier.","Still, I had an abundance of mithril, so there was no harm in owning one mithril pickaxe.","Even if the visible deposit was all there was, it wouldn’t be a problem. A pickaxe could be used anywhere.","’Will this help me mine it more easily?’","I examined the pickaxe I had received from the dwarf.","At a glance, it looked like an ordinary pickaxe.","However, its handle was slightly short. It had probably been made according to dwarven proportions.","Clang! Clank!","Even so, it performed far better than my previous pickaxe.","It had a satisfying weight and excellent durability. Thanks to it, I managed to mine a considerable amount of mithril.","Eventually, I turned a fist-sized chunk of mithril over in my hands and frowned in confusion.","’This is strange. It definitely feels more like stone.’","Not only was its texture stone-like, but it also lacked the distinctive solidity of metal.","I tilted my head before sending the mithril to the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls: (Video of me mining mithril) Look. It breaks apart like stone.]","[Passing Dwarf: That should be impossible. What the hell is going on? The piece you gave me is a lump of metal;;]","[Wild Grylls: You’re actually good at this, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: Hey, no matter what, don’t insult my pride like that. I might not look it, but I’m a master metallurgist.]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry. I apologize. Anyway, I showed you the evidence.]","[Passing Dwarf: Fuck, lol. I feel like everything I know is falling apart. Don’t you sense anything strange about it?]","I was just about to answer, Not at all.","Slide—","A fragment of mithril lying on the ground moved slightly.","’...What?’","For a moment, I thought my eyes had deceived me.","But then an astonishing scene unfolded, immediately proving otherwise.","Slide—scrape—","The mithril fragments scattered around during the mining process began moving little by little.","Where were they going?","Toward the mithril vein, which continued to shine brilliantly.","I left the Gallery window open and stared blankly at the sight.","Tap—","Before long, the fragments merged with the mithril vein.","They became one again as though they had never broken away.","I witnessed the entire process clearly with my own two eyes.","It looked almost as though the vein were forcibly gathering up pieces of its severed flesh.","’...No way.’","Half doubtful, I placed my hand upon the mithril vein.","There was something I needed to test.","The first rule of auctions and private trades: living creatures could not be traded.","The second rule: to trade an object, every side of that object had to be visible.","There was no need to concern myself with the rules after that. They weren’t particularly important.","The reason I specifically recalled the first and second rules was simple.","’You have to pass the first rule before the second rule is applied.’","That was how the system’s algorithm worked.","If something failed to pass the first rule, trading it was impossible from the outset.","If it weren’t, I wouldn’t still be trapped here. The first rule couldn’t be circumvented through tricks.","In other words—","[Living creatures cannot be traded.]","This proved that the mithril vein was alive like a living creature.","In this insane forest, even the minerals were alive and breathing."]},{"title":"Chapter 116","paragraphs":["Mining (3)","What was life?","It was a remarkably profound question.","A being promised death at the very moment it was granted life.","A being that raced toward death and therefore struggled to leave behind biological or spiritual descendants of its own.","A subject worthy of deep philosophical and scientific study, as well as a creation of God.","Life itself was the very embodiment of mystery.","That raised another question: What standards distinguished living things from nonliving things?","Scholars had established various criteria for defining life, but those criteria were ultimately subjective.","Distinguishing life in a completely objective sense was practically impossible.","The Gallery system was probably no different. Its creator’s subjective views must have been reflected in it.","The problem was that I had been able to trade other objects without difficulty until now.","Before my eyes lay mithril, displaying its brilliant splendor.","For some unknown reason, the Gallery had classified this mithril as a living creature.","I stared at the mithril and sank into thought.","A single question filled my mind.","’Why?’","Minerals detached from the vein could be traded.","However, the entire vein couldn’t be traded because it had been classified as a living creature.","’Does it have a core inside it like the guardian?’","If so, this was dangerous.","It meant the mithril vein might become active like the guardian.","I couldn’t be certain because it was buried underground, but I couldn’t help feeling uneasy.","The Gallery had classified it as a living creature, so I needed to exercise caution.","’Considering it stayed still even after I hit it so many times...’","The guardian had reacted the moment I used mana.","This thing, however, hadn’t responded even when I struck it with mana-infused attacks.","What kind of ecology did this vein possess?","It was difficult to understand.","In the end, all I knew was that the vein was alive.","What if it didn’t assume a definite form like the guardian and instead remained amorphous like a slime from some game?","What if one day, while I was sleeping, it suddenly sprouted upward in the shape of spikes?","What would happen then?","I would suffer a critical injury at the very least.","The human body was fragile.","The moment one of those spikes pierced my head, I would bid farewell to this world.","As long as such a danger existed, I couldn’t ignore a living mineral vein beneath my home.","’Should I ask the dwarf first?’","A living mineral vein.","The dwarf was the only person I could ask about something like this.","If even he didn’t know, I planned to post a question in the Gallery.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. Emergency. Emergency. Let me ask you something.]","[Passing Dwarf: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Are there such things as living... mineral veins?]","[Passing Dwarf: What kind of nonsense is that? What score did you get in language class at school?]","[Wild Grylls: My parents died, so I focused more on working than school. I barely met the attendance requirements.]","[Passing Dwarf: Ah, fuck. If you say it like that, you make me sound like an asshole;;]","[Wild Grylls: Then be serious and answer me.]","[Passing Dwarf: What do you mean, a mineral is alive? Are you talking about the mithril?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. After hearing what you said, I observed it for a while. The fragments lying nearby wriggled around before reattaching themselves to the vein. I tried trading the vein just in case, but all I got was a notification saying living creatures couldn’t be traded.]","[Passing Dwarf: I don’t know. Just ask the Gallery. I can tell you aren’t talking nonsense, but I honestly have no idea, lol.]","Even the dwarf, an expert, gave up trying to understand it.","In the end, I decided to ask the Gallery.","Surely someone would know.","Just in case, I recorded the entire process. I also broke off a few fragments.","This was possible because I could take photographs and videos of the Gallery window itself.","Title: Can Minerals Be Alive?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the mithril vein)","(Video showing the notification that appeared when I tried trading the mithril)","(Video of the fragments wriggling toward the vein and reattaching themselves)","It’s exactly as shown in the videos. Passing Dwarf identified it as mithril.","But he said mithril isn’t supposed to be alive.","Has anyone ever seen anything like this?","What the hell is it, and why is this happening?","└ Heavenly Demon: It crawls like an earthworm. It appears to be struggling to survive.","└ SwordMaster: Doesn’t it look like it’s trying to increase the size of its body?","└ What the fuck am I looking at?","└ I never thought I’d live to see mithril fragments crawling like earthworms;;","└ Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, does this make any sense?","└ Could there be some kind of core embedded inside it?","└ Forget that. Grylls, give me some mithril. I’ll put it to good use.","└ Come to think of it, that really was mithril, lol.","└ Everyone was so shocked that they focused on the video instead of the mithril, lol.","└ This bastard assessed the situation quickly, lol.","└ Allfather: The Gallery classified it as a living creature... That is effectively the same as saying the mineral possesses an ego.","└ Wild Grylls: An ego?","└ Allfather: Yes. The Gallery appears to prohibit the trading of anything it determines possesses an ego. That is the conclusion I reached through many years of research.","└ Then are you saying plants don’t have egos? Medicinal herbs and trees can be traded just fine.","└ Allfather: Possessing an ego means being capable of thought. It means learning through thought and developing even further.","└ You sound like one of those people who claims cancer is alive. Why doesn’t cancer count?","└ Allfather: Who told you that?","└ I read it in an old book.","└ Allfather: It seems you’re the one without an ego. Judging by how you refuse to think for yourself and entrust your sense of self to others, that is. Would you care to entrust that head of yours to me through a trade? As it happens, I have a friend for it.","└ Allfather: In any case, it isn’t completely unheard of for an inanimate object to develop an ego. Have you ever heard of an ego weapon? It is a weapon that possesses a consciousness of its own.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Ah! I know about those too! The Hero’s Holy Sword is also a weapon with an ego!","└ Allfather: An excellent example. However, even I have never seen an unprocessed mineral possess an ego... You should exercise caution. It may give birth to a guardian.","└ A mithril guardian? That’s fucking insane, lol.","└ Would he even be able to defeat it?","└ Mithril alone is already difficult enough. If a guardian emerges, Grylls will probably just die.","└ That’s genuinely horrifying;;","└ Wild Grylls: Then there must be a specific part responsible for the mithril’s ego, right?","└ Allfather: That is most likely the case.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: In the Holy Sword’s case, it’s the jewel embedded in the center of its hilt!","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t ask you.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Okay...!","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry. I’m anxious, so I spoke too harshly.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: It’s all right! I’ve been called much worse! Someone even called me a fucking bitch before!","└ Wild Grylls: ;;","└ Wild Grylls: Anyway, you’re saying this mineral vein possesses an ego, correct? An ego capable of thinking and making decisions for itself.","I suddenly felt sorry for the head moderator, but I decided to move on.","Such were the hardships of being a moderator.","I stared at the mithril vein, which was presumed to possess an ego.","How was I supposed to make this thing move?","I was afraid that an accident might occur if I continued mining.","\"Ahem. Hello, my friend?\"","\"...?\"","\"If you can hear me, could you move your body out of the way?\"","So I made the suggestion as politely as possible.","It might have made me look like an idiot, but I was completely serious.","Of course, the mineral vein didn’t move.","It didn’t have ears, after all. Not every living creature had them.","Would a jellyfish listen if you spoke to it in a human language?","Absolutely not.","\"Haa... This won’t do.\"","I couldn’t leave it like this.","I made a decision for the greater good.","Even if I had to tear apart the entire rear section of the cave, I would mine out all the mithril.","I would rather defuse the bomb myself than sleep with it beneath me.","’If neither of us had ever become aware of the other, it probably would’ve remained still.’","Ignorance was bliss.","It felt as though I had unnecessarily awakened something that had been sleeping.","Still, what else could I do?","It had already happened.","As a precaution, I placed Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and began mining.","Crack! Thud!","Instead of mining the mithril directly, I carefully chipped away at the rock surrounding it.","I needed to see just how large this mithril deposit was.","Fortunately, it seemed to exist only inside the cave.","’Games really are completely different from reality.’","In a certain blocky world, you could dig all the way down to lava with nothing more than an iron pickaxe.","It seemed only superhumans could become protagonists.","I was merely an ordinary human dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons by some god’s prank.","I felt like sighing, but mining took priority.","Crack! Thud!","How much time had passed?","Once I had dug down to a depth roughly equal to my height, the vein’s overall shape gradually began to emerge.","\"Oh, for fuck’s sake. Seriously?\"","I took it back.","What I had seen was merely the tip of the iceberg.","No matter how much I dug, I couldn’t find the end.","Just how far did this vein extend?","It was impossible to estimate.","’This is driving me insane.’","At this rate, I would have to tear apart not only the rear section but the entire cave.","Still, I needed to sleep inside the cave.","More than anything, I wanted to rest.","With a troubled heart, I stared at the glittering mithril vein.","’Was it Gyeongju? I heard people find artifacts just by digging in their yards there.’","Meanwhile, finding mithril had given me nothing but a headache.","Worse still, this was a mineral that might eventually produce a guardian.","An orichalcum guardian was horrifying enough, but a mithril guardian?","’I don’t have a choice. I’ll have to mine all of it.’","I changed my plan.","I would mine the mithril and locate the source of its life.","I didn’t know whether it would truly become a guardian, but I couldn’t ignore the worst-case scenario.","Clang! Clank! Clank!","And so I continued mining diligently.","My hands gradually began to go numb, but I endured it.","If I failed to eliminate this thing, my life might be in danger.","It was mining with my life on the line.","Fortunately, I had the pickaxe the dwarf had given me.","I stored the detached mithril fragments and chunks inside my spatial bag.","\"Huff... Haa...\"","After swinging the pickaxe for an hour, I was the first to give out.","Meanwhile, the mithril vein continued displaying its unyielding form.","Strangely, it seemed to grow harder the more I struck it.","More precisely, it became tougher the deeper I dug.","’I’ll have to make sure the dwarf crafts that mithril pickaxe for me.’","Either that, or I needed to complete my Aura Blade.","Unfortunately, I wasn’t making any progress with it.","Still, I had to do as much as I possibly could.","Didn’t they say that small gains eventually accumulated into a mountain?","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, I’ll give you a lump of mithril, so please have a weapon made from it. Consider it repayment for the sword you gave me.]","[Heavenly Demon: There is no need for this. Your kindness may well be your greatest weakness.]","[Wild Grylls: The sword you gave me has saved my life several times. Without it, I would’ve died long ago. So please accept this.]","[Heavenly Demon: Refusing would also be discourteous. I shall accept it with gratitude.]","I used my break to give the Heavenly Demon a lump of mithril.","[Wild Grylls: Mithril isn’t some trivial trinket, so you’ll accept it, right?]","[PraiseTheSun: Not even the king of a nation could call mithril a trivial trinket;;]","[Wild Grylls: Then please accept it. It’s repayment for all the shields you’ve given me.]","[PraiseTheSun: You already gave me a fully mature Mandrake. I thought that was more than enough.]","[Wild Grylls: So you don’t want it?]","[PraiseTheSun: No one dislikes free gifts. Thanks. I’ll use it to make an accessory.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","I also gave a lump of mithril to PraiseTheSun, who had gifted me the shields.","Afterward, I resumed mining.","It was an endless battle.","However, even by evening, I had failed to extract all of it.","’I’ll have no choice but to sleep as far away from it as possible.’","My hands were numb after swinging a pickaxe all day.","I massaged my tingling palms and accessed the Gallery.","There were approximately thirty minutes left until dinner, so I planned to browse the Gallery until then.","’The dwarf sent me a message.’","I had given the dwarf more mithril whenever I extracted some.","I had also repeatedly insisted that he make me a pure-mithril pickaxe.","Since he had messaged me, I assumed he had either completed it or was currently crafting it.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey. We’re fucked.]","However, the message I received was nothing like what I had expected.","It was short and concise, yet perfectly summarized the situation he was facing.","Instead of feeling anxious, I was confused and immediately replied.","[Wild Grylls: What happened?]","[Passing Dwarf: The mithril won’t melt.]","[Wild Grylls: ? What are you talking about?]","[Passing Dwarf: No matter what I do, it won’t melt, so I can’t pour it into a mold. I can’t even break it.]","The dwarf then continued.","[Passing Dwarf: I examined it and found that it contains an excessive amount of mana. I’d need a specially constructed furnace to melt it. So I think I’ll have to send it back.]","[Wild Grylls: You aren’t saying I’ll have to melt it and make the equipment myself, are you?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. That’s exactly what I’m saying.]","[Wild Grylls: F—]","[Passing Dwarf: Still, anything made from it will be insanely powerful, lol.]","In other words, my workload had increased yet again."]},{"title":"Chapter 117","paragraphs":["Mining (4)","One obstacle after another. That was the perfect way to describe how I felt right now.","After all the trouble I had gone through to mine the mithril, even the dwarf told me he couldn’t melt it.","The moment I heard that, a crushing sense of futility washed over me, but I barely managed to pull myself together.","I had no idea what was so special about this damned mithril, but I needed an explanation.","[Wild Grylls: Explain it in detail. Is it really just because it contains so much mana?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. It’s difficult to melt, and even if you do melt it, an ordinary furnace can’t withstand it.]","[Wild Grylls: Explain why. I don’t think I’ll be convinced otherwise. It’s not that I don’t trust you. It’s just the situation.]","[Passing Dwarf: I get what you mean. Most ordinary metals...]","I carefully read the dwarf’s explanation.","Most metals were buried underground, so they naturally absorbed mana from the earth.","Ordinary soil didn’t contain much mana, so there was no issue with putting metals mined from it into a furnace.","However, the deeper one dug—or in places like the Forest of Four Seasons, where the earth contained an abnormally high amount of mana—the situation was different.","Minerals mined from such places generally contained highly concentrated mana, so a special furnace was required.","He explained that using an ordinary furnace instead of a special one could cause an explosion.","[Passing Dwarf: It’s basically just a furnace that consumes an absurd amount of mana.]","[Wild Grylls: Can’t an individual own one?]","[Passing Dwarf: The furnace is bigger than an entire mansion, you human ;; It’s not something we use often in the first place, so the state manages it directly.]","[Wild Grylls: What kind of ridiculous inefficiency is that?]","[Passing Dwarf: Do you think our dwarven technology is a joke? Do you have any idea how cutting-edge that thing is?]","[Wild Grylls: A cutting-edge joke.]","[Passing Dwarf: Anything becomes a bomb if you forcibly compress it into a confined space and then let it burst. Naturally, the mithril gets blown away too.]","[Wild Grylls: What the hell is the special furnace made of, then?]","So there was nothing I could do about it. All I could do was sigh.","Building an ordinary furnace would already be enough to drive me insane, but now I needed a special furnace?","He had even said it was much bigger than an entire mansion, so constructing one was completely out of the question.","At this rate, the mithril I had worked so hard to mine would become a useless burden.","I needed to find some way to use it, but nothing came to mind.","[Passing Dwarf: Why don’t you try making something yourself? Since you’re in the Forest of Four Seasons, it should be no different from ordinary metal there.]","[Wild Grylls: Didn’t you say it could only be melted in a special furnace?]","[Passing Dwarf: That place is already overflowing with mana. So just give it a try.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know how to build a furnace.]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s a solid chunk of mithril, so just heat it in a forge and hammer it into shape. If you want to use a mold, build a furnace, melt the mithril, and pour it in.]","[Wild Grylls: Isn’t that contradictory? You just said I needed a special furnace.]","[Passing Dwarf: Is your brain actually an anvil? It explodes because the mana escapes when the material changes state. I was going to cast it because I wanted to finish quickly, but I noticed in time. If I’d realized any later or started hammering it, I’d be in the hospital right now.]","[Wild Grylls: Aha. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: This is seriously upsetting. I only tried to finish it quickly because I felt bad for you, yet you don’t appreciate my sincerity at all...]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry ;; Is there anything you want?]","[Passing Dwarf: Just give me one crab shell, hehe.]","[Wild Grylls: Damn it ;; Fine.]","He had taught me something valuable, so I was perfectly willing to give him one crab.","I ended my conversation with the dwarf and contacted the registered users to whom I had given mithril.","It was necessary, if only to prevent an unexpected accident.","[Heavenly Demon: Dost thou mean true silver? This lady still possesses it.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s a relief. Apparently, it might explode if you try to make equipment with it. Could you return it to me?]","[Heavenly Demon: Is it because true silver contains an immense amount of qi?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? How did you know?]","[Heavenly Demon: It was simple. This lady wished to absorb it, but feared it might lose its essence, so I chose to wait.]","[Wild Grylls: If you return it, I’ll forge a sword for you myself.]","[Heavenly Demon: May this lady look forward to it?]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm... No? It might take a long time.]","[Heavenly Demon: I appreciate thy honesty. This lady shall wait without expecting too much. It matters not what weapon this lady uses.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Allfather: So you can’t even work it, let alone hammer it?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll ask.]","[Wild Grylls: He says engraving and cutting are fine.]","[Allfather: Then I’ll keep mine. I’m going to use it as a ring.]","[Wild Grylls: Be careful anyway.]","I received the mithril I had given to the Heavenly Demon.","Allfather decided to keep his.","When I asked the dwarf, he explained that there was only a risk of explosion when the material changed states.","There was no problem with carving it down while keeping it in the same state.","’Come to think of it, if that weren’t the case, carrying it around would be no different from carrying a bomb.’","Even if heat caused it to change shape, there was no need to worry. Why?","Because if it was hot enough to deform metal, a person would have died long before that became an issue.","After gathering all sorts of information, I closed the gallery.","’Thankfully, I don’t have to do everything myself.’","According to the dwarf, he could sharpen the blade for me.","He said all I needed to do was flatten the mithril into shape.","If that proved too difficult, I could obtain a mold and simply pour molten mithril into it.","’The downside is that I’d have to build a furnace.’","Besides, an ordinary mold might not withstand the temperature of molten metal.","In the worst case, even the furnace I had worked so hard to build could melt.","Each option had clear advantages and disadvantages, so I couldn’t help agonizing over the decision.","’Let’s eat first.’","Whatever happened, food was important. I could continue worrying about the mithril tomorrow.","When I went up to the river, I found two fish caught in the trap. Satisfactory.","I was about to clean them as usual when a thought occurred to me, and I stopped.","’Should I try cutting one with mithril?’","There were several mithril fragments that had broken off while I was mining. Some of them had sharp edges.","Just how sharp was mithril?","With that expectation in mind, I sliced open the fish’s belly.","Sliiice.","It felt similar to using a dagger.","That was all.","Although the edge hadn’t been sharpened, I couldn’t help feeling slightly disappointed.","’Would it be different if I used aura?’","So I channeled aura into it, and to my surprise...","Even though I used only a small amount of mana, the aura blazed like fire.","It was possible that I had simply grown stronger, so I channeled aura into my dagger as well, but there was a clear difference.","To make sure, I tried using aura with several other tools, but the result was the same.","Compared to the mithril, I had to pour far more mana into them before the aura displayed its full power.","’So that’s what it was.’","Its mana efficiency was incredible.","That alone explained everything.","This seemed to be what the dwarf had meant when he said its performance would be exceptional.","I could be certain precisely because it was mithril, not orichalcum.","’This will be a huge help in prolonged battles.’","Aside from my fight against the Orichalcum Guardian, I had never run out of mana before.","However, mana—or rather, aura itself—was an extremely inefficient technique to begin with.","It might be different if it took a defined shape like an Aura Blade, but mine burned like flames. Anyone could see how inefficient that was.","Perhaps this mithril could be even more efficient than the Heavenly Demon’s sword. It might even accelerate my training.","’So it isn’t completely useless.’","For someone like me, whose survival was paramount, efficiency was an important consideration.","This mithril drastically improved that efficiency, making it practically indispensable.","I would have to use it to make various tools.","Its performance was comparable to steel, yet it was much lighter. It was perfect.","’Mining it is still a problem, though.’","There was nothing I could do about that. I would simply have to work my aaaass off.","I finished dinner and cleaned everything up before going to bed.","I planned to leave the section I had dug out as it was and continue mining tomorrow.","’As for the elixir... I’ll keep it above my head.’","A thief might sneak in during the night and steal something.","Namu-Ppareumbo would probably wake up and stop them, but it was better to be prepared.","Once I had finished setting everything up, I logged into the gallery.","I didn’t have anything in particular to say. I was simply curious whether anything had happened.","’Tomorrow will mark exactly half a month.’","A lot had happened over the past fifteen days. Today, the leader ape had beaten the living daylights out of me.","Tomorrow, I planned to retrieve the orichalcum from the Orichalcum Cave and receive the crystal orb that would serve as a security camera.","While I was at it, I would also work on building a furnace. I could ask the dwarf about its structure.","’I have so much to do.’","Every time I finished one task, two more appeared. Whenever I finished those two, five more took their place.","Mithril, in particular, could only be processed within the Forest of Four Seasons.","With complicated feelings, I browsed through the gallery. I needed something to help me unwind.","[Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.]","While browsing the gallery, a particular title caught my eye.","At first, I thought it was an ordinary clickbait post, but then I realized it had been posted by a registered user.","’Who is that?’","I’ll Become a Duke. The username seemed vaguely familiar.","Curious, I opened the post.","Title: Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.","I’ll Become a Duke","(A photograph of a finely crafted pair of leather shoes)","(A photograph of the leather shoes remaining undamaged after water was poured over them)","(A photograph showing that the shoes could not easily be cut with a knife)","They were photographs of shoes.","Come to think of it, I had completely forgotten.","I had promised to give a mature Mandrake to anyone who provided me with a good pair of shoes.","The moment I made that offer, several people uploaded photographs of shoes, but I disliked most of them.","One of them had even tried to scam me, so I gave him a casual middle finger and left it at that.","Furthermore, the competition had died down after the dwarf—or rather, the dwarf’s friend—gave me a pair of shoes.","Everyone said that no matter how hard they tried, their efforts would be meaningless before the craftsmanship of a dwarven artisan.","I also liked the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend, so I had stopped paying attention to the matter.","’But this person...’","This registered user was different. Despite all the time that had passed, he had continued working on them.","Of course, if all he had to show for his efforts was a poor result, I would have ignored him.","└ There isn’t even a single scream, so they really must be sturdy, hahahaha.","└ Maybe he’s gritting his teeth and enduring it in silence, hahaha.","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A photograph revealing his masked face) I knew you would say that, so I filmed this too. I recorded it with a crystal orb.","└ Damn, look at how thorough he is, hahahaha.","└ What’s with the mask? It looks like something you’d wear to a ball. Is he a noble?","└ Who’s the person hitting him with the sledgehammer?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: My son.","└ Hahahahahahahahaha!","└ What a devoted son, damn, hahahahaha!","└ Even if he’s your son, he’s hitting you way too hard, hahahaha!","(A video of someone repeatedly striking the shoe wearer’s foot with a sledgehammer)","└ S-Sir ;; Y-You can stop now ;;","└ How many times is he going to hit him? Damn, hahahaha!","└ At this rate, his foot is going to be completely crushed ;;","If only that video hadn’t been there.","No matter how durable the shoes were, who would strike them with a sledgehammer while someone was still wearing them?","Then again, that made him even more trustworthy. Hadn’t he risked his own body to prove the quality of his product?","After staring at it in discomfort for a moment, I hurriedly left a comment before he injured himself any further.","There were no issues with the shoes’ performance, so I could safely proceed with the trade.","└ Wild Grylls: S-Sir, you don’t have to do that. You aren’t injured, are you?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A video of him removing his foot from the shoe after the sledgehammer test) Correct.","└ Wow. He’s thorough as hell. Now that’s proper product verification ;;","└ Who made those? I want a pair.","└ I’ll buy them!","└ Buy me a pair too!","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. You win. I think those are better than the pair my friend made ;;","└ The dwarf has declared defeat!","└ If even a dwarf admits defeat, they must be the real deal, hahaha.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll buy them. It’s already late, though. Can we make the exchange tomorrow?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: That is possible.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a private message.","I sent him a message because it seemed we needed to discuss the matter privately.","Despite his stiff way of speaking, he was passionate. I found myself liking him.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, I’ll Become a Duke. I saw the shoes. You need a mature Mandrake, correct?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: You don’t need anything else?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: I do not. I urgently need a mature Mandrake.]","He urgently needed a mature Mandrake. I could sense the desperation in his words.","Someone close to him was probably suffering from an illness.","Otherwise, he would have no reason to reject everything else and insist solely on the mature Mandrake.","’He seems trustworthy.’","Both the video and his messages suggested that he was someone I could trust.","After telling him I would send the mature Mandrake tomorrow, I closed the gallery window.","Tomorrow would be my fifteenth day—exactly half a month—and I also planned to consume the inner core.","Building the furnace and completing my trade with I’ll Become a Duke...","I had plenty to do.","’The Guardian won’t wake up while I’m asleep, will it?’","Fortunately, nothing like that happened.","\"Ah. What the hell? What is this now?\"","Except that the entire section I had worked so hard to mine had completely regenerated.","I didn’t want an unlimited supply, but it looked like I was going to be forced to enjoy one.","’Is it a planarian or something?’","Planarian mithril.","I had no idea what kind of horrifying hybrid this was.","This seemed to be what the dwarf meant when he said that its performance, at least, would be excellent.","I could be sure of that because it was mithril, not orichalcum.","’This will be a great help in prolonged battles.’","Aside from my battle against the Orichalcum Guardian, I had never run out of mana before.","However, mana—or rather, aura—was an extremely inefficient technique to begin with.","It might be different if it took on a defined shape like an Aura Blade, but mine burned like flames. Anyone could tell at a glance how inefficient it was.","It might even be more efficient than the Heavenly Demon’s sword. It could also help accelerate my training.","’So it isn’t completely useless.’","For someone like me, whose survival was paramount, efficiency was an important consideration.","This mithril drastically increased that efficiency, making it practically indispensable.","I would have to use it to make various tools.","It performed about as well as steel while being much lighter, making it perfect for the job.","’Mining it is still a problem, though.’","There was nothing I could do about that. I would just have to work haaaarder.","I finished dinner, then cleaned everything up before going to bed.","I planned to leave the rear section of the hole as it was and continue digging tomorrow.","’As for the elixir... I’ll keep it above my head.’","A thief might sneak in during the night and steal something.","Namu-Ppareumbo would probably wake up and stop them, but it was better to be prepared just in case.","Once I had finished setting everything up, I logged into the gallery.","I didn’t have anything in particular to say. I was simply curious whether anything had happened.","’Tomorrow will mark exactly half a month.’","A lot had happened over the past fifteen days. Today, the leader ape had beaten the living daylights out of me.","Tomorrow, I planned to retrieve the orichalcum from the Orichalcum Cave and receive the crystal orb that would serve as a security camera.","While I was at it, I should also work on building a furnace. I could ask the dwarf about its structure.","’I have so much to do.’","Whenever I finished one task, two more appeared. Whenever I finished those two, another five appeared.","Mithril, in particular, could only be processed within the Forest of Four Seasons.","With mixed feelings, I browsed through the gallery. I needed something to help me unwind.","[Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.]","As I browsed the gallery, one particular title caught my eye.","At first, I thought it was ordinary clickbait, but then I realized it had been posted by a registered user.","’Who is that?’","I’ll Become a Duke. The username seemed vaguely familiar.","Curious, I opened the post.","Title: Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.","I’ll Become a Duke","(A photograph of a finely crafted pair of leather shoes)","(A photograph of the leather shoes remaining undamaged after water was poured over them)","(A photograph showing that the shoes could not easily be cut with a knife)","They were photographs of shoes.","Come to think of it, I had completely forgotten.","I had promised to give a mature Mandrake to anyone who gave me a good pair of shoes.","As soon as I made that offer, several people uploaded photographs of shoes, but I disliked most of them.","One of them had even tried to scam me, so I gave him a casual middle finger and left it at that.","Furthermore, the competition had died down after the dwarf—or rather, the dwarf’s friend—gave me a pair of shoes.","Everyone said that no matter how hard they tried, all their efforts would be meaningless before a dwarven artisan.","I also liked the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend, so I had stopped paying attention to the matter.","’But this person...’","This registered user was different. Despite how much time had passed, he had continued working on them.","Of course, if he had put in all that effort only to produce a disappointing result, I would have ignored him.","└ There wasn’t even a single scream. Those shoes must be seriously sturdy, hahaha.","└ Maybe he’s just gritting his teeth and enduring it in silence, hahaha.","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A photograph revealing his masked face) I knew you would say that, so I filmed this as well. I recorded it with a crystal orb.","└ Damn, look at how thorough he is, hahahaha.","└ What’s with the mask? It looks like something you’d wear to a ball. Is he a noble?","└ Who’s the person hitting him with the sledgehammer?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: My son.","└ Hahahahahahahahaha!","└ What a devoted son, damn, hahahahaha!","└ Even if he’s your son, he’s hitting you way too hard, hahahaha!","(A video of someone repeatedly striking the shoe wearer’s foot with a sledgehammer)","└ S-Sir ;; Y-You can stop now ;;","└ How many times is he going to hit him? Damn, hahahaha!","└ At this rate, his foot is going to be completely crushed ;;","If only it hadn’t been for that video.","No matter how durable the shoes were, who would strike them with a sledgehammer while someone was still wearing them?","Then again, that made him even more trustworthy. Hadn’t he put his own body on the line to prove the quality of his product?","After staring at it uneasily for a moment, I hurriedly left a comment before he injured himself any further.","There were no issues with the shoes’ performance, so I could safely proceed with the trade.","└ Wild Grylls: S-Sir, you don’t have to do that. You aren’t injured, are you?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A video of him taking his foot out of the shoe after the sledgehammer test) Correct.","└ Wow. He’s thorough as hell. Now that’s proper product verification ;;","└ Who made those? I want a pair.","└ I’ll buy them!","└ Buy me a pair too!","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. You win. I think those are better than the pair my friend made ;;","└ The dwarf has declared defeat!","└ If even a dwarf admits defeat, they must be the real deal, hahaha.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll buy them. It’s already late, though. Can we make the exchange tomorrow?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: That is possible.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a private message.","I sent him a message because it seemed we needed to discuss the matter privately.","Despite his stiff manner of speaking, he was clearly a passionate person, which made me like him.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, I’ll Become a Duke. I saw the shoes. You need a mature Mandrake, correct?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: You don’t need anything else?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: I do not. I urgently need a mature Mandrake.]","He urgently needed a mature Mandrake. I could sense the desperation in his words.","Someone close to him was probably suffering from an illness.","Otherwise, he would have no reason to reject everything else and insist solely on the mature Mandrake.","’He seems trustworthy.’","Both the video and his messages suggested that he was someone I could trust.","After telling him I would send the mature Mandrake tomorrow, I closed the gallery window.","Tomorrow would be my fifteenth day—exactly half a month—and I also planned to consume the inner core.","Building the furnace and completing my trade with I’ll Become a Duke...","I had plenty to do.","’The Guardian won’t wake up while I’m asleep, will it?’","Fortunately, nothing like that happened.","\"Ah. What the hell? What is this now?\"","Except that the entire section I had worked so hard to mine had completely regenerated.","I didn’t want an unlimited supply, but it looked like I was going to be forced to enjoy one.","’Is it a planarian or something?’","Planarian mithril.","I had no idea what kind of horrifying hybrid this was."]},{"title":"Chapter 118","paragraphs":["Alloy (1)","By now, I was tired of even saying, \"I’ve seen everything.\"","Everything in the Forest of Four Seasons was one enormous, unsolvable mystery.","It would be best to accept things quickly and move on. Hadn’t I recently encountered a talking gorilla?","I should probably just... go with the flow. While keeping meticulous records, of course.","’Why is everything here useless to me?’","What I needed were survival supplies, not resources like this.","Of course, I could use those resources to craft armor and various other tools.","However, that would take far too long, and I didn’t even have a furnace.","They were the very definition of a white elephant. I wasn’t even particularly good at knapping stone tools like a primitive man from the Paleolithic era.","’It’s not like I can sell this, either.’","I sighed. It seemed impossible to extract this mithril through ordinary mining.","Unless I carved out the entire floor around it, I had no choice but to leave it alone.","Still, if I looked at it positively, I had an unlimited supply of resources.","If I could build a furnace and acquire the necessary skills as a blacksmith, I couldn’t ask for anything more.","’The problem is that it’ll take years at the very least.’","I sighed again before turning around. Whatever the case, I still had work to do.","My daily routine began in the morning. By now, it had become familiar.","I went up to the river, caught fish, and ate my fill.","For some reason, only one fish had been caught today, which was slightly disappointing.","’Good thing I’ve stored some from the previous days.’","I still had plenty for now. However, it would become a problem if I continued catching only one fish a day.","After having breakfast with my animal companions, I got to work.","My first task was to send the mature Mandrake to I’ll Become a Duke.","After that, I planned to visit the Orichalcum Cave and retrieve some orichalcum.","I had originally intended to use the orichalcum to make a door, but that plan had been abandoned, so I no longer needed the mineral.","Still, I figured there was no harm in having a few pieces, so I planned to keep them in reserve.","’Let’s build the furnace after lunch.’","It looked like the task would require both brains and strength, so it would be better to take my time.","According to the dwarf, molten metal was nearly as hot as lava.","He also mentioned that mithril had a higher melting point, so it would be even hotter.","’I also need charcoal, right?’","Charcoal was essential for producing higher temperatures.","Since I needed enough heat to melt metal, I would require much greater firepower.","That alone made my prospects look bleak, but there was at least one fortunate aspect.","The furnace didn’t need to be very large. Since all it had to do was melt the ore, a small one would suffice.","Even so, I couldn’t afford to relax. I would be handling fire, the very definition of a double-edged sword.","’I’m glad I’ve been steadily collecting charcoal.’","Until now, I had only used it for laundry and as a deodorizer. I never imagined I would use it in a furnace.","Charcoal truly was divine and all-purpose. I would have to work on producing more of it in the future.","After completing my preparations, I set out to obtain the mature Mandrake and the orichalcum.","As always, I carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and brought Wonmo, my adorable bodyguard, along with me.","Wham! Thud! Smack!","\"Gueek! Gueeek! Gweeeek!\"","First came the mature Mandrake.","By now, I was familiar with the capture method.","Though calling it a \"capture method\" was generous when all I did was beat it senseless. Not that it mattered.","After capturing the mature Mandrake, I headed toward the Orichalcum Cave.","Fortunately, I didn’t encounter any dangerous animals along the way.","It was partly because I was following a familiar route and partly because I remained thoroughly vigilant.","’Orichalcum acquired. But does this not need to be refined either?’","That thought occurred to me as I picked up several chunks of orichalcum scattered across the ground.","Perhaps it didn’t need to be processed separately, considering Princess Cheonggu and King Leor had used theirs as soon as they received it.","Then again, that might be a unique characteristic of orichalcum. I would have to ask the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls has registered an item for trade.]","[Wild Grylls: Here it is. I sincerely hope everything works out for you.]","[I’ll Become a Duke: Thank you very much! May the Goddess’s blessing be with you!]","After returning to the cave, I exchanged items with I’ll Become a Duke.","Judging by his mention of the Goddess’s blessing, perhaps he was from the Holy Kingdom.","’Come to think of it, the mature Mandrake can be traded without any problems.’","Had the system determined that mature Mandrakes lacked self-awareness?","They didn’t merely let out terrifying battle cries; they even operated as a colony.","It was truly strange, but I decided to accept it since the outcome benefited me. Thinking too deeply about it would only make my head hurt.","’These are nice. Sturdy too.’","Just as the video had shown, the shoes I received from I’ll Become a Duke prioritized durability.","They were so tough that they were even better than the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend.","However, that durability came at the expense of comfort and convenience.","’Still, these are perfect for me.’","I could wear the dwarf’s shoes when revisiting places I had already explored and I’ll Become a Duke’s shoes when exploring new areas.","That seemed like the best way to categorize them. Inside the cave, I could simply wear sneakers.","’I should get just one more pair.’","Since the two pairs served different purposes, I needed a spare as well.","With that in mind, I immediately posted in the gallery. People might assume the offer had already ended.","Title: Looking for One More Pair of Shoes","Wild Grylls","I safely received the shoes provided by Passing Dwarf and I’ll Become a Duke.","However, since I’ll likely use them for different purposes, I think I need one more pair as a backup.","As before, I’ll give a mature Mandrake to whoever provides a suitable spare pair.","└ Heavenly Demon: When dost thou intend to give this lady her sword?","└ Wild Grylls: I-I’ll give it to you soon!","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady was merely jesting. There is no need to hurry, so take thy time.","└ SwordMaster: You’re giving her a sword?","└ Heavenly Demon: He says he shall personally craft a sword of true silver for this lady.","└ SwordMaster: Damn it. I’m a little jealous of that. Even I’ve never used a sword made of mithril ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmph. Perhaps thou shouldst have been more generous.","└ SwordMaster: I gave him an elixir too, you know ;;","└ Wild Grylls: The Heavenly Demon gave me her own sword, so I’m giving her this one in return. Would you like one too, SwordMaster?","└ Heavenly Demon: That fool. So this was his intention all along.","└ SwordMaster: Honestly, I’m tempted, but I’m fine. Unlike a certain someone, I’m strong enough even with a cheap sword.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady possesses a mace.","└ SwordMaster: You evil bitch.","└ Is Grylls making it himself? I thought he asked the dwarf to do it.","└ Passing Dwarf: That was the plan, but the mana concentration inside the mithril was too high, so I returned it. It’ll explode the moment it melts.","└ Is orichalcum safe?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Orichalcum is safe because of its mana-absorbing properties. But that applies exclusively to orichalcum.","└ So Grylls was handing out bombs?","└ Looks like he was planning to assassinate them.","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t know either ;; That’s why I have to make it myself.","└ Princess Cheonggu: I’m making good use of the orichalcum you gave me. The security recording orb I mentioned yesterday is ready, so just let me know whenever you want it.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. How do I view the recorded footage?]","[Princess Cheonggu: Tap it twice again to close its eye, then tap it three times. To watch the recording, press and hold it. One thing to keep in mind is that the recording will be deleted automatically once you watch it, so be careful!]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll be careful. And thank you.]","[Princess Cheonggu: If you’re grateful, what should you say?]","[Wild Grylls: I hope Chae-U wins next season!]","[Princess Cheonggu: Hehe. Very good.]","The moment I saw Princess Cheonggu’s comment, I sent her a private message.","I planned to give her orichalcum in return. The more of it she had, the better.","[Princess Cheonggu: If you tap the orb twice, it’ll open like an eye. Just think of it as watching whatever direction the eye is facing.]","I examined the security orb I had received from Princess Cheonggu.","It was mostly blackish-purple and about the size of my face.","’Am I supposed to hang it up like a block of fermented soybean paste?’","Installing it would be another chore. Still, I planned to remain inside the cave all day, so I had no immediate need for it.","After looking it over from various angles, I tapped the security orb twice.","Flash!","\"Whoa.\"","Just as Princess Cheonggu had explained, it opened like an eye. It resembled the eye of a reptile.","It looked terrifying. It practically radiated the message, I’m watching you.","Tap, tap, tap—","When I tapped it three times, the eye quietly closed. I then pressed and held it with my finger.","With a flash, a holographic screen appeared.","The hologram displayed my face as seen from above.","\"Wow.\"","No matter how I looked at it, my skin had improved. I couldn’t find a single blemish.","I stared at my face in the hologram for a while before closing it.","Now that I had confirmed how the security orb worked, it was time to begin training. I couldn’t afford to skip even a single day.","’Starting today, I’ll also be consuming the inner core.’","I planned to receive the second mnemonic verse from the Heavenly Demon.","The gist of the verse was not to surrender my body to the heavens, but to read their flow.","I was worried that it would contain expressions even more difficult than those in the first verse, but that was fine.","If I didn’t understand something, I could keep struggling with it until I did. I had never expected it to be easy.","’I’ll eat the inner core after lunch, once I’ve had time to digest.’","The fish also produced effects similar to those of a spiritual medicine.","If I consumed the inner core immediately after lunch, I might overdose.","Since I needed to avoid danger whenever possible, it would be better to wait until the meal had mostly been digested.","’I also need to catch a crab for the dwarf.’","It was going to be a busy day. I couldn’t postpone anything.","In that case, I should begin working right away. Once I finished lunch, I planned to start building the furnace.","The furnace didn’t need to be large. It only had to melt the mithril into molten metal.","However, I would have to obtain the necessary materials from the dwarf.","The most important component was heat-resistant stone. It needed to withstand temperatures exceeding a thousand degrees.","’The dwarf said he’d provide that.’","I had also heard that he would give me bellows to pump air into the furnace. He was genuinely supplying me with everything.","When I asked whether he was really fine with that, he said sharpening a mithril sword would be sufficient compensation.","Whenever he acted like this, I couldn’t help thinking how dwarven he was.","Flop! Flop!","When I went up to the river, I found two fish caught in the trap. That was a relief, at least.","I put them in the oven, ate my meal, and began making preparations.","Before that, however, there was something I needed to check—the mithril at the rear of the cave.","An endlessly regenerating supply of mithril was certainly useful, but there was something I wanted to know.","’How exactly does it regenerate?’","Its regenerative ability was remarkable, like that of a planarian.","Moreover, only the section I had mined yesterday had regenerated.","I also wondered where its core was located. At the same time, I was afraid it might awaken like the Guardian.","’I can’t let my guard down.’","I had mined quite a lot of mithril yesterday.","All I had to do now was melt it and pour it into a mold.","Once I decided that all my preparations were complete, I sent the dwarf a message.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. You there?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Did you catch the crab?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll catch it after building the furnace. I also want your advice.]","[Passing Dwarf: Advice about what?]","[Wild Grylls: Mithril is an extremely rare mineral, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: Calling it rare doesn’t even begin to cover it. There are countless mines in the world, yet whenever someone finds mithril, it makes the newspapers. What do you think?]","[Wild Grylls: Is orichalcum the same?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Most of it ends up in Magic Towers, but it’s just as rare as mithril. For reference, the newspapers went wild when you discovered the Orichalcum Cave.]","So it was that significant.","Since I was stuck in here, I knew nothing about what was happening outside.","People occasionally mentioned something appearing in the newspapers, but I had never paid attention. I assumed they were just shitposting.","[Passing Dwarf: Why are you asking, anyway? Are you trying to rub it in my face?]","[Wild Grylls: No. I want an expert’s opinion.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hmm. Thou hast some discernment. What dost thou wish to ask, foolish mortal?]","[Wild Grylls: Ugh ;; Maybe I should just find another dwarf.]","[Passing Dwarf: You’ll hardly find another dwarf specializing in metallurgy who wastes his time on the gallery, hahaha.]","[Wild Grylls: Sigh. You know how I currently have both mithril and orichalcum?]","[Passing Dwarf: Are you bragging?]","[Wild Grylls: Let me finish talking. What do you think would happen if I melted them together and made a sword from the mixture?]","An alloy of one rare mineral and another.","That was what I wanted.","There was so much of both around me that I could practically trip over them, so they no longer felt particularly remarkable.","However, outsiders—especially dwarves—would react very differently.","[Passing Dwarf: An alloy? You want to combine mithril and orichalcum?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. Doesn’t that sound good?]","[Passing Dwarf: You’re talking about using caviar to make fried rice, hahahaha.]","The dwarf laughed as though the idea were utterly absurd.","But then—","[Passing Dwarf: Let’s try it immediately. Do you need anything? Tell me what you need. I’ll get all of it for you.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s a good idea?]","[Passing Dwarf: My balls are trembling with excitement right now.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s fucking disgusting ::]","In the end, he was still a dwarf."]},{"title":"Chapter 119","paragraphs":["Alloy (2)","There was one thing men could never resist.","Something that looked utterly stupid but also incredibly fun. Pure entertainment that appealed directly to their instincts.","Most of those ideas were idiotic and frequently caused accidents, but one couldn’t always choose the safest path.","And what if the likelihood of success seemed extremely high? What if there were so many opportunities that even failure could simply be laughed off?","That was how an unstoppable bulldozer who feared no failure was born.","It was fun, and its performance was practically guaranteed. An endeavor that offered both romance and practicality.","There was no resisting it.","The dwarf cared more about the romance, while I cared more about the practical benefits. We made an excellent team.","[Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you heat-resistant bricks, so use them to build it. You’ll have to coat the outside with mud yourself.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. Is there anything else? Like a container for the molten metal.]","[Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you that too. But it’s damn heavy, so be careful. Even professionals often make mistakes while pouring molten metal.]","[Wild Grylls: How should I install the bellows?]","[Passing Dwarf: Since you’re only using the furnace to melt the metals, making a hole in the side should work. Just make the opening fairly long.]","One by one, I obtained the materials and instructions needed to build a makeshift furnace from the dwarf.","The dwarf provided most of the materials, but assembling them was my responsibility.","In truth, the assembly itself was much easier than building the oven.","I wasn’t going to refine the metals separately. All I had to do was melt them.","I stacked the bricks I had received from the dwarf into a square structure, then plastered the outside with mud.","I didn’t forget to leave an opening for the bellows.","The furnace was approximately fifty centimeters wide and long, while its height rose slightly above my knees.","However, it needed to become narrower toward the top, naturally, to retain as much heat as possible.","Lastly, I had the container for holding the mithril and orichalcum, along with the tongs needed to move it.","I thought that was everything, but the dwarf had given me something else as well.","[Wild Grylls: What’s this blue powder? It isn’t some kind of drug, is it?]","[Passing Dwarf: Snort it straight up your nose. It’ll send you to heaven.]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry ;; Do I add it to the molten metal?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. No one has ever made an alloy of mithril and orichalcum before, so I gave it to you just in case. Adding that powder should help them mix properly. Impurities might rise to the surface, so skim them off carefully.]","According to the dwarf, it was made from finely ground and processed mana stones.","He explained that it was useful when producing alloys.","I had no reason to reject something that could help, so I gladly accepted it.","’I received the mold too.’","Finally, I also received the mold. It came with a lid.","It seemed that the molten metal was supposed to be poured through a hole in the exact center of the lid.","Creak—","When I carefully opened it, I found the shape of a longsword carved into the mold.","Since it was a mold used by dwarves, there should be no risk of the molten metal melting through it.","I closed the lid again and listened to the dwarf’s precautions.","If the dwarf wanted, I planned to make more of the alloy, and I would also give him the crab soon.","[Passing Dwarf: I’m emphasizing this again—always be careful around molten metal. I’m serious.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay, okay. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: If you get hurt, I won’t get to touch the mithril-orichalcum alloy.]","[Wild Grylls: You bastard, hahaha.]","[Passing Dwarf: Seriously, if you spill the molten metal, just run as far away as possible. That’s your best option.]","[Wild Grylls: Because it might splash everywhere?]","[Passing Dwarf: That too, but mainly because even I don’t know what will happen.]","He also warned that the molten metal might splatter like hot oil, so I absolutely had to wear protective equipment.","I considered wearing a helmet, but decided against it because it would only obstruct my vision.","Instead, I received a pair of goggles from the dwarf. They were a spare pair he had.","One might argue that I was receiving far too much from him, but it was fine.","I couldn’t tell whether he was being sincere or joking. The fact that he was a dwarf made it even harder to tell.","In any case, all the preparations were complete. All that remained was to put the plan into action.","’He said an eight-to-two ratio would be best, right?’","It was the ratio recommended by the dwarf. Naturally, mithril accounted for the larger portion.","Orichalcum had a strong affinity for mana, but it wasn’t as durable as mithril.","Rattle—","I poured about half the charcoal I had accumulated into the makeshift furnace.","It was such a waste that it nearly brought tears to my eyes, but I was willing to sacrifice it for the sword.","’I should build a dedicated charcoal kiln too.’","After building one thing, I immediately found myself needing another.","Moreover, charcoal could be used almost anywhere. It was an exceptionally versatile material.","I stared at the charcoal inside the furnace, decided there was enough, and moved on to the next step.","’It really is as heavy as the dwarf said.’","It was a thick, wide container capable of withstanding extreme heat.","It was already heavy when lifted normally, but since I had to use the tongs for safety, it felt twice as heavy.","Hoping the minerals inside would melt properly, I placed the container inside the furnace.","’Now I just have to light the fire—’","Whoosh!","I threw a burning branch onto the pile of charcoal.","After a while, the charcoal began glowing red, and the heat gradually intensified.","\"Ah. Wait.\"","Now that I thought about it, I should have lit a fire at the bottom first and then added the charcoal. I had reversed the order.","I cursed my own stupidity, but what could I do? I had already thrown the burning branch in.","As the charcoal gradually heated up, I checked to make sure I hadn’t forgotten anything.","\"Ppareumbo, take Wonmo somewhere farther away.\"","\"....\"","\"Kkyuu?\"","Just in case, I asked Ppareumbo to take Wonmo away from the area.","Now it was time to concentrate.","As the furnace gradually heated up, I grasped the bellows with both hands.","It was common knowledge that fire burned more intensely when supplied with oxygen.","Fwoooosh—","I slowly pulled the bellows open, filling them with air.","Whoooom!","Then I pumped the air directly into the furnace.","Fwoooosh!","The flames inside the furnace became far fiercer than before. I could tell from the sound alone.","I worked the bellows vigorously, helping the charcoal produce even more heat.","Whoom! Whoooom!","The more air I pumped into the furnace, the more violently the flames raged.","But it still wasn’t enough.","I continued working the bellows until the flames began turning white.","From time to time, I added more charcoal to increase the intensity even further. Since this was my first attempt, I grew slightly anxious that I might fail.","Rooooar!","Eventually, all the charcoal ignited, producing a fierce blaze.","The flames seemed to fluctuate between yellow and white.","This should be enough.","I stopped working the bellows and wiped away my sweat.","Despite standing some distance away, I could feel the tremendous heat.","I was reluctant to approach, but I had no choice if I wanted to inspect the minerals.","Rooooar!","\"Ugh...\"","I frowned. Even moving slightly closer made the skin on my face sting.","Still, I needed to confirm whether the metals were melting properly. I endured the heat and inspected them.","’The container is intact... and the minerals seem to have shrunk.’","Their size had visibly decreased. The change in the orichalcum was especially noticeable.","Liquid streamed down the surface of the mithril as though it were sweating.","The minerals were melting.","My hard work was finally producing results.","’I should add more charcoal and keep working the bellows.’","Now that I had confirmed the minerals were melting, all that remained was to maintain the fire.","I continued pumping the bellows vigorously before gradually retreating from the heat.","I hadn’t been working for very long, yet the heat had caused sweat to pour from my body like rain.","’That dwarf did this every day?’","And I was only using a makeshift furnace. The dwarf must have worked in an even harsher environment.","No one’s work was ever easy, especially work connected to the very foundations of civilization.","Others had been enduring these hardships on my behalf, yet I had lived without appreciating them.","’I should sprinkle in some of this powder too.’","Following the dwarf’s instructions, I sprinkled in the blue powder.","The minerals were now about halfway melted and had become soft and sludgy.","I stirred them with the tongs to help them melt more evenly, then sent the dwarf a message.","[Wild Grylls: (A video of the melting minerals) They’re melting. I’m sweating like crazy ;;]","[Passing Dwarf: Tough, isn’t it?]","[Wild Grylls: How did you do this every day?]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s fine once you get used to it. An expert can even drink molten metal, hahaha.]","[Wild Grylls: Want a sip?]","[Passing Dwarf: I prefer booze to molten metal.]","Of course he did. I chuckled.","Since even the mithril was melting, it might not be a bad idea to keep him updated in real time.","[Passing Dwarf: Ah, right. You’ll need to quench it too. I completely forgot.]","[Wild Grylls: Quench it? I’ve heard of that, but do I really need to?]","[Passing Dwarf: Of course you do. It’s a weapon. I’ll give you some oil, so find a suitable metal container and fill it.]","[Wild Grylls: Why oil instead of water?]","[Passing Dwarf: If you use water and mess it up, the sword might break. Oil is better.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay.]","[Passing Dwarf: Don’t panic if it catches fire. That’s normal.]","An expert really was different. He even explained useful tips like these in detail.","However, regardless of how many tips he gave me, I was still the one who had to do everything.","After preparing the oil for quenching, I looked inside the furnace.","Bubble, bubble, bubble—","The mithril and orichalcum had completely melted and were beginning to boil.","Something resembling impurities floated on the surface, so I immediately skimmed it off.","How did I skim it off? By using yet another tool the dwarf had given me.","Perhaps because I had sprinkled in the blue powder, the impurities were easily filtered out, leaving behind pure molten metal.","’Now I just have to pour it into the mold.’","This was the most important moment.","I swallowed nervously and grasped the container with the tongs.","It had been heavy when empty, but with molten metal inside, it was considerably heavier.","Just in case, I circulated mana throughout my body and slowly carried it toward the mold.","Then I carefully tilted the container over the small hole in the center of the mold.","Trickle, trickle, trickle—","I was supposed to stop once the molten metal filled the hole. That was the method the dwarf had taught me.","However, I couldn’t pause midway through pouring. Molten metal cooled quickly.","Focusing completely, I carefully watched the hole.","I could feel the strain gradually building in my forearms, but I endured it.","Trickle, trickle—pour!","Now!","The moment the hole could no longer contain the molten metal, I immediately stopped.","A little molten metal remained in the container, but that didn’t matter. I had plenty of raw material anyway.","I set down the container and tilted the mold slightly.","The molten metal filling the hole spilled out.","This step was essential because the metal couldn’t be allowed to harden while completely blocking the hole.","\"Phew.\"","I exhaled. My first attempt had gone fairly well.","Now I only had to wait for the molten metal to harden somewhat.","[Wild Grylls: (A video of the mold filled with molten metal) I’m almost finished.]","[Passing Dwarf: Pant... Pant...]","[Wild Grylls: ;;]","Just how excited was he that he couldn’t even form words?","Chuckling, I waited for the molten metal to harden.","I had heard that it usually took around ten to fifteen minutes.","I could clean up while I waited. The furnace came first.","’I have no choice but to wait until the charcoal burns out.’","Most of the charcoal had already turned gray rather than black.","Even if I didn’t extinguish it myself, it would eventually go out on its own.","’I’ve been fairly fortunate despite all my misfortunes.’","I wiped the sweat streaming down my body with a towel.","If the minerals hadn’t come in solid chunks, I would have struggled far more than this.","I would also have to make a dagger and a spare sword later, so it seemed I still had plenty of hardship ahead of me.","’Has enough time passed?’","After waiting a while, I slowly opened the mold’s lid.","A beautifully shaped sword appeared before my eyes.","It was an alloy of green mithril and blackish-purple orichalcum.","’It’s surprisingly dull in color.’","I wouldn’t describe it as beautiful. It was simply... plain and gloomy.","It was neither green nor blackish-purple, but an ordinary silver. A particularly dark silver, at that.","I was slightly disappointed, but its appearance didn’t matter as long as it performed well.","I unconsciously reached for the sword, only to flinch and stop myself.","’That was close.’","I had assumed it had cooled, but I felt intense heat as soon as my hand approached it.","I tapped it several times with the tongs the dwarf had provided to check whether it had hardened, then carefully picked it up.","Now all I had to do was slowly lower it into the container of oil and quench it.","Hiss! Fwoosh!","Just as the dwarf had warned, the oil caught fire the moment I inserted the sword.","However, he had said there was little risk of an accident, so I remained calm and continued quenching it.","After repeating the process several times, the oil no longer caught fire.","And with that, my first sword was complete.","\"Phew.\"","I exhaled as I gazed at the sword, wisps of smoke still rising from it.","Seeing the finished product filled me with pride. It was a tool I had made with my own hands.","I would have liked to sharpen the blade myself, but I should leave that pleasure to the dwarf.","He had begged me to let him hold the sword, saying that he would be satisfied as long as he could sharpen its blade.","[Wild Grylls: (A photograph of the completed sword) It’s finished. It has cooled down. Want me to send it now?]","[Passing Dwarf: Please... just let me sharpen the blade....]","[Wild Grylls: I-I’ll send it over ;;]","He sounded so desperate that I couldn’t even bring myself to tease him.","I sent the longsword to the dwarf.","’I sweated a lot, but it wasn’t particularly difficult.’","After briefly rehydrating, I checked the time.","There was still plenty left. I could use it to complete my remaining tasks.","’Wonmo is... asleep.’","As it happened, Wonmo was taking a nap.","This seemed like a good opportunity to find the crab I had promised the dwarf.","I hung the security orb I had received from Princess Cheonggu above the cave entrance.","How did I hang it? Just like a block of fermented soybean paste. Of course, I made sure it wouldn’t sway.","\"Ppareumbo, I’ll be back soon.\"","\"....\"","After saying goodbye to Ppareumbo, I left the shelter.","***","Around the same time, Gareth—the dwarf to whom Grylls had sent the sword—was staring at it in awe.","\"Daaamn...!\"","He exclaimed in admiration as he gazed at the sword Grylls had given him.","The blade was still blunt, and the grip had yet to be finished. That unfinished sword now rested in Gareth’s hands.","However, something about it was different.","When Grylls had crafted it, the sword had been dull and gloomy.","Shiiimmer—","But that was no longer the case.","Gareth stared at the sword, which now gleamed a brilliant green.","Blackish-purple points of starlight were embedded across its luminous green surface.","It looked as though an entire green galaxy had been captured within the blade.","\"This is so fucking cool.\"","Gareth murmured in pure enchantment."]},{"title":"Chapter 120","paragraphs":["Alloy (3)","Most people knew dwarves as a race that loved alcohol and minerals.","However, that was only half true.","All dwarves were fond of alcohol, but the same could not be said of minerals.","It was simply that their distinctive physiques and innate physical abilities gave them tremendous potential in mineral-related work.","Naturally, this caused dwarven society to develop around the mining industry.","The pace of that development was also unparalleled.","While the other races remained in the Paleolithic or Neolithic eras, the dwarves alone progressed through the Bronze Age and reached the Iron Age.","Some scholars even argued that dwarves had played an enormous role in the development of the other races.","As time passed, the dwarves ceased to be the only race leading civilization.","However, the impact they had made during that era was so great that, even as the times changed, their image as the \"race of alcohol and minerals\" endured.","\"Ooh... Oooooh...!\"","And Gareth, the gallery’s registered user known as Passing Dwarf, perfectly matched that stereotype.","He didn’t merely enjoy alcohol; he loved it, and he possessed extensive knowledge of metallurgy.","That dwarf was currently staring at the sword in his hands and repeatedly exclaiming in admiration.","Shiiimmer!","Blackish-purple stars shone within a green galaxy.","It was a poetic description, but one that perfectly suited the sword Gareth was holding.","The sword had originally been a dull silver, but at some point, it had begun to glow.","’This is the most beautiful sword I’ve ever seen...!’","Gareth was a dwarf who specialized in metallurgy. Naturally, he possessed extensive knowledge of a sword’s quality and performance.","Although his excessive love of alcohol had left him less skilled than other artisans, his discerning eye was as accurate as any master’s.","The mithril-orichalcum alloy Grylls had created—and the sword forged from it—","It unquestionably ranked first among all the swords Gareth had ever seen, far surpassing every other weapon.","\"It still has a few rough edges, but....\"","Honestly, aside from the materials, the sword itself was closer to a mass-produced weapon.","When crafting a delicate tool like a sword, which needed to transmit force efficiently, one generally didn’t use a mold.","Only by forging it directly with a blacksmith’s own hands could one create a sword that was both practical and beautiful.","Therefore, the sword’s craftsmanship couldn’t be described as exceptional.","However, its materials were so absurdly extraordinary that they compensated for every flaw.","Even tools made from solid mithril were nearly impossible to find, yet this sword contained orichalcum as well.","The result resting in Gareth’s hands completely captivated him.","’I didn’t even channel much mana into it. Just how efficient is this thing?’","Mana was the reason the sword displayed such beautiful colors.","Yet despite receiving only a small amount of mana, it shone like a galaxy.","It was the joint creation of mithril, which naturally contained an extremely high concentration of mana, and orichalcum, which possessed a strong affinity for mana.","Gareth had known from the beginning that the experiment was unlikely to fail, but the resulting masterpiece exceeded even his wildest imagination.","’This isn’t the time for that. I need to sharpen the blade.’","After admiring the sword’s brilliant appearance, Gareth came to his senses.","Why had Grylls sent the sword to him?","It certainly wasn’t a gift.","He had sent it so Gareth could assess the alloy’s performance and sharpen the blade.","Gareth had already gained a rough understanding of its performance, so it was time to work on the edge.","’And he can produce a virtually unlimited amount of this....’","As Gareth sharpened the blade, he wondered what would happen if the sword’s existence became known to the world.","Calling it an uproar would be an understatement. Countless people would attempt to steal it.","A solid mithril sword alone would cause chaos, yet this sword contained orichalcum as well.","’Even the legendary masterpieces weren’t this impressive. Not even the Holy Sword.’","The Hero’s Holy Sword, Revolution.","Ares’s blessing had imbued it with divine power, but the material itself was ordinary steel.","’Perhaps the sword the Heavenly Demon gave him might be comparable.’","It was supposedly made from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron, one of the highest-ranked minerals in existence.","It was far rarer than mithril, orichalcum, and adamantium, which were known as the three great rare minerals.","If the Heavenly Demon’s claim wasn’t mere boasting, her sword might be somewhat comparable.","The fact that it was made entirely from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron was already absurd.","’It looks like he plans to give this sword to the Heavenly Demon....’","Gareth abruptly stopped sharpening the blade, his expression clouding with concern.","Was it truly wise to give this sword to someone else so readily?","Of course, the sword unquestionably belonged to Grylls. Gareth had no say in the matter.","He was simply anxious.","How would the world react once this sword’s existence became known?","Was it really safe to give such a sword to the Heavenly Demon, a shut-in who spent all her time fooling around on the gallery?","It was a serious concern.","’She must hold a fairly high position if she possesses a sword made from Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron....’","After worrying for a while, Gareth set aside his concerns and finished sharpening the blade.","He also crafted and attached the handle himself.","Thus, the mithril-orichalcum alloy sword, now bearing the touch of a dwarven artisan, was completed.","’What should we call the mithril-orichalcum alloy?’","Since it was an alloy that had never existed before, even deciding on its name was difficult.","Only Grylls could produce it.","Gareth nodded to himself.","It would be better to let Grylls name both the alloy and the sword.","Slice—","To test the sharpness of the blade, Gareth cut through a stack of paper.","Even though he merely touched the blade against it, the stack was sliced apart with ease.","’Since it’s mostly solid mithril, it’s incredibly light too.’","It was lighter than steel while surpassing a steel sword in performance. It also possessed outstanding mana efficiency.","On top of all that, it produced a brilliant glow whenever mana was channeled into it.","’Judging solely by its performance, doesn’t this seem more like a Holy Sword?’","After entertaining that almost blasphemous thought, Gareth immediately sent Grylls a message.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey. I finished sharpening the blade. I attached the handle too, so take it.]","[Wild Grylls: Haha, perfect timing. I just got back from catching the crab.]","[Passing Dwarf: You don’t have to send it immediately. I’m going to eat it for dinner.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay.]","[Passing Dwarf: By the way, are you giving that sword to someone else?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m planning to give it to the Heavenly Demon. She gave me her sword, remember? Of course I should repay her.]","Gareth began typing a message, then stopped.","Grylls had clearly already made up his mind, so Gareth had no place interfering.","Moreover, Grylls was inside the Forest of Four Seasons. Even if the existence of the sword and the identity of its maker became known, he wouldn’t be placed in danger.","Who would dare enter the Forest of Four Seasons merely to obtain that alloy?","Even if someone managed to acquire it, they wouldn’t be able to leave.","Only Grylls could do that.","’I just hope the Heavenly Demon doesn’t make some pointless post about it.’","Although she posted less frequently now that she was busy working as a junior moderator, she used to flood the gallery with pointless posts.","Hoping that the sword’s existence would remain secret for as long as possible, Gareth sent another message.","[Passing Dwarf: This is fucking ridiculous, hahaha.]","It was absurd, but it was undeniably true. Gareth let out a hollow laugh.","Only Grylls could give an answer like that. Whenever Gareth heard such things from him, he experienced a strange feeling.","[Passing Dwarf: Are you planning to give one to anyone else?]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know. Maybe I’ll only make one for myself. Though I might reconsider if someone offers me a suitable trade.]","[Passing Dwarf: Be as careful as possible about who you give one to. That sword is far too good. It could cause a bloodbath.]","[Wild Grylls: It’s that impressive?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah, it’s that impressive. It’s an alloy of mithril and orichalcum, for fuck’s sake ;;]","[Wild Grylls: There’s so much of both here that I practically trip over them, so I don’t really understand how valuable they are.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, and I’m going to make one more sword and a dagger. Can you sharpen them for me? If that’s too much trouble, just attach the handles.]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah, I can easily do that much. But I have one condition.]","[Wild Grylls: What is it? Another crab?]","[Passing Dwarf: No. I’ll give you an ingot mold, so make an alloy ingot for me. I want to keep it as a souvenir.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: Oh, and what are you going to call the alloy and the sword?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll let the Heavenly Demon name the sword herself. I’m not sure about the alloy. Mithrilicon?]","[Passing Dwarf: You put absolutely no thought into that name ;; But it actually sounds decent.]","[Wild Grylls: Heh.]","Mithrilicon.","It was certainly an uninspired name, but it suited the alloy well enough.","It wasn’t an official name anyway, so there was no harm in calling it something simple.","[Wild Grylls: Anyway, thanks for helping me. I’ll send you the crab this evening.]","[Passing Dwarf: Okay. Make sure you make that ingot for me.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll make it right away. I’ll send it with the sword and dagger. By the way, do I need to quench the ingot too?]","[Passing Dwarf: No. Just leave it to cool.]","The conversation ended there. He had probably returned to work.","As Gareth closed his conversation with Grylls, a thought occurred to him.","’That bastard isn’t going to find adamantium next, is he?’","The frightening part was how likely that seemed.","Wi Seorak, the Demonic Brain of the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult and the gallery’s registered user Smart Demon, led an extremely busy life.","He was responsible for countless duties befitting his title of Demonic Brain.","He had been particularly unable to rest lately, ever since the atrocities committed by the Holy Kingdom of Eldorado had come to light.","The relationship between the Central Plains and Eldorado had never been particularly significant, but things were different for other nations.","Many countries had been affected by the Immortal King incident to varying degrees.","While they were embroiled in conflict, the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult had no choice but to devise plans of its own.","Wi Seorak’s primary responsibility was to strengthen the cult’s influence.","Step. Step. Step.","Even if he had possessed two bodies, he still would have been overwhelmed with work. Yet Wi Seorak was currently following a woman.","She had narrow shoulders and hair tied into a single tail. Her dignified black attire radiated authority.","In her hand was a dull silver sword.","’Why is she going outside?’","Wi Seorak was currently following the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","As usual, she had summoned him while he was in the middle of his daily duties.","He had been deeply worried from the moment he received the summons, and now even their destination seemed unusual.","Moreover, she was holding a sword he had never seen before.","Setting aside its blade, judging solely by its shape, it didn’t seem to be a high-quality weapon.","It looked so crude that even a sword made by an ordinary blacksmith would have been better.","’Who gave her that sword? Don’t tell me it was Grylls.’","There was no other reason for her to suddenly acquire a new sword.","Wi Seorak accessed the gallery.","Grylls had only uploaded two new posts since the one he had made that morning.","’Mithrilicon....’","One of the posts explained how he had used a makeshift furnace to create an alloy by mixing mithril and orichalcum.","Naturally, the responses had been overwhelming.","An alloy of true silver—mithril—and true gold—orichalcum.","It was significant enough to turn the entire world upside down.","’Could that sword have been made from it?’","Using his exceptional intellect, Wi Seorak reached a hypothesis.","The sword Yu Sowol was currently holding had been forged from that alloy.","Ordinarily, he would never have entertained such an absurd idea.","However, he had already read Grylls’s post.","The post explained that a dwarf had provided him with a mold and various tools.","Using them, Grylls had crafted a sword for the Heavenly Demon and planned to keep the remaining weapons for himself.","\"Your Heavenliness.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"May I ask why you brought me with you?\"","If she merely intended to test the sword’s performance, she could have done so alone. Yet Yu Sowol had brought him along.","Surely she didn’t intend to reveal her identity as a registered user. She must have another reason.","Yu Sowol answered in an unconcerned voice.","\"Recently, this lady’s benefactor gifted her a sword. However, he told this lady to name it herself.\"","\"A name... you say?\"","\"Indeed. This lady possesses little talent for naming things. Therefore, this lady summoned thee, believing it would be better for thee to name it.\"","\"....\"","She had summoned an extremely busy man merely to name a sword.","Wi Seorak stared at her in disbelief.","But who was Yu Sowol?","She was a being who looked down upon others not merely with her eyes, but with the gaze of heaven itself.","\"Thy face is filled with discontent.\"","\"It is not.\"","\"Do not speak words thou dost not mean.\"","\"My apologies.\"","\"Thy willingness to apologize swiftly is commendable.\"","Yu Sowol casually overlooked Wi Seorak’s disrespect. She genuinely didn’t seem to care.","Just as Wi Seorak breathed an inward sigh of relief, Yu Sowol stopped walking.","\"Hmm? Your Heavenliness, this place is....\"","\"This should suffice.\"","Yu Sowol had stopped at the edge of a cliff.","It was a strange place where only a single towering tree stood.","Countless mountain ranges stretched beyond the tree, creating a truly magnificent view.","’W-What? We were inside a building just moments ago.’","Wi Seorak couldn’t conceal his bewilderment.","Though he was known as the Demonic Brain, he was still a martial artist.","His cultivation was by no means shallow, so he could sense even the slightest flow of qi. Yet by the time he regained his senses, he was already standing atop a cliff.","It was as if they had teleported.","Yu Sowol slowly raised the sword.","Wi Seorak suppressed his confusion and stared at her back.","Shiiimmer!","\"A green... galaxy?\"","When Yu Sowol infused the sword with qi, it began to glow.","The surface of the blade overflowed with beauty, appearing to contain an entire green galaxy.","Yu Sowol merely glanced at the sword’s magnificent appearance without stopping.","Her arm gradually rose until the sword pointed toward the heavens.","Swoosh—","Then she lowered it with extraordinary gentleness.","She didn’t even slash downward. She merely lowered it.","The movement was so light that only the sound of the blade cutting through the wind could be heard.","It was an elegant motion, almost as though she were painting a picture.","Craaaack—","However, the aftermath was anything but gentle.","The tree that had stood tall and straight split down the middle, its two halves slowly separating.","The intact tree had been severed without the sword ever touching it.","’As expected....’","Wi Seorak swallowed as he watched.","He had anticipated it, but Yu Sowol had grown far stronger than before.","With this level of power, she would have no difficulty spreading the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult’s prestige.","\"Hmm.\"","However, Yu Sowol herself appeared dissatisfied.","She stared at the sword and murmured quietly.","\"This is not a particularly good sword.\"","\"What? What do you mean...?\"","\"A sword can only be called a sword if it cuts what its wielder desires.\"","\"...?\"","As he listened to her incomprehensible words, Wi Seorak suddenly sensed something strange.","The landscape visible beyond the vertically split tree seemed wrong.","The first thing he noticed was the clouds.","The clouds, which should have formed a single continuous mass, had shifted out of alignment.","And it wasn’t merely the clouds.","A thin line had been drawn across the very sky.","Everything on either side of that line was misaligned.","Grylls exclaimed in admiration as he gazed at his newly crafted sword.","\"Is it a glow-in-the-dark sword? That’s cool.\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 121","paragraphs":["The Beastman (3)","\"Grrrrr.\"","The beastman glared at Baek So-cheon and let out a low growl.","\"Damn it! Because I saved you, that bastard seems to be furious with me now.\"","\"Be careful! His claws are incredibly sharp!\"","\"What do you mean, be careful? You’re supposed to stop him!\"","Whoosh!","The beastman charged at Baek So-cheon.","Thud!","Just before it could pounce on him, Yeom Hwasin’s kick sent it flying into the distance.","\"You bastard! I’m your opponent.\"","Yeom Hwasin stepped in front of Baek So-cheon.","Once he began displaying his true abilities, the situation changed entirely. It became obvious that he had deliberately allowed himself to be driven onto the defensive earlier.","Of course, the beastman was formidable as well. Its claws had managed to leave wounds on Yeom Hwasin’s skin. The final blow Yeom Hwasin had used to create the illusion of danger had even gouged him deeply enough to draw blood. Granted, it had merely damaged Yeom Hwasin’s thick skin, but drawing blood from someone possessing an Indestructible Vajra Body was an extraordinary feat in itself.","Yet despite all that, the ultimate conclusion remained unchanged.","There was still no one in the Murim capable of defeating Yeom Hwasin.","As though proving that fact, a single blow from Yeom Hwasin sent the beastman flying. In the next instant, Yeom Hwasin’s massive body followed it like a shadow.","Smash!","Another merciless blow from Yeom Hwasin struck it squarely in the face.","Its face caved in, but the beastman did not die.","When it crashed to the ground, Yeom Hwasin brought his foot down upon it.","Boom!","The kick struck its chest, yet the beastman still did not die. It thrashed desperately, raking its claws across Yeom Hwasin’s shin.","The frantic struggle was highly dangerous, forcing Yeom Hwasin to leap backward.","The beastman seized that opening and launched itself from the ground.","Realizing that it was losing against Yeom Hwasin, it chose another target. It hurled itself toward Baek So-cheon, driven by an instinctive desire to kill him before it died.","With half its face crushed and the last of its strength behind its charge, the beastman was terrifying.","Just as Baek So-cheon realized he would be unable to evade without using his internal energy—","Grab!","The creature stopped directly in front of him.","Yeom Hwasin had arrived using Shifting Form and Position and seized the beastman by the back of its head.","Forcing its mouth open from behind, Yeom Hwasin shouted,","\"Kill it!\"","Without hesitation, Baek So-cheon drew the Ghost Shadow Sword and plunged it into the beastman’s mouth.","Stab!","The blade pierced through the back of its neck. Its body might have been as hard as steel, but the inside of its mouth was not.","Yeom Hwasin grabbed the protruding blade and swiftly spun it in a circle.","Rip! Slice!","The beastman’s severed head dropped to the ground.","The two men collapsed onto the ground and sighed in relief. Baek So-cheon belatedly expressed his gratitude. Had Yeom Hwasin not intervened earlier, he would have been forced to use his internal energy or suffer a serious injury.","\"Thank you.\"","\"Not at all. Thanks to you, I killed it easily.\"","Each of them had saved the other once.","\"About what happened earlier—what would you have done if I hadn’t saved you?\"","\"I would have become even more handsome.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Wouldn’t a long scar across my face make me look more impressive? I’m the Leader of the Cheukcheon Alliance, yet my face is far too unblemished. Look closely. Isn’t my skin as smooth as a child’s?\"","\"Your skin looks your age, but your mental age certainly is that of a child!\"","\"Don’t be jealous.\"","Baek So-cheon shook his head with a dumbfounded expression.","His gaze fell upon the beastman’s corpse.","\"To think they unleashed a creature like this! They truly are unforgivable.\"","Had they failed to eliminate it, this bloodthirsty creature would have wandered the world, slaughtering everyone it encountered.","\"You’re right.\"","\"What do you mean, I’m right? You’re going to forgive them anyway, aren’t you?\"","\"I must forgive them. If a blade cuts you, you put it back in its sheath. There’s no need to go so far as to break the blade, is there?\"","\"Do you truly wish to unite the Murim so badly that you’re willing to go this far?\"","\"What else should I do? Play the part of a benevolent leader of the unorthodox factions?\"","Baek So-cheon had no reply to that.","He buried the beastman and the two men who had come before it in the same place. They said that enemies from a previous life were reborn as husband and wife. Perhaps the three of them might be born as spouses in their next lives.","\"Why bother burying them? Just leave them there.\"","\"When you have the opportunity to bury the dead, you should do so.\"","\"And who will ever know?\"","\"I’ll know, and so will you.\"","\"This is a world where being kind only brings you losses.\"","\"Isn’t that why I’m fighting you? I’m trying to prevent the world from becoming such a place. I’m going to sleep first.\"","Baek So-cheon lay down.","\"Aren’t you going to sleep?\"","At Baek So-cheon’s question, Yeom Hwasin added several more pieces of firewood to the fire.","\"As you said, sitting here and staring blankly into the flames isn’t so bad.\"","Baek So-cheon fell into such a deep sleep that it almost seemed reckless, while Yeom Hwasin silently watched over him until the campfire burned out.","At last, they arrived at the Flood Dragon Sect.","The carriage slowly approached its main gate in the distance.","\"How many antidotes do we have left?\"","\"One pill.\"","If the Flood Dragon Sect did not possess an antidote, Jong Mujin would die.","\"What will you do if they don’t have an antidote for the blood poison that afflicted Warrior Jong?\"","The Seven Unorthodox Families were an alliance of seven clans. Another sect rather than the Flood Dragon Sect might have used the poison, or they might have entrusted the task to an outsider. In either case, the Flood Dragon Sect might not possess an antidote.","\"They’ll have one.\"","\"Why are you so certain?\"","\"Don’t they say that if three people gather, one among them can be your teacher? Seven of them gathered together, so surely at least one of them was intelligent enough to make the right decision.\"","Although Yeom Hwasin spoke as though he were merely guessing, he probably knew their personalities and dispositions well. After all, he had known that Jeong Gyun had defected to the Frenzied Demon Blade.","He might even have already guessed what decision they had reached.","Pretending not to notice, Baek So-cheon drove the carriage onward.","\"Then let’s find out whether their clever one was as intelligent as you and whether the other six followed him as innocently and obediently as I did.\"","\"Don’t belittle yourself. You’ll soon return to our path as well.\"","Wondering what he meant, Baek So-cheon glanced back through the small window behind the driver’s seat.","Yeom Hwasin merely stared out the window, apparently having no intention of explaining.","The gates of the Flood Dragon Sect stood wide open.","Its sect leader, Yeoh Jeol-saeng, personally came out to the entrance to welcome Yeom Hwasin.","\"Welcome, Alliance Leader.\"","\"Have you been well?\"","The two warmly exchanged greetings. After offering Baek So-cheon a formal greeting as well, Yeoh Jeol-saeng asked Yeom Hwasin,","\"What brings you to our sect without any prior notice?\"","\"I was passing by and stopped because I needed to ask Sect Leader Yeoh for assistance.\"","The two men behaved as if the previous attack—and the fact that one had attacked while the other had been attacked—had never happened.","\"What assistance do you require?\"","\"One of my subordinates has been poisoned with blood poison. Do you happen to possess an antidote that can treat him?\"","\"Then you’ve come to exactly the right place. Our sect happens to possess an antidote that is highly effective against blood poison.\"","\"Haha, what a relief.\"","\"Someone, hurry and bring the patient inside!\"","At Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s command, the Flood Dragon Sect’s warriors came forward and carried Jong Mujin from the carriage.","\"I’ve prepared drinks for you. Please come inside.\"","\"Let’s do that.\"","Yeoh Jeol-saeng guided Yeom Hwasin and Baek So-cheon to the great hall, where a drinking table had been prepared.","The men caught up with one another as though they shared an entirely ordinary relationship. Cups of wine and laughter passed around the table, but in his heart, Yeoh Jeol-saeng traveled through hell and back several times. He had no way of knowing when Yeom Hwasin might change his mind and kill him with a single blow.","However, their punishment for this incident was not death, but something else.","\"I’m considering establishing an elite unit within the alliance composed of promising young talents.\"","\"Ah, I see.\"","A fleeting look of panic crossed Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s face before disappearing.","\"It seems only proper that the proud heirs of the Seven Unorthodox Families should lead these young talents. What does Sect Leader Yeoh think?\"","In other words, Yeom Hwasin intended to bring their children to the Cheukcheon Alliance and hold them hostage.","They had only two choices: accept his demand or go to war with him.","Yeoh Jeol-saeng chose to innocently and obediently follow the will of their one clever man. They had already made an internal decision to accept any conditions Yeom Hwasin imposed.","\"You are absolutely right. My eldest son possesses considerable leadership ability, so I am confident that he will be of great assistance to you, Alliance Leader.\"","\"As expected. Sect Leader Yeoh’s loyalty brings me immense joy. However, I wonder what the others will think.\"","\"I’m certain they’ll be delighted.\"","Now that they had reached the main subject, the drinking session did not continue for long.","\"You must be tired after traveling so far. You should retire early and rest.\"","\"Let’s do that.\"","A subordinate came forward and guided Yeom Hwasin and Baek So-cheon to their quarters. Baek So-cheon quietly left the hall. Although Yeoh Jeol-saeng’s name was also written in his Book of Death, that did not mean he intended to kill him here.","Only after Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin had left did a secret door finally open, revealing the six other family heads.","They had hidden there intending to join forces if Yeom Hwasin attempted to kill Yeoh Jeol-saeng. Each of them cared only about his own family, but there was at least one truth they all understood.","If they divided, they would all die.","Do Jeonggil, the leader of the Heavenly Society who had accurately discerned Yeom Hwasin’s intentions earlier, had once again predicted the outcome correctly. He had expected that Yeom Hwasin would never kill Yeoh Jeol-saeng.","\"He even knew that we were hiding here.\"","\"It certainly seemed that way. He projected his energy in this direction.\"","\"That’s right. I felt it as well.\"","From the beginning, Yeom Hwasin had come here while considering the possibility that not only these seven leaders, but also numerous other ambushers, might be lying in wait.","\"One certainly has to acknowledge his courage.\"","This time, Yeom Hwasin had decisively demonstrated that his courage stemmed from his overwhelming strength.","Cheol Han spoke with an angry expression.","\"Do we truly have to send our children to him?\"","Yeoh Jeol-saeng replied,","\"Now that he has even killed the beastman, we have no choice but to do as he says.\"","\"Is there truly no other way?\"","\"There’s no need to worry. At the very least, he isn’t the sort of man who would kill our children without reason.\"","In the end, they all nodded. Once their opponent displayed such overwhelming strength, they found themselves feeling more at ease instead.","At that moment, Do Jeonggil presented an unexpected glimmer of hope.","\"There is one variable.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Baek So-cheon. I don’t believe he has changed his convictions. He is a man with the blood of the orthodox factions flowing through his very bones.\"","\"Then why is he traveling with Alliance Leader Yeom?\"","\"I don’t know. However, one thing is certain. If anyone ever succeeds in killing Yeom Hwasin, it will be Baek So-cheon.\"","They all hoped that would happen.","Of course, they did not know that their names were written in Baek So-cheon’s Book of Death, or that as their enemy, Baek So-cheon would prove even more terrifying than Yeom Hwasin.","In any event, the rebellion of the Seven Unorthodox Families ended there. None of them had died, but their heirs had become hostages, and if war erupted, they would have to stand at the forefront against the orthodox factions.","Considering that they had attempted to take Yeom Hwasin’s life, this was a reasonably favorable outcome.","\"For the time being, let us restrain ourselves and observe the situation.\"","The seven family heads cupped their fists to one another before departing.","Jong Mujin regained consciousness the next day. After learning what Yeom Hwasin had done for him, he performed a deep bow.","\"I will never forget this kindness.\"","His already profound loyalty deepened even further at that moment.","Through this incident, Baek So-cheon learned many things from Yeom Hwasin. In particular, restraining one’s anger for the sake of a greater objective was something few people could accomplish, yet it was an essential virtue for anyone who wished to achieve great things.","In addition to gaining insights into martial arts, Baek So-cheon was also learning how to govern and command people.","Yeom Hwasin said to him,","\"Now that the troublemakers are out of the way, our journey should continue, shouldn’t it?\"","Baek So-cheon climbed into the carriage first.","\"Let’s go.\"","Yeom Hwasin burst into hearty laughter at his enthusiasm.","\"Hahaha!\"","Jong Mujin once again took the driver’s seat. Although they had not told him their destination, the carriage headed north once more.","No one could stop the road that even the Seven Unorthodox Families had failed to block.","The carriage continued north.","The scenery around them gradually turned white as a snowy landscape began to unfold.","After traveling endlessly northward, the carriage finally stopped at the foot of a snow-covered mountain.","\"You’ll have to continue on foot from here.\"","\"Wait for us here.\"","\"Understood.\"","Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin began climbing the snowy mountain. The desolate area contained neither people nor even animal tracks.","Crunch. Crunch.","Walking through the pure-white snow felt surprisingly pleasant.","Eventually, Yeom Hwasin stopped before a sheer wall of ice that rose like a cliff.","\"Where are we?\"","\"The Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","The Northern Sea Ice Palace was the most mysterious sect in the Murim. It never involved itself in the affairs of the martial world, and it possessed enough power that no other sect dared treat it lightly.","Given their relentless journey northward, Baek So-cheon had suspected that the Ice Palace might be their destination.","However, he could never have anticipated Yeom Hwasin’s next words.","\"This is where we will restore your dantian.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 122","paragraphs":["The Absolute Prohibition (1)","\"Did you just say that the Northern Sea Ice Palace can restore my dantian?\"","Baek So-cheon stared at Yeom Hwasin in astonishment. Judging by his expression, he was not joking.","\"That’s right. As far as I know, the Ice Palace is the only place capable of repairing your dantian.\"","Yeom Hwasin had surprised him many times before. At that moment, he surpassed all his previous records.","\"Didn’t you say you would restore it only after your martial arts reached the next stage?\"","\"As repayment for saving my life, I’ll restore your dantian first.\"","Baek So-cheon remembered what Yeom Hwasin had said earlier—that he would soon return to their path. He now realized that Yeom Hwasin had been referring to this.","\"Why are you looking at me like that?\"","\"You truly are an impossible man to understand.\"","\"I’m not such a complicated person. Perhaps I seem complicated precisely because I’m too simple.\"","A sudden thought occurred to Baek So-cheon.","When Yeom Hwasin had been endangered by the beastman, had he truly not expected Baek So-cheon to save him?","Could he have been planning to restore Baek So-cheon’s internal energy from that very moment?","Yeom Hwasin was such an unpredictable man that it was impossible to tell what he was thinking.","Looking up at the ice wall, Baek So-cheon asked,","\"Do we have to climb over this to reach the Ice Palace?\"","\"No. We only need to wait here.\"","Baek So-cheon was puzzled.","The Northern Sea Ice Palace stood between the orthodox and unorthodox factions, but strictly speaking, it was closer to the orthodox side. How could it have a connection with Yeom Hwasin?","\"I didn’t know the Cheukcheon Alliance had dealings with the Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","\"It doesn’t.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I’m saying that the Ice Palace Master and I know each other personally. Officially, the Cheukcheon Alliance has no relationship with the Northern Sea Ice Palace.\"","\"What sort of relationship do you have with the Ice Palace Master?\"","\"You might say that we are destined to fulfill a long-cherished wish.\"","\"Whose wish do you mean?\"","Yeom Hwasin merely gave him an enigmatic smile and said nothing more about it.","\"I hope it’s my wish.\"","\"So do I. However, you should prepare yourself.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"There’s a possibility that restoring your dantian will fail. Even without knowing the details, it obviously won’t be an easy task, will it? If something goes wrong, you might die.\"","Yeom Hwasin lowered his voice as though attempting to frighten him, but Baek So-cheon remained completely unconcerned.","\"That’s your problem. You have far too little attachment to life. But that’s all right. You’ll soon recover not only your internal energy, but also your hope.\"","If anything, Yeom Hwasin appeared more excited than Baek So-cheon.","Although Baek So-cheon remained outwardly composed, his heart was also pounding with anticipation and excitement.","’How will they restore my dantian? If it is restored, what will happen to the internal energy I already possess? Will the two merge, or will I be able to control them separately?’","Of course, as Yeom Hwasin had said, the process would not be easy. The treatment itself might be extraordinarily dangerous, and his recovery of internal energy might be discovered in the process.","However, Baek So-cheon had realized something with certainty during this journey.","To oppose Yeom Hwasin, he needed to restore his dantian. Furthermore, he needed to use that process as an opportunity to grow even stronger if he wished to defeat him.","\"Let me ask you one honest question.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Why are you trying to restore my internal energy? Don’t give me any nonsense. I want an honest answer.\"","\"If I tell you, what will you do for me?\"","\"I’ll honestly answer one of your questions as well.\"","\"Very well. Then I’ll tell you. I’ve encountered a wall on my path to the next stage. I realized that I cannot break through it using ordinary methods, so I intend to choose an extraordinary one.\"","\"And that extraordinary method is restoring my internal energy?\"","\"If I fight a battle in which I genuinely feel threatened with death, perhaps I’ll be able to break through that wall.\"","Baek So-cheon nodded. If Yeom Hwasin had encountered a wall, that method was certainly worth attempting. It was also something only those at their level could try.","\"Now, is it my turn to ask a question?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Yeom Hwasin moved his lips as though about to ask something, but soon backed down.","\"I’ll ask when I think of something later.\"","\"You should ask while you still can. You’re old enough to start becoming forgetful, aren’t you?\"","\"Hahaha!\"","They conversed and waited for a long time, but no one appeared.","\"Putting aside the wall blocking your martial arts, don’t you think we should do something about the wall in front of us first?\"","Yeom Hwasin pounded on the ice wall and shouted,","\"Go and deliver this message! If you don’t open it immediately, I’ll smash my way inside! Consider yourselves warned!\"","He seemed convinced that someone behind the ice wall was listening to their conversation.","\"It doesn’t seem as though you’re welcome here.\"","\"Where in the martial world would anyone welcome me?\"","\"Given the situation, will they really repair my dantian?\"","\"I am me, and you are you.\"","\"But this is my first time here as well.\"","\"Did you think restoring your dantian would be that easy? We might have to lie down in front of their Palace Master’s residence and refuse to move.\"","\"I can’t bring myself to tell them to cut my stomach open if they want me gone, so you’ll have to do that on my behalf.\"","\"Leave it to me. Being unreasonable is my specialty.\"","Baek So-cheon chuckled.","Life truly was unpredictable. Who could have imagined that he would one day stand at the entrance to the Northern Sea Ice Palace, trading jokes with the Leader of the Cheukcheon Alliance?","Even after they waited for a long time, no one appeared.","Perhaps Yeom Hwasin had expected this cold reception from the beginning, for he did not become angry at all.","\"How long have we been waiting?\"","\"I believe it has been half an hour.\"","\"We’ve waited long enough.\"","When Yeom Hwasin walked toward the ice wall, Baek So-cheon quickly asked,","\"Surely you aren’t going to smash it simply because they refuse to open the door?\"","\"Why wouldn’t I?\"","Yeom Hwasin infused his fist with internal energy.","\"I’ll smash it on the count of three. One, two...\"","He raised his fist high, appearing genuinely ready to destroy the wall.","At that very moment—","Rumble.","A door opened in the ice wall. It had been concealed so perfectly that they only realized a door had been there after it opened.","A woman dressed in white politely greeted the two men.","\"I apologize for keeping our honored guests waiting. I will escort you to the Palace Master.\"","The woman led them inside. Judging by her swift and agile steps, her martial arts had reached the peak level.","Following her guidance, the two walked down an extremely long corridor.","The walls on either side looked as though they were made of ice, but closer examination revealed otherwise. The corridor had been constructed from stone that resembled ice, and beautiful paintings decorated it throughout.","There were various scenes: an adorable pair of male and female birds perched upon a snow-covered branch, children laughing and playing as they rode sleds across the ice, and a grandparent walking hand in hand with a grandchild through the snow.","Although every painting depicted things commonly seen in a cold region, each scene was filled with warmth.","Yet precisely because of that warmth, the presence of the hidden mechanisms beyond the paintings felt even more deadly. It was the same chilling presence one might sense from only the highest-grade mechanisms inside the Murim Alliance Leader’s residence.","In truth, these mechanisms were likely even more powerful than those of the Murim Alliance, certainly not weaker.","Throughout the history of the Murim, no martial faction had ever brought down the Northern Sea Ice Palace. In other words, the power and potential hidden within this place surpassed imagination.","Despite possessing such strength, its people had never left the Northern Sea and continued to live here quietly.","\"Do you know why they never leave the Northern Sea?\" Yeom Hwasin asked.","\"I don’t.\"","\"Because they live under an Absolute Prohibition forbidding them from leaving the Northern Sea and entering the Central Plains.\"","\"Whose command was it?\"","\"Whose do you think? The useless old generations of the Ice Palace who have already become bones beneath the earth.\"","The woman walking ahead of them quickened her steps slightly. It was clear that the conversation made her uncomfortable.","\"How did you learn about this?\"","\"I heard it from those who wished to leave this place.\"","\"There are people here who want to leave?\"","\"There were in the past, and there still are today. To them, the Northern Sea is nothing more than a vast prison from which they wish to escape.\"","The woman ahead of them visibly flinched again. Her reaction revealed just how sensitive this subject was within the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","Baek So-cheon guessed that the Ice Palace must have its own complicated internal circumstances. After all, even a group of beggars living beneath a bridge would establish a hierarchy and engage in politics. Why would this place be any different?","Fortunately for their guide, Yeom Hwasin said nothing more about the matter.","At the end of the long corridor, they emerged into a garden.","The scenery was breathtaking enough to draw an involuntary gasp of admiration.","Baek So-cheon was genuinely impressed.","In the distance stood the majestic buildings of the Northern Sea Ice Palace. Designed to appear as though they had been sculpted from ice, they were dazzlingly beautiful.","Trees covered in frost flowers surrounded them, while statues carved from ice decorated the grounds. Each was so intricate and beautiful that they were works of art capable of stopping people in their tracks.","The men and women passing through the garden were all dressed in white, and every one of them was strikingly handsome or beautiful. Some were martial experts, while others knew no martial arts whatsoever.","They greeted the two visitors with bright, radiant smiles as they passed. They all appeared happy, as though they were strolling through the gardens of paradise.","Yeom Hwasin stopped and asked Baek So-cheon,","\"What do you sense from them?\"","Baek So-cheon answered honestly.","\"They feel unnatural.\"","\"Exactly! You noticed it as well.\"","There was something artificial about their apparent happiness. It felt as though this joyous scene had been deliberately staged because the two men were visiting.","Even if that was not the case, their happiness did not feel genuine.","Eventually, the two arrived at the Palace Master’s residence.","Martial experts stood in a line on either side of the hall. Every one of them had reached a level ranging from the peak to the transcendent realm.","At their center sat a woman dressed in a magnificent pure-white robe adorned with elaborate ornaments.","She was Seo Bingbing, the current Palace Master of the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","She was far younger than Baek So-cheon had expected. At the youngest, she appeared to be in her mid-twenties, and at the oldest, in her early thirties. Judging by her age, Baek So-cheon assumed she had not inherited the position of Palace Master very long ago.","By contrast, all the experts standing guard around her were older women.","\"Why have you come to our palace again?\"","Her first words were prickly and openly hostile.","Yeom Hwasin grinned at her.","\"It’s good to see you too.\"","At that moment, Baek So-cheon understood.","’Something happened between these two.’","Judging by how she treated her guest, Yeom Hwasin had undoubtedly done something that infuriated her.","\"Our palace is not a place just anyone can enter whenever they please.\"","\"But I’m not just anyone, am I? The friend who came with me is also someone special.\"","Everyone’s attention turned toward Baek So-cheon.","Baek So-cheon cupped his fists toward Seo Bingbing and spoke calmly.","\"I am Baek So-cheon.\"","\"I know who you are. Great Hero Baek, you are a hero of the orthodox factions. Why are you traveling with a villain like him?\"","She openly called Yeom Hwasin a villain without hesitation.","\"As you may have heard from the rumors, I lost my strength and ended up in this state.\"","\"That is truly unfortunate.\"","At Seo Bingbing’s lament, Yeom Hwasin laughed.","\"There will be no need to pity him any longer.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"This man is going to regain his original strength.\"","\"The entire world knows that Great Hero Baek’s dantian was destroyed. How can he possibly regain his original strength?\"","Yeom Hwasin stared directly at her.","\"Because the Divine Physician of Life and Death will treat him and restore his dantian.\"","Seo Bingbing’s expression instantly hardened at the mention of the Divine Physician of Life and Death.","Baek So-cheon, on the other hand, was astonished.","\"He is still alive?\"","The Divine Physician of Life and Death had once been hailed as the reincarnation of Hua Tuo and was considered the greatest physician of his time.","Even Ban Wol-ryang, the Divine Physician of the Murim Alliance, had acknowledged him as the greatest physician of their generation. That alone demonstrated just how exceptional his medical skills were.","However, he had eventually vanished from the Murim, and no one had seen him since. Everyone had assumed he was dead, but it appeared that he had come to the Northern Sea Ice Palace.","Seo Bingbing spoke in a tone as cold as her expression.","\"The Divine Physician of Life and Death is not here.\"","Yeom Hwasin remained relaxed, as though he had already anticipated that answer.","\"The Divine Physician of Life and Death must be here. And he must treat this man.\"","The corners of Seo Bingbing’s lips curled upward as she asked provocatively,","\"Why?\"","Baek So-cheon was hardly the only person Yeom Hwasin possessed a talent for startling.","Words that shocked everyone present emerged from his mouth.","\"Because in return, I will lift the Absolute Prohibition.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 123","paragraphs":["The Absolute Prohibition (2)","Silence descended over the hall.","Amid the heavy silence created by those forbidden words, the first to react was the old woman standing beside Palace Master Seo Bingbing.","She radiated a frost-like aura. She was Shim Nahu, the Grand Elder of the Ice Palace.","\"The Absolute Prohibition is our palace’s most sacred and supreme principle! How dare you spout such nonsense!\"","Had her opponent not been Yeom Hwasin, she would have immediately charged forward and struck him with her palm.","\"Is there really anything absolute in this world?\"","\"What exactly are you trying to say?\"","\"How long do you intend to remain confined to the Northern Sea?\"","\"Throughout the ages, our palace has distinguished itself as the guardian of the Northern Sea. Why would you say such a thing?\"","\"The guardian of the Northern Sea? What exactly is there to protect here? Are you planning to guard the snowmen beside the road?\"","\"Silence!\"","Shim Nahu openly unleashed her killing intent. Yeom Hwasin, however, remained perfectly relaxed.","\"What I’m saying is simple. Stop limiting yourselves to the Northern Sea and become guardians of the Central Plains.\"","Just as Shim Nahu was about to shout at him, Seo Bingbing stepped in first. She spoke calmly to Yeom Hwasin.","\"Alliance Leader Yeom, that is enough. Although you are the Grandmaster of the Unorthodox Factions, I can no longer tolerate your insane ramblings.\"","\"I’ve been called a madman countless times, so perhaps I truly am insane. However, what I just said wasn’t the rambling of a madman.\"","\"Mad people never believe they are mad.\"","Their exchange was tense, but Baek So-cheon noticed something.","Compared to Shim Nahu, Seo Bingbing was not particularly angry.","When Yeom Hwasin had said that he would lift the Absolute Prohibition, Baek So-cheon had seen the expression that appeared on Seo Bingbing’s face. It had contained surprise, excitement, and intense emotion—but not anger.","Everyone had been staring at Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin, so no one else had noticed her expression.","Perhaps believing that he had adequately delivered his declaration of war, Yeom Hwasin changed the subject.","\"Coming to such a cold place has left me chilled to the bone. I need a drink to warm myself. Let’s continue our discussion tomorrow.\"","Seo Bingbing addressed one of her subordinates.","\"They are honored guests. Take good care of them.\"","Shim Nahu, on the other hand, continued glaring fiercely at the two men until they left the hall.","The gazes following them as they departed fell into two distinct categories: extreme hostility and hopeful anticipation.","Yeom Hwasin had been telling the truth.","There were undoubtedly people among them who wished to leave this place.","After leaving the Palace Master’s residence, Baek So-cheon said to Yeom Hwasin,","\"We need to talk.\"","Yeom Hwasin grinned.","\"Why do you think I had them prepare a drinking table?\"","***","\"What are you thinking about so deeply?\"","Na Sarin’s voice snapped Cheon-geuk back to her senses.","\"Ah, I’m sorry.\"","Cheon-geuk hurriedly reached for the wine bottle to fill Na Sarin’s cup, only to realize that it was already full.","The two women were drinking together for the first time in quite a while. Cheon-geuk had been the one to suggest it, yet she was the one distracted by other thoughts.","\"Are you worried about Warrior Baek?\"","Na Sarin understood her feelings better than anyone.","\"Yes. His opponent is Yeom Hwasin, after all.\"","\"That is certainly understandable.\"","\"I think I may regret falling in love with him.\"","\"Do you regret it?\"","\"To be honest, I thought I could walk away from my relationship with him at any time. I told myself that merely experiencing love with such a wonderful man was enough. Even when I first became intimate with him, I refused to attach too much meaning to it. I kept telling myself it was nothing significant and tried to control my feelings. But...\"","\"It isn’t that easy, is it?\"","\"I never knew I was this weak.\"","\"You aren’t weak. You’re strong.\"","\"Strong?\"","\"Of course. A weak person cannot truly love someone. Alliance Leader, keep loving him. That love will make you even stronger.\"","\"Thank you, Elder.\"","The two women had just raised their cups for a toast when a voice interrupted them.","\"May I join you?\"","An unexpected guest had visited the teahouse.","Astonishingly, it was Ak So-gun, the Murim Alliance Leader.","\"Alliance Leader.\"","Cheon-geuk and Na Sarin rose and greeted him respectfully.","Ak So-gun cupped his fists and returned their greeting. Although Cheon-geuk was young, she was still the leader of an organization, while the older Na Sarin was his senior in the martial world.","\"I was passing by when you suddenly came to mind, so I decided to stop in. I hope I haven’t interrupted a private moment between the two of you.\"","Judging by the bamboo hat pulled low over his head, he appeared to have left with only the bare minimum of guards.","\"What greater honor could there be than sharing a drink with the Murim Alliance Leader? Please, come and join us.\"","\"Thank you for saying that.\"","Ak So-gun joined the two women at their table. He picked up the wine bottle and moved to fill Na Sarin’s cup first.","\"Allow me to pour you a drink.\"","\"Alliance Leader, I should be serving you first.\"","\"This is a private gathering. As your junior in the martial world, allow me to pour you a cup.\"","Ak So-gun poured wine for Na Sarin.","If word spread that the Murim Alliance Leader had personally poured wine for an assassin, it would undoubtedly become the subject of all kinds of gossip.","However, Ak So-gun no longer cared.","Once the conflict with the Cheukcheon Alliance had been resolved, he intended to hand the position of Alliance Leader over to Baek So-cheon and retire from the martial world with On Byeokhwa.","After making that decision, he had finally freed himself from the opinions of others.","Looking back, he realized that he had spent his entire life bound by how the world perceived him.","\"Once again, thank you for saving my life in the past.\"","When Ak So-gun mentioned the time she had retrieved the Heavenly Outer Primordial Salve for him, Na Sarin responded modestly.","\"My insignificant talents merely happened to be useful for the right purpose. There is no need to think too much of it.\"","Na Sarin filled Ak So-gun’s cup in return.","The three of them drank together.","Although they were an unexpected combination, the atmosphere was pleasant. Na Sarin possessed extensive experience in the martial world and exceptional insight, allowing her to converse easily with Ak So-gun.","Cheon-geuk quietly drank while listening to their conversation.","After discussing various matters, Ak So-gun asked her,","\"Alliance Leader Cheon, do you know where Warrior Baek went to train?\"","In truth, Ak So-gun had not stopped by accidentally.","Zhuge Hyeon had reported that the Cheukcheon Alliance’s movements had changed after Baek So-cheon departed for training.","Ak So-gun was worried that Baek So-cheon might have become entangled with Yeom Hwasin. Knowing how close Baek So-cheon and Cheon-geuk were, he had come to ask her directly.","Cheon-geuk hesitated.","When Zhuge Hyeon had visited previously, she had lied and claimed that she did not know Baek So-cheon’s whereabouts. Now that the Alliance Leader had come personally to ask, she found herself in an uncomfortable position.","After a moment’s consideration, Cheon-geuk decided she could not lie twice.","\"When the chief strategist visited me earlier, I was unable to tell him the truth. However, I will be honest with you, Alliance Leader. He is currently with Yeom Hwasin.\"","\"As I suspected!\"","Ak So-gun appeared to have expected it to some extent.","However, his expression soon darkened as worry overwhelmed him.","\"This is all because I’m not capable enough.\"","Cheon-geuk drove the point home.","\"That’s right.\"","Ak So-gun flinched and stared at her in surprise. Na Sarin, who sat beside her, also turned toward Cheon-geuk in shock.","’Alliance Leader, are you drunk?’","However, Cheon-geuk was not drunk at all. She emptied her cup before continuing.","\"This happened because you and I are both weak. If we had been strong, would that bastard Yeom have been able to run rampant like this? Baek So-cheon was taken from us because we were weak. If not for him, war would already have broken out this spring. He is holding Yeom Hwasin back on our behalf—no, on behalf of the entire Murim. In that sense, Alliance Leader, this wine is a toast to our defeat.\"","Ak So-gun stared blankly for a moment before giving a hollow laugh.","\"You are right.\"","Who else in the world could speak to him so bluntly in such a situation?","Moreover, he was the Murim Alliance Leader. No matter what happened, everyone politely assured him that it was not his fault.","But now that he thought about it, how much comfort had those words ever provided? They had been nothing more than empty formalities.","Cheon-geuk’s frank honesty, however, was strangely comforting.","\"But let’s not worry too much.\"","Having already spoken so openly, Cheon-geuk continued.","\"I once read in a book that forty percent of our worries concern things that will never happen. It said that less than ten percent of our worries are about matters that truly require concern, but because we spend our time worrying about the other ninety percent, we fail to address what actually matters.\"","She repeated the same lesson about worrying that she had once shared with Baek So-cheon.","After listening to her, Ak So-gun’s expression brightened.","\"You are right, Alliance Leader Cheon. It seems that I, too, have been ignoring the things I should worry about while wasting my time on pointless concerns.\"","The three resumed drinking.","When they had emptied one bottle, Ak So-gun rose from his seat.","\"I should leave now. Thank you for the drinks.\"","\"Please take good care of yourself.\"","Just as Ak So-gun was about to leave, Cheon-geuk made an honest confession.","\"Actually, I haven’t been able to follow the advice about worrying that I just gave you. I spend the entire day doing nothing but worrying about him.\"","Ak So-gun smiled.","\"Isn’t that precisely why we continue reading books? Because the teachings written in them are not easy to follow, we read them repeatedly in an effort to discipline our hearts. Alliance Leader Cheon, may I visit you from time to time?\"","\"You’re welcome anytime.\"","They cupped their fists to one another before parting.","After leaving the teahouse, Ak So-gun walked along the road and gazed at the Alliance Leader’s residence in the distance.","\"Geukan.\"","\"Yes, Alliance Leader.\"","The voice of Chief Guard Pung Geukan answered from somewhere in the air.","\"When I leave the alliance and look around, I see an entirely new world like this. It seems I spent far too much time trapped inside that place.\"","After a brief pause, Pung Geukan answered,","\"Because you remained there, Alliance Leader, countless people were able to live freely in that new world.\"","A smile appeared on Ak So-gun’s lips.","\"Thank you for saying that. Let’s return.\"","With his bamboo hat pulled low, Ak So-gun began walking toward the Alliance Leader’s residence.","Standing beside the teahouse window, Cheon-geuk and Na Sarin watched him depart.","Meeting Ak So-gun had made Cheon-geuk think about Baek So-cheon even more.","\"What do you think he’s doing right now?\"","Na Sarin answered calmly.","\"Judging by everything we’ve seen from him until now...he is probably becoming stronger even at this very moment. And he is undoubtedly leaving an unforgettable impact on someone.\"","Cheon-geuk turned toward Na Sarin and forced a cheerful expression.","\"Then I’ll work just as hard. I’ll train diligently and try to become a positive influence on others.\"","Na Sarin smiled with satisfaction and nodded.","\"I believe you have already influenced someone.\"","***","Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin were drinking together in their assigned quarters.","Baek So-cheon had many questions for him.","\"What exactly is going on?\"","\"Where should I begin?\"","\"Let’s start with the Divine Physician of Life and Death. Why is he in the Northern Sea Ice Palace?\"","Seo Bingbing had claimed that he was not there, but that could not possibly be true. If he were not here, Yeom Hwasin would never have traveled such a great distance.","That, at least, was something Baek So-cheon could trust him about.","\"He has extremely deep ties to the Ice Palace. When the previous Palace Master was hovering between life and death, the Divine Physician of Life and Death saved her.\"","\"So that is why he is staying here.\"","\"That’s right. To be exact, he has lived here for the past four years.\"","Since Yeom Hwasin had even specified the length of time, it was clear that the Divine Physician of Life and Death was indeed here.","\"What relationship do you have with him?\"","\"The wounds you inflicted upon me in our last battle were more severe than they appeared.\"","\"Ah! So the Divine Physician of Life and Death was the one who treated you.\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"He disappeared from the martial world some time ago. Were you the one who kept him hidden?\"","\"Didn’t he disappear long before I was injured?\"","\"Then did you find him after he entered seclusion?\"","\"No. I don’t know how he learned about my condition, but he came to the Cheukcheon Alliance himself.\"","\"Are you saying he treated you of his own free will?\"","\"That’s right. He treated me voluntarily.\"","\"I can’t believe it.\"","\"I understand. He originally belonged to the orthodox side, after all. However, once you hear why he came to me, you’ll understand why he saved me.\"","\"Tell me.\"","\"In exchange for treating me, he asked me to kill someone.\"","\"...!\"","The Divine Physician of Life and Death, who had devoted his entire life to saving others, had asked Yeom Hwasin to kill someone?","It was difficult to believe, but Baek So-cheon could sense that Yeom Hwasin was not lying.","\"It was someone only I could kill.\"","\"Who was it?\"","An astonishing name emerged from Yeom Hwasin’s mouth.","\"The Murim Alliance Leader, Ak So-gun.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 124","paragraphs":["The Divine Physician of Life and Death (1)","\"The person the Divine Physician of Life and Death asked you to kill was the Alliance Leader?\"","Baek So-cheon was genuinely stunned. He had never imagined that Ak So-gun’s name would be mentioned.","\"That’s right. The man he asked me to kill was Ak So-gun.\"","What kind of grudge could have driven him to ask for the Alliance Leader’s death?","\"Do you know why?\"","\"I don’t. I didn’t bother asking. It was probably for some trivial reason anyway. In any case, Ak So-gun was someone I already intended to kill, so I was secretly delighted.\"","Baek So-cheon could tell that Yeom Hwasin was telling the truth.","\"If you’re that curious about the reason, ask him while you’re receiving treatment.\"","\"If he is the Alliance Leader’s enemy, will he really treat me?\"","\"Aren’t you the friend of the man who will kill Ak So-gun for him?\"","\"We aren’t friends.\"","\"Even if we aren’t, you should pretend that we are. That way, you’ll receive treatment.\"","\"To go that far...\"","Yeom Hwasin cut him off firmly.","\"You need the treatment.\"","Their gazes met in the air.","\"Very well. Since we’ve come this far, let’s find some way to get me treated.\"","\"Good. That’s more like you.\"","They emptied their cups and refilled each other’s. With one unexpected secret after another being revealed, Baek So-cheon found himself drinking without restraint.","\"Then how can the Absolute Prohibition be lifted?\"","\"There are two methods: an easy method and a difficult one.\"","\"What is the easy method?\"","\"Eliminate everyone who opposes lifting it. We send those trapped by the laws of the dead to join the ancestors they love so much.\"","\"That certainly sounds like your kind of solution. Why haven’t you used it?\"","Baek So-cheon believed Yeom Hwasin was entirely capable of killing them all. He could not allow the friendliness Yeom Hwasin showed him to make him forget the man’s true nature. If necessary, Yeom Hwasin was someone who could eradicate every last blade of grass in the Ice Palace.","\"Unfortunately, that would only make me feel better. It wouldn’t actually lift the restriction.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Instead of answering, Yeom Hwasin asked a new question.","\"Do you know why the experts of the Northern Sea Ice Palace have been unable to enter the Central Plains?\"","When Baek So-cheon shook his head, Yeom Hwasin revealed another hidden truth.","\"Because a restriction was placed upon them that allows their internal energy to function properly only in cold environments.\"","\"Ah!\"","It was a secret of the martial world that Baek So-cheon had never heard before.","\"Then how can the restriction be lifted?\"","\"One must enter the forbidden grounds of the Ice Palace and retrieve a secret treasure capable of lifting it. I’ve heard that with the treasure, the restriction can be removed permanently, allowing them to use their internal energy even outside cold regions.\"","\"Naturally, that must be difficult.\"","\"They say that not a single person has ever succeeded.\"","\"What happens if someone fails?\"","\"I don’t know. No one who failed ever emerged from that place. Unless they decided to settle down and start a family inside, they probably all died.\"","\"So you intend to enter and retrieve the treasure?\"","Yeom Hwasin did not answer.","When he merely stared at Baek So-cheon with a peculiar smile, Baek So-cheon immediately realized what he was plotting.","\"Surely you aren’t planning to send me inside.\"","\"Why wouldn’t I?\"","\"You...truly are unbelievable!\"","\"Once your internal energy is restored, I believe you’ll be better suited to handling it than I am. To be honest, breaking through forbidden grounds like that isn’t easy for a man my age. My judgment isn’t what it used to be, and my mind no longer works as quickly.\"","\"Is that really the only reason?\"","\"If you insist on another reason, haven’t I already told you? If you encounter a fortuitous opportunity or gain enlightenment while lifting the Absolute Prohibition, you will become even stronger than you are now.\"","\"You plan to fight a stronger version of me and use that battle to reach the next realm?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"What will you do if I become stronger than you?\"","\"Then I’ll die.\"","\"And you’re all right with that?\"","\"If I remain trapped at my current level for the rest of my life, I will live a life worse than death. Can you understand that feeling?\"","\"...I can.\"","Baek So-cheon truly understood him.","He would have felt the same way in Yeom Hwasin’s position.","At present, Baek So-cheon’s heart was entirely focused on leaving the Murim Alliance and living freely. But what if all that desire had instead been focused on martial arts? What if the next stage seemed almost within reach, yet he remained unable to cross the threshold?","What if that continued for the rest of his life?","\"It would be truly agonizing.\"","\"Ordinary people would say that martial arts of such a level should already be enough. They would say that excessive ambition only brings misery. Because that is the reality we live in, you are my one and only true confidant.\"","So that was it.","That was why Yeom Hwasin had allowed him to live.","Baek So-cheon understood that feeling better than anyone.","He raised his cup first.","\"Let’s drink.\"","Yeom Hwasin drank with him.","\"Very well. Let’s assume I agree to enter. Earlier, the opposition to lifting the Absolute Prohibition seemed intense. The elderly expert beside the Palace Master appeared especially furious.\"","\"That old woman is Shim Nahu. She is the Grand Elder of the Ice Palace and holds its real authority.\"","\"Will Elder Shim simply allow me to enter? No, before that, I doubt she’ll even allow them to treat my dantian.\"","Yeom Hwasin then revealed another fact.","\"I received my treatment here at the Ice Palace. Stabilizing my extreme yang internal energy required the Ice Palace’s Yin-Cold Ice Bed.\"","The Yin-Cold Ice Bed was an artifact of the Northern Sea Ice Palace that radiated a freezing chill. It was said that someone practicing extreme yin internal energy could gain far more power than usual by sitting upon it and circulating their energy.","It served a similar function to the Dragon Spring within the Murim Alliance’s Heavenly Dragon Secret Grounds.","\"Ah, so that is how you came to know the Palace Master.\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"Then why do they treat you so poorly?\"","\"Near the end of my treatment, I accidentally broke the Yin-Cold Ice Bed.\"","\"Good heavens! No wonder they’re angry!\"","\"However, they couldn’t hold me directly responsible. I hadn’t broken it intentionally.\"","Yeom Hwasin had probably experienced changes in his body while unconscious. Even if that had not been the case, they would have been unable to punish him because of his connection to the Divine Physician of Life and Death, who had saved the previous Palace Master’s life.","The moment Baek So-cheon heard that, a thought suddenly occurred to him.","\"Did you attain the Indestructible Vajra Body here?\"","\"That’s right. Around the time my treatment was completed, the extreme yin and extreme yang energies collided, causing a tremendous transformation in my body. The Yin-Cold Ice Bed shattered during the process through which I attained the Indestructible Vajra Body.\"","While Baek So-cheon had been wandering in despair after losing his internal energy, unimaginable events had been taking place here.","\"In any case, while I was receiving treatment, I had several opportunities to speak with Palace Master Seo. That was when I learned that she desperately wished to lift the Absolute Prohibition. Shim Nahu and the other elderly experts want to preserve it, while the younger experts wish to abolish it. Palace Master Seo only treated me coldly at first because she was mindful of them. In truth, she desperately hopes I’ll lift the Absolute Prohibition.\"","\"Is an outsider permitted to lift it?\"","\"I asked Palace Master Seo the same question last time. She told me that if the people of the Ice Palace had failed to lift it for so long, perhaps it had always been meant for an outsider to overcome. She said that believing an Ice Palace martial artist had to be the one to lift it was itself an outdated way of thinking. I told her she was clever.\"","Baek So-cheon chuckled.","In a sense, Seo Bingbing had also been drawn into Yeom Hwasin’s plans.","\"Until now, they couldn’t accept outsiders because of those old people. Outsiders weren’t even allowed to enter this place in the first place.\"","\"But that rule was broken because of you.\"","\"Change is necessary for progress.\"","Baek So-cheon finally had a rough understanding of the situation.","What would happen if the Northern Sea Ice Palace lifted its restriction and entered the Central Plains?","What role would it play in the Central Plains’ martial world?","Baek So-cheon asked honestly,","\"If their restriction is lifted and they enter the Central Plains, wouldn’t that disadvantage your side?\"","\"Why do you think it would?\"","\"Isn’t the Northern Sea Ice Palace closer to an orthodox faction?\"","\"That’s your misconception. Don’t assume people are righteous simply because they wear white clothes and smile. They are an organization that cares only about its own interests.\"","Baek So-cheon thought he had a point.","The people of the Ice Palace had been bound by the restriction for generations. Once it was lifted, they were hardly likely to submit themselves to a different form of restraint.","\"The situation in the Murim will become even more complicated.\"","Yeom Hwasin smiled and emptied his cup.","\"That benefits us. Don’t you orthodox factions always make mistakes whenever circumstances become complicated?\"","\"That is prejudice.\"","Baek So-cheon answered firmly, but he could not deny it entirely.","At the very least, the word \"turmoil\" was generally favorable to the Cheukcheon Alliance.","\"Although the Palace Master wishes to lift the prohibition, she didn’t seem able to express it openly.\"","\"Even as Palace Master, she cannot disregard Shim Nahu and her faction.\"","\"What do you plan to do?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"You don’t know?\"","\"From now on, you’ll have to handle it yourself.\"","\"Are you serious?\"","\"Of course. I can’t think of any method other than smashing everything to pieces.\"","\"You understood the situation and still brought me here without any plan?\"","\"You are the plan. Hahaha!\"","Yeom Hwasin heartily drank his wine, and Baek So-cheon emptied his cup alongside him.","Indeed, this was the moment when he needed to rely on his own methods instead of Yeom Hwasin’s.","\"Let me confirm one thing.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Are you certain that the Divine Physician of Life and Death is here?\"","\"I’m certain!\"","In that case, there was one method Baek So-cheon could attempt.","He did not know whether it would work.","***","The following day, Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin were summoned to the Palace Master’s residence again.","The elderly experts, including Shim Nahu, stood closest to Seo Bingbing, while the experts became progressively younger the farther they stood from her.","Now that Baek So-cheon understood the palace’s internal circumstances, he realized the arrangement was less about protection and more about surveillance.","Shim Nahu stepped forward in Seo Bingbing’s place.","\"You two must leave immediately.\"","Her tone was utterly cold.","Yeom Hwasin looked at Baek So-cheon with an expression that seemed to ask what he intended to do now.","Baek So-cheon addressed Seo Bingbing.","\"There is something I must convey before we leave.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"The Murim Alliance Leader said he had a message for the Divine Physician of Life and Death.\"","At the mention of the Murim Alliance Leader, everyone present flinched in surprise.","A smile appeared on Yeom Hwasin’s lips. He appeared to have guessed what method Baek So-cheon intended to use.","\"Tell us the message. I’ll deliver it to him later.\"","\"I must deliver it personally.\"","A brief silence followed.","Baek So-cheon spoke as though the matter were of no particular concern to him.","\"Understood. If the Divine Physician of Life and Death isn’t here, I’ll deliver it on another occasion. We should leave.\"","\"Let’s go.\"","Baek So-cheon cupped his fists in farewell and turned around without hesitation. Yeom Hwasin followed him.","They had taken a little over ten steps when a voice came from behind them.","\"Stop.\"","Baek So-cheon turned around.","A secret door in the rear wall stood open, and an old man was standing before it.","He was Won Gyeongdan, the Divine Physician of Life and Death.","He had been hiding behind the secret door and listening to their conversation.","Won Gyeongdan loudly asked Baek So-cheon,","\"What did that Ak fellow say to me?\"","Ordinarily, he should have shown proper respect by referring to him as Alliance Leader Ak. However, his urgency caused his true feelings to emerge.","\"Do you wish to hear the message here?\"","Baek So-cheon’s question startled the Divine Physician of Life and Death. In his urgency, he had rushed outside without considering the situation.","\"Let us speak privately.\"","Before Shim Nahu could interfere, Seo Bingbing addressed Won Gyeongdan first.","\"I will immediately arrange a private meeting between you and Great Hero Baek.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Seo Bingbing then turned to Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin.","\"Please go ahead and wait. The Divine Physician will join you shortly.\"","\"Understood.\"","Following an Ice Palace warrior’s guidance, Baek So-cheon and Yeom Hwasin left the hall.","When they reached the guest reception room and were alone, Yeom Hwasin burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! That was truly an excellent method.\"","\"It was nothing more than a petty deception.\"","If someone hated another person enough to want him dead, how could he not be curious about a message that person had supposedly sent?","Baek So-cheon had simply taken advantage of human nature.","\"Still, you lied without so much as blinking.\"","\"After spending time with a certain person, I’ve become like ink from staying too close to it.\"","\"I hope the ink stains you even blacker.\"","Indeed, Yeom Hwasin might have started this affair, but it had now become Baek So-cheon’s concern as well.","\"I’ll handle everything from this point onward. You can sit quietly beside me and eat.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 125","paragraphs":["The Divine Physician of Life and Death (2)","Grand Elder Shim Nahu blocked Won Gyeongdan, the Divine Physician of Life and Death, as he was on his way to meet Baek So-cheon.","\"Physician Won, I have something I wish to discuss with you.\"","\"Please speak, Grand Elder.\"","Until now, the two had always treated each other with the utmost courtesy. One was the Ice Palace’s benefactor and honored guest, while the other was the true authority who held its power firmly in her grasp.","\"I know you are busy, so I shall come straight to the point. What happened between you and the Murim Alliance Leader?\"","Won Gyeongdan’s expression stiffened slightly at her question. Even coming from the Grand Elder, it was exceedingly rude to ask him something like that.","\"It is a personal matter, so I cannot tell you.\"","\"This concerns the safety of our palace.\"","\"My personal affairs will not endanger your palace.\"","\"You must make absolutely certain that they do not.\"","\"I am busy, so I shall take my leave. We will speak again another time.\"","Neither of them looked pleased as they walked away.","Shim Nahu was displeased with Won Gyeongdan for appearing out of nowhere and causing trouble, while Won Gyeongdan could hardly have been pleased by her discourteous attitude.","Someone had been watching the exchange from afar.","It was the Ice Palace Lord, Seo Bingbing, accompanied by her bodyguard and most trusted subordinate, Lee Dan, also known as Chutae. Lee Dan was a remarkably handsome young man.","\"We must find a way to lift the Absolute Golden Decree this time.\"","Lee Dan answered her.","\"Everything depends on the meeting between Baek So-cheon and the Divine Physician.\"","Seo Bingbing turned to him.","\"Make sure Elder Shim’s people cannot approach the place where those two meet. She may try to ruin this.\"","\"Yes, understood.\"","Seo Bingbing looked up at the Ice Palace buildings, which glittered like jewels beneath the reflected sunlight.","\"Yes, they’re beautiful. So beautiful that I’m utterly sick of them.\"","***","Baek So-cheon and Won Gyeongdan sat facing each other alone.","Yeom Hwasin had excused himself, claiming that he needed to grind some ink, though he was probably secretly eavesdropping on their conversation.","\"Allow me to introduce myself properly. I am Baek So-cheon.\"","\"I am Won Gyeongdan.\"","\"I have long heard of your great reputation, Divine Physician.\"","\"What reputation could someone like me possibly have? You are the one known throughout the world.\"","After exchanging formal greetings, Won Gyeongdan got straight to the point.","\"What exactly did Alliance Leader Ak ask you to tell me?\"","\"That was a lie.\"","\"What?\"","\"I lied to lure you here. The Alliance Leader never said anything of the sort.\"","Won Gyeongdan rose from his seat with a displeased expression.","\"Then we have nothing more to discuss. I have no intention of restoring your internal energy, either, so you would do well to leave the palace at once.\"","As he turned to leave, Baek So-cheon spoke.","\"If you refuse to treat me, Alliance Leader Yeom will never grant your wish.\"","\"What?\"","Won Gyeongdan spun around in shock.","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"I know what you demanded of Alliance Leader Yeom in exchange for treating him.\"","Won Gyeongdan’s face hardened. He had specifically asked Yeom Hwasin to keep it an absolute secret, yet the man had revealed it to Baek So-cheon.","\"He promised me that he would kill him.\"","\"If he intended to keep that promise, the Murim Alliance Leader would already be dead.\"","\"We are talking about killing the Murim Alliance Leader. How could such a thing be easily accomplished?\"","\"Is that the excuse he gave you? With Alliance Leader Yeom’s current abilities, killing the Alliance Leader is far from impossible. He has simply chosen not to kill him.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Because he still needs the Alliance Leader.\"","\"Why does he need him?\"","\"Because he believes he can control me as long as the Alliance Leader remains alive.\"","\"You?\"","Baek So-cheon knew he would never change Won Gyeongdan’s mind without revealing at least part of the truth.","\"Do you still not understand? To Alliance Leader Yeom, you are merely someone to be used. And not only you. That is how he sees everyone around him.\"","Won Gyeongdan stared at Baek So-cheon before asking suspiciously,","\"Why are you telling me this? Do you think this will persuade me to treat you?\"","\"Would you tell me what happened between you and the Alliance Leader?\"","\"Why should I tell you such a thing?\"","\"For the sake of true revenge.\"","Until now, Baek So-cheon had been cooking with truth as his main ingredient. It was time to add a little falsehood as seasoning.","\"True revenge?\"","\"The fact that you wanted the Divine Physician to kill the Alliance Leader must mean your grudge against him runs extremely deep.\"","\"And?\"","\"There is a way to make him suffer even more than killing him would.\"","\"What way?\"","\"By letting me learn the truth. You know that the Alliance Leader treasures me more than anyone else.\"","Baek So-cheon explained how Ak Sogun had still refused to kill him even after being struck by the Heaven-Beyond Origin Drum.","\"That is the kind of relationship the Alliance Leader and I share. But if a shameful secret that left him unable to hold his head high were exposed to me, nothing could cause him greater anguish. He might even take his own life.\"","After saying this, Baek So-cheon apologized inwardly.","’Alliance Leader, I’m sorry. Given the circumstances, I hope you will understand.’","But what he truly needed to apologize for was what came next.","Still deeply suspicious, Won Gyeongdan asked,","\"If the two of you are so close, why would you do this to your Alliance Leader?\"","\"Because we are not as close as the world believes.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I discovered that the Alliance Leader has two faces.\"","Won Gyeongdan’s eyes gleamed.","\"You discovered it too? How?\"","As expected.","It was exactly as Baek So-cheon had predicted. Won Gyeongdan clearly saw Ak Sogun that way.","Baek So-cheon was taking a gamble. Part of him feared that Ak Sogun truly might have committed some unforgivable act.","Yet deep in his heart, he trusted Ak Sogun. Without that trust, he could never have attempted something like this.","\"After spending so many years with the Alliance Leader, I discovered his duplicitous nature. He is a cowardly man whose outward appearance is completely different from what lies within.\"","\"He is a thoroughly despicable bastard!\"","\"He even took back the sword he had bestowed upon me.\"","\"Exactly! That is how petty the bastard is.\"","When considered calmly, the story did not add up. Ak Sogun had only reclaimed the sword because he was trying to avoid taking Baek So-cheon’s life. Moreover, Baek So-cheon was currently wearing that very Ghost Shadow Sword at his waist.","However, Won Gyeongdan’s heart was already overflowing with resentment toward Ak Sogun, so he focused only on what appeared on the surface.","\"Very well. I will tell you the truth.\"","The suspicion in Won Gyeongdan’s eyes was replaced by hatred.","\"Ak Sogun stole the woman I loved. He even denied me the position of Divine Physician of the Murim Alliance so that he could take her away from me.\"","Baek So-cheon was so shocked and bewildered that he could not speak for a moment. It was a reason he had never imagined.","Won Gyeongdan glared at him venomously.","\"Why? You do not believe me?\"","\"That is not it. Would you explain exactly what happened?\"","\"There was a woman I loved. We shared a profound emotional bond. But then Ak Sogun stole her from me.\"","\"Who was she?\"","\"Someone you know.\"","\"Could you be referring to Senior On Byeokhwa, the former Secret Pavilion Lord?\"","\"Yes. It was her.\"","\"Ak Sogun truly committed a shameless act!\"","Until now, Baek So-cheon had referred to him as the Alliance Leader, but this time, he deliberately called him Ak Sogun.","Inside, however, he was relieved.","Had it been another woman, he might have remained uncertain. But Baek So-cheon knew On Byeokhwa well. He knew how deeply she and Ak Sogun loved each other and, more importantly, he knew her personality. She was absolutely not the kind of woman who would fall for another man without first properly ending things with the man she already loved.","\"How did you first meet Senior On?\"","\"I treated her father.\"","Perhaps remembering that time, Won Gyeongdan’s expression brightened.","\"You must have grown close to her because of that.\"","\"That is right.\"","\"Which of you confessed first?\"","\"Neither of us ever confessed. No, there was no need. We both knew how deeply we loved each other.\"","The moment he heard this, Baek So-cheon understood.","This old, pitiful physician had mistaken her gratitude toward the physician who saved her father for romantic affection.","\"Was she your first love?\"","\"She was also my last. I still love her even now.\"","Won Gyeongdan had never told anyone this before, and speaking it aloud left him feeling as though ten years of pent-up frustration had finally been washed away.","\"That bastard intended to ruin me completely. Is that not obvious from how he appointed that incompetent Ban Wollyang as the Murim Alliance’s Divine Physician instead of me?\"","Once his heart had become twisted, it caused him to see everything in a distorted light.","Ak Sogun and On Byeokhwa probably had no idea that Won Gyeongdan harbored such hatred. Most acts of vengeance born from hatred were like that. On Byeokhwa would likely be astonished to learn that he believed himself to be in love with her.","Won Gyeongdan’s sudden disappearance from the murim must also have coincided with the time Ak Sogun and On Byeokhwa fell in love.","\"Ah!\"","A sigh escaped Baek So-cheon.","When he had asked Yeom Hwasin why the Divine Physician of Life and Death bore such a grudge, the man had answered,","\"I don’t know. I saw no reason to pry. It would surely be something trivial anyway.\"","If Yeom Hwasin heard this reason, he would undoubtedly burst out laughing and declare that he had been right.","But Baek So-cheon did not think it was trivial.","To this old physician, who had never experienced love even once in his life, On Byeokhwa’s smile must have represented the love of a lifetime.","It had nothing to do with the intelligence that had allowed him to master the greatest medical arts under heaven.","Even the supreme masters of martial arts had gaping holes in their hearts. Yeom Hwasin, who kept a woman resembling his first love at his side, was the same. So was Baek So-cheon himself, who sought to complete his life by leaving everyone behind.","Won Gyeongdan smiled happily at Baek So-cheon’s sigh, mistaking it for disappointment in Ak Sogun.","\"Did he say that Alliance Leader Yeom would keep his promise only if I healed you?\"","\"He will.\"","\"Why does he want you healed?\"","At times like this, Won Gyeongdan displayed perfectly sound judgment. It was only when it came to that love affair that his mind became abnormal and warped by hatred.","\"He intends to make me his successor.\"","Just then, Yeom Hwasin’s voice transmission reached him.","—Hahahaha! Isn’t that what you truly want? Become my successor from now on! Hahahaha!","Baek So-cheon pretended not to hear and continued.","\"Otherwise, why would Alliance Leader Yeom spare the man who drove a sword through his chest? You treated him, so you should know better than anyone.\"","\"If I restore your martial arts, will you kill that Ak bastard?\"","Baek So-cheon knew that this was the most crucial moment.","His answer blended truth and lies.","\"Because of the affection we once shared, I cannot do that. But I will ensure that Alliance Leader Yeom keeps his promise to you.\"","\"Truly?\"","\"I mean it.\"","Won Gyeongdan smiled brightly.","\"Good. I will repair your dantian. Hahaha!\"","He was a man willing to do anything if killing Ak Sogun meant he could reclaim On Byeokhwa.","After Won Gyeongdan left, Yeom Hwasin entered the room.","\"Hahaha! Congratulations, my lying successor!\"","\"Stop joking. I’m not in the mood.\"","\"Why? Do you feel guilty for deceiving that old man so thoroughly?\"","\"That too. But more than anything, it leaves a bitter taste in my mouth. What exactly is affection between a man and a woman? Can it truly leave behind hatred this deep?\"","\"That is not affection. It is obsession. Obsession is like a snowball. Once it starts rolling, it grows without end.\"","Baek So-cheon nodded.","The snowball in Won Gyeongdan’s heart had probably grown so large that it could grow no further.","Had Baek So-cheon still been in his twenties, he would have been furious with Won Gyeongdan. He would have wanted to shout, You stupid old fool! If you’re going to lose your mind, at least do it quietly! What the hell do you think you’re doing?","But now, at the age of thirty-nine, he felt more pity than anger toward the man.","Then again, traveling together with Yeom Hwasin like this would have been unthinkable for his younger self.","\"You have broken through one obstacle, but another remains.\"","\"You mean Elder Shim?\"","\"You truly are clever. That’s right. That old woman will never permit the treatment. How do you intend to deal with Shim Nahu? No, don’t spoil the fun by telling me in advance. I’ll watch it myself.\"","Yeom Hwasin looked positively thrilled, as though he were about to watch a troupe perform in the marketplace.","\"This is the most important moment of your life. If you cannot overcome this hurdle, you will never recover your dantian. You will have to do everything within your power.\"","Baek So-cheon recalled how he had lied without the slightest change in expression and murmured,","\"Sometimes, even I wonder how far I am capable of going to achieve my goals...\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 126","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (3)","The Mythricon sword that Passing Dwarf had told me to give away with as much caution as possible.","Originally, I had planned to give it away only after someone provided proof that they had reached the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","But then some middle-aged man verified his identity in a bizarre way.","Apparently, he was fairly famous, because several people recognized him.","He was the teacher of the Hero who was currently on the run after being branded a traitor.","The revelation that such a man had been assigned to the investigation team caused an uproar in the Gallery.","’The manager seemed to know him too.’","More than anything, I couldn’t stop thinking about how shocked the manager had seemed.","They were so stunned that they even stopped adding exclamation marks to the end of every sentence.","Not only that, but they also sent me a private request.","[DontAbandonTheHero: Um... Mr. Grylls! May I ask you for a favor?!]","[Wild Grylls: What kind of favor?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: The gift you said you’d give to someone who proves they’re part of the investigation team! Could you give it to Mr. Ludwig, who just made that post?! I can vouch for him!]","[Wild Grylls: Do you know him?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: Yes! I know him very well!]","[Wild Grylls: Well, if the manager is asking...]","[DontAbandonTheHero: Thank you! The next time you do something that deserves a ban, I’ll grant you immunity!]","And thus, a transaction that wasn’t quite a transaction took place.","I could simply make another sword, so it wasn’t as though I was losing anything.","More importantly, the investigation team needed to survive after entering the forest and reach my location.","One might ask why I didn’t give them an elixir as well, but that was a different matter.","The elixir was something Starlight Princess had painstakingly created.","I might have obtained it through a trade, but it still contained her goodwill.","If I casually gave that goodwill away to someone else, Starlight Princess might feel uncomfortable.","That was simply how people’s feelings worked.","’Since they’re an investigation team, they should have brought various medicines with them.’","They would surely have prepared excellent medicines, even if none were as effective as an elixir.","All that remained was to wait for them to arrive.","No one knew how long it would take.","This was a region where space shifted unpredictably.","Moreover, the land itself was comparable in size to a small country. If we were unlucky, we might never encounter one another.","’They might settle down somewhere suitable, just like I did.’","If they could use the Gallery, locating them would be dozens of times easier.","However, it was common knowledge that the Gallery could not be accessed from within the Forest of Four Seasons.","Eldorado was convinced that it could be used here, but there was no way to know for certain.","Perhaps I was simply special.","’Would they have entered by now?’","I checked for posts written by the middle-aged man who had introduced himself as Ludwig.","He had not posted anything since receiving the sword.","It almost looked as though he had taken the gift and run.","I wished he had at least posted proof when he entered the Forest of Four Seasons, but there was nothing of the sort.","Perhaps he really was just an old-fashioned middle-aged man who had accepted the gift and immediately entered the forest.","’If the Gallery worked inside, he would’ve written something... What a shame.’","It had been not five minutes, but an entire hour.","Yet no new post appeared.","The Gallery users also seemed curious about Ludwig’s whereabouts, but there was no obvious way to find out.","Still, there was one indirect method.","I could ask the manager.","The manager could see the real-time locations of not only fixed-nickname users but anonymous users as well.","It was a privilege and authority unique to the manager.","That should allow us to figure out his general location.","’I should ask.’","The manager seemed to know him, and the matter was important to me as well.","I immediately sent the manager a message, hoping they were still browsing the Gallery.","[Wild Grylls: Manager, do you happen to know where the fixed-nickname user LudwigVanerold is? Is he still outside the Forest of Four Seasons?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: He’s still in front of the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons! I sent him a message, but he isn’t replying!]","[Wild Grylls: Do you think something happened?]","[DontAbandonTheHero: I don’t know either! I think we’ll have to wait and see!]","’Did something happen?’","That thought occurred to me after hearing the manager’s explanation.","The Gallery users had said that while they called it an investigation team, it was effectively a purge.","After all, anyone sent into the Forest of Four Seasons was highly likely to be officially declared \"missing.\"","\"Or maybe he’s too old-fashioned to know how to send messages?\"","It wasn’t entirely impossible.","However, there was no way to be certain of that either.","I could begin forming a proper plan only after the investigation team entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","’No. What plan?’","Space changed however it pleased in this place.","What could I possibly rely on besides luck?","If they were lucky, they might land in the same forest as me.","If they were unlucky, they could appear on the opposite side.","According to the manager, my current location was near the center of the Forest of Four Seasons.","The chances of encountering them were abysmal, but I had no choice except to believe it would happen.","’For now, let’s make some charcoal.’","There was almost nothing I could do until they entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","I had my own work to do, so I planned to focus on it for the time being.","’Let’s see. The charcoal kiln...’","The campfires I had lit until now had produced only a tiny amount of charcoal.","It wasn’t even enough to fill a single small container.","I consumed large quantities of charcoal whenever I forged swords or made other tools.","One way or another, I needed to obtain charcoal in bulk.","I knew nothing about this sort of thing, but I knew someone who did.","[Starlight Princess: The most important part of making charcoal is cutting off the oxygen supply.]","[Wild Grylls: Cutting off the oxygen supply?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Charcoal is produced through incomplete combustion, and depriving the fire of oxygen creates the necessary conditions. Would you like me to explain it in detail?]","[Wild Grylls: No, it’s fine. Thank you very much, though.]","[Starlight Princess: No problem. Feel free to ask me whenever you have a question related to alchemy.]","That person was Starlight Princess, a genius in the field of alchemy.","She was also the fixed-nickname user who had previously taught me about smoking food.","One might ask why I hadn’t consulted Allfather instead, but his area of expertise seemed different, so I asked Starlight Princess.","Passing Dwarf specialized in metallurgy—in other words, metals—so I had not even considered asking him.","’I need to cut off the oxygen supply...’","Cutting off the oxygen supply would cause incomplete combustion, thereby producing charcoal.","As I slowly pondered her advice, my eyes landed on the oven.","More precisely, I noticed the clay plastered into the gaps in the oven.","It had hardened by now and served as an adhesive.","’That’s it!’","Inspiration struck.","I immediately began gathering wood.","There was a path the leader gorilla had previously created with a single punch.","Since the fallen trees lay across the ground and formed the path, gathering wood was easy.","’I’ll follow that path later.’","After gathering the wood, I arranged it upright as though building a campfire.","Now I needed to light it—","Except I didn’t.","I first had to cover it with clay to cut off the oxygen supply.","If I applied clay directly to the wood, it would neither adhere properly nor remain in place.","’I’ll make a rough frame with branches.’","So I wrapped branches around the pile, particularly those that still had dried leaves attached.","Once they were all in place, I slathered clay over everything until it took the form of a kiln.","But I was not finished yet.","The wood needed to burn fiercely at first, so I made several ventilation holes throughout the kiln.","I also made an opening at the very top.","That was where I planned to insert the flame.","Fwoosh!","Finally, I placed a burning branch into the opening at the top and checked whether the wood had caught fire.","The upper section naturally burned well, but the bottom was what mattered.","That was why I had made the ventilation holes.","Once I was certain the lower section was burning properly, I sealed every vent and cut off the oxygen supply.","\"Cough! Cough! Ugh, that’s strong. Maybe I shouldn’t have checked.\"","I had opened one of the holes to see whether the wood was burning properly, only to inhale a lungful of smoke.","In any case, now that I had confirmed it was burning well, I could move on to something else.","’What’s the situation now?’","I accessed the Gallery and checked whether anything had changed.","However, Ludwig had not written any new posts. Instead, unverified rumors about the investigation team were circulating.","There had been internal strife within the investigation team. The gift Grylls had given Ludwig was so powerful that it had caused an incident.","All kinds of speculative posts were running rampant, but their credibility was virtually nonexistent.","’Why would they start fighting among themselves? Their chances of survival are already low enough.’","Please don’t fight.","Just enter peacefully and come meet me.","Well, honestly, there was no guarantee they would even be able to enter.","It would be better to treat it as nothing more than a faint hope.","After browsing the Gallery for a while, I closed it. Nothing in particular stood out.","’Wait. Even if they enter the forest, will they be able to reach me?’","Smoke occasionally rose high into the sky, but that would not be nearly enough.","Compasses did not work in this damned forest, and its terrain was difficult to comprehend, making it extremely easy to get lost.","I was fine because I had accumulated some experience and generally stuck to familiar routes, but newcomers could not possibly possess that kind of knowledge.","’I should at least make some signposts.’","I would place signposts around the forest so they could find my location.","It might seem a little ridiculous, but it was an effective method.","I immediately prepared my tools.","There were no signposts listed in the Auction House, so I had no choice but to make them myself.","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","There were trees everywhere nearby.","I fashioned a signpost from a suitably sized piece of dry wood.","I made a grooved board and a post separately, then fitted them together.","’It would be better to paint it white so it stands out, right?’","I bought paint from the Auction House.","Even that was expensive.","In the center of the arrow-shaped board, I drew a house.","A trapezoid atop a square, with a window drawn inside the square.","It was meant to indicate that someone lived there.","It looked presentable enough.","Its height reached somewhere between my chest and neck, so it should be easy to notice.","Title: Made a Signpost","Wild Grylls","I made a signpost just in case the investigation team passes nearby. I’m about to go set it up.","Members of the investigation team! If you see this, just follow the arrow! It points to where I am!","└ Heavenly Demon) You made it quite neatly. Between this and the sword, you appear to be exceptionally skilled with your hands.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you, haha.","└ Aren’t you getting your hopes up too much? Kekekeke.","└ I thought this bastard was joking, but he’s actually serious. Kekekeke.","└ What are you going to do if no one ever enters the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll hug Wonmo and sob.","└ Wild Grylls) Really?","└ Of course that was a lie. Ke.","└ Wild Grylls) You bastard. Keke.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) If you really do meet him, please welcome him warmly! Mr. Ludwig is a genuinely kind person.","└ Wild Grylls) Won’t that only matter if he actually enters the forest? There still hasn’t been any news about him coming in.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) That’s true! Honestly, I hope he doesn’t enter!","└ Wild Grylls) You’re crushing my hopes.","└ DontAbandonTheHero) I’m sorry, but I think it’s better for your hopes to be crushed than for someone’s life to be sacrificed meaninglessly!","└ Wild Grylls) Damn it. TT Now I have nothing to say.","└ That’s sad, Grylls... But the manager is right.","└ You’re the strange one. Normally, anyone who enters the Forest of Four Seasons dies within a few days.","└ Wild Grylls) If someone is reasonably skilled, their chances of survival should be higher. My senior survived here too.","└ Your senior? Don’t tell me you mean that skeleton.","└ Have you finally acknowledged him as your senior? Keke.","└ That’s strangely adorable. Kekekeke.","└ What did Wonmo do to deserve that? Kekekekeke.","└ Wild Grylls) He’s my only means of emotional healing.","└ Are you that lonely? Want me to come visit you?","Even the manager had indirectly told me to abandon hope, but I refused to give up!","Of course, that did not mean I wanted Ludwig to risk his life just to enter the forest.","I was simply... preparing for the possibility that the investigation team would become \"castaways.\"","’Are they still waiting outside the entrance?’","With that thought in mind, I made even more signposts.","I planned to install them along every route I had traveled thus far.","’I want to talk to another person too.’","After two weeks, loneliness was slowly beginning to creep in.","While Grylls was kindly making and installing signposts—","Bam!","\"Aaaaaaargh!\"","A holy knight went flying toward the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","He flailed his arms as though desperately protesting that he did not want to enter.","The holy knight remained visible for only a brief moment.","The instant he passed through the \"entrance\" to the Forest of Four Seasons, he vanished without a trace.","\"Whew...\"","The holy knight who had kicked him in the back—Ludwig—exhaled heavily.","Then he slowly turned and faced the hostile watchdogs.","Swoosh—","Ludwig leveled the sword that appeared to contain a flowing emerald galaxy.","Then, radiating a dazzling aura, he spoke.","\"Does anyone else wish to enter?\"","Just as Grylls had hoped, Ludwig was kindly \"procuring\" survivors for him."]},{"title":"Chapter 127","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (4)","Ludwig was rigid and frustratingly inflexible, but he was also a man who understood honor.","As a believer in Ares, as Ares’s shield, and as the teacher of the holy knights.","Everyone acknowledged Ludwig’s honor, and he himself took great pride in it.","Naturally, he could not help but become angry when that honor was tarnished—especially through underhanded means.","But perhaps the previous incident had been the last one that could still be contained.","No matter how fiercely he resisted, he would eventually be forced into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Now that he had been driven to the edge of a cliff, his actions seemed like nothing more than a desperate final struggle.","Even so, he stepped forward to preserve his honor until the very end.","And not merely his own honor, but the lives of others as well.","’They all escaped safely.’","Ludwig looked around.","Reis and the other members of the investigation team had already scattered in every direction.","Before long, they would become the \"seeds\" of a revolution.","All of this had been made possible by the sword—the one he had received as a gift immediately before entering the Forest of Four Seasons.","Even Ludwig himself regarded the power of the sword that gleamed like an emerald galaxy with awe.","He had fought countless battles as the Sword of Ares, yet he had never encountered a weapon this terrifying.","’If mishandled, this could easily become a demonic sword.’","Unlike the Holy Sword Revolution, it amplified its wielder’s abilities.","However, even the wielder struggled to control it, and a single mistake could result in the user cutting himself down.","It was fortunate that Ludwig had restrained himself while fighting.","Otherwise, he might have placed himself in grave danger.","’What manner of being could have created this sword?’","Its power was astonishingly great.","The problem was that it was excessively powerful.","It was so difficult to control that he could not focus solely on the battle. The slightest misstep caused his aura to run rampant.","Breathing heavily, Ludwig stared ahead.","The watchdogs were still glaring at him.","They all wore helmets, so he could not see their faces, but he could sense it clearly.","They were afraid.","\"What are you afraid of?\"","\"Come. Your enemy stands before you.\"","Ludwig spoke in his usual blunt voice.","If the Hero was the Sword of Ares, then Ludwig was the Shield of Ares.","For the watchdogs to break through him was practically unthinkable.","Moreover, Ludwig now held a terrifyingly powerful sword.","With the rest of the investigation team having escaped, the watchdogs had no options left.","They could attack Ludwig and die by his hand, or they could return and be purged by the Pope.","With the Forest of Four Seasons behind him, Ludwig had nowhere to flee either.","But neither did he possess the strength to break through the watchdogs.","He had pushed himself too hard while scattering the seeds of revolution.","He was managing to hold his ground only because of the sword.","Both sides were trapped in a complete deadlock.","There seemed to be no way out.","’What should we do?’","’What do you mean, what should we do? Why aren’t we attacking him already?!’","’Didn’t you see what just happened? The last people who tried were thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons!’","’Damn it. I wish there were a cliff behind him instead.’","The watchdogs whispered among themselves.","Ludwig was not the only thing they feared.","There was also the Forest of Four Seasons behind him.","The moment they entered that place, they would never emerge again.","Beginning with Archbishop Odon, several watchdogs had already been forced inside.","They had witnessed those people vanish without a trace the instant they crossed the entrance.","Naturally, they could not help hesitating.","’They are wavering.’","With the wisdom accumulated throughout his long life, Ludwig immediately sensed the atmosphere among the watchdogs.","They, too, were hesitating because they had been trapped with nowhere to go.","’Not that my own situation is any better.’","Ludwig’s prospects were far from bright.","In fact, they were bleak.","Even if he broke through the watchdogs and survived, his honor would be dragged through the mud.","As long as the Pope maintained an iron grip over Eldorado, manipulating the media would be a trivial matter.","Furthermore, Ludwig had been the Hero’s teacher.","That made him the perfect scapegoat.","They would claim that the Hero had fallen because Ludwig had corrupted her with his beliefs.","The outcome was so obvious that Ludwig could only chuckle bitterly.","Because he understood honor, he wished above all else to prevent his own from being disgraced.","’It was wise to deal with that pig first.’","With Archbishop Odon gone, there was no one left to issue orders.","Every senior member had either been killed by Ludwig or forcibly thrown into the Forest of Four Seasons.","No one knew whose orders to follow.","Confusion was the natural result.","\"It seems you understand your predicament. If you return like this, you will be purged. If you attack me, you will die.\"","\"I have a proposal.\"","At Ludwig’s words, the watchdogs looked at one another.","Their gazes silently asked whether they should hear him out.","But since they had no better solution, they decided to listen.","\"Even if you return now, the Pope will have you killed. The same will be true even if you kill me.\"","\"What? What are you talking about...?\"","\"No one desires to destroy my honor more than the Pope. Do you know why he arranged for me to disappear?\"","Ludwig was stubborn.","But he was not stupid.","His personality resembled that of a certain Gallery manager, tempered by many years of experience.","\"It is to prevent me from becoming a martyr.\"","\"Even if you bring him my head, the Pope will make every one of you disappear. He will fabricate some pretext and place the blame upon you. I will be declared missing, and you will be executed. Everyone who remembers what happened here will vanish.\"","It was not an absurd claim.","In fact, it was a highly plausible assumption.","The Pope had built his reputation by purging those he branded \"subversives.\"","To preserve that reputation, he would not care if dozens—or even hundreds—of innocent people became casualties.","The watchdogs were part of that scheme.","No matter what happened, their fate remained the same.","They were destined to die.","\"H-How are we supposed to believe that...?\"","\"Because he must have done the same thing to the Immortal King.\"","\"...\"","\"If he could drive an entire kingdom to ruin, destroying a single person would be easy. Countless people will die in the process.\"","The moment Ludwig mentioned the Immortal King, the watchdogs who had been about to object fell silent.","Eldorado had gone so far as to commit a massacre merely to ruin the king of a small nation.","There was no guarantee that the same cruelty would not be directed at them.","The reasoning fit too perfectly for the watchdogs not to waver.","The instant Ludwig sensed cracks forming in their faith, he made his proposal.","\"Therefore, flee.\"","\"Choose whether to escape beyond the Holy Kingdom’s borders or wait until I recover.\"","\"...Will you kill us once you recover?\"","A watchdog with a deep voice spoke.","Tension filled his words.","Ludwig stared silently at him before giving an unexpected answer.","\"No.\"","\"Then what will you do?\"","\"I will enter the Forest of Four Seasons.\"","\"What?\"","The unexpected answer left every member of the watchdog unit visibly bewildered.","That was only natural.","They had assumed that Ludwig had been struggling so desperately because he did not want to enter the Forest of Four Seasons.","But that was not the case.","In truth, Ludwig had resolved to enter the forest long ago.","He explained his reasoning so they could understand.","\"If I sacrifice my honor, I may preserve the honor of others. They can claim that I instilled corrupt beliefs in the Hero and turned her into a traitor.\"","\"...\"","The Pope had erected human shields to protect his own honor.","Ludwig, however, had chosen to become a shield himself.","It was an action befitting the Shield of Ares.","Perhaps Ludwig’s words and actions had stirred something within them.","One by one, the watchdogs hesitantly began lowering their weapons.","Their instinctive desire to survive.","The sincerity contained in Ludwig’s words.","Everything fit together perfectly, breaking their will to fight.","\"A wise decision.\"","\"...When will you enter?\"","\"In one hour.\"","The moment Ludwig answered, he sat cross-legged.","It was a posture for practicing his mana cultivation technique.","The watchdogs could not help but find it absurd.","The man who had threatened their lives moments earlier was now cultivating mana right in front of them?","His actions defied common sense, and murmurs naturally spread among them.","’Should we attack?’","’Are you insane? What if it’s a trap?’","’If he fully recovers, he might turn on us.’","’Ludwig would never do that. Trust him.’","In the end, the watchdogs trusted Ludwig.","They knew how upright he was.","Even without their earlier conversation, his character was anything but corrupt.","On the contrary, he was every bit as noble as the Hero.","While Ludwig practiced his cultivation technique, the watchdogs gradually withdrew.","Eventually, most of them retreated, leaving only a few behind to confirm that he entered the forest.","An hour passed, and Ludwig finished cultivating his mana.","He slowly opened his eyes and looked ahead.","Only two watchdogs remained in sight.","’It seems most of them have left.’","Even after sensing his surroundings, he detected no one else.","Ludwig slowly rose to his feet.","The watchdogs flinched when he stood, seemingly frightened before he had even done anything.","Ludwig stared at them before speaking in his characteristically blunt voice.","\"You two.\"","\"Y-Yes?\"","Ludwig’s tone was gentler than before, causing the watchdog to answer respectfully without even realizing it.","\"Are you the newest recruits?\"","\"Y-Yes?\"","\"I asked whether you are the newest recruits.\"","The unexpected question made the watchdogs glance at each other.","After hesitating, they answered in considerably timid voices.","\"Y-Yes, sir! That’s correct! I only recently completed my apprenticeship!\"","\"I joined one year before this fellow!\"","They answered with rigid military discipline.","Ludwig chuckled.","At the same time, he felt sorry for them.","Even such fresh-faced recruits had been dragged into this filthy business.","’What will become of the Holy Kingdom’s future?’","He had fulfilled his duty as the Shield of Ares, yet he had failed to protect the kingdom from within.","For the Holy Kingdom to regain its true form, its rotten parts would have to be carved away.","That role could not be fulfilled by a shield.","Only a \"sword\" could accomplish it.","Ludwig turned and looked toward the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","The entrance rippled like an aurora, revealing all manner of environments beyond it.","Ludwig feared little, but he was still human.","He, too, felt fear of the unknown.","’What kind of place... lies beyond this?’","Fear of the unknown.","And curiosity.","After a brief hesitation, Ludwig slowly extended his hand.","His hand passed through the aurora.","He felt nothing.","Having taken the first step, it was time to enter with his entire body.","He slowly closed his eyes and murmured.","’Ares, please protect me.’","Step. Step.","Moving both legs, Ludwig entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","A strange sensation enveloped his body.","He slowly opened his eyes.","\"...\"","The first thing he saw was an expansive grassland.","The entire plain was covered in green.","It looked nothing like a forest.","After staring blankly at the grassland, he turned around.","He should have been able to see the place where he had stood moments earlier.","Instead, as if it had all been a lie, there was nothing behind him but verdant grassland.","’Is this where the man called Wild Grylls lives?’","Ludwig immediately attempted to access the Gallery.","He was still unfamiliar with it, but accessing it itself was not difficult.","[The Gallery cannot be accessed in this region.]","Although it was easy enough to attempt, accessing it had become impossible.","Ludwig stared at the message before silently closing it.","The Gallery was inaccessible.","That could mean only one thing.","’This is undoubtedly the Forest of Four Seasons.’","The Gallery could not be used within the Forest of Four Seasons.","That fact had not changed.","Then how was Grylls able to use it?","The question suddenly occurred to him.","’I can ask him when I meet him.’","Ludwig slowly began walking.","The grassland might be vast, but he would surely encounter Grylls eventually.","He did not know when that would happen, but moving was far better than remaining still.","Of course—","Munch. Munch. Munch.","\"...\"","Searching for Grylls and the welcome he received were two entirely separate matters.","Ludwig tilted his head upward and stared at a certain animal.","Its body was predominantly yellow and covered in brown patterns.","Its long legs towered over Ludwig, and powerful muscles stood out beneath them.","But one feature drew his attention more than anything else.","It went beyond unusual and entered the realm of grotesque.","’Its neck...’","Its neck was absurdly long.","It was so long that the animal could effortlessly eat leaves from the tops of towering trees.","Its head, neck, and torso seemed almost entirely disconnected, giving it a bizarre appearance.","Even Ludwig, who possessed a wealth of worldly experience, had never seen such an animal before.","’...What kind of ridiculous animal is that?’","Had Grylls seen it, he would have called it a \"giraffe.\"","Ludwig watched the giraffe eat for a long while before shaking his head.","’This truly is hell.’","There was no other explanation for the existence of such a creature.","With that thought, Ludwig walked past the giraffe.","Munch, munch. Munch, munch.","The giraffe paid him no attention and continued happily eating leaves."]},{"title":"Chapter 128","paragraphs":["This Hellish Place (5)","The Forest of Four Seasons did not place everyone at the same starting point upon entry.","Unless people entered while holding hands, each person would inevitably begin in a different location.","Even if they did hold hands, there was no guarantee they would arrive in the same place.","People had been seen entering, but not a single one had ever come back out.","Still, after countless years of accumulated research, a few things had finally been learned about it.","One of them was that anyone entering the Forest of Four Seasons would be dropped into one of its regions at random.","Only someone truly fortunate would arrive near a person who had entered before them.","\"Ugh...\"","A paladin groaned as he rose to his feet.","His helmet concealed his face, but his attire made his affiliation obvious.","He was the senior surveillance officer whom Ludwig had kicked into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Ordinary paladins typically wore pure white armor, whereas the surveillance officers wore armor so dark it was nearly black.","It was originally armor worn by \"inquisitors,\" but those men had now become the Pope’s private soldiers.","\"Damn it. Where the hell am I now?\"","The surveillance officer looked around and cursed.","He already knew where he was, of course, but desperately wanted to deny it.","He vividly remembered Ludwig kicking him in the back and sending him into the Forest of Four Seasons.","’Damn it...’","He surveyed the scenery, which was completely different from how the Forest of Four Seasons had appeared from outside.","Instead of a lush green forest, the area was filled with dry, skeletal trees.","Whether it had been covered in volcanic ash or ravaged by a wildfire, everything was gray.","And that was not all. The ground was just as bad.","There was at least solid earth where the surveillance officer had fallen, but everything beyond it was a swamp.","’Was I lucky?’","If he had fallen directly into the swamp, he might have died the moment he entered.","That did not mean he was safe, however.","What kind of place was this?","It was the Forest of Four Seasons, known as hell on earth.","A demonic realm from which not a single survivor had ever returned.","The surveillance officer swallowed hard.","’It’s not over yet. That bastard Grylls was living here just fine.’","Even if no one had managed to escape, there was at least one survivor.","That fact gave the surveillance officer hope.","He then checked himself for injuries and inspected his weapon to ensure it was undamaged.","Aside from the spot where he had been kicked in the back, nothing particularly hurt.","[The Gallery cannot be accessed in this region.]","However, he could not access the Gallery.","He was also one of its users.","Having seen it in action, he knew just how useful the Gallery could be in an environment like this.","When a message appeared informing him that it was unavailable, he could only click his tongue.","’So much for it being accessible.’","Using Wild Grylls as evidence, the Pope had proclaimed that the Gallery could now be accessed from within the Forest of Four Seasons.","That propaganda had worked well enough to provide the impetus for dispatching the investigation team.","Only after entering the Forest of Four Seasons did the surveillance officer realize that the Pope had told a blatant lie.","There was a saying that everything leaving the Pope’s mouth—aside from carbon dioxide—was a lie.","The surveillance officer now wholeheartedly agreed.","His mistake had been falling for the Pope’s honeyed words.","’I’ll get out of here no matter what. I’m way stronger than that bastard. There’s no way I can’t escape.’","The surveillance officer ground his teeth.","He would escape within a few days and cut off Ludwig’s head.","The Pope was the true cause of all this, but he was far too powerful. So the surveillance officer directed his resentment toward the comparatively weaker Ludwig instead.","It was the typical behavior of one who bullied the weak and submitted to the strong—a blatant display of selfishness.","’First, I should check my mana.’","Before setting off, the surveillance officer examined the mana within his body.","His fierce battle with Ludwig had consumed a considerable amount of it.","Since he only needed to inspect it, there was no reason to perform the mana cultivation method.","\"...Hmm?\"","Then he noticed something strange.","The surveillance officer’s eyes widened slightly.","Normally, his mana should have been circulating, however faintly, yet it was not moving at all.","No.","It was circulating.","It was merely doing so at an absurdly slow pace.","Alarmed by this inexplicable phenomenon, he hurriedly tried to activate his mana.","’Wh-What’s wrong with my mana?’","It still refused to budge.","Only when he forced it to move could he barely sense it.","Fearing the worst, he even tried to manifest his aura, but it was useless.","His aura would not emerge either.","He had effectively been dropped here with nothing but his bare body.","His chances of survival had plummeted far lower than anticipated.","Suspecting that he might have suffered an injury without realizing it, the surveillance officer carefully examined himself.","Yet he found nothing unusual.","In the end, he risked the danger and began performing the mana cultivation method.","’Wh-What is this...?!’","The moment he began cultivating, he understood the cause.","It was the mana.","More precisely, it was not the mana inside his body, but the mana outside it.","The ambient mana was far too dense.","The mana outside his body was suppressing the mana within him.","It was the same principle by which water pressure in the deep sea crushed objects.","’That’s impossible! That bastard Grylls clearly...!’","The surveillance officer could not believe it.","This was entirely unexpected.","Grylls threw mana around at every opportunity, yet he himself could not use it at all.","He found it impossible to accept.","’No. If I have enough time...’","It was still too early to despair.","The surveillance officer steadied his shaken resolve.","If the external mana prevented him from using the mana inside his body, then he simply had to fill himself with the mana outside.","He did not know how long that would take, but it was not impossible.","’I need to find somewhere safe.’","The surveillance officer quickly assessed the situation.","This swamp was dangerous.","He had no idea what sort of monster might suddenly emerge from it.","The forest where Grylls lived would undoubtedly be much safer.","Having reached that conclusion, he began walking to escape the swamp.","Shing—","He also drew his sword so that he could respond at a moment’s notice.","Although he could not use mana, he still possessed considerable physical prowess and should be able to survive.","’Archbishop Odon should have entered before me... Where could he be?’","The surveillance officer thought of Odon, who had entered the Forest of Four Seasons ahead of him.","Like him, the clergyman had been forcibly sent inside by Ludwig.","He wondered whether he should search for Odon.","Unlike the surveillance officer, Odon specialized in support and possessed virtually no combat ability.","Furthermore, they had just discovered that mana could not be used in this region.","The longer Odon remained alone, the lower his chances of survival would become.","’There’s nothing I can do about the Archbishop. I should find the others first. There must be more people Ludwig sent in here like me.’","Unless something unexpected happened, the surveillance officer decided to abandon Odon without hesitation.","His own combat ability had already been cut in half.","He could not afford to protect someone who possessed no combat ability whatsoever.","Clergymen normally exercised healing abilities through divine power, but that was only possible when they actually possessed divine power.","It would not have been an exaggeration to say that Archbishop Odon had \"none,\" so the surveillance officer expected nothing from him.","After all, Odon had risen to the position of archbishop by attaching himself to the right faction.","If the surveillance officer wanted to escape this hellish forest, he needed to join forces with the strong—not with people who would become liabilities.","’Still... if I happen to run into him, I can’t exactly pretend I didn’t see him...’","The surveillance officer had just finished sorting out his thoughts when it happened.","[...please.]","A voice reached the surveillance officer’s ears.","At first, he thought he had misheard it.","He stopped walking and focused on the sound.","[...save me, please.]","This time, he heard it again, faint though it was. The surveillance officer hurriedly looked around.","He needed to determine exactly where the voice was coming from.","\"Is someone there?! If you are, speak louder!\"","Shouting in a swamp was not a wise thing to do.","A beast might hear him and approach. Given the circumstances, however, he had little choice.","The surveillance officer shouted at the top of his lungs, praying that his voice would reach whoever was out there.","[I’m here! Over here! I’m right here!]","This time, he heard it clearly. The surveillance officer turned toward the source of the voice.","It sounded slightly echoey, but he paid it no mind because of the language being spoken.","It was not the language of some foreign nation, but the language of Eldorado itself.","’And this voice... Archbishop Odon?’","The surveillance officer hurried toward the voice.","Perhaps fortune had favored him, and the Archbishop had regained consciousness close to where he had fallen.","He had just been calling the man useless, but another person was still another person.","’If worse comes to worst, I can use him as a human shield.’","What a shameless change of heart.","It perfectly demonstrated what desperation could reduce a person to.","[I’m right here! Is anyone there?!]","The voice grew closer and closer. Both of the surveillance officer’s feet sank into the water.","It only reached his ankles for now, so he ignored it. Confirming the source of the voice came first.","At last, he reached the place it was coming from.","\"A-Archbishop?! You’re alive?\"","[Oh! You came...!]","The surveillance officer found the Archbishop.","Surprisingly, he appeared completely unharmed.","The strange quality of his voice was suspicious, but otherwise, he looked far too healthy.","[Come this way. I believe the exit is over here.]","\"What? The exit...?\"","[Yes. Someone else helped me as well.]","Archbishop Odon pointed toward the exit with a benevolent expression. The surveillance officer’s suspicions deepened.","The direction he was pointing in led toward the deepest part of the swamp.","The water was already slightly above his ankles here, and anyone could tell that it was far deeper over there.","’Before that...’","There was something even stranger.","It was something he had only just noticed.","Archbishop Odon was short, while the water here was deep enough to cover one’s ankles.","So why was Archbishop Odon standing on top of the water?","Powerful individuals might be capable of walking across water, but Odon was not one of them.","It was strange.","More than merely strange, it was ominous.","\"Wh-Who the hell are you?!\"","[What? Whatever do you mean...?]","\"You vile monster! Reveal yourself!\"","The surveillance officer retreated and pointed his sword at the figure, his voice trembling with fear.","Perhaps it sensed the terror in his voice, because Odon—or rather, the creature disguised as Odon—stopped hiding itself.","Ssssh—","Odon’s form faded like a mirage.","What appeared in its place was, shockingly, a corpse.","It was a shriveled, emaciated corpse. A tentacle was tightly coiled around its neck as though it had been strangled.","The surveillance officer immediately recognized the corpse.","Anyone could tell that it was Odon.","’Wh-What the hell is this?!’","Rrrrrumble!","Whether or not he was horrified, an ominous phenomenon began within the swamp.","The ground started to shake as though an earthquake had struck.","Had Grylls been there, he would have fled the region without even looking back.","However, the surveillance officer had only just entered the Forest of Four Seasons for the first time.","He could do nothing but stand there dumbfounded until the monster made its move.","Splash!","A hand suddenly emerged from the deep pool.","It resembled a human hand, but its skin was smooth like that of an amphibian.","Perhaps as camouflage, the hand possessed a dull, musty color resembling tree bark.","SPLAAAASH!","The monster planted its hand against the ground and heaved itself fully into view.","The surveillance officer could only stare in horror at the creature, which was several times larger than he was.","It had hideous teeth, a long body, and an antenna protruding from its head.","Odon’s corpse had been dangling from that antenna.","Whoosh!","The hand-bearing anglerfish that had emerged from the depths of the swamp reached toward the surveillance officer.","The instant he saw it move, the surveillance officer hurriedly stepped backward in an attempt to escape.","But that very action led him to his death.","As had already been stated, this was a swamp.","Squelch!","\"Urgh!\"","If he had merely remained still, it would have taken longer for the swamp to swallow him.","The surveillance officer lost his balance and fell, and the swamp anglerfish did not miss its chance.","Grab!","\"Aaargh!\"","The swamp anglerfish seized the surveillance officer violently with its humanlike hand.","He struggled against the crushing pressure closing around his body, but it was useless.","He could not use mana in his current state.","He was destined to be devoured.","Crunch. Crunch.","Meanwhile, the swamp anglerfish placed Odon’s corpse, which it had caught with its antenna, into its mouth.","It chewed the corpse into pieces with its razor-sharp teeth.","The anglerfish then wrapped its tentacle-like antenna around the surveillance officer’s neck.","Squeeeze!","\"Ghhhhh...\"","A deflating wheeze escaped his throat, and it was not long before the strength began draining from his body.","Clunk!","His violent struggles had loosened his helmet, causing it to slip off and fall into the swamp.","Inside the armor was nothing but a shriveled mummy, just like Odon’s corpse.","Limp—","The swamp anglerfish released its grip, leaving the surveillance officer dangling from its antenna.","Having drained all his life force, the anglerfish descended into the deep water once more.","Only the antenna holding the surveillance officer remained above the surface.","[A-Archbishop?!]","Amazingly, the mouth of the surveillance officer’s mummified corpse moved, producing his voice.","It was an utterly grotesque sight, as though the antenna were controlling his body.","[You vile monster! Reveal yourself!]","It went beyond simply imitating his voice.","[Is anyone there?! There’s someone here! I need help!]","Its imitation was as perfect as if it had extracted all his memories.","[Please! Anyone—help me!]","The Forest of Four Seasons was a hellish place.","Thwack! Thwack! Thwack!","\"Phew. This should be enough, right?\"","I muttered in satisfaction as I hammered the signpost into the ground.","I had spent quite a lot of time making this signpost.","Still, seeing it firmly planted there filled me with pride.","’I hope they manage to survive.’"]},{"title":"Chapter 129","paragraphs":["Click (1)","After perfectly installing the signpost, I returned to the shelter.","It felt a little strange to say this when I was the one who had made it, but I had designed it so that anyone could easily tell people lived nearby.","Moreover, I had already advertised(?) it on the Gallery, so everyone should recognize it.","’Not that I expect to meet them anytime soon.’","I had taken every measure available to me, but I did not get my hopes up.","The Forest of Four Seasons covered an area comparable to a small country.","Above all, it was a place where space constantly shifted, so no one knew how we might encounter each other.","If we were lucky, we could meet soon. If we were unlucky, we might never meet for the rest of our lives.","’Or they might settle somewhere else...’","In the worst-case scenario, they might already be dead.","That was what worried me most.","Would the investigation team really be able to reach this place safely?","I had no way of knowing.","At least the admin’s location-tracking ability could give me some idea of their chances of survival.","’I just need to keep a close eye on Ludwig’s location.’","He was the registered user who had announced that he would enter the Forest of Four Seasons.","I planned to keep track of his movements.","The admin seemed worried about him as well, so I could simply ask for updates frequently.","If even the admin could no longer locate him, it would be genuinely heartbreaking.","’It’s not as if I’m safe either, though.’","I had plenty of problems of my own, but at least I had dependable allies.","There was Namu-Ppareumbo, who I suspected had fought the leader gorilla.","Then there was Wonmo, the owlbear cub whose presence was remarkably effective at soothing the mind.","The investigation team had nothing.","The presence or absence of a companion with overwhelming combat power like Namu-Ppareumbo would make an enormous difference.","’I really did well to survive back when I was so weak.’","I now had enough strength to endure even if a crisis arose, but that had not been true on my first day.","When the Mad Dog bit me, I thought I was screwed, and I had nearly died for real when I encountered the saber-toothed tiger.","Feeling grateful that I had survived until now, I arrived at the shelter.","’Still, I have work to do.’","I had given Ludwig my sword, so I no longer had a spare.","I needed to make a new one.","Fortunately, I had just produced a large amount of charcoal, so forging one would not be difficult.","I also had spare materials, allowing me to use them without hesitation.","’I should keep collecting mithril and orichalcum.’","I never knew when, where, or to whom I might end up giving another sword.","I should make two in total, including one I could give to someone else.","However, I intended to discuss it with the dwarf first.","Sending one off without consulting him would be rude.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. I’m going to send you another sword in a little while. Can you sharpen it for me?]","[Passing Dwarf: I don’t mind, but did you seriously give him that sword?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. He was entering the Forest of Four Seasons, so I figured I should give him something. It benefits me if they manage to survive somehow.]","[Passing Dwarf: You naïve fool. What are you going to do if that registered user killed everyone else and ran off? That sword is already terrifying enough.]","I understood what the dwarf was worried about.","He was concerned that Ludwig might take the sword and run.","It was a sword whose performance was so exceptional that even the Heavenly Demon had called it a bad thing.","The dwarf was suggesting that Ludwig might have become greedy and deserted the investigation team.","[Passing Dwarf: What is?]","[Wild Grylls: Honestly, it doesn’t really matter to me lol]","[Passing Dwarf: You bastard lololol You’re enjoying all the pleasure with none of the responsibility lololol]","[Wild Grylls: Everyone said he was a good person, though. The admin said he knew him too.]","[Passing Dwarf: Good grief. You did that just because you trusted what other people said? Hah... The milk’s already spilled, so you can’t take it back now.]","[Wild Grylls: But you know what?]","That was what I said, but the admin’s request had actually played a large part in my decision.","I would have hesitated if he had not asked me.","I had already learned through the Gallery that someone named Ludwig was part of the investigation team.","However, after seeing verification like the old man’s and receiving the admin’s request, I somehow felt that it would be fine to give him the sword.","’This should increase their chances of escaping, even if only slightly.’","The more attention the outside world paid to the Forest of Four Seasons, the higher my own chances of survival would become.","I also intended to try(?) my hardest to attract people’s attention.","The easiest way to do that was to spread mithrilcon.","However, if I mishandled it, a war could break out just as the dwarf had warned.","It was a metal everyone desperately wanted but could not obtain.","People were already frantic to get their hands on it.","If too much of it circulated, tragedy would inevitably follow.","Fortunately, it could not even be processed without a specialized furnace.","I intended to exploit the fact that I was the only person capable of making things from it.","Strange people might begin clinging to me, but I planned to ignore them whenever possible and create a deterrent.","[Wild Grylls: I finished making it. Sharpen it for me.]","[Passing Dwarf: The more I think about it, the more ridiculous it gets. Some people might never touch that metal once in their entire lives, while someone else has it spread all over his house and front yard lolol]","[Wild Grylls: You know what they say if you’re jealous, right? Hehe.]","[Passing Dwarf: Piss off lol]","From the dwarf’s perspective, I supposed it really was as easy as a single click.","In reality, it practically was.","The tremendous heat made it difficult, but the process itself was not particularly complicated.","Even if I failed, I had unlimited opportunities to try again, so I could work without feeling pressured.","I examined the newly returned sword from various angles before leaning it against the cave wall.","[Wild Grylls: I made another one. Sharpen this too.]","[Passing Dwarf: How long has it even been since you made the last one?]","[Wild Grylls: You just put them in together, melt them, and pour the metal into the mold. That’s it.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hahahaha, this is seriously ridiculous. Hey, do you even realize that’s also an insanely difficult process?]","[Wild Grylls: Not really? It worked because I did exactly what you told me. Hammering is the hardest part, isn’t it?]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s true, but... Haah. I don’t even know anymore. I’ll take the sword for now.]","Then I made one more sword.","It was a spare for my spare.","I would have liked to make yet another one, but it was already getting late, and I was running low on materials.","Besides, I now wanted to make something other than a sword.","A pickaxe, for example.","I already had the pickaxe the dwarf had given me, but I wanted to mine mithril more easily.","Since I had gone to the trouble of creating a new metal, I also wanted a new tool made from it.","’I should forge the pickaxe myself instead of casting it.’","This was how I would gradually improve my skills.","At the same time, I could give the dwarf something useful and receive his advice in return.","Without a proper master, it would be impossible for my skills to improve by leaps and bounds. However, as I had mentioned earlier, I had plenty of opportunities to practice.","’It’s already evening.’","While I was busy working, the sun had gradually descended, and the sky had begun to darken.","It was about time to prepare dinner and browse the Gallery while I was at it.","The more important of the two was browsing the Gallery.","An important post might have been buried while I was working.","’I wonder if Ludwig still hasn’t entered yet.’","I also considered the possibility that he had taken the sword and run, just as the dwarf feared.","This world was not as kind as I wanted to believe.","There were plenty of good people, but there were also plenty with rotten personalities.","[Apparently, the investigation team has scattered?]","I was browsing the Gallery after dinner and my cultivation session when I noticed that title.","So many new posts had appeared that I was checking mainly the popular ones, and one title immediately caught my attention.","It claimed that the investigation team dispatched by Eldorado had scattered in every direction.","There was no way I could simply pass over a title like that, so I immediately opened it.","Title: Apparently, the investigation team has scattered?","My clergyman friend just got back and told me. Apparently, the investigation team scattered at the entrance to the Forest of Four Seasons.","According to my friend, the leader of the investigation team started a rebellion and escaped, but I don’t know the details. Anyway, it’s true that the investigation team fled.","It’ll be in the newspapers soon enough, but I’m spoiling it early so the Gallery users won’t be too shocked.","└ Hey, you just spoiled some huge news, you bastard.","└ Become a clergyman too if you’re jealous.","I immediately sent the admin a message.","He must have seen the post as well.","Just as I expected, he had already read it and replied immediately.","└ I’d rather be a wealthy unemployed man than a clergyman lol","└ Honestly, I want to be a wealthy unemployed man too. It’s terrifying here T_T","└ Wait, doesn’t that mean all of Grylls’s friends are gone?","└ Oh lololol, you’re right lol","└ What will Grylls do now that he’s all alone...? He even made a signpost.","└ Starting a rebellion is still better than dying.","└ They were practically forced into the forest. I would’ve fought back too lololol","└ Didn’t they also have the sword Grylls gave them?","└ Yeah. I heard it looked like it contained a green galaxy. That description made me wonder if the bastard was lying lol","└ What kind of sword glows green? Lololol","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Just so you know, Mr. Ludwig isn’t the kind of person who would accept someone’s goodwill and run away! He always prays to the Goddess and performs good deeds!]","[Wild Grylls: Forget that. Do you know where he is right now?]","I wanted his location, not a defense of his character.","After seeing that post, his current location was the only thing that mattered.","The contents were deeply unsettling.","The investigation team had scattered in every direction.","My heart sank as I wondered whether the dwarf’s concerns had become reality.","Most users remained skeptical, but I had no choice but to believe the post.","The sword’s description perfectly matched the one I had given Ludwig.","’Th-Then where is Ludwig right now?’","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Well... I’m sorry, but I can’t determine his current location...!]","[Wild Grylls: What is that supposed to mean?;;]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: It’s true! I’m receiving a message saying that he’s somewhere his location cannot be determined!]","[Wild Grylls: Then what about me? That doesn’t make any sense.]","Was the admin lying to me?","The suspicion briefly crossed my mind.","He had been able to determine my location without any trouble before.","He had told me I was at the exact center of the Forest of Four Seasons.","Yet now he claimed he could not locate Ludwig.","It was a complete contradiction.","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: I swear to the Goddess! I can’t determine his location, but I can still send him messages!]","[Wild Grylls: What does that have to do with anything?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: If a registered user dies, I receive a message saying the user no longer exists! Therefore, there’s a high possibility that he entered the Forest of Four Seasons!]","[Wild Grylls: Even so, it’s a little strange that you can’t determine his location.;;]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: You were able to use the Gallery from the very beginning! It’s much more likely that you’re the exceptional case!]","[Wild Grylls: That’s extremely convincing.]","I was not being sarcastic.","It really was.","It was better to treat me as an exception.","How many times had everyone been astonished by the things I had done until now?","It would also be strange to judge my experiences solely by this world’s standards.","’Anyway, there’s a high probability that he entered the Forest of Four Seasons...’","In that case, there was nothing I could do right now.","Since even his location could not be tracked in real time, I had no choice but to wait patiently.","[Wild Grylls: I suppose we have no choice but to wait.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Um...! I know this is a difficult situation, but could you please find Mr. Ludwig?!]","[Wild Grylls: I might be able to guide him toward my location, but I don’t think I can search for him.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: That alone would be enough! I’ll help you as much as I can!]","[Wild Grylls: How?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Hmm...!]","The admin contemplated the matter for a while before cautiously replying.","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Whenever I pray to the Goddess, I could ask her to help you find Mr. Ludwig?]","[Wild Grylls: Does she grant your requests just because you pray?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Yes!]","His confident answer left me speechless.","Did the Goddess really answer his prayers?","If so, that was what you could truly call doing something with a single click.","’I’d be willing to close my eyes and pray if it really worked.’","Of course I would.","Pooooour!","\"Ah, seriously. Again?\"","I just wished she would make this damn rain stop first.","Rain fell frequently in the forest, as one might expect from such a region.","That rain restricted Grylls’s activities.","However, the grasslands were divided into wet and dry seasons, making their climate different from the forest’s.","During the dry season, there were no restrictions on movement, and animals could roam freely.","It was currently the dry season.","The same applied to Ludwig, who had newly entered the Forest of Four Seasons.","He stood motionless, staring at a cave.","Under normal circumstances, he would have entered and explored it. However, his current situation made him hesitate.","The powerful ambient mana had rendered him almost completely incapable of using his own.","Fortunately, given his level of skill, he could still wield a minuscule amount.","Shimmer—","Even that tiny amount was enough to make the sword radiate green light.","Ludwig alternated his gaze between the sword and the cave entrance before nodding.","’It would be best to investigate.’","If he was lucky, the cave might be empty.","With that hope in mind, he entered.","A short while later—","\"Raaaaaargh!\"","Ludwig began fleeing from a three-headed lion."]},{"title":"Chapter 130","paragraphs":["Click (2)","Who was the most confused by the Holy Nation of Eldorado’s decision to dispatch an investigation team?","Kadir, the previous Hero’s close friend?","No.","Ludwig’s family or the families of the other investigators?","Not them either.","It was Asella, the renegade Hero who had ties to Ludwig.","’What in the world is the Holy Nation...?’","Inside a room at an inn where she had barely managed to secure food and lodging, Asella carefully studied a newspaper under the light of a single lamp.","[Shocking! Was the Renegade Hero Created by the Paladins’ Instructor?]","[Corrupt Ideology Inevitably Gives Rise to Misguided Convictions.]","[Eldorado Begins Ideological Inspections: Those Who Do Not Pray to the Goddess Ares Once a Day to Be Considered Subversives.]","It had only been one day.","These articles had poured out just one day after news spread that the investigation team had fled.","Their condemnatory tone made it seem as though they had been prepared in advance.","Asella was bewildered.","What pained her most of all was what they were saying about Ludwig.","[Former Paladin Instructor Ludwig Revealed to Have Insulted Ares.]","[Ludwig, the Blasphemous Paladin—Where Is He Now?]","[Paladins Trained Under Ludwig to Undergo Extensive Investigation...]","Ludwig was an instructor responsible for raising and training paladins.","Asella knew better than anyone how upright and uncompromising he was.","Had she not grown under his teachings before being selected as the Hero?","He had treated Asella so warmly that even she could tell he was especially fond of her.","To Asella, an orphan who had grown up starved of an adult’s affection, Ludwig had practically been a father.","’There must be... some misunderstanding...’","Asella clutched the newspaper tightly.","Eldorado had repeatedly disappointed her of late.","Nevertheless, Eldorado was a nation founded to worship the gods, including Ares.","It was also Eldorado that had taken in an orphan like Asella and raised her into a respectable paladin.","’Is all of this... my fault?’","Asella recalled the moment she had drawn the Holy Sword, Revolution.","The instant she drew it, the Goddess herself delivered an oracle.","Its contents had been difficult to believe.","It was a deeply shocking prophecy declaring that Asella would destroy Eldorado.","At first, she thought it was a misunderstanding, but by the time she came to her senses, she had already become a fugitive.","Eldorado subsequently proclaimed her a renegade on a national scale, leading to the present situation.","’I’m not a renegade...’","Asella knew better than anyone that she had not betrayed her faith.","Therefore, she concluded that the Goddess Ares had misunderstood her.","The notion that a goddess could be mistaken might sound profoundly blasphemous.","However, Asella’s circumstances were more than sufficient to cause such cognitive dissonance.","’Even if I prove that I’m not a renegade... will Teacher be able to restore his honor?’","Ludwig’s reputation had already begun plummeting.","Eldorado completely controlled the press, and this was a considerable incident.","Even the Immortal King incident appeared to be getting quietly swept under the rug, leaving her heart heavy.","Recently, Eldorado had done nothing but disappoint her.","Perhaps this was its true face.","Perhaps it had merely worn the mask of a \"Holy Nation\" and pretended to be righteous all this time.","’The Holy Nation I knew wasn’t like this...’","The Eldorado Asella knew had truly been a beautiful place.","It was a nation where everyone lived happily under the protection of the gods, including the Goddess Ares.","It was a place protected by paladins devoted to service and sacrifice.","A place where even orphaned children could not only realize their dreams but become Heroes.","Yet Eldorado’s recent conduct was the complete opposite.","’It must have lost its way...’","Just as people sometimes lost their way, nations were likely no different.","Eldorado had originally been founded to resist the threat of the Demon King, Mephisto.","However, as culture developed, Mephisto began pursuing conciliatory policies.","He had become so obsessed with ball games that he came to consider violence taboo.","He had even offered a courteous apology, leaving Eldorado without a clear purpose.","’At times like this, you have to keep believing. Abandoning someone when they’re struggling is the worst thing you can do.’","It was one of the life lessons Ludwig had taught her.","Remaining beside those who were suffering was the true virtue of a paladin.","The same should apply even when the one suffering was a nation.","Asella steeled her resolve once more.","She remained completely unaware that she herself was one of the people suffering most in the entire world.","The other was currently working himself to the bone in the Forest of Four Seasons.","’I wonder what Mr. Grylls is doing right now?’","Curious about Grylls’s situation, Asella accessed the Gallery.","Because he had given Ludwig a sword, the investigation team had been able to scatter safely.","Had the newspapers not claimed that Ludwig had wielded an evil \"demonic sword\" to help wicked individuals escape?","Various testimonies had also been circulating throughout the Gallery, so Asella was certain it was Grylls’s gift.","[I Seriously Resent the Heavens.]","\"Huh?!\"","A strange sound escaped Asella as if she had bitten her tongue.","Anyone would have reacted that way after seeing the title of Grylls’s latest post.","Since ancient times, the heavens had been regarded as the domain of the gods.","Whether he meant it figuratively or literally, she could not simply ignore it.","’Has Mr. Grylls committed blasphemy again?’","Since he committed blasphemy at every opportunity, she immediately opened the post.","If that was what he was doing, she intended to give him a stern warning.","Title: I Seriously Resent the Heavens","Wild Grylls","(Video of rain pouring outside the cave)","How long has it even been since the last rainfall? Why the hell is it raining again?","The oven and furnace are fine because I covered them with waterproof tarps, but I think my fish traps are going to get washed away again.","The heavens definitely hate me. This is why I curse them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You resent the heavens...? Does that mean you dislike this lady as well?","└ Wild Grylls: No, no. You’re the exception, Heavenly Demon. Haha. You stand even higher than the heavens.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is also true.","└ Ugh, he’s going to wear his tongue out from all that flattery lololol","└ Just look at how perfectly those two play along with each other lololol","└ Are you two seriously using the Gallery to socialize? Lol","└ Are you going to the Forest of Four Seasons to socialize with them? Lolol","└ We should allow this one. That’s gone beyond ordinary socializing. ;;","└ Lololol, the Forest of Four Seasons should obviously be treated as an exception~","└ SwordMaster: Since you’re in a forest, it seems to rain frequently. Why not devote this opportunity entirely to training?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve been doing that constantly, but my aura just keeps getting bigger.","└ SwordMaster: Wait, what?;; What kind of training are you doing to become absurdly strong like that?","└ Wild Grylls: Nothing special... I eat, practice my cultivation method, consume an inner core, and practice my cultivation method again. That’s all.","└ SwordMaster: You consume inner cores as though they were medicine?","└ Wild Grylls: For now, yes. I’ve set aside enough for Ppareumbo to eat, but I still have extras. Is that strange?","└ SwordMaster: What the fuck? I’ve never met anyone who gobbles down inner cores like medicine. ;;","└ That’s why he’s becoming ridiculously strong lolololol","└ At this rate, won’t his aura eventually reach the heavens?","└ Is he going to shout, \"My aura is the aura that will pierce the heavens!\" someday?","└ Wasn’t that what that absurdly powerful Sword Saint used to shout? Lololol","└ Yeah, lololol. I thought it was so damn cool back then, but now it’s just... lolololol","└ What are you talking about? It’s still cool.","└ Starlight Princess: Don’t resent the heavens too much. I resented them too, but I was fortunate enough to survive.","└ Wild Grylls: That wasn’t the heavens. I was the one who helped you.","└ Starlight Princess: When you put it that way, I don’t really have anything to say. Still, you mustn’t think too negatively! It’s always important to maintain a positive attitude.","└ Wild Grylls: Was that how you lived, Starlight Princess?","└ Starlight Princess: No, haha. I spent every day waiting to die.","└ Wild Grylls: Ma’am...;;","└ Starlight Princess: But just as I met you, Mr. Grylls, you might meet a benefactor someday too!","└ When will that day come?","└ One thing’s for sure—it’ll take months at the very least lolol","└ Apparently, Ludwig entered the Forest of Four Seasons, so they’ll meet someday. In heaven, of course. Lol","└ Youuuuu are seriously horrible lololol","The post had not been expressing resentment toward Ares, but toward the sky itself.","Still, his dislike of the gods was indirectly apparent throughout it.","’A person who hates the gods because he doesn’t want to hate people...’","Asella was troubled.","Would she be able to change Grylls’s mind?","Yet if he could not resent the gods, he would probably begin resenting people instead.","Grylls’s mindset was something she would need to contemplate carefully.","Humans were creatures incapable of living normally without hating something.","There was a reason their emotions were described through joy, anger, sorrow, and pleasure.","’Then I should guide him toward hating them a little less!’","Asella’s characteristic optimism asserted itself.","She left a comment on Grylls’s post, where new replies were still appearing steadily.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: At times like this, you should pray to the heavens! Try praying for the rain to stop!","└ Wild Grylls: Stop trying to sell me snake oil.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Gods don’t sell snake oil!!! Please, just listen to me this once!","└ Wild Grylls: Sigh. Fine. What am I supposed to say?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: \"I beseech Ares, Goddess of War and Wisdom. Please quell the heavens’ wrath and grant me the freedom to go about my activities!\"","└ Wild Grylls: Just wait. I’ll go pray with all my heart.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Very good!","Asella quietly waited for his next comment, praying that something good would happen.","About thirty seconds passed.","Grylls did not leave another comment.","Instead, he created a new post that made Asella’s eyes widen.","[You Fraudulent Admin!!!]","Wondering what had happened, she opened it without hesitation.","Title: You Fraudulent Admin!!!","Wild Grylls","(Video of a torrential downpour outside the cave, as though a hole had opened in the sky)","What? God will listen if I pray?","What a load of crap. The gods definitely hate me too.","Perhaps all her persuasion had borne fruit, because Grylls had replied that he would pray.","In truth, Grylls had only done it because he had nothing better to do, but Asella was simply delighted.","’This should help him let go of at least some of his hatred toward the gods.’","He had prayed, only for the rain to become even heavier.","That was the entire point of his post.","Asella stared blankly at the Gallery for a moment before quietly disconnecting.","’Lady Ares can’t grant every prayer!’","It was an answer befitting the ever-optimistic Asella.","Knock, knock, knock—","\"Excuse me, guest. Are you inside?\"","Someone knocked on the door just as she closed the Gallery.","Asella recognized the voice as the innkeeper’s, but immediately began circulating her mana on instinct.","Once her mana was circulating, she examined not only the presence behind the door but every presence throughout the inn.","’There’s someone... beside the innkeeper.’","It was not merely their presence that was suspicious.","’Are you certain she’s here?’","’Yes. I distinctly saw her orange hair.’","’Then we will enter immediately. You will receive your reward after we capture the renegade alive.’","’Oh, thank you very much.’","They were speaking extremely quietly, but Asella heard every word.","Rather than the sounds directly reaching her ears, it felt as though their presences themselves had taken form.","’They’ve already tracked me down...’","She had not even stayed here for several days, yet her pursuers had already caught up.","Asella bit her lip and hurriedly prepared to leave.","The first thing she did was seize the Holy Sword, Revolution, before heading toward the window.","’I still need more time. Time for this misunderstanding to be resolved.’","Asella opened the window and leaped outside.","Crash!","At the same moment, she heard the door being forced open.","The pursuit squad had smashed it down.","Of course, Asella had already escaped through the window, leaving them with nothing to find.","’Goddess, please grant me the strength to overcome these trials.’","Without losing her faith in the Goddess, Asella fled.","At the same time Asella began running to shake off her pursuers—","\"Aaaaaagh! You bastards! Get lost!! This is my home!\"","\"Kyeeeeng!\"","\"Keeng! Kek!\"","Grylls was struggling against an unexpected wave of beasts.","\"Get out of my house right now!\""]},{"title":"Chapter 131","paragraphs":["Click (3)","I really hate rain. I hated it even before I fell into this godforsaken place.When it rained, I couldn’t see the clear blue sky, and the weather became unbearably humid.","The rainy season was especially awful. It was already hot enough, but the humidity went completely berserk on top of that. It felt like it was going to kill me.","If air conditioners had never been invented, wouldn’t I have melted into a puddle long ago?","Rumble—!!","\"What absolutely fucking shitty weather.\"","I cursed as I watched the torrential rain pouring down so heavily that it nearly blocked my entire field of vision.","I had even prayed for the rain to stop, but what the hell was this?","Instead of answering my prayer, someone had punched a hole in the sky.","This was why I hated gods. I liked religious people, but I hated gods.","’Does that bastard seriously hate me so much that he’s telling me to go fuck myself?’","If so, what a petty bastard. I shook my head.","Anyway, since this was the first rain in almost a week, I had prepared thoroughly.","I put up waterproof covers to keep the oven and furnace from getting wet, and I brought the container holding the fish into the cave.","Unfortunately, I had no choice but to leave the fish traps in the river where they were. It had been raining since morning.","The rain had startled me awake, and I had rushed around taking emergency measures.","\"I’ll have to learn the signs that rain is coming.\"","I had roughly figured out how often it rained. But if I could identify the warning signs, I would be able to prepare much more reliably.","It would be nice if I could rely on common knowledge from my original world, but...","This was the Four Seasons Forest. Ordinary common sense didn’t apply here.","I would have to identify the warning signs unique to the Four Seasons Forest.","’When is this going to stop?’","I gazed outside at the downpour. It showed no sign of letting up.","This storm was on an entirely different level from the last one. The river must have risen tremendously by now.","And as the water rose, all sorts of sea creatures would probably swim upstream.","’What’ll come up this time? Surely it won’t be something like a shark, right?’","It would be best to remain on high alert for a while. I didn’t want to get robbed blind again like last time.","I was blankly watching the endless rain when—","\"Keeeeng!\"","\"Hm?\"","An animal’s cry pierced through the pounding rain.","Wondering what was happening, I looked outside the cave.","\"Keeeeeng!\"","\"Keng! Keng!\"","\"Squeak! Squeak!\"","A whole crowd of small to medium-sized animals had gathered outside the cave.","There were raccoons like the one Fast Sloth had butchered last time, along with rabbits, deer, wild boars, enormous rats, and even animals I had never seen before.","Just as I wondered why these creatures were gathered outside, the raccoon standing at the very front met my gaze.","\"Keng! Keeeng!\"","\"Squeak-squeak?\"","\"Oink?\"","I had a bad feeling about this. I cautiously closed the iron gate.","The moment those animals flooded into the cave, the place would descend into chaos.","Besides, there was no telling what diseases those beasts might be carrying.","\"Kek! Kek-kek!\"","When the raccoon saw me quietly closing the gate, it pointed a finger at me and began protesting.","It seemed to be saying something along the lines of, \"We should all help one another survive! Do you only care about yourself, you selfish bastard?!\"","My answer was extremely simple.","I casually raised my middle finger.","I had no idea whether the animals understood its meaning, but as long as it made me feel better, that was enough.","’You can’t trust these damn beasts.’","Of course, Fast Sloth—the one who lived in symbiosis with the adorable Wonmo—was an exception.","More importantly, these animals were partly to blame. They should have built their homes sooner.","’Not that I’m in any position to say that after stealing this cave from its original owner...’","Anyway, I wasn’t letting anyone into this house. They were welcome to try forcing their way in.","I snorted and firmly barricaded the cave entrance. Apparently, the raccoon had an idea of its own.","\"Keng!\"","\"Oiiink!\"","The raccoon slapped the wild boar on the flank.","The boar immediately began pawing the ground with its hind legs as if preparing to charge.","The moment I saw that, an instinctive sense of unease washed over me.","That bastard was definitely going to charge.","In that case, I had only one option.","Heavy armament.","Those bastards couldn’t get past the iron gate anyway, so I could use it to wage a defensive siege.","\"Oiiiiink—!!!\"","While I was equipping myself, the boar charged at tremendous speed.","Perhaps it was only natural for an animal that inhabited the Four Seasons Forest, but its speed was extraordinary.","The same went for its size. It was as huge as one of the monsters from an old movie.","However, after surviving in the Four Seasons Forest for half a month, I had learned one important lesson.","Shunk—!!","And that was that range was everything.","Whoever had the longer reach was king.","Before the boar could slam into the iron gate, I drove my aura straight through the center of its forehead.","It might have been a little risky if I were still using the Heavenly Demon’s Sword.","But the weapon I was holding now was the Mithricon Sword.","Its physical size had already grown to ridiculous proportions, and the aura blade produced by the Mithricon Sword was even larger.","Thanks to that, I stopped the boar before it could collide with the gate.","Thud!","The boar collapsed with its forehead pierced through.","The impact sent a tremor and a deafening thud through the pounding rain.","Most of the beasts appeared stunned, apparently never imagining that the boar would die so easily.","Keeping my flame-like aura blazing around the sword, I beckoned with the blade.","\"Come at me.\"","\"Come at me, you fucking beasts! Come at me!!\"","\"Keeeeeng!!!\"","And thus began a siege fought across a single iron gate.","Using my overwhelming reach and the gate as a barrier, I fought to keep the animals from getting inside.","Clang—!","I occasionally took some damage from the rabbits and deer, whose kicks were incredibly powerful.","Thank goodness it was an iron gate. If it had been made of wood, it would have shattered long ago.","\"Get the hell out of my house!!!\"","\"Keeeeeng!\"","The siege to defend my home finally ended with the death of their leader—the raccoon.","Once the raccoon died, the other animals scattered in every direction.","Still breathing heavily from the unexpected siege, I eventually collapsed onto the ground.","’Seriously, the craziest things keep happening...’","It hadn’t been like this last time. How strange.","Maybe the torrential rain had destroyed all their homes.","I let out a long sigh and looked beyond the iron gate.","Various animals lay dead outside, including the boar I had killed first.","I would have liked to butcher them, but I didn’t have the time.","’And with all this rain, they’ll rot quickly.’","It was a shame, but I would probably have to throw them away.","I could just dig a pit and bury them—the same place where I had buried the gorillas.","Title: Just Fought a Siege","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the dead animals outside)","(Photo of the iron gate on the verge of breaking)","These beasts suddenly tried to force their way into my house, so I fought a siege against them.","If the homeowner says no, that means no. What kind of animals try to barge in by force? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Could you not have shown them a little mercy? If you behave too heartlessly, you are bound to lose the people’s support.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not living in civilization. I’m in the wilderness ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Ah, right. I had forgotten. It slipped my mind for a moment.","└ Sword Master: A siege against animals... How absurd. You weren’t injured, were you?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. I just sliced them apart with aura from a distance, and they all died.","└ Sword Master: It seems to have been strangely effective.","└ What did the animals do wrong? They only wanted shelter from the rain...","└ Wild Grylls: Last time, I saw some raccoon steal my fasting pills. That taught me never to trust those damn beasts.","└ Didn’t Fast Sloth tear that one in half?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah, yeah. Still better than letting them make a mess of my house.","└ By the way, has anyone ever fought a siege against ordinary animals rather than monsters?","└ Humanoid monsters like orcs and goblins sometimes raid settlements, but I’ve never heard of animals doing it.","└ It has happened. Wolves are the animals that have fought humans most frequently.","└ Why aren’t there any wolves among those animals? You’d normally expect to see some.","└ They’re territorial animals, so maybe they’re somewhere else?","After watching the users converse among themselves, I closed the Gallery.","When I looked outside again, the rain seemed slightly weaker than before.","It would probably stop in about an hour.","’From now on, I should assume it’ll rain roughly once a week...’","Animals come looking for shelter whenever it rains heavily.","I recorded that in my journal.","Completely unaware that I had just fought a grueling siege, Wonmo was sleeping without a care in the world.","Then again, the siege had been entirely unexpected, so I could understand.","Drip— Drip—","The rain stopped roughly an hour later. I looked outside.","The bright sun greeted me as if it had never rained at all.","Thud! Thud!","Not that it helped me much. I still had to go through the trouble of burying all the animal carcasses.","Praying that no earthworms would appear, I dug into the ground.","Fortunately, no enormous earthworms emerged.","\"Pwah!\"","\"...And what are you supposed to be?\"","Only a strange mole popped out.","The mole stared at me with its bright, round eyes before hurriedly scurrying away.","Apparently, it had been hiding underground when the sudden downpour flooded its home.","After staring after it in disbelief for a moment, I finished burying the animal carcasses.","’The drainage channels are working properly... I guess the only thing left is to head upriver.’","The river would still be greatly swollen, so there was no need to rush.","I had plenty of other things to do anyway, so taking my time was fine.","’If this happens every time it rains, it’s going to be a serious headache.’","Now I had to consider not only the animals inhabiting the Four Seasons Forest, but the weather as well.","I checked the oven and furnace for damage, then armed myself.","Since I had no idea what might emerge from the swollen river, I equipped the Heavenly Demon’s Sword instead of the Mithricon Sword.","Wonmo was still sleeping peacefully, so I left Fast Sloth behind to watch over him.","By the time I reached the river, I came face-to-face with exactly what I had expected.","Roooooar—!!!","\"Goddammit.\"","I cursed as I stared at the swollen river.","It looked like someone had turned a waterfall sideways.","Naturally, the fish traps I had installed had been swept away without a trace.","Fortunately, there was something to salvage around the riverbank. Several fish were flopping around on the ground nearby.","If I took them back with me, they should be enough to last until I obtained new traps.","’But...’","One fish in particular caught my eye.","Last time, it had been an eel. This time, it was a pufferfish.","Yes, a pufferfish—the kind with a round body shaped like Wonmo’s.","A creature that lived in the sea had somehow been swept all the way here.","’Did it rain over the ocean too? Or what?’","Some species of eel lived in freshwater, so I could understand that much. But the pufferfish was even stranger.","It should have been a species that lived exclusively in the sea, so by what mechanism had it been swept all the way here?","Of course, regardless of the answer, I had no intention of eating it.","Pufferfish were poisonous.","Their poison alone was enough to kill a person. And since this was the Four Seasons Forest, the poison would be worse, if anything—certainly not milder.","’I’ve heard they’re incredibly difficult to prepare too.’","You could get away with preparing an ordinary fish rather carelessly, but not a pufferfish.","They were notoriously tricky to handle. Simply \"following along\" with someone else’s instructions wouldn’t cut it.","According to the Gallery, countless people had died after watching videos on how to prepare pufferfish and trying it themselves.","Unless you were a professional, it was best not even to touch one.","’Just to be safe, I should send it back.’","Holding my shield in front of me, I gently nudged the pufferfish toward the river.","Apparently feeling threatened, the pufferfish puffed up its body.","Now that I looked more closely, it wasn’t an ordinary pufferfish. It was a porcupinefish covered in spines.","The instant one of those spines pricked me, I would probably be poisoned.","The medicine the All-Father had given me had granted me resistance to poison, but there was still no harm in being careful.","’I’ll send you back home, so hurry up and go.’","I was gently tapping the pufferfish and rolling it along when—","Grrrrrrumble—!!!","An ominous noise came from its body.","Boom-boom-boom—!!!","Its spines literally exploded in every direction.","Fortunately, I had raised my shield the instant I sensed danger, so I suffered practically no damage.","The problem was that it didn’t end there.","Boom! Bang! Bang! Kaboom!","The ejected spines exploded again, releasing clouds of purple mist.","It puffed up its body once, fired its spines twice, and then made those spines explode for a third layer of defense.","\"...\"","I couldn’t help but marvel at the fact that it possessed three separate self-defense mechanisms.","And even that wasn’t the end.","Sssshhh—","New spines regenerated from its smooth body like a shark replacing its teeth.","The moment I saw that, I freaked out, abandoned my plan to gently push it back, and kicked it as hard as I could.","Splash!","My kick sent the pufferfish sailing directly into the river.","Now it would drift downstream to the lake—or perhaps return to the sea.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","Coughing violently, I hurried back home.","’How did this happen when I was being so careful?’","This truly was an astonishing place.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 132","paragraphs":["Click (4)","I had finally come to a realization.","This damned forest was the complete opposite of a children’s fairy tale.","Things that looked obviously dangerous—bears, tigers, and even the Guardian, for example—were actually manageable.","Their appearance instinctively warned you that they were dangerous and that your life would be at risk if you failed to respond.","But that wasn’t true of the little ones.","Things that looked ordinary—or were genuinely tiny—were far more dangerous.","It was the same in martial arts novels.","Beware of children, the elderly, and women.","Small creatures had survived in the Four Seasons Forest despite their diminutive size.","And what did that mean?","It meant they possessed at least two ways of utterly fucking up their opponents.","Why two instead of one?","One was a visible move meant to threaten the enemy.","The other was an unexpected trump card designed to catch the enemy completely off guard.","I had concluded that a creature needed both to survive in the Four Seasons Forest.","Until now, that had been closer to speculation.","But after what the porcupinefish had just done to me, I was certain.","’The saying \"small peppers are the hottest\" fits perfectly.’","Except this pepper wasn’t merely spicy. Eating it would literally melt my body.","At this rate, would a yellow rat that fired lightning appear someday?","Or perhaps a dinosaur that breathed fire would start roaming around.","Why was I suddenly saying all this?","\"Wohmo...\"","\"Squeak?\"","\"Daddy’s bodeh won’t moof.\"","Because the porcupinefish’s poison had left my body half-crippled.","My slurred speech was the least of my problems. My body refused to move the way I wanted it to.","I kept dropping anything I tried to pick up, and I couldn’t even walk without staggering.","Fortunately, I had barely managed to keep my balance and return to the cave. Otherwise, I might have collapsed in the middle of the forest.","Rustle—","Fast Sloth had been silently watching me. Apparently realizing that my condition was serious, it handed me something.","It was an elixir filled with shimmering golden liquid.","I barely managed to take it and gulped it down.","That wasn’t all. I also drank the antidote I had prepared in advance.","Finally, I circulated my internal energy according to my cultivation method.","I did everything I possibly could.","\"Ugh...\"","As time passed, my body gradually returned to normal. Strength began flowing back into my limbs.","I let out a long sigh and reviewed what had just happened.","That had been an incredibly close call.","’If I hadn’t taken the medicine the All-Father gave me, I would’ve collapsed on the spot.’","My resistance to poison was the only reason it had been this mild. Without even that, I probably would have died instantly.","What was the name of pufferfish poison again?","It started with \"tetra\" or something.","Anyway, it was one of the deadliest poisons in the world.","And since the creature inhabited the Four Seasons Forest, its poison would have been even more vicious—certainly not weaker.","’This is a place where the smallest things are the scariest.’","Until now, I had consistently applied insect repellent to avoid being bitten.","What would happen if I were poisoned by some venomous bug or if a wound developed a secondary infection?","I didn’t even want to imagine it.","I carefully examined my body to ensure nothing was wrong and checked whether all my senses had properly returned.","Perhaps thanks to the combination of the elixir and antidote, I couldn’t feel anything particularly wrong.","My internal energy cultivation was proceeding smoothly too, so I appeared to have made a complete recovery.","Every Gallery user had agreed that there was no better way to assess one’s physical condition than by practicing an internal energy cultivation method.","’If I’d been missing even one of the things I had, my life would’ve been in danger. The Gallery really did save my life.’","This was a place where the slightest lapse in vigilance could send you straight to the grave.","You had to remain wary of everything if you wanted to survive.","’Putting that aside, should I build a proper door...?’","I stared at the iron gate blocking the entrance and remembered the siege from earlier that day.","The animals had presumably lost their homes in the torrential rain and attempted to force their way into mine.","Fortunately, I had easily stopped them with the aura I had honed thus far. But there was no telling what might come next time.","If a creature as strong as Fast Sloth threatened me and demanded that I hand over my home...","That would have been a little difficult.","’At the very least, I need to fortify this place whenever it rains.’","I planned to continue using the same tactic—using the iron gate as a shield while attacking through it.","If I installed an actual door, I would lose the ability to counterattack. More importantly, it would probably be smashed apart in no time.","A single charge from that boar could send the door I had worked so hard to build crashing down, just like my hopes and dreams.","’If I’m unlucky, I might have to defend against a monster wave once a week.’","Grumbling inwardly, I got to my feet.","My body had fully recovered, so I didn’t have time to sit around feeling sorry for myself.","Just as the shark giant had previously found its way to my shelter, there was no telling what kind of animal might visit this time.","I would have to remain vigilant and watch the surrounding area for at least a day or two.","Crackle! Pop!","The first thing I did was light a campfire to dry the surroundings, which had become damp from the rain.","After that, I returned to the riverbank to collect the fish flopping on the ground and inspected the drainage channels.","By the time I had finished everything, evening was approaching.","The sky was growing dark.","’Tomorrow will be Day Eighteen, right?’","I thought about it as I marked another line on the cave wall.","Roughly three days had passed since the expedition incident.","If a man named Ludwig had truly entered the Four Seasons Forest, his first day would be coming to an end around now.","Was he still alive and well?","Or was he dead?","Unlike me, he probably didn’t have any elixirs.","’If I’d known this would happen, I would’ve given him a bottle.’","\"...\"","Regret was still regret, no matter how quickly it came.","I prayed that Ludwig would safely reach the place where I was staying.","Honestly, if even this prayer went unanswered, then God would be something far beyond merely petty.","Rumble!","Or so I almost said, but there were some things in human affairs that simply couldn’t be helped.","I glanced outside.","Despite the thunder, no rain fell.","Could the heavens genuinely be listening to me?","’Nah. It must be a coincidence.’","Resolutely dismissing the idea, I accessed the Gallery.","I wondered what everyone had discussed while I had been cleaning up.","Normally, the Gallery would have been filled with all sorts of random shitposts. Recently, however, most of the discussions had revolved around the expedition.","That remained true now.","More than half the posts concerned El Dorado or the expedition.","Most topics quickly lost people’s interest, but this one seemed to have staying power because it was somewhat connected to reality.","’Nothing here particularly interests me.’","The only thing that could really be called a new topic was the Messiah Empire—more specifically, its emperor.","Apparently, the emperor, who had been sick and on the verge of death, had regained his health.","As for what kind of man he was, they said he had led the Messiah Empire to prosperity.","He had given his full support to Ash, who was now renowned as a Sword Master, and had also implemented policies that provided various benefits.","But that was as far as his talents went. His diplomacy was mediocre, so he was best described as an emperor suited strictly for domestic affairs.","Title: What happens to the Crown Prince now that the Emperor’s back on his feet?","Personally, I’d rather the throne still pass to Crown Prince Arnold. I fucking hate the emperor.","└ Why do you hate him?","└ The policies that emperor bastard implemented sent the prices of magic items through the roof.","└ Ah, kekekeke. I know exactly what you mean.","└ Aren’t the side effects still pretty bad?","└ Yeah. This is actually better than it used to be.","└ If he hadn’t pulled that bullshit, public opinion wouldn’t have gone down the drain, kekeke.","└ The current Messiah emperor seriously has no business handling diplomacy, kekeke.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: That was only true at the time. Didn’t things improve afterward? Policies are meant to be judged over the long term.","└ Fuck off. Do you even know how much we’re still paying to import magical goods from the Iris Kingdom?","└ This bastard’s probably a noble. That’s why he has no idea how hard life is for commoners.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: That’s not true. His Majesty was looking far into the future. I’m certain future generations will evaluate him favorably.","└ So what? We’re struggling to put food on the table right now, kekeke.","└ Besides, the average level of martial strength across the continent went up because of the posts Sword Master made, so those policies are fucking meaningless now, kekeke.","└ Can’t you just admit he’s fucking incompetent? Why all the excuses? Kek.","└ AbsoluteSupremeArnoldRules: You uneducated vermin. Do you have any idea who my father is?","└ Why? Did your mother never tell you?","└ Oh, kekekekeke.","└ Terrifying. Absolutely terrifying, kekekeke.","└ What does that mean?","└ He’s indirectly mocking him for growing up alone with his mother and not having a father, kekeke.","└ We really have to explain jokes like that now? Kekeke.","Well, it was the same Gallery as always—a place overflowing with every kind of joke imaginable.","But with nothing except political posts at the moment, it had become far less entertaining.","Judging by the fact that the head moderator wasn’t intervening, he seemed to be absent.","The Heavenly Demon only removed posts that went too far. Nothing more, nothing less.","’There’s a Cheonggu match tomorrow, so that’s a relief.’","Political discourse would obviously be swept away by the dopamine rush of every goal.","I wondered how many people would lose their minds tomorrow.","Would Cheonggu Princess avoid becoming one of them?","I planned to remain at the shelter tomorrow as well, so I could browse the Gallery without worrying.","If I wandered around unnecessarily, some strange creature might show up at my shelter while I was gone.","’I should stick to smoked food until tomorrow.’","There might be another creature like the shark giant that could track me by scent.","Of course, there was no guarantee that something like that would appear again. There was simply no harm in being prepared.","’But why does it feel so cold?’","Maybe it was because the rain had been a torrential downpour rather than an ordinary shower.","As the moisture evaporated, the temperature also dropped enough to make me shiver.","Thank goodness I had a campfire. Without it, I would already have been trembling uncontrollably.","The uniform Cheonggu Princess had given me also helped. Its long sleeves and trousers provided excellent insulation.","’I should use the hide as a blanket.’","I had originally been using the tiger hide as a carpet, but I planned to use it as a blanket tonight.","With the temperature dropping so suddenly, the campfire alone probably wouldn’t be enough.","The human body was fragile. I had to keep it warm by any means necessary.","One mistake, and I might ascend to heaven in my sleep.","Crackle! Pop!","I added more firewood to the campfire, raising the temperature inside the cave.","I could feel the chill gradually fading. The cave was becoming pleasantly warm.","\"Squeak...\"","My cave companions approached the campfire to warm themselves as well.","Wonmo lay down right beside it and even began dozing off.","’Why does he look so fat now?’","I had noticed him growing plumper as time passed, but... now he was completely round.","At this rate, he might soon start rolling across the floor, just like his name suggested.","Still, it was fine because he was cute.","Being round made him even cuter.","Besides, gaining weight in the wilderness meant he had accumulated plenty of energy reserves.","’He’s still young, so eating a lot should be good for him, right?’","Food was already scarce here. The fact that he could gain weight at all was a good thing.","Maybe it was because I practiced an internal energy cultivation method, but instead of gaining fat, I felt as though I was only putting on muscle.","As far as I knew, muscles—especially human muscles—weren’t particularly energy-efficient compared to those of other animals.","’It’s not like I can afford not to build muscle.’","With danger lurking everywhere, muscle was essential. It might not be very efficient, but I had no choice.","I posted in the Gallery that I was calling it a day, then lay down on the floor.","The chilly weather made me instinctively curl into myself.","\"Fast Sloth, you should get under the blanket too. It’s cold.\"","I had already covered Wonmo separately, so I invited Fast Sloth next.","Fast Sloth merely stared at me without doing anything.","I spread open the blanket and invited it again.","\"Come in here.\"","Fast Sloth slowly backed away.","Did it really dislike me that much?","’Wait a minute. Come to think of it, that bastard still hasn’t washed itself, has it?’","Its body was probably crawling with mold and insects. I had completely forgotten.","In the end, Fast Sloth went to sleep a short distance away.","It was near the campfire, so I wasn’t worried.","Before going to sleep, I quietly closed my eyes and circulated the mana within my body.","Rather than practicing a cultivation method, I simply wanted to feel the mana itself.","Even that could serve as a form of training.","’I still have no idea how to create an Aura Blade.’","Would I really be able to control the aura that kept increasing day and night?","I did my best to suppress my anxiety and drifted off to sleep.","The weather continued growing colder, but thanks to the campfire, I was able to endure it.","And so, that eventful day came to an end.","The following morning—","\"B-B-B-Brrr...\"","The biting cold woke me early.","Why was it so damn cold?","I couldn’t believe that a single torrential downpour had turned the weather into this mess.","’C-Campfire... I need to light the campfire first...’","Wrapping both arms around myself, I stepped outside.","And then—","\"...Huh?\"","A completely white forest greeted me.","Forgetting even the cold, I stared around at the snow-white landscape.","Everything was white, no matter where I looked.","White powder had piled atop both the oven and the furnace.","And that white substance was none other than—","\"Don’t tell me it snowed?\"","It was snow.","I muttered in disbelief.","This was why the place was called the Four Seasons Forest.","\"...This is fucking ridiculous.\"","I felt as though I finally understood the reason.","\"...\"","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 133","paragraphs":["Winter (1)","I had assumed the name Four Seasons Forest was purely metaphorical.","A demonic realm overflowing with every imaginable environmental feature, where a variety of seasons seemed to live and breathe.","That interpretation wasn’t exactly wrong. Even across the river, numerous different terrains stretched out before me.","Of those, I had thought the volcanic region was truly beyond salvation.","But the volcanic region wasn’t the only hopeless place.","This place was just as hopeless.","Title: It snowed, haha","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the snow-covered forest)","(Photo of the ground blanketed in white snow)","(Photo of the tools covered in snow)","It was fucking freezing this morning, and I couldn’t figure out why. Turns out it snowed overnight?","Yesterday, it was pouring like the middle of the rainy season, and now this happens out of nowhere. What a headache, haha.","How the fuck am I supposed to clear away all this shitty white garbage?","└ Heavenly Demon: How beautiful. But how could the season change overnight?","└ Sword Master: It must be because this is the Four Seasons Forest. As expected, that place is completely divorced from common sense.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Just as the Heavenly Demon said, it’s pretty. It looks like somewhere from a fairy tale.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. How unusual for you to say something sensible.","└ Cheonggu Princess: I feel like I’ll get banned if I keep going, so I’m not doing it anymore, haha.","└ Can something like that really happen overnight? That’s fucking incredible.","└ That’s why it’s called the Four Seasons Forest.","└ How are you supposed to prepare when the seasons change without warning? Humans seriously can’t live there, kekeke.","└ Most people die within a day anyway. Grylls would’ve been killed by Mad Dog if he hadn’t had the Gallery.","└ Starlight Princess: It’s strange that the season suddenly changed to winter. Weren’t there any warning signs?","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of Wonmo after growing so fat that he became round) This guy did gain weight extremely quickly.","└ Starlight Princess: Oh my. He’s absolutely adorable. The name Wonmo suits him perfectly.","└ Hey, pick him up and roll him. I want to know whether he really rolls.","└ Kekekekeke. What if he actually rolls really well?","└ Wonmo! Roll out!","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly awful.","└ PraiseTheSun: Wow. It almost never snows in our country, but it must snow over there whenever it gets the chance.","└ Does it even snow in Setan? Isn’t it a desert?","└ It does, but only once in a blue moon. The problem is that any rain or snow over there is practically a natural disaster, so we’re screwed whenever it happens.","└ Why? Doesn’t the sand absorb all the water anyway?","└ If the packed sand collapses, we’re fucked. Besides, most houses in Setan are built from mud, so they’re extremely vulnerable to rain.","└ Passing Dwarf: Aren’t you cold? I heard those clothes are pretty thin.","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m fuuuuucking freezing. Can you give me a set of clothes?","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you whatever I have left over. But I’ll have to ask my friend if you want something custom-made.","└ Wild Grylls: Ask him for now. If that isn’t enough, tell him I’ll give him another fully grown mandrake.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, wait a bit. It might take some time to find winter clothes that fit you.","The sudden arrival of winter was already a problem, but the most serious issue was the sharp drop in temperature.","Perhaps because of their fur, Wonmo and Fast Sloth seemed capable of enduring it.","I wasn’t.","The cold felt as though it were slicing into my flesh. Even wrapping myself in the hide I had been using as a carpet did little to help.","’I miss central heating.’","How wonderful would it be if I could simply turn on the heat?","Shivering violently, I looked around the area near the cave.","\"...\"","Fortunately, nothing particularly noteworthy stood out except the thick blanket of snow.","But that alone wasn’t enough to put me at ease. I still had to investigate the other areas.","’I wonder if winter came to the gorillas’ territory too.’","It was likely, but I couldn’t be certain.","That area was a tropical rainforest.","I had never heard of winter coming to a tropical rainforest.","Then again, this was the Four Seasons Forest, so it wasn’t entirely impossible.","I barely managed to warm myself beside the campfire as I waited for a message from the dwarf.","To distract myself from the cold, I also searched the Gallery for information.","└ Wild Grylls: It’s freezing. Can’t I do something with my internal energy cultivation method?","└ Heavenly Demon: Circulating your cultivation method should raise your body temperature somewhat. However, you will have to maintain it continuously.","└ Sword Master: The Heavenly Demon is right. Think of it as roughly similar to generating heat.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll start immediately.","└ All-Father: Truly... That forest has gone beyond fascinating and entered the realm of the mystical. To think it transitioned into winter overnight. Were there no traces of autumn?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not sure. It came so suddenly that I didn’t notice anything.","└ All-Father: I see. Still, the existence of winter means you are fortunate, Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: What do you mean by that?","└ All-Father: Winter is a period during which energy consumption increases drastically because of the cold. Creatures that inhabit regions where only winter exists are usually large, but those living in places with all four seasons tend to be smaller on average. This is especially true of insects.","└ Ah, I’ve heard of that. Places that are comfortable for humans are also comfortable for animals.","└ Isn’t Wyd like that? The insects there are fucking enormous, kekekeke.","└ Wyd is a country where fairies genuinely exist. It’s a terrifying place.","└ Suspiciously: That’s also why most of us beastfolk are so large... Still, it warms my heart whenever we have a bountiful harvest, kek. You people can’t grow corn, can you?","└ Fuck, I’m from the Central Plains, and all I can do is sigh. Why is all our land such garbage?","└ Garbage, my ass, kekeke. You’re the ones refusing to develop it because you claim to live in harmony with nature. Even the elves develop their land these days.","└ Didn’t elves have a nature-friendly image in the past?","└ Yeah, but once the Elven Queen took the throne, she started developing the country like crazy. That’s when their potential exploded.","└ The Elven Queen is genuinely insane. She can seize control of public opinion with a single speech and steer everyone in the direction she wants, kekeke.","└ Yeah. She knows exactly what the elves want. That makes her even scarier.","└ Even the Council of Elders united because they thought, \"That bitch is seriously fucking crazy,\" kekekeke.","Amid all the useless chatter about rumors and current affairs, the All-Father’s information particularly caught my attention.","Animals in regions that experienced winter tended to be smaller on average.","In other words, the region where I lived was inhabited by animals that were \"comparatively\" small.","’What the fuck? This is what a place with comparatively small animals looks like?’","Wonmo’s mother alone had been as enormous as a house.","The saber-toothed tiger had genuinely been about the size of a house.","If those counted as comparatively small, how enormous were the creatures elsewhere?","I couldn’t even imagine it.","A sense of futility washed over me. I wished I hadn’t asked.","’But there’s an even more serious problem...’","Food.","Still shivering, I headed outside.","There was something I hadn’t managed to check because of the extreme cold—the fish.","Worried that something might have happened to them, I looked inside the iron container.","\"Oh, great. I’m screwed.\"","Not only had the water in the container frozen solid, but so had the fish.","Natural frozen storage.","I could only sigh.","Title: Do I have to throw this away?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fish frozen solid)","They froze completely in that short amount of time. Do I have to throw them away, or should I just extract their inner cores?","└ Heavenly Demon: There is no need to worry. If they possess inner cores, they will not freeze to death.","└ Wild Grylls: Is that even possible?","└ Heavenly Demon: They are called inner cores for a reason. You may trust me.","└ Sword Master: Do you really expect him to believe you when you blindly demand his trust? You should offer a more scientific explanation.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you provide one?","└ Sword Master: No. I’m a muscle-brained idiot who only ever studied martial arts, haha.","└ Wild Grylls: ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: As I recall, even your martial arts were rather unimpressive.","└ Sword Master: You fucking bi—","└ Heavenly Demon: What did you just say?","└ Sword Master: Head Moderator, the assistant moderator is abusing her authority. ;;","└ DontThrowAwayTheHero: Swearing was wrong too! But Heavenly Demon, please don’t do that again!","└ All-Father: As the Heavenly Demon said, if they possess inner cores, they should still be alive. They are likely not even hibernating, but simply continuing to live normally.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you explain that scientifically?","└ All-Father: Yes. Most fish that possess inner cores contain a substance called ardorotoxin, which... (omitted) ...and that is how it works.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh. I see.","└ Hmm. I understand perfectly.","└ I was actually just about to explain it myself.","└ The harvest of bullshit is plentiful this year, kekeke.","└ Says the bastards who couldn’t even get into the Academy, kekeke.","Without winter clothing, outdoor activity was almost impossible.","I was wearing both the uniform Cheonggu Princess had given me and the one I had received from King Leor, yet I was still cold.","If I hadn’t possessed even these, wouldn’t I have frozen to death already?","’Isn’t there some magical item that can warm up the inside of a room?’","The thought suddenly occurred to me, so I made another post in the Gallery.","I needed to warm the cave first before deciding whether I could venture outside.","Even then, food remained a concern.","For the moment, I couldn’t obtain any myself.","I would have to visit it to know for certain, but in weather this cold, the river had probably frozen solid too.","I still had smoked tiger meat, but I had no idea how long winter would last.","’Did those animals come to my cave yesterday because they were preparing for winter?’","It wasn’t entirely implausible.","Shivering, I added more wood to the campfire.","Title: Is there a magic item that can warm an entire room?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the campfire)","It’s still too cold with just a campfire. Isn’t there some kind of item that can warm an entire room?","└ Heavenly Demon: My bedchamber is always warm. I shall ask one of my aides and return.","└ Sword Master: Such items exist, but they usually only warm the sleeping area. We use fireplaces to heat entire houses.","└ Wild Grylls: Would it be difficult to heat the whole room with something like a crystal orb?","└ Passing Dwarf: You’d probably have to tear out the entire floor to do that. But there’s mithril beneath the floor of your cave, isn’t there?","└ Cheonggu Princess: The dwarf is right. If you’re going to use a crystal orb, it would be more efficient to renovate the house instead.","└ Wild Grylls: Then what would be the best option?","└ Passing Dwarf: You’d be better off building a fireplace. It’s easier to punch through the ceiling than the floor.","└ Wild Grylls: But that sounds hard...","└ Passing Dwarf: Then freeze to death, kek.","└ Wild Grylls: Sigh.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ll upload some basic construction instructions. Follow those. It’s easy as long as you have bricks.","So I would have to punch a hole somewhere after all.","I let out a hollow laugh.","With winter attacking without warning, renovations had become essential.","’The ceiling is still the better option.’","If only because of the mithril, I couldn’t tear out the entire floor.","I thought about the materials I would need and began preparing.","[ Wild Grylls: Well, it’s better than nothing.]","[ Passing Dwarf: I’ll send you this and upload the post immediately, so keep an eye out.]","Before that, I received winter clothes from the dwarf.","They were only meant to serve as a temporary measure.","The clothes were made from fur and leather that looked warm at a glance.","The hat in particular was so large that \"voluminous\" seemed like the only appropriate word.","It resembled the kind of winter clothing a rifle-carrying hunter might wear.","\"Whew.\"","Once I put everything on, the cold became somewhat bearable.","There was nothing I could do about my freezing feet, though.","I would just have to wear a pair of thick socks. As luck would have it, the Gallery had a suitable pair available.","Now that I had winter clothing, the only remaining task was to install a fireplace in the cave.","The dwarf had said he would upload the post immediately, so I just needed to follow his instructions.","[ Passing Dwarf: Here are the winter clothes. I couldn’t give you shoes because I didn’t have any in your size.]","Title: Here are the fireplace plans. Take a look.","Passing Dwarf","(Photo of a fireplace cross-section diagram)","(Photo of a fireplace)","This should be enough, right? The principle itself is simple, so you should be able to build it quickly.","└ Wild Grylls: Thanks. But if I light a fire in it, I’ll need to seal the cave entrance too, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, obviously. Don’t bother trying to install a door. Just cover the entrance with thick cloth or leather. That’ll work better.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay.","The cross-section allowed me to understand the structure, aided by the dwarf’s explanation.","The construction itself wasn’t difficult.","The chimney was the problem.","I would have to seal the gaps between the bricks so that smoke couldn’t leak out.","I had used mud to seal the gaps in the bricks when constructing both the oven and the furnace.","And what did that mean?","Clang! Clang!","\"Argh! This is driving me insane!\"","It meant I had to suffer through the backbreaking task of digging into ground that had frozen solid.","Rain had fallen yesterday, followed by snow today, so the ground was practically ice rather than soil.","For a moment, I considered pouring hot water over it.","I quickly abandoned the idea.","I would only be creating more work for myself. Pouring water onto the ground in winter was sheer madness.","’I’ll have to dig it up with a pickaxe.’","In the end, I had no choice but to \"mine\" the soil with a pickaxe.","Why the hell was I being put through this?","After gathering all the soil I needed, I purchased a ladder from the auction house.","I needed it to climb above the cave’s ceiling and look for a suitable location.","The ladder I had previously bought for butchering was a folding ladder, so it wasn’t long enough.","The ladder I purchased this time was tall enough to reach high places.","’Somewhere around here...’","I was examining different parts of the ceiling in search of a suitable spot when a tiny white object gently landed on the back of my hand.","I couldn’t feel it because I was wearing gloves, but that didn’t matter.","Tap— Tap—","It wasn’t just one.","More white objects drifted down one after another.","I raised my head toward the sky.","Dark clouds had gathered without my noticing, completely obscuring the sun.","\"Wow...\"","Garbage was falling from the sky.","What a truly godforsaken place.","Perhaps the weather had read my mind.","Whoooooosh—!!!","\"Aaaaaaargh!!!\"","In the span of thirty seconds, the snow evolved into a full-blown blizzard.","’What the fuck did I do to deserve this?!’","It was so unfair I could die.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 134","paragraphs":["Winter (2)","I had thought this many times before, but God definitely hated me.","Otherwise, He wouldn’t have sent a blizzard specifically to stop me from renovating my home.","’But didn’t I hate Him first?’","I had spent my entire life blaming God because I didn’t want to hate people.","Had that snowball finally rolled all the way back to me?","Lost in this mixture of armchair philosophy and nonsense, I waited for the blizzard to stop.","The situation outside the cave was nothing short of a natural disaster. The entire landscape was buried in snow.","I had never experienced a blizzard even on Earth, so encountering one after coming here was absurd.","Title: Save me","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the blizzard raging outside the cave)","Now there’s a blizzard too. Somebody save me.","└ Heavenly Demon: What utter chaos. The weather does whatever it pleases.","└ Sword Master: The animals living there are fascinating too. How do they survive in such an environment?","└ Wild Grylls: I think they instinctively know what’s coming. Wonmo gaining weight proves it.","└ Heavenly Demon: Wonmo aside, did Fast Sloth show no changes?","└ Wild Grylls: Nope. Nothing in particular. It still has the same stupid expression.","└ Those creatures survived because they’ve adapted, kek.","└ I wonder what the gorillas are doing.","└ Eating bananas, probably.","└ What if yellow dust blows in during spring too? Kekeke.","└ Where would the sand come from?","└ The terrain across the river changes all the time. If it turns into a desert during the spring season, the dust could blow over from there.","└ That makes enough sense to be terrifying, kekekeke.","└ If yellow dust really comes, it’ll be legendary, kekeke.","A blizzard was already bad enough, but yellow dust in spring?","That would drive me completely insane.","The problem was that the possibility wasn’t merely nonzero—it was actually rather high.","This damned forest was a place where miracles manifested and the impossible became possible.","Even the sea and river had overturned common sense. There was no reason the weather would be any different.","’At least the blizzard has stopped.’","The blizzard that had descended as though determined to sweep everything away had completely vanished.","All it left behind was an even thicker layer of white garbage.","Thank goodness this wasn’t the military.","When garbage fell from the sky there, clearing it was a never-ending task.","’And I don’t know when another blizzard might come.’","I should hurry.","I grabbed my pickaxe and climbed onto the part of the ceiling I had previously selected.","I wasn’t going to break through the entire ceiling immediately. That would only create more work and waste time.","Clang! Clang! Crunch!","I opened only a small hole.","Then I stuck my face through it and looked down into the cave.","Fast Sloth was staring up at me with its usual vacant expression.","Now I simply had to use this hole as a starting point and gradually build the brickwork upward.","Before that, I should boil some water to thaw the soil—","’Ah. Right.’","I realized something belatedly.","I opened the valve connected to the hose to check whether water would come out.","Just as I had feared, nothing emerged despite the open valve.","The river had probably frozen.","Even if it hadn’t, the water inside the hose itself might have frozen solid.","’I’ll have to make water from snow.’","Fortunately, the recent blizzard meant I could use snow instead.","So much had accumulated in that short time that it squeaked beneath my feet.","While waiting for the water to boil, I decided to prepare the foundation for the fireplace.","The structure itself wasn’t difficult, but since it was my first time building one, I had every reason to proceed carefully.","’Before stacking the bricks, I need to start with the floor...’","I repaired the floor before laying any bricks.","I designed it so that the ashes wouldn’t pile up inside but would collect underneath, while fresh air could flow in smoothly from outside.","There were so many features to consider that I had to move repeatedly between the inside and outside of the cave.","However, temperature control was directly tied to my survival.","As long as it kept me from freezing to death, the effort was worthwhile.","People from warm regions might not understand, but winter was mercilessly harsh in most parts of the world.","You had to prepare for every threat while the weather was still warm.","Otherwise, you could die from hypothermia, starvation, or any number of other causes.","Since ancient times, Koreans had made such preparations during kimchi-making season.","There was even a saying:","’Every season is merely preparation for winter.’","As I began preparing for the cold, I also started worrying about various illnesses—especially the common cold.","’Why don’t humans have fur? Is it because fur catches fire easily?’","While wondering why humans lacked fur and were therefore so susceptible to colds, I decided to ask the All-Father about it later.","Anyway, I had finished digging the ground. All that remained was to stack the bricks.","Since I planned to apply mud between them like cement, I prepared hot water first.","I was boiling it outside so that I could also use it to thaw the surrounding ground.","\"Hm?\"","\"Kiyuuung...\"","But then I noticed a strange animal near the campfire.","At first, I thought it was a raccoon dog, but a closer look revealed that it wasn’t.","It was an animal often mistaken for a raccoon dog—an actual raccoon.","The raccoon was holding both hands toward the campfire to warm them.","It hadn’t entered the cave and was still outside, so I didn’t mind.","However, I planned to chase it away if it stayed too long.","’Or Fast Sloth will teach it a lesson.’","Just as I thought that and picked up the container of hot water, the raccoon glanced at me.","Then it stuck its hands into the campfire.","Literally into the fire.","I couldn’t help but jump in surprise.","That wouldn’t merely burn its hands. Its entire body could catch fire.","But what kind of place was this?","It was the Four Seasons Forest, where small creatures weren’t merely dangerous—they were downright horrifying.","Fwoosh!","The raccoon stared at its hands as they caught fire and began blazing.","Then it put them straight into its mouth.","It looked as though it were eating the flames.","By the time I had become too dumbfounded to speak, the raccoon proudly returned to the forest.","I couldn’t even begin to understand what I had just witnessed.","Did the fire inside its body act as some kind of heater?","’Right. Trying to understand would only hurt me.’","I had more than enough problems of my own.","I began constructing the fireplace as planned.","Lay down one row, apply mud.","Lay down another row, apply more mud.","The dwarf had warned me to make sure everything was firmly secured, so I inspected the brickwork meticulously.","I had originally intended to smear the mud on with my hands, but the weather was too cold, so I bought a tool instead.","After rummaging through the auction house, I found a trowel used for applying cement.","Once I tried it, I wondered how I could possibly have managed without it.","’Now all that’s left is the chimney...’","The chimney was the most difficult part.","It had to narrow as it extended upward.","Mud alone wouldn’t secure it properly as I built higher, so I needed another solution.","’I’ll need a frame.’","Since I was using mud instead of cement, the framework was important.","After considering my options, I purchased a suitably sized iron container from the auction house.","I then stepped outside to do the hammering. I didn’t want to wake Wonmo.","Slice! Slice! Slice!","First, I cut the iron container into flat panels.","A sword infused with aura was more than sufficient.","I then cut away the middle, leaving only the outer edges intact.","With that, the frame was complete.","It was shaped like a squared arch and made from thick iron, so it was sturdy.","’The size should be about right too.’","It would be fine as long as the smoke could escape properly.","If it collapsed...","Well, I would just have to build it more carefully next time.","This was the best I could do.","I continued stacking the bricks one by one until the chimney reached the hole in the ceiling.","The work inside the cave was finished, so I had to head outside again.","I needed to bring wet mud, bricks, a pickaxe, and finally, a hammer.","Crunch! Crack!","I widened the hole with the pickaxe and carefully refined its edges with the hammer.","Since I couldn’t work with perfect precision, the hole ended up wider than the chimney, but that was fine.","I had brought the mud specifically to seal the gaps.","Thanks to my spatial bag, I had been able to carry everything at once.","\"Good. Finished!\"","After neatly completing the chimney, my makeshift fireplace was finished.","A chimney sticking out of the top of a cave looked somewhat peculiar.","But the job wasn’t truly complete yet.","The most important thing was its performance.","I needed to test whether the fireplace worked properly.","\"Whew.\"","Had the weather grown even colder while I was working?","My breath emerged in a thicker white cloud than before.","I cleared all the stone fragments out of the fireplace and placed firewood inside.","Crackle! Pop! Crackle!","A fire sprang to life, creating a rather picturesque scene.","The sight alone warmed my heart, but I still wasn’t finished.","Cold air continued seeping in through the cave entrance.","I had to block that first.","’The dwarf said to cover it with some well-insulated cloth or leather, right?’","The tiger hide wasn’t nearly large enough.","For now, I would cover the entrance with several layers of large cloth.","This was the perfect opportunity since there was no blizzard.","If I secured them firmly with nails, they should block most of the wind.","Whenever a blizzard struck, I planned to weigh down the cloth hanging along the ground with rocks.","’It’s getting warmer now that the entrance is covered.’","This was why I had built the chimney.","I needed to close the entrance.","When I used an open campfire, leaving the entrance uncovered was the only relatively safe option. A fireplace was different.","I felt comfortable as the cave’s interior gradually grew warmer.","At some point, Fast Sloth had also approached the fireplace and begun warming itself.","\"Nice, isn’t it?\"","It nodded in response.","For some reason, that made me feel proud.","This was the perfect time to make a Gallery post.","I photographed the fireplace and uploaded the pictures.","Only then did I realize that building it had taken a full two hours.","I had been so focused on the construction that I hadn’t noticed the time passing.","Title: Finished building the fireplace","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the fire burning inside the fireplace)","(Photo of Fast Sloth staring blankly into the flames)","(Photo of Wonmo sleeping beside the fire after wandering over at some point)","This is the makeshift fireplace I spent two hours building. I think I’ll be able to get through winter without too much trouble, haha.","└ Heavenly Demon: I think this every time, but you are remarkably skilled with your hands. To think you could even construct a fireplace.","└ Sword Master: I agree. Were you always good at making things?","└ Wild Grylls: I used to be amazing at folding colored paper.","└ Does that really count as being good with your hands? ;;","└ Of course it does. I can know exactly how to fold something and still fail, kekeke.","└ Some people really are naturally gifted or hopeless with their hands.","└ Passing Dwarf: You did a pretty decent job. Did you apply mud between the bricks?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. I also cut and made the frame myself.","└ Passing Dwarf: Oh, nice. Did you check whether smoke is coming out of the chimney?","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t, but I’m sure it’s fine.","└ Passing Dwarf: Check immediately unless you want them to find your mysterious corpse tomorrow.","└ Wild Grylls: Sounds like a pain.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then die, kek.","It was annoying, but I checked and confirmed that smoke was escaping through the chimney.","Going outside also allowed me to feel just how drastic the temperature difference was.","The fireplace genuinely performed well. The inside of the cave was remarkably warm.","’I should rest for a while.’","Perhaps because I had poured all my concentration into building the fireplace, my body felt heavy with fatigue.","I should eat lunch before resting.","Naturally, I was having smoked meat.","All I had to do was warm it over the fireplace, making it extremely convenient.","’I’ll give the inner core to Fast Sloth. As for Wonmo... I guess I don’t need to give him any?’","Perhaps Wonmo had entered hibernation, because all he did was sleep.","Even while I worked, he remained curled into a ball, sleeping soundly.","I decided not to wake him.","He would get up when he was hungry.","After eating, I browsed the Gallery while waiting for my food to digest.","[ Chae-U vs. Beger: Kone scores the opening gooooooal!!! ]","’Oh. There was a match today?’","Coincidentally, Cheonggu Princess had uploaded a post about it.","I had been so busy lately that I had forgotten about today’s match.","Cheonggu Princess would probably feel a little disappointed.","I should at least leave a comment now.","I opened the post.","This is what an attacking line looks like! This is Chae-U! This is how you build an attack!! Do you understand now, you filthy Leor vermin?!","└ King Leor: Kekekeke, look how excited you are. You bastards can’t even qualify for the Champions League.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Yeah, well, you’re still going trophyless this season too~","└ King Leor: And have you lot lifted a trophy in the past ten years?","└ Cheonggu Princess: We’re winning the Devil Cup this time. Unlike a certain trophyless team, kek.","└ King Leor: You’ll still crash and burn next season. Enjoy this while you can.","└ Cheonggu Princess: (Video of Leor conceding the opening goal six minutes into the first half) Oh? What’s this? That goal positively reeks!","└ King Leor: When the fuck did Svi concede again? This is fucking bullshit.","Title: Chae-U vs. Beger: Kone scores the opening gooooooal!!!","Cheonggu Princess","(Video of a goal being scored five minutes into the first half)","└ Cheonggu Princess is seriously vicious, kekekeke.","└ Chae-U supporters have always been like that, kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: There was a match today? I’ve been so busy that I didn’t know. Sorry. Let’s go, Chae-U!","└ Cheonggu Princess: Excellent! Now that the Saint has appeared, we’ll win again today! What score do you predict?","└ Wild Grylls: They often attack like that and then concede. Their defense is weak, so I’m predicting 4–2. Chae-U scores the four, by the way.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Four whole goals! Thank you!","└ King Leor: What score do you predict for us?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t watch Leor’s matches much, so I’m not sure, but I think you’ll lose. You threw away your lead in the last match too.","└ King Leor: Come on. You said something nice about Chae-U, so why us...?","└ Wild Grylls: You can clearly see their lack of concentration in the goal they just conceded.","└ Cheonggu Princess: How dare you doubt the Saint! How rude!","└ King Leor: Sigh. Svi’s stamina really has declined, so it’s hard to argue with that.","Cheonggu Princess and King Leor fought whenever there was a match.","Opposites attracted, as the saying went.","They supported different teams, but their personalities were remarkably similar.","Whoooooosh—!!!","Had another blizzard started outside while I was browsing the Gallery?","The cloth covering the entrance repeatedly swelled outward before settling down again.","The razor-sharp wind was an added bonus.","With the weather fluctuating so wildly, I should probably avoid outdoor activity for a while.","Rain was irritating enough, but a blizzard was an even greater disaster.","’I should practice my cultivation method.’","I spent an hour circulating my internal energy and another thirty minutes practicing swordsmanship.","By then, the matches should have been ending, so I checked the Gallery.","[ Chae-U vs. Beger: Final score 4–2! Chae-U wins despite showing defensive instability, exactly as the Saint predicted! ]","[ Leor vs. Balrog: Final score 0–2. Leor suffers a shocking defeat after showing signs of declining stamina. ]","Everything had unfolded exactly as I had predicted.","Naturally, countless users flocked to my comment to make their pilgrimages to the \"holy site.\"","I felt somewhat uneasy, but I dismissed it as a coincidence.","’More importantly...’","I looked at Fast Sloth, which was still staring blankly into the flames.","It hadn’t behaved like this when I used an ordinary campfire.","Why was it acting that way now?","\"Hey. You’ll ruin your eyes. Move back.\"","\"...\"","\"Come on. I said move back.\"","I felt as though I finally understood how my mother had felt when she tried to drag me away from the computer.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 135","paragraphs":["Winter (3)","Around the time Grylls’s activities became restricted by the untimely onset of winter, the world outside the Forest of Four Seasons was bustling for various reasons.","The Holy Kingdom and El Dorado were in an uproar over the investigation team and the Immortal King incident.","In Mephisto, the hooligans refused to accept the outcome of the match and were burning everything in sight.","Even the relatively peaceful nations remained active, each for its own reasons.","\"Are you the one who presented Us with a fully matured mandrake?\"","The man wore an expression that radiated weariness with everything in the world. Yet even that could not conceal his dignity.","His golden hair still shone without having lost its color, and his beard was immaculately groomed.","The very picture of a handsome middle-aged man spoke in an indifferent voice.","Though every conceivable trace of annoyance showed on his face, his solemn bearing was impossible to hide.","\"Y-yes! That is correct, Your Majesty.\"","Count Gorgon, standing opposite him, bowed deeply as he answered.","A short distance away from Count Gorgon stood Arnold, a handsome young man with golden hair, watching the exchange.","\"Raise your head. You are practically Our savior.\"","\"I-I am deeply honored, Your Majesty.\"","\"There is no need for that. So, what is it that you desire?\"","The middle-aged man who discarded the preamble and went straight to the point was named Robert.","Robert Louis Messiah II, Emperor of the Messiah Empire.","Despite the curious reputation of being an \"emperor suited only for domestic affairs,\" he wielded immense authority.","In truth, being suited for domestic affairs meant possessing outstanding administrative ability—something impossible without tremendous power.","It was precisely because he held such fearsome authority that he had been able to steadily strengthen the foundations of the Messiah Empire.","\"Th-this humble servant desires nothing. I am satisfied simply knowing that Your Majesty has recovered your health.\"","\"Is that so? Very well. We shall consider a reward appropriate for you. You may withdraw.\"","\"May Your Majesty enjoy a long and healthy life.\"","Count Gorgon bowed deeply once more before departing.","His tactful wish for the emperor’s longevity was an added touch, rather than a conventional farewell.","Even at those considerate words, Robert maintained his impassive expression.","Soon, only Robert and Arnold remained in the emperor’s bedchamber.","Robert remained silent for some time, while Arnold stood still and waited for his father to speak.","\"...My son.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","\"You have truly done something unnecessary.\"","Robert finally spoke amid the heavy silence, his words tinged with reproach.","Arnold flinched and stole a glance at him.","Perhaps lost in thought, Robert merely stared up at the ceiling.","\"Thanks to you, my plan has fallen apart.\"","\"What plan... do you mean?\"","\"...\"","Robert did not answer. His attitude made it clear that he did not want to explain.","He then looked at the bewildered Arnold and quietly spoke.","\"You said this item came from the Gallery?\"","\"Yes. That is... correct.\"","\"The Gallery truly has all manner of things. And to think this came from the Forest of Four Seasons...\"","Robert stroked his beard as though pondering something deeply, then continued.","\"What did you say his name was? Count Golla?\"","\"Count Gorgon.\"","\"Right, of course. Leave this matter entirely to him. I have something else I must do.\"","\"And what would that be...?\"","\"I must prepare your succession ceremony.\"","\"...\"","Arnold’s eyes widened.","Robert had spoken calmly, but the content of his words was anything but calm.","A succession ceremony meant that the throne would be passed down.","It meant Arnold would soon ascend as emperor.","Arnold was briefly exhilarated that the moment he had long desired was finally approaching, but he soon brought his excitement under control.","His experiences thus far had taught him that excitement could ruin everything.","\"I shall have the succession ceremony prepared within a month. Things will become quite busy.\"","\"Father, I am not yet—\"","\"Even after consuming the mature mandrake, my health is not what it once was. It is becoming difficult for me to endure.\"","Robert cut Arnold off before he could finish.","Arnold inwardly cheered, but patiently waited for Robert to continue.","\"So you must prepare yourself thoroughly as well. Recent developments in the Holy Kingdom are concerning, and Alvenheim’s movements are equally suspicious.\"","\"I will remain vigilant.\"","\"If you overcome these difficulties, you may become an even greater emperor than I.\"","\"That is not true. You have strengthened the very foundations of the empire, Father.\"","\"That was all thanks to Ash.\"","\"Pardon?\"","Arnold’s eyes widened, wondering if he had misheard.","\"Cough! Cough! Cough!\"","Of course, when Robert broke into a violent coughing fit, Arnold’s doubts immediately turned to concern.","Startled, Arnold turned to summon the imperial physician.","Before he could, however, Robert raised a hand to stop him.","\"Cough. It is nothing. A minor cough is unavoidable at my age.\"","\"Father...\"","\"In any event, the empire has no shortage of talented people, so there is no need to worry about internal affairs. If necessary, you can write a letter to the former captain of the Imperial Guard.\"","There was only one person he could mean by the former captain of the Imperial Guard.","Ash Menethil, the strongest sword in the empire and a warrior who possessed Swordmaster as an official title.","Though he had currently entered a state of partial seclusion, he was someone who would gladly heed Robert’s request.","The emperor had been Ash’s patron and had supported him wholeheartedly, while Ash had repaid that kindness in full.","Someone had flooded the Gallery with invaluable tips, causing the continent’s average combat strength to rise, but that was no cause for concern.","Ash’s reputation alone ensured that no one would dare treat the empire lightly.","\"So you need only focus on external affairs. The situation appears to be growing increasingly serious.\"","\"Yes, I understand.\"","\"Then withdraw. I wish to be alone.\"","\"The imperial physician...\"","\"I shall summon him myself.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","Arnold bowed and left the bedchamber, leaving Robert alone.","Robert blinked in silence for a while before eventually releasing a sigh.","Then, with a wistful look unlike any he had shown before, he muttered softly,","\"I didn’t want to work...\"","It was the grumbling of an office worker exhausted by his job.","And that was not all.","\"Why did something like a mature mandrake have to exist...? I was planning to enjoy a comfortable retirement...\"","Robert muttered in a voice filled with irritation and weariness toward everything in the world.","Had his health truly deteriorated?","To some extent, yes.","But he was not bedridden to the point that he could barely attend to his duties.","It was closer to malingering—though his act did involve actual poison.","He had consumed a poison that caused symptoms resembling a cold but had no lasting effect on his health.","He had also informed the imperial physician beforehand, allowing them to make his condition appear far more serious than it truly was.","The reason he had gone to such lengths was simple.","He did not want to work.","The position of emperor—or king, for that matter—inevitably came with overwork.","Robert had been unable to escape it either, and in the end, he had resorted to this.","One might say he lacked a sense of responsibility as emperor, but it was not truly a problem.","He had already transferred the entirety of state affairs to his son, Arnold.","Only the succession ceremony remained, yet he had been unable to endure even that long and had taken to his bed.","I only hope El Dorado and Alvenheim don’t start any trouble during the next month.","With several troublesome factions already causing chaos, Robert wanted the succession ceremony completed as quickly as possible.","He would have to work again for that to happen. The mere thought was horrifying.","After briefly growing distressed over all the work awaiting him, Robert looked into the air.","As he did, a window floated into view.","It was the Gallery, which his son Arnold had also recently begun enjoying.","Those were good times.","What had Robert been doing while pretending to be ill—though technically not entirely pretending?","He had been amusing himself on the Gallery.","Even a dignified emperor could not resist a secret indulgence.","In fact, after working so diligently all those years, he had become absorbed in the Gallery as a way of rewarding himself.","I want to live like that too.","Why did he have to be the emperor?","He did not mind the nickname \"emperor suited only for domestic affairs,\" but why did he have to be emperor in the first place?","Why had his father only sired one son?","All sorts of thoughts crossed his mind.","While browsing the Gallery, Robert found a post by someone who had recently gained considerable fame.","Title: The fast sloth is zoning out by the fire","Wild Grylls","(The fast sloth staring into the fire)","This little bastard was zoning out in front of the fire, so I tried to pull him away, but he wouldn’t budge.","Even when I forcibly dragged him away, he went straight back. Some of his fur has already been singed, but he’s still doing this. LOL","└ Heavenly Demon: Strangely adorable. It seems to understand how precious warmth is.","└ SwordMaster: The fast sloth has an unexpectedly cute side to it.","└ Starlight Princess: Is Wonmo there too? I want to see him.","└ Wild Grylls: (Wonmo sleeping curled into a ball) Here he is.","└ He’s seriously adorable every time I see him. LOL","└ Isn’t he waking up? Is he actually hibernating?","Wild Grylls was said to have fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","His daily records had recently become Robert’s favorite reading material.","Robert wanted nothing from Grylls. As emperor, he already possessed everything a man could have.","I’m strangely envious.","He was simply envious of the life Grylls was currently living.","It was not entirely raw survival, since he received bits of support here and there, but he was still living in the wilderness.","Robert wanted to live that way too.","He wanted to build an oven, hunt, and catch fish.","He finally understood why people wanted to take up farming as they grew older. After living such a busy life, they began to yearn for freedom.","Not absolute freedom, but freedom earned through one’s own efforts—a life where every action produced a direct result.","Now that Robert had entered middle age, reading Grylls’s posts only intensified that desire.","It would be nice if my safety could be guaranteed...","Of course, Grylls’s objective was survival and escape, not simply enjoying life in the wilderness.","Robert, on the other hand, wanted the wilderness lifestyle without any of the danger.","Whenever Grylls found himself in peril, Robert nearly had a heart attack.","I suppose I’ll have to settle for living vicariously through him.","For that to happen, Grylls could not die.","The Gallery was perfect for filling the loneliness of his life.","And so Robert made his decision.","In another month, he would be free from the burden of being emperor.","Until then, he would provide Grylls with whatever support he could.","First, I need to create a registered username...","A short while later, Robert came up with:","[AbsolutezZoneRobertIsAwesome]","\"Heh-heh.\"","It was a username that perfectly demonstrated that the apple did not fall far from the tree.","His son already used the same name, which only made it better.","Chuckling to himself, Robert tried to register it.","[This username has already been registered.]","Robert was momentarily speechless.","Someone is actually using an idiotic fucking username like this?","His son was.","****","The fast sloth had caused me plenty of trouble by staring into the fire all day, but I had decided to let it go.","No matter how much I struggled with him, I was the only one who suffered.","It was better to leave him alone.","Surely the fast sloth would move away from the campfire eventually.","That was what I told myself.","Whoooooosh!!!","Regardless, the blizzard was still raging outside.","Part of me wanted to pull aside the flapping cloth and take a look, but I restrained myself.","If I did that and the cloth tore free from its fastenings, it would be a disaster.","In the end, I had no choice but to remain inside the cave all day.","Considering that it had rained yesterday, I had effectively spent nearly two days trapped inside.","What would I have done if I hadn’t smoked the meat?","I ate smoked meat for dinner, while the fast sloth ate one of the inner cores I had stored away.","Weather this goddamned awful might continue, so I would probably have to go hunting again soon.","If that proved impossible, I would have to rely on fish.","Whatever I caught, smoking it would be essential.","If the blizzard stops tomorrow, I’m going to have a rough time.","Just how much snow would accumulate?","I was a little worried.","To bring the day to a close, I added more firewood to the campfire.","Ordinarily, one person would have to remain awake to keep it burning, but that was difficult in my current situation.","All I could do was pile on as much firewood as possible.","Isn’t there some kind of device that can automatically feed firewood into a fire?","Something like that would be perfect.","I went to sleep and brought the day to an end.","And then the next morning arrived.","\"...You still haven’t slept?\"","The campfire was still blazing.","And, of course, the fast sloth was still sitting in front of it.","Had this little guy actually been adding firewood throughout the night?","I was dumbfounded.","Still, thanks to him, I stayed warm.","The cloth was no longer flapping, so it seemed the blizzard had stopped sometime during the night.","I pushed against the curtain to check the situation outside.","It stopped dead.","\"Huh?\"","Something was wrong.","Why would the curtain not move?","I had even removed the stones holding it in place, yet something was clearly amiss.","For a moment, I wondered if the curtain itself had frozen solid, but that was not it.","When I pulled it backward instead of pushing it out, it came away without resistance.","\"...What the hell is this?\"","Behind the curtain was a pure white wall.","At first, I had no idea what I was looking at, but it did not take long for me to realize the truth.","\"Oh.\"","It was all snow.","Snow that had been compressed into a solid mass.","Just how much snow had fallen for it to block the entire cave entrance?","I was utterly bewildered.","But there was an even greater problem—one directly related to my survival.","How am I supposed to clear all of this?","As though having garbage fall from the sky were not bad enough—","Bam! Bang!","\"Aaaaaaargh!!!\"","—it also taught me just how precious time was.","I furiously \"mined\" through the snow with my pickaxe as I shouted,","\"Someone’s in here!!!\"","I was beginning to hate winter.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 136","paragraphs":["Disaster (1)","Title: I’m fucked.","(A photo of the cave entrance completely blocked by snow)","It appears that I’m fucked.","That is the conclusion I reached after careful consideration.","I’m fucked.","└ Heavenly Demon: Is all of that snow?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It’s hardened from the cold, so I’m digging through it with a pickaxe.","└ Heavenly Demon: Would it not be easy to excavate with sword energy?","└ Wild Grylls: I can, but no matter how much I dig, more snow keeps falling from above. I have no idea how much has accumulated.","└ SwordMaster: Isn’t that dangerous? What if you run out of oxygen?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m surviving thanks to the chimney I opened yesterday. It looks like the fast sloth kept adding firewood, so all the snow around it melted.","└ SwordMaster: It feels like the fast sloth has saved your life several times now.","└ Why do those sentences sound so literary?","└ Just three sentences perfectly convey how fucked he is. LOL","└ There’s profanity in it, but it somehow doesn’t even feel like swearing. LOL","└ Can snow really pile up that high? Is this another effect of the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ No. Places with heavy snowfall are often like that. Apparently, the snow frequently piles up as high as the doors.","└ Just look at northern Messiah. I heard the people there shovel snow every day. LOL","└ I’m from the north, and clearing snow is more irritating than subjugating monsters. It really is garbage falling from the sky.","└ All-Father: Even so, that is an abnormal amount of snowfall. It should be difficult for that much to accumulate overnight.","└ Wild Grylls: No matter how much I dig, more snow keeps pouring down from above.","└ All-Father: A word of advice: why not spend the time you are using on the Gallery digging through the snow instead? This appears dangerous.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m still digging while posting.","Though \"mining\" with a pickaxe would be more accurate than digging with a shovel, I was working hard.","The problem was that I had no idea how much snow had accumulated above me. Every time I dug some out, more came cascading down to fill the space again.","If the fast sloth had not added firewood throughout the night, the chimney would have become blocked too.","If the chimney—my only source of oxygen—had been buried as well...","I did not even want to imagine it.","The fast sloth was an enormous help not only in combat, but in everyday life as well.","But if it snows this much, can the other animals even survive?","And not just the animals.","I had to wonder whether the plants could survive either.","Nothing should have been able to grow properly beneath this much snow.","Yet countless trees stood tall enough to form an entire forest.","Either they possessed enough vitality to withstand the snow, or there was some other explanation.","If winter in the forest is already this awful, how fucked up must the other environments be?","The forest supposedly had a relatively \"ordinary\" climate, yet it had become like this.","The snowy mountains and desert could only be worse.","The rainforest where the gorillas lived was probably no different.","It made no sense for only my territory to be this extreme.","I’ll never finish if I just keep digging blindly.","I briefly considered climbing out through the chimney, but quickly abandoned the idea.","The chimney was not especially wide. If I became wedged inside, it would be a disaster.","I was better off seeing this through and excavating the snow blocking the entrance.","I have to clear the entrance before it snows again.","If another snowfall came now, I might be trapped inside this cave for the rest of my life.","Even the chimney was no guarantee of safety.","Actually, forget the chimney. I was worried about the cave itself.","Once snow accumulated, its weight became tremendous.","Could this cave withstand the weight of all that snow?","Especially after I had slightly modified it to install the chimney?","I could not simply sit around doing nothing.","\"Fortunately, I have plenty of firewood.\"","I removed the curtain that had covered the entrance and lit another campfire.","The snow had frozen solid, so I decided to melt it with fire.","Of course, I was not going to sit around and wait. Once the snow had melted to a certain point, I would resume digging.","Crack! Thud!","As time passed, the snow softened and became easier to excavate.","I remained cautious, since melting snow could flow down and extinguish the campfire.","Who knew how much time had passed?","Eventually, the cavity no longer refilled whenever I removed more snow.","At last, the end was in sight.","\"Whew!\"","After all that labor with the pickaxe and shovel, I could finally see the result.","I had somehow managed to remove all the snow filling the cave entrance.","But that only applied to the entrance itself.","The surrounding area was another matter entirely.","Even directly outside the cave, the snow stood far above my head. Elsewhere, it had accumulated even higher.","People in Russia and Canada live in places like this?","How did they manage?","I was genuinely curious.","As I stared at the space I had cleared around the cave entrance, I suddenly remembered my time in the military.","I remembered shoveling whenever it snowed and scattering calcium chloride to prevent the ground from freezing.","Does this world even have a term for calcium chloride?","This world used alchemy rather than chemistry.","Historically, chemistry had developed from alchemy.","But considering how effective elixirs were, alchemy here was probably every bit as advanced as chemistry.","Wouldn’t producing calcium chloride be relatively simple?","If that isn’t possible, I can always use salt.","I had once heard that ordinary salt could be scattered in place of calcium chloride.","Something about it being more beneficial despite concerns over environmental damage.","I’ll ask about it after I finish working. For now, let’s spread some salt.","Salt was available through the auction house.","It was expensive, but it was an essential survival resource with plenty of demand, so it was never out of stock.","I proceeded section by section, scattering salt over the ground exposed by my shovel before clearing the next area.","Fortunately, it did not begin snowing again, allowing me to set up additional campfires along the way.","Still, I had to figure out how to keep this path clear and secure enough space to move around.","At this rate, I’ll need to build an emergency exit, not just a chimney.","It seemed I would soon need to borrow the wisdom of people who lived in cold regions.","I did not know how long this winter would last, but it did not seem likely to end anytime soon.","It was nearly lunchtime by the time I finished clearing the area around my shelter.","This isn’t a barren snowy mountain. There are definitely plants here...","I pondered the mystery while removing the snow covering the oven and furnace.","As I had already noted, animals and plants should not have been able to survive under this much snow.","The place should have been as barren as a snowy mountain.","There was no way these conditions would remain unchanged forever.","Perhaps everything would return to normal as early as tomorrow.","I had not been here long, and so many dramatic things had happened that I could not help forming all sorts of theories.","If the season could abruptly change to winter, perhaps it could just as suddenly become summer.","Imagining this immense amount of snow melting away offered me some comfort.","But imagination was imagination, and reality was reality.","It might snow again, so I should move everything I can into the cave.","The iron drum filled with frozen fish, the bellows, and all my assorted tools—everything that could be moved.","I could not relocate the makeshift oven or furnace, so I had no choice but to leave them outside.","They were unlikely to collapse under the snow, and even if they did, I could always rebuild them.","Or so I reassured myself.","With that, my winter preparations and precautions against isolation were nearly complete.","I had finally found a moment to rest and was about to open the Gallery when—","Ruuuuumble—","An ominous sound reached my ears, and the ground trembled faintly.","The moment I felt the noise and vibration, I rushed into the cave without hesitation.","Then, keeping my composure, I picked up my sword and shield.","My objective was not to take shelter, but to prepare myself. It was a lesson I had learned during my time here.","It was better to prepare like this than sit around waiting for whatever fate had in store for me.","Rustle—","Just before I left, the fast sloth reached out to me.","Did he want to come along?","But the fast sloth had to watch over the hibernating Wonmo.","I deliberately ignored his outstretched hand and stepped outside the cave.","Ruuuuumble!","The noise and vibrations had grown even stronger.","What in the world was coming?","Judging from its momentum, it had to be moving quickly.","That made me even more tense. I had no idea what might suddenly appear.","Just in case, I began circulating my mana and even manifested my aura.","After concentrating on the noise and vibrations for some time, I finally realized where they were coming from.","Behind... the cave?","It was coming from the exact opposite direction of the entrance.","The instant I realized that, I whipped my head around.","It was strange that the disturbance was coming from behind the cave rather than the forest, but this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","Nothing that appeared here could truly be considered strange.","Even if it was—","Rrrrrumble!","—not a living creature, but a natural disaster.","\"Oh, fu—\"","At the sight of the avalanche surging from behind the cave like a tidal wave, I experienced the illusion that time had slowed.","In that brief moment, I glanced down and saw the fast sloth looking up at me from inside the cave.","His expression seemed to say, This is why you should have listened to me instead of going out alone, you idiot.","When he had reached out earlier, he had not been asking to come with me.","He had been trying to stop me.","Roooooar!!","\"Gah! Urgh! Uwaaagh!\"","No matter how powerful an animal might be, it was helpless before the forces of nature.","The same applied to me.","I hurriedly drove my sword into the ground, but it was useless.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was simply too effective.","Rather than anchoring me, it sliced straight through the ground as the avalanche swept me away.","Its effectiveness had backfired at the worst possible moment.","W-wasn’t I being swept toward the river?","Even amid the confusion of being carried away by the avalanche, I forced myself to remember the direction.","This avalanche was heading toward the river.","And the space beyond the river changed constantly.","This was dangerous.","One wrong move, and I might never be able to return to my shelter.","Not the sword—the shield...!","I flailed with my shield instead of the Heavenly Demon’s sword, hoping it would catch on a branch or anything else.","With most of my body already buried beneath the snow, it was closer to a desperate struggle than a calculated maneuver.","Still, I had to do something.","When it came to survival, you had to try whatever you could.","Jerk!","The result of my desperate effort came quickly.","I did not know which tree I had caught on, but I could clearly feel my clothes snagging against something.","I had been prepared to abandon the Heavenly Demon’s sword if necessary, but fortunately, I stopped at just the right moment.","\"Mmmphhh!!\"","Of course, that did not change the fact that the avalanche continued battering my entire body.","I endured and endured, waiting for it to end.","\"Pwah!\"","After what felt like an eternity, the avalanche finally passed.","Ordinarily, an avalanche would leave snow piled everywhere, but strangely, this one had swept all of it away.","Thanks to that, I was not buried beneath a snowdrift and could breathe normally.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","I coughed and looked around.","The avalanche seemed to have carried away all the accumulated snow, exposing the bare earth beneath it.","Before anything else, I needed to figure out where I was.","If I had crossed the river, it would be the worst possible outcome.","I’m not across the river.","Apparently, I had snagged on a tree near the river.","I could see the frozen river from where I was, confirming it.","On the other side was terrain utterly different from this place—a pure white, snow-covered mountain.","An immense amount of snow covered the mountain as well.","The avalanche that had just passed had clearly gone in that direction.","Had the snow moved on its own?","Or had the forest expelled it?","I could not tell.","Was the terrain around here even capable of producing an avalanche in the first place?","Was there a mountain nearby?","This was confusing.","Perhaps the forest was literally alive and had cleansed itself.","With weather this awful, no plants would remain if the forest could not purify itself somehow.","It would have become just like the snowy mountain across the river.","It was a highly plausible theory.","If even the forest is like this, what the hell is happening in the other regions?","I was becoming increasingly frightened.","I quickly gathered myself and returned to the cave.","\"...Ah.\"","There, I was greeted by the devastated remains of my shelter’s yard.","Not only had the barricade been swept away, but so had the makeshift furnace and oven.","I could rebuild the furnace and oven, but the barricade was a serious problem.","So this is why there’s no civilization here.","Civilization could never develop when everything was regularly swept away.","While Grylls was filming a disaster movie all by himself—","Whoooooosh!!","—another disaster was unfolding in the grasslands of the Forest of Four Seasons.","The region naturally had distinct wet and dry seasons, so heavy rain during the wet season was to be expected.","But what would happen if far too much rain fell?","It was still a grassland, so wouldn’t the earth absorb it all?","\"Blub! Blub!\"","\"Groooan! Grooan!\"","It did not.","An actual flood had struck the grasslands, harming countless animals.","Those who suffered the most were the animals unable to find shelter—particularly the young.","Still small and weak, they were simply swept away.","\"Hmm.\"","There was someone observing the scene in real time.","It was Ludwig.","He was still wearing his heavy armor to preserve his defenses.","\"So that is why this animal has such long legs.\"","\"...\"","He was currently sitting atop a giraffe, using it to escape the disaster.","Giraffes were ordinarily known for having foul tempers, but this one did not attack Ludwig.","The bumps on its head had given it enough intelligence to judge him harmless.","I would have been in serious trouble without this animal.","Sitting on the giraffe’s back, Ludwig looked up at its face.","The giraffe stood calmly even amid the flooded grasslands.","It had merely moved beneath a massive tree to escape the rain for a while, remaining steadfast and composed.","Boom! Thud! Thud!","Then a thunderous noise reached Ludwig’s ears, accompanied by vibrations that shook the ground.","When he turned toward the source, he witnessed a sight that was difficult to believe.","Thud! Boom! Thud!","It was a turtle.","Not a sea turtle, but a tortoise.","Instead of an ordinary shell, it carried an enormous mountain upon its back.","Naturally, a creature capable of carrying a mountain was itself terrifyingly immense.","As the rain poured down heavily enough to flood the grasslands, animals climbed onto the tortoise’s back.","Had Grylls seen it, he would have called it a living Noah’s Ark.","\"...\"","Ludwig silently watched the tortoise lumber onward before turning his head away.","People can actually survive in a place like this?","Ludwig was becoming increasingly curious about Grylls.","The irony was that Grylls’s entire yard had just been swept away.","I should find shelter on higher ground. I have an excellent steed, so it should be manageable.","It was a giraffe, not a horse.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 137","paragraphs":["Disaster (2)","The sight of my completely devastated yard left me disheartened, but I tried to think positively.","I would treat this as a learning experience and prepare more thoroughly next time.","There was nothing I wouldn’t do to survive in this damned forest.","I could ask the dwarf to replace the barricade, and I could begin by gathering the materials needed to rebuild the furnace and oven.","I had already built them once, so as long as I retained access to the Gallery, restoring them should not be difficult.","Yet that sapling survived.","Everything else had been swept away, but the sapling given to me by Let’s Grow a Tree remained firmly rooted.","I was extremely curious about what kind of tree it was, but I decided not to dwell on it. Its survival was a good thing.","I should focus on preparing for disasters first.","These could not be called mere changes in climate. Each one was closer to a full-fledged natural disaster.","This was a place where an avalanche could occur despite the terrain seemingly making one impossible.","As someone had said, spring might bring not yellow dust, but an outright sandstorm.","I need to build an emergency exit too, and postpone any crafting projects until winter ends.","This was my first winter, and it was taking place in the Forest of Four Seasons. I had a mountain of work ahead of me.","I sighed at the overwhelming prospect and turned my head.","In that direction stood the grave where my senior had been buried.","How did that man survive here?","He had clearly lived here longer than I had. The sheer length of his diary made that obvious.","The diary should contain everything he experienced before his conflict with the gorillas led to his death.","They must have finished translating it by now, right?","I had entrusted the translation to All-Father and Necromancy Is Love .","Yet aside from information about the Immortal King and the gorillas, I had learned nothing from it.","It would have been nice if the diary had warned me that winter could arrive early.","I should ask.","I planned to remain holed up in the cave until the season changed.","This was as good an opportunity as any to ask about it.","I contacted All-Father first.","[Wild Grylls: All-Father, are you there?]","[All-Father: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Do you remember those records from the Balkan Kingdom that I sent you? Have you finished translating them?]","[All-Father: Not all of them. The Balkan royal family used certain unique expressions, so the translation is taking longer than expected.]","That was understandable.","I had never asked him to report his progress in real time, and rushing people was not in my nature.","Still, he should have uncovered some important facts by now.","I immediately asked my question.","[Wild Grylls: Did the records mention the seasons changing abruptly?]","[All-Father: They did. It appears winter arrived in an instant for him as well, just as it did for you.]","Just as I had expected.","My senior had experienced the same phenomenon.","This proved that even this godforsaken forest followed certain rules.","[Wild Grylls: Were there any warning signs?]","[All-Father: The diary says that large numbers of animals migrated the day before. He wrote that he warmly welcomed them.]","[Wild Grylls: Does it say how long winter lasted?]","[All-Father: Yes. Winter itself did not last long. The weather warmed after approximately five days.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s a relief.]","[All-Father: It also contains a description suggesting that all four seasons occur within a single month. You should keep that in mind.]","I felt strangely embarrassed.","Still, after what had happened with the raccoons slaughtered by the fast sloth, I could hardly be blamed.","Besides, the group I had encountered had been prepared to seize my shelter if the opportunity arose.","At any rate, I now knew the warning sign.","All that remained was to learn how long this winter would last.","Several months would already have been despair-inducing. If it lasted for years, it would have been horrifying.","Thankfully, that did not seem to be the case.","What kind of premature four-season cycle was this?","It was absurd.","Still, every season except winter had been relatively livable, so I was not too worried.","So this weather is why unintelligent animals can’t survive here.","They either possessed exceptional instincts like Wonmo or were intelligent like the raccoons.","It had to be one or the other.","Otherwise, surviving in this forest would be impossible.","The greatest danger here was not its predators, but the environment itself.","[All-Father: Ah, there is also some information you should take to heart. It concerns the gorillas in the jungle.]","[Wild Grylls: The gorillas?]","[All-Father: Yes. It appears one of them has separated from the group. The gorilla you encountered merely warned you, but the one that attacked this man did so without any provocation.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds ominous.]","[All-Father: I do not know where it is now, but you should remain cautious. According to the records, unlike the other gorillas, its fur is white. Its eyes are also said to be as red as blood.]","White fur and red eyes immediately brought albinism to mind.","I should consider the possibility that it was an albino.","Albino animals stood out more than others, so their survival rates were likely lower.","If such an animal had survived until now, it must possess incredible strength.","It might have an even worse temper than the gorilla leader.","As a mutant, it might have developed unusually high aggression.","If this one had also learned martial arts, I would be in serious trouble.","It would be a difficult fight.","The problem is that I have no idea where it might appear.","So far, I had not seen anything with white fur.","I nodded as I processed the information All-Father had provided, then decided to ask whether there were any other dangers.","[Wild Grylls: Is there anything else I should be wary of?]","[All-Father: It is less a warning than an unusual detail. This man originally suffered from mana insensitivity and was incapable of using mana.]","[Wild Grylls: Mana insensitivity?]","[All-Father: Yes. It is a congenital condition that prevents a person from accumulating mana. However, while living in the Forest of Four Seasons, he gradually began accumulating it.]","[Wild Grylls: Does that mean he evolved too?]","[All-Father: I cannot say for certain. Apparently, he ate anything he could find in order to survive, and at some point discovered that he could use mana.]","All-Father’s explanation was as follows.","My senior had been unable to accumulate mana because of a medical condition, whereas I had been unable to accept mana in the first place because I came from another world.","Regardless, it proved that the medicinal plants scattered throughout the Forest of Four Seasons possessed astonishing effects.","Of course, poisonous plants were probably mixed among them, so I would have to proceed cautiously.","[Wild Grylls: Does the diary say which medicinal plant he ate? That seems like important information.]","[All-Father: Unfortunately, I do not know. He ate random plants in an attempt to kill himself, so he neither identified nor properly recorded them.]","[Wild Grylls: Yikes.]","[All-Father: If he wanted to die, he could simply have eaten a mushroom. What a peculiar man. Hohoho.]","[Wild Grylls: Sir?]","[All-Father: It was a joke. In any event, even the weeds appear comparable to medicinal herbs. Pulling up a few at random and testing them might not be a bad idea.]","The possibility that even ordinary weeds might be medicinal filled me with hope.","[Wild Grylls: I see. Could I ask you to analyze some weeds? I’ll send you several varieties.]","[All-Father: My apologies, but I expect to become rather busy from now on. I intend to begin participating in external affairs.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, I see. Then I’ll ask someone else.]","Even if All-Father was unavailable, I still had the Starlight Princess.","If she was too busy as well, then...","I would have to figure it out myself.","Once I identified their effects, I intended to send them directly to the Heavenly Demon.","That should help him finish the fast sloth’s food sooner.","After ending my conversation with All-Father, I was casually browsing the Gallery when—","[Necromancy Is Love: Save me.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Necromancy Is Love: Keep talking to All-Father.]","[Wild Grylls: Did something happen?]","I received that strange message from Necromancy Is Love .","Even when I asked what was wrong, I received no response.","I wondered whether I should contact All-Father again, but ultimately decided against it.","If it were truly urgent, he would have made a public post on the Gallery instead of sending me a message.","There really are all kinds of strange people here.","I brushed it aside and focused on my own situation.","The seasons changed approximately once a week, so I merely had to prepare accordingly.","Besides, this was already the second day of winter.","I should only have to endure another three or four days.","Does this mean farming will be difficult?","I had planned to begin farming if necessary, but it seemed impractical.","The seasons did not change monthly, but weekly. Ordinary plants would have difficulty surviving that.","Then again, perhaps crops would grow rapidly, like the sapling that had undergone a sudden growth spurt before.","Even if I stockpile crops, I’ll need to preserve them properly...","Storage was the greatest problem.","Meat could simply be salted and smoked.","Crops, however, would rot easily if left unattended.","I could not help worrying about it.","I’d need something like a refrigerator, but that’s impossible. Maybe I could use ice instead...","The instant the word ice crossed my mind, my head snapped up.","At the same time, I checked the time through the Gallery.","It was only two o’clock, so I still had plenty of time.","I hurriedly rose, armed myself, and rushed outside.","The fast sloth was taking good care of Wonmo, so there was no need to worry about him.","My destination was the river.","The abrupt change of season had frozen it solid.","Why had I failed to realize that there was a convenient source of ice right in front of me?","I can’t just collect it without preparing first. I need to build a storage container—or an icehouse.","Wait. Ice?","My ancestors had collected ice every winter and stored it inside icehouses.","I intended to do the same.","The animals were less active during winter, so as long as I remained vigilant, I should be able to gather the ice without much difficulty.","I leaned forward to check how thickly the river had frozen.","The abrupt drop in temperature had transformed it into a river of transparent ice.","At most, I have four days. I need to build an icehouse—or at least a storage container—before then.","No matter how effective salting was for preservation, it could not compare to refrigeration.","Crops and fruit would also keep better in a cool place, so this was the perfect opportunity to build one.","With my decision made, I returned to the shelter and wrote a post on the Gallery.","I knew that my ancestors had used stone icehouses, but I knew nothing about how they actually worked.","Title: Does anyone know how to build a stone icehouse?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the frozen river)","I’m thinking about building one of those stone icehouses our ancestors used. There’s a frozen river right in front of me, so it seems like a good idea.","└ SwordMaster: An icehouse? Would you like me to give you a well-insulated box? You could probably fill it with ice.","└ Wild Grylls: That would work too, but I think building an actual icehouse would be better.","└ SwordMaster: It is not a bad choice, but could you not build it slowly?","└ Wild Grylls: The diary said the seasons change every week. That’s why I should make the most of what I can only do during winter.","└ SwordMaster: What a half-baked cycle of seasons.","└ Passing Dwarf: Damn, it’s been ages since I heard anyone mention an icehouse. Refrigerators were invented around my father’s time.","└ Wild Grylls: Do you know how to build one?","└ Passing Dwarf: The principle itself is simple. It’s just difficult to construct. I’ll make a post about it soon.","└ Wild Grylls: Thanks, thanks.","└ Aren’t icehouses still fairly common?","└ There are plenty in rural areas that haven’t been urbanized. Refrigerators have been spreading there recently, though.","The dwarf had promised to explain how to build one, so all I could do now was wait.","The disaster had dealt me a tremendous blow, but it had also presented me with an opportunity.","I was beginning to understand that winter was not merely a season to endure.","The avalanche came from behind the cave, so I should build the entrance on this side.","Until the dwarf explained the structure and construction process of a stone icehouse, I began working on what I could.","First came logging.","If I wanted to survive the winter, firewood was indispensable.","\"Hm?\"","It happened while I was diligently cutting down trees.","Something behind a fallen tree caught my eye.","All the smaller plants had been buried beneath the snow, yet this one stood upright by itself.","It was a blue flower that looked as though ice crystals had blossomed into petals.","I could not tell whether it had frozen solid or simply looked that way naturally.","What is this?","Whenever I was curious, the Gallery was the obvious place to ask.","I immediately took a picture and uploaded a post.","Title: Found a strange flower.","Wild Grylls","(A plant resembling a flower made from ice crystals)","Found this while cutting down trees. Does anyone know what it is?","└ Starlight Princess: Oh! I think that’s a Frostbloom.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s that?","└ Starlight Princess: If you absorb all of it, you should gain resistance to cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh...!","└ Starlight Princess: But if you eat it as it is, your entire body will freeze solid.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh.","└ Starlight Princess: And it melts almost immediately once the weather changes, so it would be difficult to ask someone else to process it.","What is it, a goddamned sunfish?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 138","paragraphs":["Combination (1)","The Frostbloom would freeze your entire body as solid as the ice inside a stone icehouse if consumed raw.","If moved elsewhere and exposed to even the slightest change in temperature, it would melt like snow.","But if properly processed and consumed, it could grant powerful resistance to the cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there a way to process it?","└ Starlight Princess: I could probably do it with the technology in my workshop, but I’m not sure it would be possible in your environment. And even if you brought it to my workshop, it would melt immediately.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any way I could do it by myself?","└ Starlight Princess: The important part is controlling the cold energy... For reference, you can’t simply boil it like soup.","└ Wild Grylls: Tsk...","I wanted to consume it somehow.","Resistance to cold would provide an enormous advantage.","It was so cold that even thick clothing barely kept me warm enough to avoid freezing to death.","You’d need fire energy to counteract the cold energy.","Could she at least explain the basic principle?","If I could absorb the Frostbloom, it would greatly improve my chances of survival.","At the very least, I’d be far less likely to die of hypothermia.","Even simply no longer shivering in the cold would be worthwhile.","Accumulating advantages like this one by one was how I became stronger.","The Starlight Princess did not reply for some time, seemingly lost in thought.","Just when I began wondering whether she had gone off to do something else, she posted another comment.","└ Wild Grylls: Didn’t people in ancient times eat these and record their effects? They wouldn’t have had extraction devices back then.","└ Starlight Princess: Why would anyone do something like that? It could kill them.","└ Wild Grylls: Then why do people eat pufferfish?","└ Starlight Princess: Oh.","└ That’s a damn good example. LOL","└ Who was the first lunatic to think of eating pufferfish? LOL","└ One mistake while preparing it and the poison kills you immediately.","└ I’m more curious about the first person who thought of drinking milk. How did they come up with the idea of sucking on an animal’s teat...?","└ All those attempts accumulated over time and gave us the ingredients we have today. Let’s show them some respect.","└ Not admiration, but \"respect.\" LOL","└ Starlight Princess: You place the Frostbloom in an extractor, then infuse fire energy into the extracted liquid. The principle itself is simple.","└ Wild Grylls: Is that extractor something I could use?","└ Starlight Princess: It needs to be connected to a mana circuit, like a refrigerator. If I gave it to you, wouldn’t it become nothing more than an empty metal shell?","└ Wild Grylls: T_T","└ Starlight Princess: I hate to say this, but I think you should give up.","└ Wild Grylls: I really can’t just boil it in a pot?","└ Starlight Princess: Hmm... I’ve never attempted such a primitive method, so I’m not sure. The extractor is the only method I know.","Humans were fascinating.","We had eaten all manner of plants and animals.","We had even discovered methods of preparing the poisonous ones.","Pufferfish, for example, must have required an arduous process of trial and error before people discovered how to prepare it safely.","The same logic applied to the Frostbloom.","The Starlight Princess had not realized it, but this was the detail that caught my attention.","The Frostbloom was an extremely delicate medicinal herb that melted the instant the temperature changed even slightly.","Yet records existed of people consuming it and documenting both its effects and side effects.","In other words, people living in cold regions must have discovered those properties through repeated testing.","Even if there’s no record of anyone extracting it, someone must have found a way to consume it.","It was highly likely that someone had extracted it without specialized equipment or consumed it after it had been refined through some other process.","Still, this was only my hypothesis.","They said that someone who had read only one book was more dangerous than someone who had read none at all.","└ Wild Grylls: What if I post updates in real time while I experiment? If you notice anything strange, please tell me immediately.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s not a bad idea. But you must follow everything I say without question. Understood?","└ Wild Grylls: Of course. The stone icehouse takes priority, so I’ll contact you about this later.","└ Starlight Princess: Please don’t push yourself too far.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. That stone icehouse needs to be built underground. Don’t you have mithril inside your home?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t have to build it inside the cave. I can build it outside. There’s no mithril out there.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then do you know which direction the wind blows? Not in winter—in summer.","└ Wild Grylls: Why does that matter?","└ Passing Dwarf: From what I can tell, you’ll need to use convection. Cold air sinks to the floor while hot air rises.","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t know. I’m only building a temporary one anyway, so just explain the basic principles. It only needs to last one month. The seasons here apparently change every week.","└ Passing Dwarf: What kind of ridiculous place is that? Anyway, got it. I’ll make a post soon.","Now I had to learn the direction of the wind as well.","This was getting absurd.","Fortunately, the seasons here changed weekly. If they lasted an entire month each, this would have been far more troublesome.","It seemed best to build the stone icehouse as a prototype and use a storage box for everything else.","SwordMaster had offered to give me a box made from well-insulated materials, so I could simply accept that.","But it would feel wrong to receive it without giving her anything in return...","What should I give her?","SwordMaster was actually the most difficult person to repay.","The Heavenly Demon would happily accept anything I gave him, but SwordMaster was different.","She refused medicinal herbs because she did not want to become stronger, and she barely cared about food.","She was someone who focused solely on my growth, which made it difficult to decide how to repay her.","Would she like a sword?","She did not merely like swordsmanship—she loved it.","Following that logic, perhaps she would like swords as well.","A master did not blame their tools, but that did not mean they were entirely indifferent to them.","Perhaps she would even enjoy a beautiful sword.","I can think about that slowly. First, I need to understand the icehouse’s structure.","I had plenty of time to think, but not much time to build.","The avalanche had swept everything away, leaving me with a long list of things to reconstruct.","Should I rebuild the furnace and oven more sturdily from the beginning? Or should I put them inside the cave?","While considering it, I sent SwordMaster a message.","I proposed giving her an exceptionally fine sword later in exchange for an insulated storage box.","[SwordMaster: She sent me a picture just to brag about hers. ;;]","[Wild Grylls: ;;]","The Heavenly Demon was acting awfully childish for someone her age.","Still, at least she had not made a public post about it.","And the fact that she had bragged specifically to SwordMaster suggested that she regarded SwordMaster as a friend.","SwordMaster would probably fly into a rage if she heard me say that, but it should be fine.","[Wild Grylls: In any case, I’ll give it to you later. Would you accept it?]","[SwordMaster: It’s fine. A master does not blame their tools.]","[Wild Grylls: It glows when you channel mana into it, though.]","[SwordMaster: I suppose there’s nothing wrong with keeping one as an ornament rather than using it in battle.]","[SwordMaster: Did you give that sword to the Heavenly Demon?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Did I mention that before?]","It was an outstanding sword, yet she intended to use it merely as decoration.","Still, I was relieved that she was willing to accept it.","Trading a Misricon sword for an insulated box could hardly be called an equal exchange, but that did not matter.","I only had to consider all the help SwordMaster had given me.","Until now, she had assisted me almost entirely without compensation.","The Heavenly Demon might feel neglected, so I should prepare something separately for her.","With that thought, I examined the box SwordMaster had sent me.","Perhaps because plastic had not yet been invented in her world, it looked like an ordinary wooden box from the outside.","Its interior walls, however, were surrounded by multiple materials, including marble.","Given how many layers it had, it should function well as an icebox.","Now I merely needed to fill it with ice.","I moved the box inside and thanked SwordMaster.","\"The dwarf... posted it.\"","Perfectly timed, the dwarf had uploaded his instructions.","I opened the post immediately.","Title: Here’s the structure of a stone icehouse. Take a look.","Passing Dwarf","(An image of a stone icehouse’s structure)","(A cross-sectional diagram of a stone icehouse)","(An image of a stone icehouse surrounded by brick walls)","(An image of a brick-vaulted ceiling)","It looks roughly like this.","Building it properly will take a long time, so take it slowly.","When you put the ice inside, pack snow or straw into the gaps between the blocks. Buy a straw mat from the auction house and pull it apart.","└ Wild Grylls: Wait. The ceiling has to be built from bricks too? How am I supposed to do that?","└ Passing Dwarf: What do you mean, how? Use your ingenuity.","└ Wild Grylls: Damn. This is going to be brutal.","└ Where did you take those pictures? The cross-section aside, the others look like actual photographs.","└ Passing Dwarf: They were in a museum.","└ Grylls is the only bastard here living in a museum. LOL","└ Everyone else uses refrigerators while he’s stuck using a stone icehouse. LOL","People whose civilizations had barely reached the modern era were mocking me as a primitive.","I’ll have you know that I once enjoyed the pinnacle of modern civilization.","These people would wet themselves if they witnessed the destructive power of a nuclear bomb, yet they dared make fun of me.","So how am I supposed to build this?","There’s nothing else I can do, so I should shut up and build the stone icehouse.","Grumbling inwardly, I gathered my pickaxe and shovel.","Given how late it was, I had no intention of completing the work in a single day.","It’s supposed to be partially underground, right?","Ordinarily, I would have needed to account for the direction of the wind, but this one was merely experimental.","It would serve as a foundation for testing whether ice could be preserved for an entire month.","I planned to keep it small to reduce the labor involved, while still building it carefully.","The frozen ground isn’t making this easy.","Even digging the ground took a long time.","It would be better to light a campfire and work on something else while it thawed the frozen earth.","I continued digging until around four o’clock, then stopped.","I had other tasks to handle, including extracting the Frostbloom.","I’ll spend thirty minutes harvesting ice, then prepare the Frostbloom.","Carrying the insulated box, I headed toward the river.","With winter’s arrival, animal activity had dropped considerably.","Unless I encountered something that remained active during winter, such as a wolf, I was unlikely to be attacked.","I was staying vigilant just in case, so I would not be caught helplessly off guard either.","I’ll need to cut it with a saw, right?","Upon reaching the frozen river, I purchased a saw from the auction house.","I tapped the ice’s surface with the small hammer I had brought, then inserted the saw into it.","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","I began sawing out a precise square.","Now that I was cutting through it, I realized the river had not frozen all the way to the bottom. At a certain depth, the saw suddenly broke through.","Keeping that in mind, I continued cutting carefully.","\"Heave-ho!\"","Splash!","I extracted a neatly cut rectangular block of ice, and river water immediately filled the empty space.","Crackle!","Before long, even that water froze solid in the brutal cold.","Just how cold did it have to be for water to freeze almost instantly?","With considerable effort, I carried the transparent block of ice to the box and placed it inside.","I had noticed it while cutting, but the ice was incredibly thick.","Could I go ice fishing too?","The idle thought crossed my mind, but I dismissed it.","I continued harvesting ice while remaining alert in case something like a golden frog suddenly emerged.","Fortunately, there was no reaction from beneath the ice. Either all the frogs had frozen to death or they were hibernating.","Apparently, winter was the season in which I could live with relatively little fear.","\"Ugh. My hands sting.\"","That did not change the fact that my hands were freezing.","I wore another pair of gloves over the World Tree gloves, making two layers in total, yet my hands were still cold.","The icy moisture had seeped through both layers.","At this rate, I might end up with frostbite.","I hurriedly finished the work and returned to the cave.","I had collected four blocks of ice in total.","For now, I placed them inside the box, but once the stone icehouse was complete, I intended to store them there.","\"There’s... plenty of time.\"","Now that I had finished collecting the ice, all that remained was the Frostbloom.","One might ask why I did not simply extract it inside the cave, but I had an idea.","The mature mandrake.","The mature mandrake was a plant that contained yang energy.","And I had heard that yang energy represented heat.","Therefore, wouldn’t boiling the cold-energy-filled Frostbloom together with the mature mandrake work?","Thud! Smack! Thump!","\"Squeak! Skree! Gweck!\"","And so, I beat the mature mandrake senseless.","This thing had to be beaten before it would behave.","Carrying the limp mature mandrake, I returned to the cave.","I then prepared a suitable pot and lit the campfire.","As soon as the fire was burning, I made a post on the Gallery.","Title: Combining a Frostbloom with a mature mandrake","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the battered mature mandrake)","(A photo of the Frostbloom before harvesting)","Wouldn’t combining these two work?","└ Heavenly Demon: The theory itself does not seem unsound. It is an appropriate combination of yang and yin.","└ Wild Grylls: Right?","└ Starlight Princess: As the Heavenly Demon said, the theory isn’t bad. Although it does seem a little... crude.","└ Wild Grylls: Should I put them both in a pot and boil them together?","└ Starlight Princess: That would probably be best. Extracting their essences would somewhat weaken their energies, so boiling them raw may actually work better.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","Now that I had received permission from an expert, I harvested the Frostbloom.","Fortunately, human body heat did not appear to affect it, and it retained its original shape.","Now I put them in together...","I added a little water as well. That should allow their properties to seep out like a broth.","Once I covered the pot with its lid, all the preparations were complete.","Now I merely had to wait.","I did not forget to check periodically for anything unusual.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video showing the Frostbloom and mature mandrake still unchanged) Nothing has changed yet. The Frostbloom hasn’t even melted.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s probably because they’re both rare medicinal plants. You should wait patiently.","If I opened the lid, the mandrake’s screams would fill the entire cave.","I left it as it was and hurriedly asked the Gallery for advice.","How long would I have to simmer them before something changed?","I added another piece of firewood.","I wanted to work on something else, but I had no idea what might happen if I left the pot unattended.","And so I sat there, staring into the fire.","Clatter!","The pot’s lid suddenly began rattling.","\"Skreeeeeeee!!\"","The mandrake’s scream rang out from inside it.","Had it awakened after enough time had passed?","That would be a serious problem.","Do I need to beat it unconscious again?","I pressed down on the lid to prevent the mature mandrake from bursting out.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of screams coming from the pot) I think the mandrake woke up. What should I do? I’m holding the lid shut for now.","└ Starlight Princess: Letting it continue screaming isn’t good either. Even if it’s risky, you should knock it unconscious again.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","After receiving the expert’s advice, I took a deep breath.","I would have to time this perfectly.","The mature mandrake did not scream continuously. It only shrieked intermittently.","It would fall silent and then begin screaming again.","Therefore, I had to act during one of the quiet intervals.","\"Skreeeeeeee!!\"","Before long, the mandrake screamed once more.","I waited until it fell silent, then immediately removed the lid.","And what I saw was—","\"What the hell is this?\"","The mature mandrake had turned completely blue.","Its face was so blue that it looked dead, yet it was clearly alive and thrashing around.","It had originally been red, so its sudden transformation into blue was even more bewildering.","Did they fuse instead of combine?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 139","paragraphs":["Combination (2)","The mature mandrake had turned blue, apparently after absorbing the Ice Blossom.","Mature mandrakes really did resemble humans, which only made them more frightening.","Its eyes were wide open, and its mouth opened and closed like a goldfish’s. It genuinely looked as though it were moments away from freezing to death.","I wondered what I should do with it, then decided to leave a comment first.","The Starlight Princess would probably know at least something about this phenomenon.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of the blue mandrake) It turned out like this. What happened to it?","└ Starlight Princess: Huh? Why did it end up like that? Why is it blue?","└ Wild Grylls: Excuse me?;;","└ Uh. Why’d that thing turn blue?","└ Did it get a blue badge too?","└ Looks like it just died. What blue badge are you talking about?;;","Even the Starlight Princess seemed bewildered.","If that was the case, I was screwed.","But as they said, even when the sky collapsed, there was always a hole to escape through.","Not long afterward, the Starlight Princess posted another comment explaining the probable cause.","└ He’s seriously trying to turn everything in the Forest of the Four Seasons into liquor, lol.","└ He’ll be making snake wine next, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: From the looks of it, the mature mandrake seems to have absorbed the Ice Blossom... First, we need to check whether it’s still alive. Could you poke it with a chopstick or a twig?","└ Wild Grylls: I poked it, but all it did was open and close its mouth.","└ Starlight Princess: Does it scream?","└ Wild Grylls: It does, but the screaming keeps cutting out instead of continuing steadily.","└ Starlight Princess: Then the mature mandrake really must have absorbed the Ice Blossom. I never expected this to happen.","└ Wild Grylls: What should I do now?","└ Starlight Princess: Surprisingly, this isn’t a bad situation. It means their energies have blended. Eating it raw would be dangerous, so I’ll tell you how to extract its essence.","└ Wild Grylls: Can’t I just send it to you as it is? You should be able to extract it right away.","└ Starlight Princess: That wouldn’t be a bad option either, but I’m worried the Ice Blossom’s effects might disappear if something goes wrong.","└ Passing Dwarf: Can’t you just make liquor out of it? Honestly, I think that’d be better.","└ Wild Grylls: Be honest. You only said that because you want it, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: Was it that obvious? If you have another one, give me one.","└ Wild Grylls: Good grief, lol. You’re so predictable.","I casually ignored the alcoholic dwarf’s suggestion and waited for the Starlight Princess to explain the method.","The combination of an Ice Blossom and a mature mandrake was practically a first for even her.","Both were herbs that money couldn’t buy, and I had combined them.","It was an idea—and a method—that only I, someone living in the Forest of the Four Seasons, could attempt.","’Putting mature mandrakes aside, Ice Blossoms must be extremely difficult to obtain.’","In truth, if this experiment failed, even I had no idea when I would be able to acquire another Ice Blossom.","Unlike mandrakes, they didn’t grow in colonies.","I prayed that it wouldn’t fail.","This might be my first and last opportunity.","└ Starlight Princess: (Image of a mandrake’s anatomy) As you can see in the picture, mandrakes resemble humans, so their vital points are similar too. You still have a syringe, right?","└ Wild Grylls: The one you gave me before?","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. Fill it with elixir and stick it straight into the mandrake’s mouth.","└ Wild Grylls: That sounds like torture.","└ Starlight Princess: Exactly. Force-feed it until its stomach is completely swollen.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","└ Poor mandrake.","└ Humanity is sorry.","└ He’s shoving it so deep that it can’t even scream, lololol.","└ Couldn’t he just crush it and turn it into juice? I seriously feel sorry for it, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: After that, put it in a mortar and grind it finely. That should extract a highly concentrated essence.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s an extremely primitive method.","└ Starlight Princess: There’s no other way. Do you need a mortar?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I can buy one from the auction house.","I knew nothing about the process, so I had no choice but to do as I was told.","Following the Starlight Princess’s instructions, I filled the syringe with elixir.","Then I jammed it into the blue mature mandrake’s mouth.","Shnk!","\"Kkueok?! Kkuuk! Kkueoooeok!\"","The instant I inserted the syringe, the mandrake thrashed around, trying to scream.","But since I was forcibly holding its mouth shut, its struggle was futile.","Still, perhaps because it looked human, it even flailed its arms and legs.","It went so far as to grab the needle with its hands, trying to pull the syringe out of its mouth.","Whack! Smack!","\"Kkuyolk?! Kkuup!\"","So I hit it a few times and told it to stay still.","It was troublesome, but this was part of the process of extracting its essence, so I endured it.","In the end, I injected all the elixir into the mature mandrake.","Its body remained blue, but it gradually began to glow.","It seemed to be absorbing the elixir’s energy.","\"Kkiyo...!\"","Whack!","\"Gguek! Kkiyoooo...!\"","Thwack! Smack!","\"Kueek! Kkiyoooot...!\"","\"Kkiyooooot! Kkiyoooo!!\"","\"Ah, come on.\"","Had this thing taken drugs instead of absorbing an Ice Blossom?","The moment I removed the syringe from its mouth, it began making a bizarre noise.","It wasn’t a mandrake’s characteristic scream.","Instead, it sounded like something that had gotten ridiculously high. Even punching it didn’t calm it down.","It was probably recovering in real time because I had injected it with elixir.","Even its face looked completely blissed out, making it react like a genuine drug addict.","Elixir was technically a \"medicine,\" so it seemed to have had a strange effect on the mandrake.","Whack! Smack! Thump!","\"Kueek! Keek! Kkueek!\"","So I hit it a few more times.","Thanks to that, the mandrake went limp like a corpse.","I had used half a bottle of elixir, so I prepared the mortar.","For hygiene’s sake, I didn’t forget to wash both the mortar and the mandrake with water.","’She told me to grind it finely and collect the juice, right?’","According to the Starlight Princess, the juice itself was the essence.","Incidentally, although I was only mentioning it now, her method prioritized safety.","Apparently, there was a more reliable method, but it would place a burden on my survival. That was why she had chosen the safer option.","I had absolutely no intention of risking my life just to gain strength, so I obediently followed her instructions.","Thud! Thump! Thud!","I finely pounded the mature mandrake inside the mortar.","It wasn’t a small bowl-shaped mortar, but a full-sized mortar traditionally used for pounding grain.","I had bought it so I could extract as much essence as possible.","’Is this enough?’","After being pounded for quite some time, the mature mandrake had been completely pulverized.","It was still blue.","I tilted the mortar slightly and poured the essence into the empty elixir bottle, which I had washed thoroughly.","Only a few drops came out, but I wasn’t finished yet.","Squeeze!","I grabbed the finely crushed mandrake with my hand and wrung it out with all my strength.","I applied the maximum grip strength I could muster, to the point that the veins stood out on the back of my hand.","Drip! Drip!","Juice trickled down.","After repeating the process several times, I managed to fill about half the bottle.","The elixir bottle was extremely small, so it couldn’t be called a large amount, but it was enough.","Shwaaaa—","Perhaps because the essence contained elixir as well, it wasn’t an ordinary shade of blue.","It was an incredibly beautiful color, a perfect blend of ice-white and blue.","It glowed like an elixir, making it look like a precious medicine at first glance.","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of the glowing blue essence) I’ve extracted all of it. I can drink it now, right?","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. Still, just in case, I’ll give you another elixir. It contains plenty of yang essence, so it should be sufficient for emergencies.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","Now that I had even received an emergency elixir from the Starlight Princess, all that remained was to drink this.","I stared at the blue, glittering essence and took a deep breath.","Essence was a liquid containing powerful energy.","It would be easiest to think of it as an inner core in liquid form.","Therefore, I only needed to calmly control the energy while reciting the second mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","’It should be fine. I even mixed in elixir to make it safer.’","Everything was difficult the first time.","I swallowed nervously, then drank all the essence in one gulp.","From my mouth down to my throat, I felt a coldness so intense that it stung.","On top of that, it was unbearably bitter.","The bitterness was so extreme that my entire face twisted.","It was so much stronger than the cold that I nearly failed to circulate the heart method.","’Th-The heavens become me... Wait, that’s not it.’","As if I had eaten ice cream too quickly, a sharp ache rang through my head as well.","The double blow of bitterness and brain freeze made my consciousness grow hazy, but I somehow managed to recite the chant.","There was no pain, but the sensations assaulting me were intense enough to rival it, making the process far from easy.","Even so, I kept trying.","Rather than losing consciousness and being overwhelmed by the energy, I worked to accept it.","As the Heavenly Demon had taught me, to control the energy of the heavens, I first needed to understand that energy.","I concentrated on sensing every strand of energy contained within the essence.","Whoosh!","The results of the safety-focused production method combined with my efforts gradually began to appear.","The essence started flowing along the same pathways through which my mana circulated according to the heart method.","If I continued circulating it steadily, it wouldn’t take long to absorb the entire essence.","Although the inside of my body felt as cold as if it contained a solid block of ice, it was bearable.","Whoooosh!","I had no idea how much time passed after that.","Eventually, I absorbed the essence completely.","I continued circulating the heart method for a little longer before slowly opening my eyes.","The tree sloth was there, staring blankly at me.","\"Phew...\"","The fact that I could see the tree sloth meant I was still alive.","I let out a long sigh.","As I exhaled, white breath escaped my mouth.","\"Did it... work?\"","Having absorbed all the essence, I examined every part of my body.","Nothing had visibly changed.","The same was true of the cold.","I still felt chilly.","It appeared that I hadn’t gained the cold resistance that had originally been my goal.","What a shame.","’There’s nothing I can do about it. Even the Starlight Princess wasn’t certain.’","That didn’t mean I could have disregarded safety.","To report the results, I made a post in the gallery.","Title: Results of the First Attempt","Wild Grylls","Nothing seems to have changed. I guess the energies were completely neutralized.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s unfortunate. I’m truly sorry that my knowledge was inadequate.","└ Wild Grylls: No, it’s all right. You didn’t do anything wrong, Princess. It would have been strange if we succeeded on the very first try, wouldn’t it?","└ Starlight Princess: Even if we set the Ice Blossom aside, I think I need to conduct more research on mature mandrakes. Could you give me the remains later?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. You gave me an elixir too, so I’ll send them to you.","└ Passing Dwarf: See? I told you making liquor would’ve been better.","└ Wild Grylls: Nonsense.","└ Starlight Princess: It isn’t entirely nonsense. Snake wine and ginseng wine are essentially ways of drinking extracted essence too.","└ Passing Dwarf: See that? Heh.","└ Wild Grylls: Even so, alcohol is a bit...;;","└ Passing Dwarf: Just give it a try. If you make some, I’ll give you something amazing.","└ Wild Grylls: If I can make it, lol.","I would need another Ice Blossom before I could even think about making it again.","I soothed my disappointment and checked the time.","I still had a little time left.","Building the ice storage house would take too long, but I seemed to have enough time to cut firewood for the night.","Fwoosh!","\"Hm?\"","I had just coated my axe in aura to make the logging easier when I noticed something strange.","My aura had originally been nearly colorless.","But not now.","It was a vivid blue—a frigid blue that looked cold enough to sting.","’No. It really is cold.’","Although it still flickered like flames, it gave off cold air instead of heat.","Curious, I placed my hand against the aura, but it didn’t harm me at all.","’Did it just make my aura cooler?’","What was this supposed to be, all style and no substance?","I chuckled.","What mattered right now was cutting wood.","Even if its color had changed, aura was still aura.","I swung the axe, putting my back into the blow.","Thunk!","The axe blade struck precisely into the center of the tree.","Crackle—crack, crack, crack!","Starting from the point of impact, the entire tree froze solid.","My jaw dropped at the unbelievable sight.","’Just what the hell did I drink?’","I couldn’t decide whether I should be pleased or worried.","In any case, one thing was certain.","’Th-This is freaking awesome...!’","I had unintentionally obtained an incredible ability.","An Ice Blossom, a mature mandrake, and finally, an elixir.","Every single ingredient was extraordinarily rare.","Perhaps such a result was only natural after mixing all three together.","’...What would happen if I combined this with a sword?’","A completely pointless thought suddenly crossed my mind.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 140","paragraphs":["Combination (3)","I purchased some water from the auction house to properly test the effects of my aura.","One might ask why I didn’t simply melt the ice stored in the box, but if my theory proved wrong, I would have to go out and cut more ice.","I didn’t want to go through that hassle, so I decided to buy water just this once.","I poured the water into a metal bucket and submerged my sword in it.","All I had to do was manifest my aura as before and wait to see what happened.","Crackle!","The moment I manifested my aura, the water began cooling at a tremendous rate.","But the water wasn’t the only thing freezing solid. Ice started spreading across the entire metal bucket.","At this rate, I would lose the whole bucket, so I hurriedly put it away.","Apparently, the effect only applied to the area in contact with my aura, because the ice didn’t trap the sword.","’Can’t I control this?’","Freezing water was all well and good. I had obtained an incredible ability, after all.","But if I couldn’t control it, it would become a poison rather than a blessing.","I didn’t know whether my mana itself had changed, but this clearly required a thorough investigation.","’At least it seems like I can control the intensity by adjusting the amount of aura...’","Through experimentation, I discovered that I could regulate its strength by changing the amount of aura.","However, I had no idea how to turn the cold attribute on and off.","I didn’t even know whether this change was permanent or would eventually disappear.","After thinking it over repeatedly, I finally decided to ask the gallery.","Title: Let It Come...","Wild Grylls","(Video of a bucket of water freezing after an aura-coated sword is submerged in it)","My sword hungers.","Just kidding. Does anyone know why this is happening?","I froze an entire tree while logging, so I tested it and found out that my aura has gained a cold attribute.","I can’t turn it on or off at will, either. Anyone know how?","└ Heavenly Demon: What beautifully colored sword energy. It even sparkles. It is more beautiful than what those fellows from the North Sea use.","└ Wild Grylls: Do the people of the North Sea control cold energy?","└ Heavenly Demon: Most of them do. However, they control cold energy through martial arts. You know no martial art for controlling cold energy, do you?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I only know the mnemonic chants you taught me.","└ Heavenly Demon: How fascinating. Perhaps your internal energy itself has taken on the properties of cold.","└ SwordMaster: I agree with the Heavenly Demon. Elemental aura isn’t entirely unheard of, but it usually requires the user to master a special heart method. In your case, Mr. Grylls, it seems as though your mana itself has taken on the properties of cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there no way to turn it on and off?","└ Heavenly Demon: I do not know. As I said, even the North Sea Ice Palace produces cold energy through its martial arts.","└ SwordMaster: This is my first time seeing anything like it, so I don’t know either. I’ve seen people control fire and lightning, but I’ve never encountered mana that was itself elemental.","└ With performance like that, doesn’t he basically not need an ice storage house or anything else anymore?","└ For real. He wanted a refrigerator so badly that he became one himself, lol.","└ Why does this guy always get stronger in such bizarre ways?;;","└ The fact that he keeps getting stronger through such novel methods is ridiculous, lolol.","└ Starlight Princess: As the others said, it seems the essence blended with your mana and gave it the properties of cold. I never anticipated this either.","└ Wild Grylls: It isn’t necessarily a bad thing, is it?","└ Starlight Princess: If your body had been unable to withstand the cold, your mana would have frozen first. In the worst case, you could develop something similar to the Severed Meridian Syndrome I suffer from, so you should prepare for that possibility in advance.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll keep that in mind.","└ All-Father: There have been a few recorded cases of mana acquiring the properties of a particular element later in life. They were mentioned in ancient texts.","└ Wild Grylls: Did those people undergo a process like mine?","└ All-Father: No. In most cases, the elemental essence was injected directly into their mana circuits. The results were not particularly favorable.","└ Wild Grylls: What do you mean, \"not particularly favorable\"?","└ All-Father: Those injected with cold essence had their organs freeze solid, as though they had contracted Severed Meridian Syndrome. Those injected with fire essence were unable to withstand the heat, and their mana circuits quickly melted.","└ Wild Grylls: Sh-Sh-Shiver me timbers...","└ All-Father: Just in case, it would be wise to obtain mature mandrake essence, as the Starlight Princess suggested.","└ Wild Grylls: Why didn’t you warn me about this before?","└ All-Father: Because you used an elixir alongside it. An elixir is hardly some common potion. It healed your body until it could absorb and adapt to the essence, making it an ideal safeguard. The cases I mentioned involved injecting pure essence alone.","So this ability wasn’t something I could celebrate unreservedly.","I had only been able to absorb it thanks to the mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me. Without that, it could have been extremely dangerous.","Only time would tell, but side effects might appear later, so I needed to be prepared.","└ PraiseTheSun: With just one of those, you’d never have to worry about ice again. Can you give me one? I bet selling ice would be sweet.","└ Wild Grylls: Sorry, but I made this with the only Ice Blossom I had. Besides, I have no idea what side effects it might cause.","└ PraiseTheSun: I’m not going to eat it myself anyway, so I don’t care about the side effects. It’s a shame you don’t have another Ice Blossom.","└ Wild Grylls: Just who were you planning to feed it to?","└ PraiseTheSun: I have someone in mind. If you find another one later, would you be willing to trade?","└ Wild Grylls: Let’s talk after I find one. I still haven’t obtained the ability I wanted.","I might have gained the cold attribute, but I hadn’t acquired resistance to the cold.","Moreover, it could easily become an awkward, practically useless ability if I wasn’t careful, so training was essential.","Too much of anything was never good.","’But can I use this with my bare hands?’","Would the cold manifest if I channeled aura into my hand rather than a sword?","Curious, I shattered the ice inside the metal bucket with a hammer and filled it with water again.","Then I submerged my hand in the water.","Crackle!","As expected, the water froze solid.","It seemed I could use the ability perfectly well with my bare hands.","’This could come in handy when I don’t have a weapon.’","I was the type who relied heavily on weapons. I knew almost nothing about unarmed combat.","This ability might help me overcome a worst-case scenario.","Of course, as I had repeatedly mentioned, there was no telling what danger it might cause if I couldn’t properly control it.","’For the time being, I should focus on controlling it.’","Between practicing swordsmanship, circulating my heart method, and training this ability, I had a lot to do.","Was this why people said it was better to focus on mastering one discipline?","I thought it would be best to train the cold only until I could control it properly.","’It’s not like I’m planning to unleash an Ice Age.’","Even in a fantasy world, something on that scale should be impossible.","Well, there were people who could casually slice through mountains with their swords, but I was an exception.","After cleaning up, I resumed logging.","I couldn’t use my sword energy because of the cold attribute, so I had no choice but to do it with brute strength.","Still, my body had become sturdy enough that I could gather the wood without much difficulty.","’It’s about time for dinner.’","Was it because it was winter?","The sun seemed to set unusually early.","As far as I knew, the time of sunset was influenced by revolution rather than rotation.","If the sun truly was setting earlier, it meant the change was occurring on a planetary scale, not merely within this region.","’I’ve heard of the midnight sun, where daylight lasts all day.’","I wasn’t sure.","Since this was the Forest of the Four Seasons, I had no choice but to accept it and move on.","Afterward, I ate smoked tiger meat and warmed myself by adding more firewood to the fireplace.","Even after everything that had happened, our adorable Wonmo was still sleeping.","It seemed that once winter arrived, he spent all his time asleep to conserve energy.","’Well, he’s still a cub...’","The other animals had become less active anyway.","The only dangers I had encountered so far were the blizzard and avalanche.","Besides, while I had lacked experience, both of those disasters were things I could prepare for.","’I absolutely need an emergency exit... I should probably build it like the chimney.’","Considering the force of an avalanche, it would definitely need to be built from bricks.","The chimney had remained intact even when the avalanche struck. At the very least, it wouldn’t be swept away.","Still, some damage would be unavoidable, so I would have to inspect it periodically.","’What’s better than mud...? Cement, I suppose.’","Did cement exist in this world?","Or was there something different that served the same purpose?","Even on Earth, many ancient structures had remained standing for countless years.","Fortress walls in particular were so sturdy that they could barely be demolished even with cannon fire.","Despite the technological limitations of their era, people in ancient times built civilizations by using every resource available to them.","The same applied to me.","I would use everything at my disposal and survive until the very end.","’I should ask the dwarf... No, I should ask the entire gallery. This might not be his field of expertise.’","The dwarf mentioned that often. If something fell outside his field, even he wouldn’t know about it.","He had personally researched the things he had taught me so far.","Title: Anyone Know How to Bind Bricks More Firmly?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the chimney)","So far, I’ve just been slathering mud between the bricks to hold them in place. Does anyone know a better method?","I’m asking because I want to build it more sturdily if it collapses later. Mud seems like it has its limits.","└ Starlight Princess: From what I’ve heard, castles were built using a paste made by mixing lime and sand.","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, the verified user above is right. More precisely, there’s something called cement. Mix that with sand.","└ Wild Grylls: Cement? The same cement I know?","My eyes widened.","Cement existed in this world too?","I hadn’t used the word because I assumed it wouldn’t exist here, yet the dwarf brought it up immediately.","Even if the substance was the same, I had never imagined it would have the same name.","└ Wild Grylls: I never imagined it would exist here;; When was cement invented?","└ Passing Dwarf: Dunno. It’s been around for freaking ages. One thing’s for sure, though: we invented cement.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re not lying, are you?","└ Passing Dwarf: Wanna bet?","└ All-Father: He is not lying. It is said that the discovery of cement was one reason dwarven technology advanced so rapidly. Of the three necessities—food, clothing, and shelter—it made their shelters considerably sturdier.","└ Passing Dwarf: Ah, why’d you tell him? I could’ve squeezed something out of him.","└ Wild Grylls: You would’ve only asked me for alcohol anyway, lol.","└ All-Father: However, there are some suspicious aspects to its history. It was considered far beyond the technology of its era, so scholars debated the matter extensively. That is why I called it a discovery rather than an invention.","└ Wild Grylls: Are you saying it simply appeared out of nowhere?","└ All-Father: Yes. If you think about it, the gift I gave you is a similar case. It cannot be manufactured even with modern technology.","└ Passing Dwarf: What kind of cement are you thinking of?","└ Wild Grylls: Something you mix with other stuff and slather on. Then it hardens over time.","└ Passing Dwarf: You know exactly what it is. You’re loaded, so why haven’t you been using it all this time?","The gift All-Father had given me was the subspace backpack.","Although it couldn’t ignore mass, it completely disregarded spatial limitations.","It was an excellent tool that allowed me to save an enormous amount of space.","└ All-Father: Scholars hypothesize that an ancient artifact happened to survive in storage.","└ Wild Grylls: An ancient artifact?","└ All-Father: Yes. It dates back to the age when the gods still descended upon the mortal world—a civilization beyond the reach of even modern humanity.","Was he talking about the sort of ancient civilization commonly found in novels and comics?","Something like lost technology?","A civilization that had disappeared for some unknown reason, leaving only traces behind.","Earth had similar cases, so I wasn’t surprised that the same thing had happened in this world.","One needed to look no further than ancient Egypt. We still had no idea exactly how they had built the pyramids.","’Although once you’ve served in the military, you start believing humans really could have built them.’","Anyway, I set that aside and returned to the main topic.","Now that I knew cement existed, all I needed was the proper method.","The dwarf seemed to know the basics and explained them to me.","└ Passing Dwarf: If you’re spreading it between bricks, mix it with sand, not soil.","└ Wild Grylls: Why?","└ Passing Dwarf: Dunno. My father told me to do it that way.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay, lol.","└ For some reason, that sounds strangely trustworthy, lolol.","└ Isn’t that exactly the same as doing whatever your academy professor tells you?","└ Yep. Undergraduates just do what their professors tell them. Nobody knows the underlying principles, lol.","’Do I need to go downstream or to the sea?’","Everything around here was soil rather than sand.","I would only find sand downstream or at the seashore.","Even though it was winter, I wanted to avoid the sea if possible.","Going downstream would be much better.","I wasn’t going to build it immediately. I merely intended to start gathering the materials now.","’They don’t sell sand at the auction house.’","After briefly checking the auction house, I left another comment for the dwarf.","Putting cement aside, there was something else I wanted to ask him.","└ Wild Grylls: Hey. Are there weapons imbued with elemental properties?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, they exist. Hammers with the lightning attribute, swords that blaze with fire, things like that. Why?","└ Wild Grylls: How are they normally created? Does it happen naturally?","└ Passing Dwarf: Usually, I guess? The Lightning Hammer gained its power after being struck by a bolt from the sky. Its original owner got struck too and died, though, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: What about the fire weapon? Did its owner burn to death?","└ Passing Dwarf: Nope. I heard it was a sword found embedded in the middle of a volcanic crater. Why are you asking?","└ Wild Grylls: I was wondering whether one could be made artificially. For example, by adding the essence I drank to a sword while it’s being forged.","└ Passing Dwarf: There you go talking nonsense again, lol. Find another Ice-Whatever-Blossom first, then we’ll talk.","└ A cold-attributed sword would be freaking awesome, though, lolol.","└ But even if you made one, it’s not like you’d sell it.","└ Wild Grylls: It’d just be for decoration, lol.","\"Oh. There’s another one?\"","While gathering wood, I discovered another Ice Blossom.","\"There’s one here, and another one over there... Why are there so many?\"","There wasn’t merely one. There were several.","I could find them simply by searching carefully between the trees.","’Are they like seasonal produce?’","What were they, wild spring greens?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 141","paragraphs":["Combination (4)","The Ice Blossom was an herb found only in cold regions—and even there, it was exceedingly rare.","Moreover, it tended to melt as soon as the temperature rose even slightly, and it remained in bloom for only a short time.","It could grow only during the limited season of winter, had a short lifespan, and possessed the durability of an ocean sunfish.","Most importantly, it required land abundant in mana.","All those conditions combined to make it an exceptionally rare herb.","As always, however, the Forest of the Four Seasons seemed to be an exception.","There was no need to explain how much mana existed here.","The seasons changed every week, so its short lifespan wasn’t a problem either.","If I searched around the shelter, I could find Ice Blossoms with relative ease.","Therefore, to me, Ice Blossoms were nothing more than seasonal flowers.","Flowers that came into season once every four weeks, at that.","Title: Found More Ice Blossoms","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an Ice Blossom)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 2)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 3)","Are these like seasonal wild greens or something? There are quite a lot of them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You must be the only person who would describe such a precious medicinal herb as seasonal wild greens.","└ SwordMaster: All kinds of supposedly rare herbs seem to be gathered there. Those really are incredibly valuable.","└ Does this mean he’ll be able to find Ice Blossoms every winter from now on?","└ Seems like it. Wouldn’t the same apply to other herbs? Different herbs grow in different seasons.","└ What herbs grow in spring again? All sorts of medicinal herbs grow between spring and summer.","└ For real? At this point, anything he picks up will probably be considered medicinal, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: You found several rather than just one! Are","The Ice Blossom was a medicinal herb found only in cold regions—and even there, it was extremely rare.","Moreover, it would often melt away if the temperature rose even slightly, and its blooming period was short.","A single limited season called winter, a short lifespan, and the durability of a sunfish.","Above all, it could only grow in soil with an abundance of mana.","All these conditions combined to make it an extraordinarily rare medicinal herb.","But as always, the Forest of the Four Seasons appeared to be an exception.","There was no need to explain how plentiful the mana was here.","The seasons changed every week, so its short lifespan wasn’t a problem either.","I could easily find Ice Blossoms simply by searching around the shelter.","Therefore, as far as I was concerned, the Ice Blossom was nothing more than a seasonal flower.","One that came into season once every four weeks.","Title: Found More Ice Blossoms","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an Ice Blossom)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 2)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 3)","Are these like seasonal herbs or something? There are quite a lot of them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You must be the only person who would describe a precious medicinal herb as seasonal greens.","└ SwordMaster: It’s like every supposedly rare herb has gathered there. Those are genuinely precious.","└ So does this mean he’ll be able to find Ice Blossoms every winter from now on?","└ Seems like it. Wouldn’t the same apply to other herbs? Different medicinal herbs grow in different seasons.","└ What medicinal herbs grow in spring again? All kinds of them grow from spring through summer.","└ For real? But anything he picks up will probably be considered a medicinal herb, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: You found several, not just one! Are you going to use those to make more essence?","└ Wild Grylls: I’d like to gain cold resistance. I have plenty of ingredients now, so I think it should be fine.","└ Starlight Princess: All right. But could you give me the mature mandrake you mentioned yesterday?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll give you a mature mandrake and make another blue mandrake using yesterday’s method. That should make your research easier.","└ Starlight Princess: I’ll be sure to repay your trust!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey, what about me? Give me one too.","└ Wild Grylls: You reek of alcohol, so go away. Besides, I don’t have enough to spare for making liquor. I’ll consider it once I obtain the ability I want.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: If necessary, I’ll make the liquor myself, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: You little bastard!","└ Don’t worry. There are probably plenty of other medicinal herbs besides those, lolol.","└ What if he finds Sun Herbs in summer?","└ Sun Herbs only grow in deserts. It’s like how Snow Ginseng only grows on snowy mountains.","└ By that logic, shouldn’t Ice Blossoms only grow on snowy mountains too?","└ He’ll find something. We just need to sit back and watch, lol.","Now that I had found more Ice Blossoms, I ate a light breakfast and began the production process.","The first thing I needed to do was gather mandrakes.","This time, I collected several rather than just one.","I gave one of them to the Starlight Princess and processed another using the same method as yesterday.","I started by boiling the mature mandrake together with an Ice Blossom, dyeing it blue.","\"Kkuyolk?! Kkueok!!\"","Once again, I forcibly poured elixir into its mouth.","It suddenly reminded me of foie gras, the dish made from goose liver.","Apparently, they force-feed geese by inserting funnels into their beaks to enlarge their livers.","A mandrake was a plant, so it wasn’t quite as bad, but its reactions still made the process unpleasant.","Although in my case, I was forcing medicine—elixir—into it rather than food.","\"Kkiyoooooot!!\"","Whack! Smack!","The moment the elixir took effect, I beat the thrashing mandrake until it calmed down.","’Now I just need to send these.’","I sent her three mandrakes in total.","One was an ordinary mandrake, another was a mandrake combined with an Ice Blossom, and the last was a mandrake that had absorbed both an Ice Blossom and an elixir.","If she researched them one by one, the Starlight Princess should be able to figure something out.","I would have liked to give All-Father some samples and ask him to conduct research too, but I didn’t have enough.","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. I’ll send you my findings by lunchtime.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. Is the mandrake combined with the Ice Blossom still intact?]","[Starlight Princess: Perhaps because the Ice Blossom was absorbed into the mandrake, it’s still blue. If I’d known this would happen, I would’ve asked you to send it yesterday.]","[Wild Grylls: Neither of us knew. I’ll wait for your findings, then.]","Now that I had entrusted the research to the Starlight Princess, I needed to attend to my own work.","My first priority was controlling the ability.","As I had repeatedly emphasized, it would cause all sorts of trouble if I couldn’t control it.","I used aura not only in combat but also for various kinds of labor.","Logging, mining, digging, processing materials, and so on.","It was useful in countless ways.","But if everything became covered in frost—or froze solid—whenever I used it, that would be an enormous headache.","’Let’s determine why my mana is giving off cold. Has the mana itself really changed?’","I quietly closed my eyes and circulated my heart method.","I could clearly feel the mana inside me flowing through every corner of my body.","At the same time, I felt an intensely frigid sensation.","The mana itself had taken on the properties of cold.","However, contrary to the Starlight Princess’s fears, my circuits hadn’t frozen solid as they would with Severed Meridian Syndrome.","As though my body had completely adapted, the mana circulated easily without placing any strain on me.","’How should I put it...?’","Was it similar to how the waters of the Arctic and Antarctic didn’t freeze easily?","I didn’t mean that my mana contained salt.","I was merely speculating that the essence I had consumed yesterday had caused a similar phenomenon.","It wasn’t a bad thing, but I had only avoided the worst-case scenario. The ability remained troublesome.","’It would be perfect if it just had an on-and-off switch.’","How could I separate the cold energy from my aura?","As I pondered the problem, a thought suddenly occurred to me.","’Wait. All my mana gathers in my dantian, doesn’t it?’","An internal energy heart method accumulated mana within the dantian through breathing.","In other words, even if mana spread throughout my entire body, it would eventually return to the dantian.","Then what if I separated the cold energy every time the mana returned and stored it independently?","’My dantian won’t freeze solid, will it?’","That possibility was frightening too.","I stopped circulating the heart method for a moment.","This was when I needed an expert’s opinion.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, may I ask you a question?]","[Heavenly Demon: What do you wish to know?]","[Wild Grylls: Well, the thing is...]","I gave the Heavenly Demon a general explanation.","I wanted to separate the cold energy from my mana and store it inside my dantian.","However, I was worried that the cold energy might adversely affect my dantian.","I asked her to tell me whether my concern was baseless or if there was a genuine risk.","The Heavenly Demon seemed to contemplate my question for some time before replying.","[Heavenly Demon: I understand what you mean. Your concern is not unreasonable.]","[Wild Grylls: Is it dangerous?]","[Heavenly Demon: It would be dangerous if you separated them incorrectly. As you fear, your dantian could freeze solid. However, if you use the proper method, you should be able to separate them safely.]","[Wild Grylls: Could you teach me how?]","[Heavenly Demon: Of course. The principle is to create another dantian within your dantian.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds incredibly difficult.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is nothing extraordinary. If your existing dantian is meant for pure energy, the new dantian you create will be exclusively for cold energy. Wait a moment.]","After leaving that message, the Heavenly Demon disappeared for a while.","I tilted my head, unable to understand what she meant by creating a dantian inside my dantian.","I didn’t doubt her, since she was the expert in this field.","I simply couldn’t grasp the concept.","’Maybe I’ll have to perform manual labor without aura for a while.’","This strange ability was making my body suffer.","I could only laugh hollowly.","I had no idea how long I waited, but after a while, the Heavenly Demon sent me another message.","[Heavenly Demon: (Image depicting the human body and an inner core) Can you see it clearly? You should notice a small circle inside this inner core. You must gather the essence into a mass and create another inner core in this manner.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah. So it’s like a mathematical set.]","[Heavenly Demon: Is \"set\" not simply a word used when things are gathered together?]","[Wild Grylls: It’s also a mathematical term. It isn’t used very often.]","[Heavenly Demon: I see. In any case, it is enough that you understand. Now that you know the principle, you should practice.]","[Wild Grylls: Don’t you have any other advice?]","[Heavenly Demon: The second mnemonic chant I taught you will be of great assistance. I would like to teach you the third chant, but I fear it may cause you to grow stronger in yet another bizarre direction, so it would be best to postpone it. That is especially true now that your energy has acquired the properties of cold.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. Thank you very much, even if it’s only advice.]","[Heavenly Demon: This lady shall always be waiting. If you require assistance, you need only ask.]","No matter how I looked at it, the Heavenly Demon was a precious connection.","She had given me invaluable advice without the slightest hesitation.","The Heavenly Demon added that it would be better for me to learn the third mnemonic chant only after I could easily control both my cold energy and aura.","Ideally, I should wait until I could use sword force—in other words, an Aura Blade.","I agreed with her.","’If I become stronger in some stupid-ass way again, I’ll be the one who suffers.’","As someone had joked, my aura might end up piercing the heavens.","Praying that nothing like that would happen, I resumed circulating my internal energy heart method.","I recited the second mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me and visualized the image she had shown me, separating my mana from the cold energy.","Shwaaaaa—","The cold energy gradually separated as though undergoing a chemical reaction.","Following the Heavenly Demon’s instructions, I positioned that energy in the center of my inner core.","As if creating another circle within an existing circle, I slowly forced the energy together into a compact mass.","Crackle—","Perhaps because the principle resembled that of an Aura Blade, it wasn’t easy.","Whenever I finally managed to gather the energy, it would often crumble apart.","Moreover, the circulating mana flowed as rapidly as crashing waves, making even the separation process difficult.","’I can’t give up.’","An Aura Blade manifested outside the body, whereas this process took place inside me.","Relatively speaking, this should be easier.","I refused to become discouraged and continued separating the two energies.","I had no idea how much time passed.","Eventually, my efforts bore fruit.","Shortly before lunchtime, I managed to form an essence core the size of a grain of millet.","’Now, if I want to use the cold energy...’","When I touched it as though popping a balloon, the essence core immediately burst.","Reforming it wasn’t difficult either.","After all, I had already traveled that path once.","If I gradually increased its size, I would eventually be able to use ordinary aura in daily life again.","Until then, I would have to avoid using aura while working whenever possible.","’I’ll just think of it as exercise.’","I checked the time.","Before I knew it, hours had passed and it was already lunchtime.","At that exact moment, the Starlight Princess sent me a message.","Her timing was impeccable.","She had promised to share her research findings by lunchtime, so this was right on schedule.","[Wild Grylls: What did you find?]","[Starlight Princess: I have good news and bad news. Which would you like to hear first?]","[Wild Grylls: Please tell me the bad news first.]","[Starlight Princess: It seems practically impossible to gain cold resistance using an Ice Blossom. It might be possible if we disregarded safety, but no matter how hard I thought about it, every method carried significant risks.]","To acquire cold resistance, I would have to consume an Ice Blossom despite the danger.","I was disappointed for a moment, but then a question occurred to me.","’Then what about the people who gained cold resistance in the past? Were they simply lucky?’","The moment the thought occurred to me, I asked her.","[Wild Grylls: What about the people from the past? You said some died after eating Ice Blossoms, but others gained cold resistance.]","[Starlight Princess: Do you remember the pufferfish you mentioned before? This is a completely different situation.]","[Wild Grylls: A different situation?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. With pufferfish, people generally discovered which parts were safe to eat after countless attempts. But Ice Blossoms are different. Those people simply ate them.]","[Wild Grylls: They just ate them? Then how did they survive?]","The Starlight Princess gave me an intuitive explanation of the difference.","[Starlight Princess: To use the pufferfish analogy, it was eaten by people who could chew up an entire raw pufferfish and remain perfectly fine. In other words, the people who ate Ice Blossoms were simply exceptionally strong.]","[Wild Grylls: ;;;;]","So only natural-born powerhouses could eat them.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 142","paragraphs":["Combination (5)","I was dumbfounded to hear that only naturally born powerhouses could gain cold resistance, but it was still too early to give up.","What the Starlight Princess had just told me was the bad news.","There was still good news left.","I sincerely hoped it would give me some hope.","[Wild Grylls: What’s the good news?]","[Starlight Princess: There’s no risk of you developing Severed Meridian Syndrome. The ability is permanent too. And one more thing—you probably won’t ever freeze to death.]","[Wild Grylls: Didn’t you say I hadn’t gained cold resistance?]","[Starlight Princess: This is separate from that. If you progress beyond hypothermia and reach the point where you’re about to freeze to death, your body will react. You’ll probably enter hibernation on your own, then revive once the weather becomes warmer.]","[Wild Grylls: Wonmo is hibernating right now. Does it work on the same principle?]","[Starlight Princess: It’s slightly different. In your case, how should I put this...? The ability is focused entirely on survival. Ordinarily, you would die from hypothermia, but instead, you’ll continue surviving.]","[Wild Grylls: I should consider that... a good thing, right?]","[Starlight Princess: It’s better than having nothing, isn’t it? But be careful. If you collapse somewhere the weather or seasons never change, such as a snowy mountain, you could remain alive but asleep forever.]","That would be a hopeless situation.","I wouldn’t be alive or dead.","Still, as the Starlight Princess had said, it was an extremely useful survival ability.","For someone like me, who always had to consider the worst-case scenario, it couldn’t have been more suitable.","It was disappointing that I hadn’t gained cold resistance, but I was grateful nonetheless.","[Wild Grylls: What would have happened if I’d eaten the blue mandrake?]","[Starlight Princess: You most likely would’ve become an ice human. Like that mandrake, your skin would’ve turned blue rather than merely pale, and your hair would’ve turned white. You would’ve looked no different from an undead.]","[Wild Grylls: Sh-Sh-Shiver me timbers. Good thing I added the elixir.]","[Starlight Princess: I gave you the safest method available, after all.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you so much for teaching me.]","[Starlight Princess: It’s all right. My knowledge increased thanks to you too. If there’s anything else you’re curious about, you can ask me anytime.]","[Wild Grylls: What does ordinary mandrake essence do?]","[Starlight Princess: Since it contains yang energy, it warms the body. In particular, it increases the body’s regenerative abilities, making it an ideal ingredient for elixirs.]","[Wild Grylls: Then can liquor be made using the blue mandrake?]","[Starlight Princess: It wouldn’t be impossible... but the liquor would probably freeze first. It would also be dangerous.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood.]","Since the subject had come up, the Starlight Princess gifted me some elixirs.","Two of them, no less.","I thanked her and began cleaning up.","\"Now that I’ve more or less finished here...\"","It was time to handle the remaining work.","Building an ice storage house had become pointless, so I started designing improvements to the shelter instead.","I wanted to make it sturdy enough to withstand any natural disaster.","Of course, that wouldn’t be easy.","A disaster even worse than the avalanche might strike in the future.","’Should I reinforce the drainage channel with cement too?’","Now that I knew cement existed, I could think of all kinds of places to use it.","However, I had never worked in construction.","I had only used cement a few times during my military service.","Even then, the officers had handled most of the actual application. I had merely assisted them.","’Come to think of it, I did all sorts of things in the military.’","I chuckled as I searched through the auction house for cement.","Since cement was commonly used in various fields—particularly construction—quite a large amount had been listed.","After assuming cement didn’t exist at all, discovering so much of it felt strangely anticlimactic.","If I had learned about it just a little sooner—or had at least tried searching for it—my oven and furnace might never have been swept away.","’I need to erect another barricade too... I have a lot to do.’","The avalanche had swept away an enormous amount.","The situation made me sigh.","Whatever else I did, I definitely needed a barricade. The difference between having one and not having one was immense.","Even during the saber-toothed tiger attack, the barricade had bought me valuable time.","’I should ask the dwarf to make it. Although I can’t give him any liquor.’","The Starlight Princess had warned that the liquor could be dangerous, so I intended to postpone that idea.","After designing the shelter’s reinforcements, I immediately prepared my equipment.","I needed to gather sand to mix with the cement.","If I remembered correctly, there was sand downstream.","\"Fast Sloth, look after Wonmo.\"","\"...\"","I left Fast Sloth at the shelter to watch over the hibernating Wonmo.","Perhaps he didn’t want to move either, because he was simply zoning out in front of the fireplace.","It seemed neither humans nor animals wanted to go outside in cold weather.","For me, however, this was an excellent opportunity.","Considering that Wonmo had fallen asleep, other animals were probably less active or hibernating too.","Even the snakes that had always appeared at the worst possible moments to irritate me should pose less of a threat.","’I need a shovel and some sacks. The ground might be frozen, so I should take the ignition stone and firewood too.’","How wonderful it was that I could fit all of this into the subspace backpack.","Even the weight wasn’t much of an issue. Since everything took up so little space, it felt considerably lighter to carry.","After checking several times to ensure I hadn’t forgotten anything, I headed for the river.","’It feels like it’s been a long time since I went downstream.’","I followed the frozen river downstream.","Since I was already heading in that direction, it might not be a bad idea to continue to the lake and gather some food.","It wasn’t that I disliked smoked food.","The problem was Fast Sloth’s food supply.","’It’s becoming dangerous to keep feeding him nothing but inner cores.’","He ate inner cores at every meal, so my supply was steadily dwindling.","The sudden arrival of winter had prevented me from storing food that Fast Sloth could eat.","Fortunately, I had accumulated a considerable stockpile beforehand. Otherwise, I would have run out already.","’And I have no idea when the Heavenly Demon will give me more fasting pills.’","On top of that, the gorillas kept stealing every fasting pill she sent.","I would have to endure somehow until the Heavenly Demon gave me more.","’The sand is... Wow. It’s frozen solid.’","When I reached the lower reaches of the river, I discovered that even the sand had frozen.","That was unavoidable, considering it was constantly exposed to the water.","With no other option, I took out the firewood I had prepared in advance.","I only needed to keep a fire burning until the sand thawed.","Crackle! Pop!","The warm campfire, which I had lit to melt the sand, made me feel pleasantly drowsy.","I stared idly into the flames for a while before a thought suddenly occurred to me.","’Wait. Couldn’t I just break it apart with a pickaxe and thaw it later?’","Now that I thought about it, that would be a much better method.","I was going to mix it with cement anyway, so there was no need to thaw it first.","I could simply mix it with heated water later.","People said human intelligence often kicked in too late.","I was the perfect example.","’Sigh. Let’s just consider this a learning experience.’","Grumbling inwardly, I checked the sand.","It was still hard.","I could probably make a quick trip to the lake while I waited for it to thaw.","Still, I remained alert to my surroundings just in case.","There was no telling what might appear.","’I don’t see anything in particular.’","There were no giant crabs in sight, while the ordinary crabs were frozen solid.","If anyone asked whether they were still edible, I would simply call it natural frozen storage.","I placed several crabs in a sack and looked around.","The entire lake had frozen over, forming what looked like a vast road.","’I suppose I could scout the area if necessary...’","There was no reason to take an unnecessary risk.","I collected the crabs and returned downstream.","The moment I arrived, I encountered an extraordinary sight.","\"Prrr.\"","\"...\"","It was a deer.","A deer was resting beside the campfire I had built.","Could it be the same deer that had knocked out the bull shark with a single kick?","I silently stared at the deer before slowly beginning to move.","That kick could have been aimed at me if I made a wrong move, so I needed to be careful.","’What is it, some kind of gangster?’","I never imagined it would take over my campfire while I was briefly away.","Even its appearance gave off the distinct aura of a thug. If I messed with it, I would probably regret it.","However, I needed the sand.","To show that I meant it no harm, I approached slowly.","Even when I came closer, the deer merely sat beside the campfire and did nothing.","Scrape! Scrape!","It didn’t react even when I began digging up the sand with my shovel.","I couldn’t tell whether the warmth of the campfire made it unwilling to move or if it had realized I wasn’t a threat.","’Is this the composure of the strong?’","Herbivores were unusually powerful in this forest.","Sloths, gorillas, and now deer.","If carnivores were predators, then these creatures were simply gangsters.","’I’ve collected about enough sand...’","Just how long was this thing planning to stay here?","It was staring straight through me too, which made me extremely uncomfortable.","Still, it hadn’t attacked me, so everything was probably fine.","I had already accomplished my objective.","Clatter! Crackle!","Before leaving, I added a few more pieces of firewood.","It was my way of signaling that I had absolutely no intention of fighting it.","The campfire grew stronger.","Perhaps the deer understood what I meant, because although it had been watching me the entire time, it finally turned its head away.","’This should be enough, right?’","I threw the remaining firewood onto the campfire and returned to the shelter.","The deer showed no intention of leaving the fire until the very end.","Despite that minor incident, I managed to return with what I needed.","’I’ll leave the sand in the sacks and put the crabs in the icebox.’","The \"icebox\" was simply the insulated box containing the ice.","I had decided to call it that for convenience.","The moment I stepped inside the shelter, however, I noticed something strange.","Fast Sloth was still staring idly into the fire, and Wonmo was still hibernating.","Then who was the creature sitting beside Fast Sloth?","’What? I’m sure I put up the metal fence and the tarp.’","There were no signs that either the tarp or the fence had been disturbed.","That meant it had entered through another route.","However, considering that Fast Sloth wasn’t on guard, it probably wasn’t dangerous.","Still, I couldn’t afford to let my guard down.","I slowly approached and checked its identity.","\"Keeeng...\"","\"...\"","Once I came closer, I recognized it.","It was a familiar creature.","This was the raccoon that had approached me when I lit a campfire in the yard before.","The raccoon that had stuck its hand into the fire, then put the flames clinging to its hand into its mouth.","’Why is this thing here?’","I stared at the raccoon in confusion.","Then I noticed wounds on its legs and back.","There were no signs that it had entered through the entrance, so it couldn’t have arrived here while fleeing from a predator.","\"Hey. Where did you come from?\"","\"Keeeng...?\"","Unable to figure it out, I quietly approached and asked.","The raccoon looked puzzled when I came closer, then slowly rose from its seat.","I briefly wondered whether it intended to fight me, but it did something completely unexpected.","\"Keeeng... Keng...\"","It clasped its hands neatly together with a truly apologetic expression.","Anyone could tell that it was apologizing.","Its already adorable appearance, combined with that gesture, naturally stirred my sympathy.","It was far more polite and well-behaved than a certain bunch of gorilla bastards.","\"Keng... Keeeng...\"","The raccoon then pointed toward the fireplace, still wearing an extremely aggrieved expression.","Thanks to that, I could roughly understand what had happened.","Apparently, it had crawled into the chimney and fallen straight down.","It was a miracle that it had only suffered scrapes and hadn’t been burned.","’That really is unfair.’","It had even apologized, so I couldn’t bring myself to kill it.","If it had acted shamelessly like that raccoon dog, I would have treated it coldly.","Moreover, Fast Sloth appeared to understand the raccoon’s predicament, which was why he had remained still.","I patted the raccoon’s head to assure it that there was nothing to worry about.","Once I showed it some kindness, the raccoon seemed relieved and relaxed.","\"Wait here for a moment.\"","\"Keeeng?\"","It was injured, so I should at least apply some elixir.","I used the animal-grade elixir to treat the raccoon’s wounds.","When they healed in an instant, the startled raccoon began touching different parts of its body.","It was cute in a completely different way from Wonmo.","\"How is it? Feeling better?\"","\"Keeeng! Keng, keng!\"","The raccoon repeatedly clasped its hands together to express its gratitude.","Why did the Forest of the Four Seasons seem to contain nothing but intelligent animals?","It was truly fascinating.","As I watched it with a satisfied smile, the raccoon looked around and then headed toward the fireplace.","Just as I began wondering what it was doing, its bizarre behavior started.","Swoosh—","It thrust its hands directly into the blazing fire.","Unlike last time, it didn’t insert only one hand.","It clasped both hands together and placed them into the flames.","I stared, wondering what on earth it was doing.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"...What is this?\"","The raccoon eventually held out its cupped hands toward me.","Both hands were blazing with fire, yet the flames didn’t appear to be hot.","I had no idea how I was supposed to react.","Perhaps sensing my confusion, the raccoon let the fire gathered in its hands fall to the ground.","Fwoosh!","The flames fell like water and soon faded away.","I focused on the fact that the fire had fallen like \"water.\"","If fire could fall like water, couldn’t it be stored in a bottle?","With that thought, I prepared an empty bottle.","As before, the raccoon gathered fire in its cupped hands and poured it into the bottle I held out.","Fwoosh! Flicker!","The fire inside the empty bottle didn’t go out. It maintained its shape.","It continued burning even after I sealed the bottle with a stopper and cut off its oxygen supply.","When I examined it closely, I discovered that the flames were burning around a small spherical core.","’What is this?’","It was a fire that burned without fuel or oxygen, completely defying conventional scientific knowledge.","What could that mean?","Unable to figure it out, I looked at the raccoon.","Understanding the meaning behind my gaze, the raccoon placed its hands in the campfire again.","\"Nom.\"","It then put its burning hands into its mouth.","\"Fwooooo!\"","Whoooosh!","A massive torrent of fire erupted from its mouth.","The flames were bright enough to illuminate the entire cave in an instant.","My jaw dropped at the sight.","’Why the hell is there a ninja living in this forest?’","While I stood there in shock—","Smack!","\"Kegeng!\"","Fast Sloth slapped the raccoon across the back.","His stern attitude seemed to say that it shouldn’t play with fire.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 143","paragraphs":["Neighbors (1)","A raccoon that breathed fire from its mouth like some kind of ninja.","As if breathing fire weren’t impressive enough, it was even capable of storing flames inside a bottle.","I had no idea what the bottled fire could be used for, but it was such a unique ability that it was bound to prove useful somewhere.","More than anything, though, I liked its personality.","’That’s the biggest reason.’","It wasn’t merely gentle—it was polite, too. There was no way I could dislike it.","Even the Swift Sloth, who was highly sensitive about its territory, had merely smacked it on the back and done nothing more.","That alone showed just how nice this raccoon was. It made me like the little guy even more.","’Should I let it live with me? It seems perfectly capable of looking after itself.’","Whatever else might be true, there was no doubt this raccoon was highly skilled at handling fire.","Just as I had until now, I would continue to have plenty of uses for fire in the future.","If this fire-wielding raccoon lent me a hand, perhaps I would become capable of doing things I couldn’t manage before.","Even if I didn’t yet know what use it had, I might also get some of that bottled fire as an added benefit.","It had probably fallen down the chimney because it was attracted by the flames, so surely we could come to some kind of agreement.","I would provide it with shelter, and the raccoon would use its abilities for me.","I immediately made the raccoon an offer, using a mixture of words, hand gestures, and body language.","\"Keng.\"","However, the raccoon rejected my offer.","It was surprising enough that it understood me, but it even held out a paw to make its intentions unmistakably clear.","No matter how extraordinary its ability might be, the fact that it had come all the way here surely meant it had no home of its own.","In a forest as hellish as this one, a safe place to live was extremely important.","When I asked why it was refusing, the raccoon picked up a twig lying near the firewood.","Scritch, scritch—","It then began drawing a picture on the ground. I carefully studied it.","Just as its intelligence was exceptional, its drawing skills were nothing to scoff at either.","’First the Swift Sloth, and now this guy. Is drawing a basic skill for animals living in the Forest of Four Seasons?’","Somehow, it seemed better at drawing than I was.","While I was thinking that, the raccoon finished its picture. It had drawn three raccoons in total.","At a glance, they looked like a family. Did raccoons normally live in groups?","\"Keng!\"","\"Oh. This one is you?\"","The raccoon pointed at the largest member of the family.","In human terms, it was the head of the household. In other words, the father.","The two smaller raccoons appeared to be its mate and child.","’Then there’s nothing I can do.’","Whether human or animal, the head of a family had important responsibilities.","I nodded to show the raccoon that I understood.","I would have liked to give it some food as a gesture of friendship, but unfortunately, I barely had enough for myself.","The only food I had was extremely salty smoked meat, so it wasn’t suitable.","\"Keng. Keeeng.\"","\"Huh? You want some fire?\"","\"Keng.\"","\"If you want it, go ahead.\"","Instead, the little guy asked for some fire. I readily gave it permission.","I could start another fire whenever I wanted, and it was hard to even call fire a resource.","The raccoon bowed its head after receiving my permission, then held the twig it had used for drawing against the fireplace.","Whoosh!","A flame blazed to life at the end of the twig.","The twig was tiny to me, but when the raccoon held it, it looked like a torch.","Normally, it should have burned up quickly, but somehow, it burned steadily like a candle.","The raccoon gazed at its brightly burning torch with a satisfied expression.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Yeah. Goodbye. Take care of yourself. If you ever change your mind, come back here.\"","With the torch in its paw, the raccoon went on its way.","It was a shame, but perhaps we would meet again someday.","It might have lacked strength, but it was smart. It would find some way to survive.","’Unlike certain others, it’s polite and well-mannered.’","Some bastard had stolen all my Fasting Pills and then tried to settle the debt with bananas.","If possible, I wanted to maintain a steady relationship with the raccoon. First, though, I needed to figure out exactly what the fire inside the bottle was.","I watched until the raccoon disappeared from sight, then accessed the gallery.","Title: Met a fire-wielding raccoon","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the raccoon bowing politely)","(Photo of the raccoon scooping up fire from the fireplace)","(Photo of the raccoon breathing fire)","(Photo of fire inside a bottle)","(Video of the raccoon leaving with a torch in one paw)","I went outside for a little while, and when I came back, there was a raccoon in my house. It was the one that visited my house before, and apparently it fell down the chimney.","I was wondering what kind of ability it had, and it turned out to be insanely good at handling fire;;","Are there any raccoons with fire-related abilities? If there are, let me know.","Oh, and I wanted to recruit it as a companion, but it refused because it’s the head of its family. Bit of a shame.","└ Heavenly Demon: What a rare and remarkable trick. It is accomplishing something that would be difficult even with Daoist arts.","└ SwordMaster: I’ve never seen a raccoon like that in my life. What is it, a dragon? It’s breathing fire;;","└ Wild Grylls: It ate the fire and then breathed it out. Can mages do that too?","└ SwordMaster: I’m not sure. I don’t know much about that.","└ Starlight Princess: If someone tried that, their mouth and tongue would burn to a crisp.","└ Wild Grylls: Even if they just ate the fire?","└ Starlight Princess: This isn’t some strongman sideshow. Why would anyone eat fire?;;","└ The very act of eating fire is bizarre, you know;;","└ Aren’t there monsters that eat fire?","└ There are, but raccoons don’t, lololol.","└ All-Father: Fascinating. I could understand water, but a raccoon with an affinity for fire...","└ Wild Grylls: Do raccoons shoot water from their mouths?","└ All-Father: No, but they do have a habit of washing their food in water. Perhaps this one roasts its food over a fire instead.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh;;","└ All-Father: But what exactly is that fire inside the bottle? It has piqued my interest.","└ Wild Grylls: It may be hard to believe, but the raccoon scooped up the fire and put it inside the bottle. It scooped flames from the campfire like someone cupping water in both hands.","└ All-Father: Hmm... I would like to study it, but unfortunately, I don’t believe I have enough time at present. If it would not be too much trouble, could you wait two days?","└ Wild Grylls: Understood. It’s nothing urgent.","└ All-Father: Thank you.","└ Don’t tell me that’s some kind of essence too.","└ Who knows? It might also be nothing special, lol.","└ By the way, do raccoons live in groups?","└ I think it depends on the individual.","Everyone found the raccoon fascinating.","They seemed particularly skeptical about the part where it ate fire.","Well, this was the Forest of Four Seasons. It was probably best to simply accept it and move on.","’It probably won’t visit often.’","I had never seen the raccoon until winter arrived.","During the other seasons, it had probably remained within its own territory and the surrounding area.","Now that winter had come, food nearby must have grown scarce, naturally forcing it to venture farther away.","Would such a tiny creature really be able to continue surviving in this forest? I was a little worried.","’It has a special ability, so it should manage.’","It had already adapted well to the Forest of Four Seasons. It might even have a better chance of surviving here than I did.","In any case, now that the raccoon had left, I counted the Iceblooms I had remaining.","I still had about two left, so I could probably use them for something.","I might also find more if I searched the surrounding area.","’I should probably postpone gaining cold resistance, right?’","If I mixed one with something and ate it without the Starlight Princess’s help, I could end up in serious trouble.","But simply leaving them unused also felt like a waste.","’Mixing one with mandrake and giving it to Praise the Sun might not be a bad idea...’","I checked how much elixir I had left.","After mixing some with the mandrake, I had about three and a half bottles remaining.","Since there was always a chance that Wonmo, the Swift Sloth, and I could all be injured at the same time, that amount was the absolute minimum I needed to keep.","’It feels like mixing it with that fire would work perfectly.’","The fire the raccoon had put inside the bottle.","Couldn’t I mix that with an Icebloom?","However, that was merely a guess. I couldn’t be certain. I absolutely needed an expert’s opinion.","Unfortunately, even the All-Father was currently unavailable, which made things difficult.","’I’ll just get some next time.’","I still had plenty of time, so there was no need to rush.","More importantly, didn’t I need to train myself to control cold energy first?","That wasn’t all. Once winter ended, the number of things I needed to do would increase exponentially.","’The bricks, cement, and sand can go here...’","I made preparations in advance for when the weather warmed.","As soon as the thaw began, I planned to build an oven and a furnace.","I also had an emergency exit to consider, so there was a lot of work ahead of me.","’How should I build it so it won’t get swept away by an avalanche?’","An avalanche would probably occur about once a month.","And it wasn’t just avalanches. I had no idea what other kinds of natural disasters might strike.","I would need to survive another two weeks or so before I could understand the rules of this damned forest.","’It has to be extremely sturdy. Should I just construct a small building?’","Since I had bricks and cement, I could erect a building for the oven and furnace.","It would take a long time, but its durability would be guaranteed.","Of course, it would be a different story if some abnormal monster like the Boss Gorilla appeared.","There was truly nothing I could do about something like that. As long as the structure could withstand natural disasters, that would be enough.","’I need to use the space as efficiently as possible and build a separate drainage channel... This is giving me a headache.’","It might have been different if I had gone to university, but unfortunately, I had only graduated from high school.","I hadn’t had enough money, and I had been too busy struggling to survive from one day to the next.","At least I had learned a few useful things in the military. That was some consolation.","I bought a large sheet of paper and drew the cave and the surrounding area on it.","’A rectangular design would probably be the safest choice.’","If I wanted to do that, I would need to cut down more trees.","I planned to clear the path that the Boss Gorilla had personally created.","I spent the entire day working on the design, and before I knew it, the dark night had arrived.","Snow began falling after nightfall, but it wasn’t a blizzard. It was just ordinary snow.","’Is this another sign that the weather is warming?’","According to the journal my Great Senior had left behind, the weather should warm up in another two or three days.","I needed to accomplish everything I could before then. If I was lucky, perhaps I could even go hunting.","I added more firewood to the flames and sat beside the Swift Sloth.","Except when it was eating, this guy seemed to spend all its time in front of the fireplace.","’Winter has its advantages, but I still hate it.’","The most inconvenient part was that the sun set early and rose late.","The reduced activity of the other animals was certainly beneficial, but the same applied to me.","I sat silently before the fireplace until something suddenly occurred to me, prompting me to stand.","’This isn’t the time to sit around. More snow could accumulate overnight.’","So I diligently scattered salt around. Since I didn’t have calcium chloride, I had no choice but to use salt as a substitute.","The emergency exit was still only in the design phase, so it was better to prepare in advance.","With that, I finished preparing for the end of the day. The night was long, and there was nothing else to do.","’At least the gallery has found something new to talk about.’","Thanks to the recent sporting events, discussions about El Dorado had almost completely died down.","In other words, the subject was on the verge of being buried.","I didn’t particularly care, but that probably wasn’t good news for the people outside.","’The people outside can handle that themselves.’","All I could do was wait for winter to end.","I quietly passed the time after uploading a post to the gallery to conclude the day.","\"Hey. Aren’t you going to sleep?\"","\"Forget it.\"","The Swift Sloth could continue staring blankly into the fire if it wanted.","Hoping that another blizzard wouldn’t arrive before dawn, I quietly closed my eyes.","I had no idea what would happen next, but whatever came, it would certainly be difficult rather than easy.","’Knowing this would happen, should I have forced the raccoon to stay?’","With that thought in mind, the next morning dawned.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Uh...\"","The moment I woke up, the raccoon greeted me from outside the cave.","And it wasn’t alone. It had brought its family with it.","There was a raccoon that appeared to be its mate, as well as a baby raccoon hiding behind them.","The family radiated an unmistakable We’ve moved in atmosphere.","\"Keng!\"","\"...What’s this?\"","The father raccoon held something out to me.","At a glance, it resembled an ordinary balloon flower root or wild ginseng, but its color was extraordinary.","It was as white as snow, practically advertising to the world, I am a miraculous medicinal herb.","\"Keeeng! Keng!\"","Still bewildered, I accepted the herb. The raccoon bowed deeply at the waist.","Its mate and baby did the same. The shy greeting from the baby raccoon was especially adorable.","’...Did they come to hand out rice cakes to their new neighbor?’","It seemed I had unexpectedly acquired some new neighbors.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 144","paragraphs":["144","Neighbors (2)","The unexpected arrival of new neighbors.","I didn’t know why the raccoon family had moved here, but it certainly wasn’t bad news.","For starters, the raccoon was intelligent and polite. That alone was enough to make it far more likable than the gorillas.","Moreover, it was skilled at handling fire, so if we cooperated while living here, it would be a great help.","To make that happen, I first needed to understand what this family wanted.","’The most basic thing would be food...’","Regardless of how difficult hunting might be, the Forest of Four Seasons was abundant in food.","I didn’t know exactly what raccoons ate, but they were probably omnivores.","Besides, they were my \"neighbors,\" not \"family\" who lived with me like the Swift Sloth and Wonmo. They should be able to take care of themselves to some extent.","’That shouldn’t be a problem... right?’","It would be enough for us to help one another in genuine emergencies.","\"Keng. Keeeng.\"","\"That’s your home?\"","The raccoon family showed me where their home was.","It was in a tree not far from the cave—no, it would be fair to say it was right nearby.","There was a large hollow in the middle of the thick trunk.","Apparently, they lived inside it.","’Fortunately, I wasn’t planning to cut down any trees around here.’","It would have been slightly troublesome if their home had overlapped with the area I planned to clear.","Thankfully, not only was it outside that area, but it was also close enough for us to visit each other frequently.","I watched as the raccoon family entered the hollow.","A moment later, one raccoon poked its head back out. The baby raccoon appeared beside it.","There was no way I could resist taking a picture of this. I immediately snapped one for the gallery.","Title: A raccoon family moved in","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the raccoon family appearing before me)","(Photo of the medicinal herb the raccoon gave me)","(Photo of the raccoon family poking their heads out of their home)","(Photo of the raccoon waving happily)","The family of the raccoon that visited my cave moved into the neighborhood. I don’t know if this is their version of handing out rice cakes to celebrate moving in, but they gave me a medicinal herb.","Their home is a hollow in a nearby tree. Looks like we’ll be visiting each other pretty often from now on.","At least these guys are far more sociable than those gorilla bastards. I’m happy to have neighbors too.","└ Heavenly Demon: What adorable neighbors. I hope you get along well.","└ SwordMaster: Wow, I’m jealous. I don’t even have any neighbors.","└ Heavenly Demon: You never leave your home anyway. What use would you have for neighbors?","└ SwordMaster: Tch. Do you have neighbors, then? You never go outside either.","└ Heavenly Demon: They are not neighbors, but this lady’s subjects. Like that raccoon, they occasionally bring me valuable gifts. Have you ever exchanged anything with your neighbors?","└ SwordMaster: ...","└ ...No?","└ Heavenly Demon: You should at least show your face occasionally. Some people would be delighted simply to see you. Of course, if you possess an ugly countenance, it may have the opposite effect.","└ SwordMaster: I’m pretty, you know—","└ Pics or it didn’t happen.","└ Can’t believe it without proof, lol.","└ Heavenly Demon, you should post proof too. Who are you to call anyone uglier than you? Lol.","└ Heavenly Demon: As this lady has said before, I was once given the title of the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven.","└ SwordMaster: If that’s what counts, then I’m widely renowned as a beauty too, haha.","└ What a clash of titans, lololol.","└ Who’s considered the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven in the Central Plains?","└ In the previous generation, it was Yang Seolhwa. Now it’s the Heavenly Demon, though the rumors about her are a little terrifying.","└ What rumors?","└ Something like, \"Even drenched in another’s blood, her beauty could not be concealed.\" It’s chilling, but that’s what I heard.","└ Before people realized she was the Heavenly Demon, wasn’t her alias the Blood Flower?","└ A flower soaked in blood, da-da-da!","└ CCCC","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Hmm! How adorable! Unfortunately, I must ban you for one hour!","└ Wild Grylls: ??? Why? What did I do wrong?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: There’s no video! No video! If you upload one, I may let you off!","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of the raccoon family) Is this enough?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I’ll let it slide just this once!","└ Just this once...","└ The admin tells the mods not to abuse their authority, but now he’s abusing it himself, lololol.","└ Hypocrisy is a built-in passive skill for anyone with a badge, lol.","└ They really are cute, though, lol.","└ Is that one a baby? I want to hold it.","└ What happens if Grylls takes the baby away?","└ It’s just visiting the house next door, lol.","└ Ah, I see.","└ More importantly, wouldn’t Wonmo eat it?","└ Wonmo: Why is there more emergency food than there was before I went to sleep?","└ Who was the original emergency food? Don’t tell me it was Grylls.","└ Of course he’s emergency food, lololol.","We joked about it, but I couldn’t dismiss the matter as nothing more than a joke.","Even if I accepted the raccoons as neighbors, would Wonmo acknowledge them?","The Swift Sloth appeared to have accepted them, but I had no idea what Wonmo’s appetite might drive him to do.","’The weather seems to be warming up, so Wonmo should wake up soon.’","I looked up at the sky instead of the tree and exhaled.","The temperature had risen enough for me to feel the difference. Even the cloud of breath leaving my mouth had grown fainter.","By tomorrow, the weather would either change completely or begin showing clear signs of doing so.","’I’ll know once Wonmo wakes up.’","Wonmo had started hibernating as soon as winter began, so the reverse should also be true.","After staring at the raccoon family for a while, I returned to the cave.","Since they were good at handling fire, I planned to keep a campfire burning in the yard for them.","Crackle! Pop!","I made a campfire for the raccoons to use, then went inside the cave.","First, I needed to identify the medicinal herb they had given me instead of rice cakes.","’The Heavenly Demon is usually good with things like this, right?’","The Heavenly Demon was knowledgeable about inner cores and medicinal herbs of this kind.","Even if she didn’t recognize it, she could quickly determine what sort of energy it contained.","After examining the snow-white ginseng from different angles, I sent her a message.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you there?]","[Heavenly Demon: Speak.]","[Wild Grylls: You know the picture from the post I uploaded? The one that looks like white ginseng.]","[Heavenly Demon: I was examining it. It appeared to be no ordinary medicinal herb. This lady suspects it is Snow Ginseng saturated with yin energy.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll send it to you. Would you mind examining it? I’m a little hesitant to eat it immediately.]","[Heavenly Demon: Very well. I shall contact you after inspecting it.]","I sent the white ginseng to the Heavenly Demon. She would probably reply before long.","In the meantime, I considered how I could maintain a good relationship with the raccoon family.","Simply keeping a campfire burning might not be enough.","’If they’re good at finding medicinal herbs, they might become a huge help.’","What if the white ginseng proved highly effective?","I would make them a direct offer: I would provide them with food, and in exchange, they would bring me medicinal herbs.","I could either consume the herbs myself or give them to the Heavenly Demon so she could make Fasting Pills.","This was mutual aid—the very principle that kept an economy moving.","It was debatable whether it could be called an economy without any currency, but never mind that.","[Heavenly Demon: Sir, are you still there?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes, I am. Have you identified it?]","[Heavenly Demon: That raccoon has given you an extraordinarily rare medicinal herb. It is no ordinary ginseng. It contains an amount of internal energy comparable to that of thousand-year-old ginseng.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s extremely valuable?]","[Heavenly Demon: It may not compare to Humanoid Snow Ginseng or the Ten-Thousand-Year Ginseng King, the king of all ginseng, but it is still exceedingly rare. Its powerful yin energy poses a problem, but since you already possess cold energy, it should not cause you any great difficulty.]","[Wild Grylls: Can you use it to make Fasting Pills?]","[Heavenly Demon: It is possible, but doing so would feel wasteful. This lady believes it would be better for you to consume it.]","[Wild Grylls: Then how long until the Fasting Pills are ready?]","[Heavenly Demon: A full sack will be complete soon.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll use that as payment instead. I already have trouble controlling my current energy. If I ate this too, I think I’d be in serious trouble.]","[Heavenly Demon: That is a reasonable argument. I shall give this to a close aide. He should be able to sell it for a high price.]","That would be far more helpful to her than giving it to me.","I asked the Heavenly Demon to wait for a moment, then headed outside.","There was something I wanted to ask the raccoon.","\"Keeeeng.\"","\"King, king.\"","When I went outside, I found the raccoon family gathered cozily around the campfire.","All three were holding out their paws to warm their chilled bodies.","The sight of the baby raccoon stretching out its tiny paws was especially adorable.","’This is nice, but...’","I was happy to have neighbors, but someday, I would have to leave this place.","Still, we would be living alongside one another until that day came.","Since they had been the first to show goodwill, I also felt more comfortable around them.","Until I left, we could cooperate and benefit one another.","\"Raccoon.\"","\"Keng?\"","Perhaps it understood that I was calling it, because it poked up its head.","The other two did the same. Its mate and baby both lifted their heads and looked at me.","’Should I give them names?’","Or perhaps calling this one Papa Raccoon would be enough.","In any case, I took Papa Raccoon aside for a moment. He followed me without showing the slightest wariness.","I brought him into the cave and led him to none other than my map—the one on which I had marked everything I had discovered during my explorations.","\"Okay, Papa Raccoon. You see this thing you gave me?\"","\"Keng.\"","\"If you find anything similar, could you bring it to me? If you do...\"","Scrape—","I showed him the white Snow Ginseng he had given me, then dragged over an iron container.","It still held fish frozen solid—naturally frozen fish kept in eco-friendly cold storage.","\"I’ll give you these fish. They’re frozen now, but the weather should warm soon, and then you’ll be able to eat them.\"","\"If you don’t like fish, I can give you something else. I’ll be receiving some Fasting Pills soon. I can give you those.\"","Pat—","As soon as I said that, I felt someone place a hand on my shoulder.","Wondering what it was, I turned my head and found the Swift Sloth staring at me.","Its expression seemed to say, We barely have enough for ourselves, and you’re giving those away?","The Swift Sloth was ordinarily almost entirely free of greed, but Fasting Pills were a different matter.","It had become especially sensitive about them after the gorilla stole them last time.","\"You already eat them one at a time. Besides, we can make more with the medicinal herbs this guy brings us.\"","\"...\"","\"He might effectively become our supplier of ingredients for Fasting Pills, so let it slide.\"","Perhaps persuaded by my argument, the Swift Sloth withdrew its hand.","The Forest of Four Seasons might have been overflowing with medicinal herbs, but I knew next to nothing about them.","Wouldn’t it be better to leave the job to an expert(?)? Naturally, the expert would receive appropriate compensation.","\"...\"","Papa Raccoon appeared to contemplate my offer for quite some time.","Perhaps he didn’t trust me. More importantly, this was essentially a business transaction.","If things went poorly, he might end up suffering a loss. He had a family to support.","Despite the risks, however, perhaps he had decided that I was trustworthy.","\"Keng!\"","The raccoon extended a paw, readily accepting my offer.","I clasped his tiny paw to signify that our deal had been concluded.","But we weren’t finished yet. There were still things I needed to tell him.","That was why I had brought him to the map.","\"Okay. See these two places? The gorillas live here. They’re hostile toward intruders, so you must never enter their territory.\"","\"Keng.\"","\"And this is the cave where the kangaroos live together. See that pig-like creature over there? It was attacked the moment it entered. They’re not friendly. And down here is the lake, but on the path leading to it, there’s a deer...\"","I carefully taught him about every dangerous area in case something happened to the raccoons.","They might have known their previous territory well, but they might not have been familiar with this area.","After concluding my agreement with Papa Raccoon, I sent the white ginseng to the Heavenly Demon.","’I’m glad I found such good neighbors.’","Although perhaps we were business partners now rather than neighbors.","Either way, it didn’t matter as long as we got along.","’That aside, should I build them a little shelter near the campfire?’","It was something worth considering.","***","Around the same time, at the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult—","\"I FOUND GINSENG!\"","A demonic practitioner clutched the snow-white ginseng and shouted loudly enough to shake the heavens.","The man was Wi Seorak. In his hand was the pristine white ginseng.","The Heavenly Demon had summoned him and abruptly given it to him as a gift.","He had been confused at first, but it hadn’t taken him long to realize that it contained an enormous amount of internal energy.","’I-I’m sure Grylls gave this to her, but... I can’t believe she’s giving me something like this...!’","Converted into money, it was worth several years of their budget.","Selling inner cores was troublesome because their origins could be identified, but ginseng was a different matter.","They could simply claim it had been buried in the mountain behind the cult and leave it at that.","In a world ruled by money and martial strength, this was worth far more to Wi Seorak than rain after a long drought.","No, rather than mere rain, it might be the first sign of an abundant harvest.","’The Heavenly Demon is a goddess. And Grylls is invincible.’","His affection for Grylls began to soar.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 145","paragraphs":["Neighbors (3)","By subcontracting the work to Papa Raccoon, I had reduced my workload and saved a great deal of time.","Right now, time was more precious to me than gold—no, even diamonds.","Therefore, I planned to manage our arrangement flexibly so that the raccoon wouldn’t become dissatisfied.","’How should I build their shelter, though?’","Since they were neighbors I would be seeing frequently, I considered building a small resting place for them in the yard.","However, I wasn’t sure what kind of structure the raccoons would like.","They had already made themselves a tidy home, so I had no intention of making them move again.","I was only planning a \"resting place\"—somewhere they could relax comfortably in front of the campfire during the cold winter.","’Building an entire house would be too much. A small shelter should be just right.’","A structure that allowed them to fully enjoy the warmth of the campfire would be enough.","Unfortunately, I had too many problems of my own to deal with, so I couldn’t build it immediately.","The furnace and oven were urgent. A resting place for the raccoon family was not.","As I had said, the raccoon family already had a home, so I could build it once I had some spare time.","’I should at least put down a mat for them.’","I checked the wind direction. With the cave entrance as the reference point, the wind blew from behind it.","Whatever else might change, the wind consistently blew in the same direction, making it easier to design the shelter.","’More importantly, I need to make sure Wonmo doesn’t perceive them as food.’","Wonmo had been plump before entering hibernation, but he had since lost a considerable amount of weight.","In less than ten days, he had rapidly gained weight and then lost it again.","In contrast, the Swift Sloth hadn’t changed at all. Perhaps it possessed some resistance to the cold.","’I’ve already been here for three weeks.’","Today marked exactly my twenty-first day here—three full weeks.","After another week passed, it would be four weeks. In other words, an entire month.","At first, time had seemed to crawl painfully slowly, but recently, the opposite had been true.","It was probably because the sun set early during winter and I spent most of my time inside the shelter. That must have made the days feel shorter.","’That isn’t necessarily a good thing.’","Gaining experience was good, but I still hadn’t acquired any information that might help me escape.","Adapting and escaping were entirely different matters.","Still, it wasn’t as though I had learned nothing at all.","I had obtained the invaluable knowledge that I shouldn’t even consider escaping during winter.","The moment I was swept away by an avalanche, my life would be in danger.","Crackle! Pop!","\"Kiing.\"","\"Kking.\"","I was working on the overall design of the shelter when Mama Raccoon and the baby gathered around the campfire.","Papa Raccoon was away working, but why had these two come here?","’What’s that stuck on the end of the stick?’","The stick in the baby raccoon’s paws particularly caught my attention. Something had been skewered on it.","While question after question arose in my mind, the baby raccoon carefully held the stick in both paws.","It glanced at me, then cautiously approached.","\"Kkiing.\"","The baby raccoon held out the stick it had been clutching so carefully.","For a moment, I wondered if it could manipulate fire like its father, but that wasn’t the case.","I could clearly see a golden-brown grub roasted on the end of the stick.","Most creatures living in the Forest of Four Seasons boasted considerable size, even when they were young.","The baby raccoon alone was about the size of a small dog.","Likewise, the grub skewered on the stick was unusually large.","\"...You want me to eat this?\"","\"Kking.\"","When I pointed at myself and asked, the baby raccoon replied affirmatively.","Wondering what was going on, I looked at Mama Raccoon. She had both paws tightly clasped together.","Her eyes seemed to plead, Please accept my child’s kindness.","What kind of raccoon could make an expression like that?","’Eating insects is a bit much, but...’","I couldn’t reject a gift given with such sincerity.","If I closed my eyes and ate it just this once, I would probably be fine.","\"Thank you. I’ll enjoy it.\"","\"...\"","The moment I thanked it, the baby raccoon scampered away.","It hid behind Mama Raccoon’s back.","Apparently, it was shy around strangers. Still, the way it poked only its head out from behind its mother suggested that it was eagerly anticipating my reaction.","I couldn’t crush a child’s(?) expectations. Besides, this was a gift from my neighbor.","After examining the grub, which appeared to have been cooked better than expected, I popped the entire thing into my mouth.","At least it was cooked, so it should taste like protein—","Squelch!","—or so I thought, but a deeply ominous sound came from inside my mouth.","At the same time, something moist and sticky began dribbling out between my lips.","Had I made a mistake by judging an animal’s cooking according to human standards? Or had the baby accidentally undercooked it because it was still young?","I desperately suppressed the disgust and nausea rising from my stomach and forced myself to chew the grub.","’...Right. In an emergency, I might have to eat these things raw anyway.’","I couldn’t disappoint the baby raccoon, so I persevered and ate it.","Swallowing was the most dangerous part. Calling its taste and texture the worst in history would still have been an understatement.","\"D-Delicious!\"","\"Kkiing! Kking!\"","\"Kiim.\"","When I raised my thumb and praised it, the baby raccoon bounced around excitedly.","Mama Raccoon stroked the baby’s head, but she kept glancing nervously at me.","Apparently, even she knew that her baby had served me an undercooked grub.","Title: The baby raccoon gave me a present","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby raccoon holding out a stick)","(Photo of a thick grub skewered on the stick)","That herb wasn’t the only gift I received from my neighbors. The baby raccoon personally roasted this over the fire and gave it to me, lol.","It was a little undercooked, but I endured it and ate the whole thing.","└ Heavenly Demon: I think this every time I see them, but they truly are creatures who understand courtesy.","└ SwordMaster: Ugh. Why is that grub so huge? Is it because it lives in the Forest of Four Seasons too?","└ Wild Grylls: Probably. Everything here is enormous.","└ Did the bug taste good?","└ It looks so plump that it almost seems delicious.","└ Ugh;; Are there actually people who enjoy eating bugs?","└ Don’t knife-ears eat them? They have that nature-loving image, so they probably eat insects too.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: What?! We don’t eat insects! Elves enjoy meat too!","└ Elves eat meat? I can’t imagine that.","└ That’s probably just a stereotype. Knife-ears are incredibly good at politics, and that’s how they built their nature-loving image.","└ Yeah. I heard they used that image effectively because they were positioned as the opposite of the demons. They also have the World Tree.","└ Even now, they get criticized a lot over their tree-planting campaigns, so that image still exists. But they don’t eat bugs, lol.","└ What do dark elves eat, then? They live in the desert, so meat must be scarce.","└ Praise the Sun: Why would we need meat when we have sweet dates? Lol.","└ There are so many dark elves who got diabetes from eating those, lololol.","└ They really are sweet. Dates are one of their biggest exports.","└ So, Grylls, did it taste good? It looks so plump and delicious.","└ Wild Grylls: The moment I bit into it, all its guts burst and spilled out of my mouth.","└ Gyaaaaaagh!","└ Uwaaaaah;;","└ Ugh;; Just imagining it makes me want to vomit.","└ Did you still finish it?","└ Wild Grylls: The baby raccoon was watching me expectantly. How could I refuse? I forced the whole thing down.","└ The baby raccoon did that to mess with you, lololol.","└ Pure evil, lololol.","└ So it was a devil raccoon, lololol.","└ Devilcoon, lololol.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s strange. As far as I know, raccoons normally wash their food in water before eating it. Why did this one roast its food over a fire?","└ Someone here still doesn’t understand the Forest of Four Seasons. There’s a reason for everything.","└ Starlight Princess: And what would that reason be? If you’re about to spout more nonsense, then go away.","└ Because all the raccoons that washed their food in water are already dead. Didn’t you see the river in front of Grylls’s house? A frog that sprays deadly poison jumped out of it, lol.","└ That’s... surprisingly convincing!","└ The Forest of Four Seasons is so terrifying that it forces animals to defy their instincts.","└ Starlight Princess: For once, that wasn’t a completely idiotic statement.","I had heard that before as well. Raccoons supposedly washed their food in water before eating it.","The raccoon that fell into despair after trying to wash cotton candy and watching it completely disappear had been hilarious.","Still, perhaps because raccoons were quick learners, I remembered it no longer washing the cotton candy after losing it two or three times.","Maybe the raccoons in the Forest of Four Seasons had learned something similar—that water was far more dangerous than fire.","’Is that also why they developed the ability to manipulate fire?’","As someone in the comments had said, it was strangely convincing. It wasn’t entirely implausible.","Afterward, I ate a bite of smoked meat to wash away the disgusting taste lingering in my mouth.","It was literally just to cleanse my palate, so it was closer to a snack than a meal.","’Bananas are the best snack, though.’","Thinking about snacks reminded me of the banana the gorilla had given me.","It had thrown the banana at me as if to say, Take this instead of your Fasting Pills and get lost.","It had been an utterly shameless deal, but the banana itself had been genuinely delicious.","Unfortunately, that banana was a specialty(?) found only in the jungle.","I had no desire to enter the gorillas’ territory, so no matter how much I wanted another, I had no choice but to endure the craving.","’Does this forest not have any fruit or anything?’","There were plenty of mushrooms, but almost no fruit. Even when I found some, it was never anything I particularly wanted to eat.","After entertaining those pointless thoughts for a while, I closed my eyes and circulated my heart method.","The overall design of the shelter was more or less complete. All that remained was to wait for the next season to arrive.","I had nothing else to do until then, so training was my only option.","’The cold energy is gradually gathering, little by little...’","The process of separating the cold energy from my mana was also progressing smoothly.","Everything was difficult at first, but once you gained momentum, things became easier.","That didn’t mean I was neglecting my swordsmanship training. I understood the importance of maintaining balance all too well.","\"Whew.\"","By the time I finished a reasonable amount of training, it was already lunchtime.","I was just considering getting something to eat when—","\"Keeeeeng! Keeeng!\"","The raccoon’s cry came from outside.","Rather than a shout, it sounded closer to a scream.","Judging by the voice(?), it seemed to be Papa Raccoon.","The moment I heard it, anxiety surged through me, and I hurried outside.","There was no one in the yard, but the scream had come from the raccoons’ home.","After arming myself, I headed toward the tree where they lived.","\"Rssssss—\"","\"Keeeng! Keng!\"","As expected, my neighbors were in danger.","A huge snake was slithering up the tree.","Papa Raccoon stood at the entrance to the hollow, fiercely resisting with a torch in one paw.","Mama Raccoon and the baby were probably inside.","\"You bastard!\"","I immediately charged at the snake.","Perhaps it sensed my presence.","Boing!","Incredibly, it seemed to bend its body slightly before launching itself backward like a spring.","Its elasticity was astonishing, and its movements were entirely befitting a creature from the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Shaaaaaah!\"","After briefly landing on another tree, the snake coiled its body and launched itself at me again.","Inside its enormous maw, I saw fangs dripping with venom.","I would have panicked in the past. By now, however, my body had grown accustomed to the Forest of Four Seasons.","I lightly twisted aside to evade the snake’s charge, then slashed downward with my sword.","Slice!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword, combined with an aura-infused strike, cleanly severed the snake’s body.","As if being cut apart weren’t enough, its entire body began freezing from the wound outward.","I had fought the Steel-Scaled Snake before, so I didn’t bother holding back, just in case.","Thrash! Thrash! Crackle!","The snake thrashed violently at first, but it wasn’t long before its entire body froze solid.","I didn’t stop there. I cleanly severed its head.","That should have killed it for good.","’If a snake that should be hibernating has awakened...’","This confirmed it.","Winter truly was coming to an end.","I kicked the frozen snake’s head far away, then turned around.","Still holding the torch in one paw, Papa Raccoon wore an expression of immense relief.","\"Are you all right?\"","\"Keeeng.\"","Papa Raccoon bowed deeply as if expressing his heartfelt gratitude.","His family had also poked their heads out of the hollow and thanked me.","’Thank goodness he had that torch. Otherwise, they would’ve been eaten.’","Most animals were afraid of fire. Snakes were no exception.","Moreover, Papa Raccoon could breathe flames from his mouth, so the snake must have found him troublesome to approach.","Since the raccoon still had that hidden card to play, the two had probably been cautiously watching each other for an opening.","I briefly considered scattering snake repellent around the tree in the near future. Meanwhile, the raccoon family climbed down.","\"Keng!\"","Papa Raccoon then tapped the frozen body of the snake.","Was he suggesting that we eat it?","\"You want to eat this?\"","\"Keeeng.\"","\"Hmm...\"","I looked down at the snake.","It was quite large, so there would be more than enough for us to share.","I had never eaten snake before, but... it would be a waste to throw away prey I had already caught.","Even leftovers wouldn’t be a problem. Now that I had a refrigerator, storing them would be easy.","\"All right. Let’s eat it.\"","After receiving my permission, Papa Raccoon gestured for me to wait and returned to his home.","A moment later, he came back holding something.","\"Keeeng!\"","What Papa Raccoon had brought was a mushroom.","It looked like an ordinary brown mushroom.","I preferred to avoid mushrooms whenever possible, but he must have brought it for a reason.","The thought suddenly occurred to me that he might even know what effects it possessed.","\"What does this do? I’m a little wary of mushrooms...\"","\"Keeeng.\"","Had he understood me?","Rather than answering with words(?), Papa Raccoon demonstrated through his actions.","Thrust! Thrust!","He vigorously thrust his hips back and forth.","He even pumped both arms energetically in the same rhythm.","There was no need for an explanation. I could easily guess what it meant.","Apparently, men were all the same, whether human or animal.","’But even if I eat it, I have no one to use the effect with.’","Was he teasing me because he had a mate?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 146","paragraphs":["Spring (1)","I didn’t put the virility mushroom Papa Raccoon had given me up for sale at the auction house.","It wasn’t that I distrusted him.","I simply thought I needed an expert’s opinion to determine whether the mushroom really had the effect he claimed and whether it was safe for humans.","After all, this was a mushroom we were talking about.","’I should ask the Starlight Princess.’","The All-Father was currently busy and rarely accessed the gallery, so he was out.","That left only the Starlight Princess. Come to think of it, hadn’t I asked her to analyze a mushroom before?","[Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess, may I ask you a favor?]","[Starlight Princess: Of course. What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Papa Raccoon gave me a mushroom. Apparently, it’s good for virility, so I think it needs to be verified. I wouldn’t be as concerned if it were something else, but the fact that it’s a mushroom worries me.]","[Starlight Princess: All right. If it were a medicinal herb, I would need the whole thing, but since it’s a mushroom, you only need to send me a small piece.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. By the way, what did you discover about the mushroom I sent you last time?]","[Starlight Princess: I forgot to tell you! It was poisonous. It contained all sorts of substances harmful to humans.]","[Wild Grylls: I see. Thank you.]","As expected, mushrooms that openly advertised, Do not eat me, were dangerous.","The same applied even to ordinary-looking ones. It was probably better not to eat mushrooms at all.","[Starlight Princess: Mushrooms spoil quickly. You can preserve it by freezing, but... are you planning to eat it?]","[Wild Grylls: Even if I ate it, I’d have no opportunity to use its effects. I was planning to sell it.]","[Starlight Princess: I see. I’ll examine it as quickly as possible!]","[Starlight Princess: If its effects are genuine, I recommend either selling or consuming it immediately.]","[Wild Grylls: Why?]","I had nearly gotten into serious trouble after eating eel before, so I thought it would be best to stay as far away from aphrodisiacs as possible.","It might be fine for people outside, but I had no way of predicting what would happen if I ate this mushroom.","Besides, even if Papa Raccoon had personally experienced its effects, there was no guarantee it would affect humans in the same way.","’Still, he went to the trouble of giving it to me...’","For now, I decided to roast the snake.","I ate the cooked snake together with the raccoon family.","It was my first time eating snake, but it was surprisingly palatable.","Its texture was unexpectedly pleasant, and it tasted similar to chicken.","It had a fishy odor that I hadn’t even noticed in actual fish, but I covered that with salt.","\"Keng!\"","\"Kiing! King!\"","\"Kkiing.\"","The raccoon family also seemed pleased when I sprinkled salt over their snake meat.","They alternated between salted and unsalted pieces before eventually eating only the salted ones with enthusiasm.","They had probably never sprinkled salt directly onto their food before.","It was also my way of showing them what they could enjoy if they continued helping me.","The raccoon family seemed to understand, because they began holding out pieces of meat and asking me to sprinkle more salt on them.","They were unbelievably adorable.","I filled my stomach with snake meat for lunch.","[Starlight Princess: Yes. I don’t know who the wife of the man who consumes it will be, but she’ll certainly be happy.]","I gave a bitter smile.","Whoever that man was, I envied him.","Not because he could eat something like this, but because he had someone beside him.","No matter how effective the mushroom was, didn’t you ultimately need someone with whom to share those effects?","I buried my bitterness and thanked the Starlight Princess.","Then I contacted the gallery member I had in mind.","[Starlight Princess: Mr. Grylls, the test results are ready.]","[Wild Grylls: How is it?]","[Starlight Princess: That raccoon really does seem remarkably capable. The mushroom contains many substances that would greatly benefit a man, and it has no toxicity whatsoever.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s safe to sell?]","[Praise the Sun: You said you had something for me?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. You were the only person I could think of giving it to.]","[Praise the Sun: It sounds like something edible. Did you ask that dwarf about it? Is he planning to soak it in alcohol again?]","[Wild Grylls: I didn’t ask him because I suspected he would do exactly that.]","[Praise the Sun: Just give it to the dwarf. You’ve already given me plenty.]","[Wild Grylls: It’s been verified as extremely beneficial for men.]","[Praise the Sun: How much do you want for it?]","His country had been established in a desert, much like the Middle East on Earth.","Based on the information I had picked up from the gallery, its culture and general social tendencies also appeared similar to those of the Middle East.","Praise the Sun was obsessed with anything beneficial to his health.","In particular, if something was said to be good for men, he would accept it without hesitation.","[Praise the Sun: Thanks. Let me know if you ever need anything.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. May I ask for something now?]","[Praise the Sun: Name it.]","[Wild Grylls: You live in a desert, correct?]","[Praise the Sun: I do. Why?]","[Wild Grylls: Do sandstorms occur frequently there?]","Setan—the nation of the dark elves and the wealthy.","[Praise the Sun: Between spring and summer, I suppose? That’s usually when most of them occur. Do you think one might hit your area too?]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know. That’s why I wanted to ask if you have any clothing or advice that would be useful during a sandstorm.]","[Praise the Sun: We have masks that are effective against sandstorms. Still, the best option is to avoid going outside.]","[Wild Grylls: One could arrive unexpectedly, so I’d like to prepare just in case.]","[Praise the Sun: That makes sense. How many do you want?]","[Wild Grylls: Six in total. Please make one adult-sized and the remaining five smaller.]","[Praise the Sun: Are you planning to put them on your animal friends? Honestly, I don’t think they’ll need them.]","[Wild Grylls: Why not?]","[Praise the Sun: They’ve lived there their entire lives. The masks might only make them uncomfortable. Have you ever seen those videos of dogs being made to wear shoes?]","That was an extremely fitting comparison. I had seen those videos too.","The dogs felt so uncomfortable that all four of their legs moved awkwardly in different directions.","Dogs had paw pads in the first place, so they didn’t need shoes.","The same probably applied to the animals inhabiting the Forest of Four Seasons.","Just as Wonmo had prepared for hibernation in advance, they would quickly respond to any unexpected environmental changes.","’Besides, I have the Swift Sloth.’","Wonmo’s warning signs and the Swift Sloth’s advance warnings should give me enough time to prepare.","I received a mask for protection against yellow dust from Praise the Sun.","Perhaps it was also designed to protect against the desert’s intense sunlight, because the mask was pure white.","’I don’t know whether yellow dust will actually come, though.’","Even if it didn’t happen in spring, a sandstorm could occur during another season.","I had witnessed the terrain and environment across the river changing in real time.","In the worst-case scenario, a sandstorm from the opposite bank might cross the river and reach us.","’Surely the volcano won’t erupt when that area turns volcanic, right?’","If it did, I could die instantly without even understanding what was happening.","The thought was rather frightening.","Still, the ancient traces inside this cave suggested that such events were exceedingly rare.","I spent the day thoroughly preparing for the approaching change of season.","\"Kyuu...\"","\"Oh! Wonmo, are you awake?\"","Wonmo, who had been hibernating, finally woke up as well. His half-asleep expression was incredibly adorable.","He had grown so thin during his brief hibernation that I missed his former plump appearance.","So I immediately gave him something to eat. There was still some snake meat left.","I wanted to buy him a huge piece of meat from the auction house, but he had only just awakened.","If I gave him something too large right away, he might get indigestion, so I started him with a light meal.","\"Nom, nom. Nom.\"","\"Is it good?\"","\"Kyu!\"","After eating the snake meat, Wonmo began regaining his energy.","I hugged him for the first time in ages and rolled around with him. That alone filled my heart with warmth.","\"Wonmo, I’m going to introduce you to our neighbors.\"","\"Kyu?\"","After rolling around together for a while, I decided to introduce him to the raccoon family.","Although it was still chilly, the weather was gradually warming.","Perhaps because of that, Wonmo shivered slightly but didn’t retreat into the cave.","\"Okay, say hello. This is the raccoon family. This is Papa Raccoon, this is Mama Raccoon, and this is Baby Raccoon.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","\"K-Keng!\"","\"Kkiing...\"","\"...\"","Despite my friendly introduction, their reactions couldn’t have been more different.","Wonmo tilted his head in innocent curiosity, while the raccoon family trembled in fear.","Papa Raccoon at least managed to force out a greeting, but the other two couldn’t.","No matter how young Wonmo was, he was still an owlbear—a predator whose adorable appearance concealed a ferocious nature.","The raccoon family had been terrified of a mere snake. It was only natural that they would fear him.","’I just hope he doesn’t recognize them as food.’","Was that even possible?","If Wonmo perceived them as prey and attacked, I planned to stop him immediately.","I would feel terrible for the raccoon family, but I would have no choice but to make them move somewhere else.","It would be an unavoidable decision if we wanted to coexist.","And so, after they finished greeting one another—","\"Kyuuu! Kyuu!\"","\"Kkiing! Kking!\"","Wonmo ran excitedly around the yard with Baby Raccoon riding on his back.","Forget food—he seemed delighted simply because he had made a new \"friend,\" and a bright smile covered his face.","Baby Raccoon had been afraid while first climbing onto Wonmo’s back, but quickly adapted.","’Hmm. Excellent.’","As long as I kept Wonmo well-fed, a catastrophe probably wouldn’t occur.","Now that I had finished introducing the neighbors, I accessed the gallery and uploaded a post.","I couldn’t keep something this adorable all to myself.","Title: Wonmo woke up","Wild Grylls","(Video of Wonmo running around with Baby Raccoon riding on his back)","He’s already playing nicely with our neighbor. Looks like they’ll get along well from now on, haha.","└ Heavenly Demon: The sight brings peace to one’s heart.","└ Cheonggu Princess: They’re so adorable, haha.","└ Starlight Princess: I wish the gallery contained nothing but heartwarming posts like this.","└ Don’t worry. If there’s an emergency, that raccoon will be roasted alive, lol.","└ It’s emergency food, lololol.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly pieces of garbage.","There were occasional jokes about emergency food, but most people found Wonmo and Baby Raccoon adorable.","Satisfied, I checked the time. There was still plenty of time before evening.","[What the hell did Kadir say?]","[Fuck, this topic’s about to blow up again, lololol.]","[But if the Mage King went that far, doesn’t that mean this is seriously bad?]","[The Holy Kingdom really seems screwed;;]","[Quick summary]","While checking the time, I browsed the gallery to see if anything interesting had happened.","I noticed people discussing Kadir, so I opened the trending posts. The gallery was in flames.","’Why is Kadir being mentioned?’","Kadir, the Mage King, was a celebrity frequently mentioned in the gallery.","Moreover, hadn’t NecromancyIsLove recently spoken to me about him?","Since he had become the gallery’s latest hot topic, I naturally grew curious.","Title: Fuck, this topic’s about to blow up again, lololol","Kadir even issued an official statement. What happens if the Holy Kingdom keeps acting like this?","└ What did he say?","└ Kadir personally confronted the Pope. Then he got pissed off and secretly broadcast the entire meeting record, lololol.","└ ??? Is that even possible inside the Vatican?","└ He’s the Mage King;;","└ It isn’t that the Vatican is worthless. Kadir is just absurdly powerful.","Title: Quick summary","Kadir: Confess your sins to your god before it’s too late.","Vatican: Fuck off. We’ll handle it ourselves.","Kadir: The ones you should be looking toward aren’t your god, but the people of the Holy Kingdom.","Vatican: The commoners are livestock. Deal with it.","└ Did they really say that?","└ Of course not, lololol.","└ The livestock remark was pretty close, though, lol.","└ This isn’t going to turn into a civil war, is it?","└ Hard to say since there’s no one to rally around. If only the Hero were there...","Title: Outside the Vatican right now","(Video of a protest)","(Video of protesters shouting curses)","(Video of protesters throwing stones)","(Video of the Holy Knights blocking their path)","(Video of a bard playing an instrument to bolster the protesters’ morale)","└ Forget everything else—what the fuck is that bard doing? Lololol.","└ This perfectly demonstrates why an adventuring party needs a bard, lol.","└ Wow, the bard’s music completely changes the atmosphere, lololol.","└ Just watching it fills me with strength, lololol.","Apparently, Kadir had thrown another log onto the fire.","The Holy Kingdom had already been in turmoil over the Ludwig incident, and now the meeting records had been exposed as well.","’Livestock, huh...’","Apparently, no matter where you went, there were always people who regarded their own citizens as livestock.","I chuckled and closed the gallery.","It would probably be best to stay away from it for a while.","’I wonder if things will have settled down by the time I escape.’","Or perhaps the entire Holy Kingdom would be burning by then.","I had no way of knowing.","After closing the gallery, I turned toward the yard.","\"Kyuuung!\"","\"Kkiiiiiing!\"","Wonmo was repeatedly throwing Baby Raccoon into the air and catching him.","To Wonmo, it was merely \"fun.\" From Baby Raccoon’s perspective, however, it must have felt like facing \"death\" itself.","Papa and Mama Raccoon appeared to be pleading with Wonmo to stop, but their efforts were meaningless.","\"Hey! Park Wonmo! You can’t do that!\"","I hurriedly stopped him.","We still had a long way to go.","***","\"Prrr.\"","\"...\"","Ludwig was still riding atop the giraffe.","He stared blankly down at the animal blocking his path.","\"Prrrr.\"","\"Neigh.\"","The creature standing before him was none other than a horse.","More specifically, it was a horse covered in black and white stripes—a so-called zebra.","A Holy Knight riding a giraffe, confronted by a zebra blocking his way.","It was truly a bizarre standoff.","’It appears to be dangerous. To have such conspicuous tattoos in the middle of the grasslands...’","Tap, tap—","Ludwig lightly nudged the giraffe’s sides with his legs.","The giraffe obediently began walking.","Ludwig’s bizarre adventure was still ongoing."]},{"title":"Chapter 147","paragraphs":["Spring (2)","The Mage King, Kadir.","The story of his life was filled with tales that sounded as though they had come straight out of a children’s book.","He had single-handedly defeated a dragon, vanquished every renowned mage who challenged him, and accomplished countless other legendary feats.","But the most fairy-tale-like part of his story was undoubtedly his friendship with the Hero.","The Hero as the protagonist and a mage as his companion—it was a combination commonly found in fairy tales.","Even their achievement resembled one: together, they had defeated the Undying King.","The Undying King had appeared due to the atrocities of the Holy Kingdom, at a time when the demon race was gradually shedding its image as servants of a Demon King.","Whatever the Undying King’s past might have been, the previous Hero and Kadir had joined forces to subjugate him.","Although the previous Hero had tragically lost his life in the aftermath, his death was recorded as a noble sacrifice.","As the Hero’s closest friend, Kadir had also quietly mourned him while temporarily burying the regrettable truth.","However, after confronting the vile and dark secrets concealed by the Holy Kingdom, even that tragic truth began to feel meaningless.","’The ones who claim they have no desire for money are always the greediest.’","The same was true of justice. Those who went around proclaiming themselves righteous were never right in the head.","That was exactly what El Dorado was like now. Those who were supposed to distance themselves from greed had become consumed by it.","Outwardly, they pretended to be devout and respectable, but Kadir had noticed the truth long ago.","El Dorado’s image as a \"Holy Kingdom\" had already crumbled.","’I can hardly wait to hear what kind of nonsense they’ll spout.’","Thus, after making thorough preparations, Kadir headed for El Dorado.","He did not bother asking permission from the Kingdom of Iris, the nation in which the Magic Tower was located.","He was the Magic Tower itself, as well as a mage whose power rivaled that of an entire nation. Who could possibly stop him?","He was not called the Mage King for nothing. Even the king of Iris had to tread carefully around him.","And so, Kadir visited the Holy Kingdom of El Dorado alone.","El Dorado was greatly flustered by his sudden visit, but they immediately welcomed him as an honored guest.","He had given them some advance notice, and they also had ties dating back to the incident with the Undying King.","Before long, Kadir was allowed to enter the Holy See without any obstruction.","\"...What did you just say?\"","\"We merely follow the will of God. What will of their own could servants such as us possibly possess?\"","And within the Holy See—more precisely, during his meeting with the pope and the cardinals—Kadir could only stare at them in disbelief.","As the previous Hero’s friend, he knew perfectly well just how corrupt El Dorado’s upper echelons had once been.","However, those who held power back then were different from those who held it now. Humans had short lives, so generational changes occurred quickly.","He had assumed that things might have improved at least a little by now, but after only a brief conversation, he realized that they had become even more rotten than before.","’These bastards are genuinely beyond saving.’","Maintaining a calm expression, Kadir stared at Pope Louis II.","On the surface, he was an elderly man with a benevolent appearance, but a cunning serpent lurked within him.","A serpent ready to devour a person at any moment.","’Every rotten aspect of El Dorado is embodied in this one pope.’","Kadir clicked his tongue inwardly.","Judging by appearances, Kadir looked younger than the pope, but the two were actually around the same age.","He glanced around at the other cardinals. They said nothing, apparently having already become the pope’s obedient hands and feet.","\"Servants of God... What an ambiguous phrase. Then are you saying that the merciless slaughter of the Undying King’s people was also God’s will?\"","\"Do you think we took pleasure in it? We merely followed the instructions given to us.\"","\"Were they instructions from the previous pope, or from God?\"","\"The pope’s words are God’s message.\"","Their constant invocation of God truly was useful in every situation.","Simply claiming that something was God’s will allowed them both to attack and defend as they pleased.","In the distant past, Aris might personally have inflicted divine punishment upon them for their blasphemy.","However, as the ages passed and human civilization developed, the gods ceased interfering with the world.","’Perhaps they left because they were disappointed.’","That was highly likely. Even Kadir, who did not believe in any god, was feeling tremendously disappointed.","No—it had gone beyond disappointment. Hatred was rapidly swelling within him.","Especially because he knew just how noble the previous Hero had been.","\"So God gave you that command... Is that truly what happened?\"","\"Are you suggesting that God failed to make the correct decision?\"","\"No. I’m asking whether you received a divine revelation or prophecy. The Hero told me that it was his homeland, not God, that pressured him into it.\"","\"....\"","That was your doing, wasn’t it? Don’t lie to my face.","I was the Hero’s friend. I even have recently uncovered evidence.","When Kadir asked with those implications behind his words, Louis II’s expression stiffened slightly.","The same was true of the other cardinals. They made no attempt to conceal their discomfort.","Kadir habitually stroked his thick beard and quietly continued.","\"There is a saying in the Central Plains: ’You cannot hide the sky with the palm of your hand.’ Do you truly believe the world will never learn the truth? I would advise you to repent while you still can.\"","\"My apologies, but....\"","\"Ah, of course, you probably weren’t the ones giving orders back then. You would have been the ones receiving them. It would have been wiser to emphasize that fact and apologize. What a shame.\"","\"....\"","If they had not been the ones who issued the orders at the time, Kadir could understand that much.","But if they still refused to apologize, they were irredeemable pieces of filth.","Either that, or their skulls were simply empty.","\"See here. Your words are going too—\"","Just as one of the cardinals could no longer contain his anger, Louis II raised a hand to stop him.","The cardinal had no choice but to swallow his fury.","Louis II then spoke while maintaining his same benevolent smile.","\"I fully understand what you are trying to say, Lord Kadir. However, I hope you will understand that we merely follow the will of God.\"","\"I wonder whether God would truly accept that interpretation of His will.\"","Kadir snorted.","His mocking words implied that people would no longer believe anything they said.","Kadir could ridicule them to their faces only because he was the previous Hero’s companion and possessed fame and power that no one could ignore.","Anyone else would already have been beheaded and had their head displayed on a pike.","However, even Kadir had failed to anticipate one thing.","There was always another level beneath rock bottom.","\"O Mage King, do you know why we—and humanity as a whole—believe in God?\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Because we are ignorant and foolish. We constantly make the wrong choices, so God must guide us. Of course, even God does not always make the correct choice, but His choices are at least far better than ours.\"","To summarize it simply:","[Humanity is made up of mindless animals.]","Strictly speaking, the pope was referring to the people of El Dorado rather than humanity as a whole, but there was nothing wrong with interpreting it that way.","Everyone was supposedly equal before God, so what difference did it make?","Kadir ultimately had no choice but to laugh in disbelief.","He could not tell whether they were shameless or simply insane.","\"I understand your views perfectly now. Thanks to you, I feel as though my eyes have finally been opened.\"","\"I am pleased that we could be of assistance.\"","\"That shameless façade of yours won’t last much longer.\"","Snap!","Kadir snapped his fingers as he spoke. Louis II immediately realized what that action meant.","Kadir had undoubtedly cast a spell.","The pope became visibly alarmed and hurriedly demanded,","\"What have you done...?\"","\"Ah, nothing significant. Just as my eyes have been opened, I merely helped open the eyes of the people as well.\"","\"Do you think you’ll emerge unscathed after doing this?\"","\"Do you even know what I’ve done before saying that?\"","Kadir’s answer was to respond to shamelessness with shamelessness.","Ignoring Louis II’s fury, Kadir leisurely rose from his seat.","Realizing that something was wrong, one of the cardinals hurriedly attempted to summon the holy knights.","\"Your Holiness! We have a disaster!\"","\"What happened?\"","\"A-a video of this meeting is currently being broadcast throughout El Dorado!\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Louis II could not comprehend the messenger’s report.","This was not merely relay magic. A recording of their meeting was somehow being leaked throughout El Dorado.","Unable to understand what was happening, Louis II glared at Kadir.","\"Ah, it’s nothing remarkable. I merely imitated the Gallery that you branded as evil.\"","\"You imitated it?\"","\"The ability to record and replay everything one sees without the assistance of any device... Don’t you think it is a truly fascinating form of magic?\"","Kadir chuckled. It was a thoroughly eccentric laugh.","By the time Louis II’s face had twisted like that of a demon, Kadir leisurely raised a hand.","\"You will have a difficult time for a while. You brought all of this upon yourselves, so don’t resent me for it.\"","\"Do you believe God does not know the truth?! Have you truly become a follower of that Gallery as well?\"","I obtained a book from there and even deciphered it, you bastard.","Kadir firmly suppressed those words. It was not yet time to reveal that.","That was something he needed to disclose only after more time had passed and he was ready to advance to the next stage.","\"The Gallery? I have no idea what you are talking about. It seems you have something weighing on your conscience.\"","\"You...!\"","\"I’ll leave you to deal with this yourselves. I must be going.\"","He had started a fire and was now fleeing the scene. Kadir had tossed a bundle of firewood onto the dying embers.","El Dorado soon became so chaotic that it teetered on the brink of civil war, throwing the entire world into an uproar.","As Kadir leisurely returned to the Magic Tower, he thought,","’This is when we need the Hero... No. Perhaps it’s better that the Hero isn’t here right now.’","The Hero was currently on the run after being falsely branded a traitor.","No matter how violent the protesters became, they would inevitably scatter without a central figure around whom they could rally.","Would the Hero return, or would the Holy See make the first move?","’This is going to be a rather long battle.’","While chaos consumed El Dorado, Kadir quickly returned to the Magic Tower.","Teleportation was easy when one used magic—although that was only because he was Kadir.","The moment he returned to his beloved laboratory, he opened the refrigerator.","\"The blue mushroom I received before... There it is.\"","[Kill them.]","\"Later.\"","Kadir casually ignored the Undying King’s request and closed the refrigerator.","***","The Gallery was ablaze with discussion over the claim that humanity was made up of mindless animals.","To me, it was little more than watching a fire from across the river, so it did not matter all that much.","My reaction amounted to little more than, Huh, something strange is happening in the world.","Nothing I said would be of much help, and the Gallery probably would not help me either.","I merely found it fascinating that the small ball I had set rolling had transformed into a gigantic meteor plummeting toward the world.","’It’s gotten much warmer.’","I could physically feel that the end of winter was approaching.","My thick winter clothing was beginning to feel uncomfortably warm. Still, I would probably continue wearing it until tomorrow.","It was time to start maintaining my home again. The first problem was the ground, which had frozen solid and then thawed.","Rain had fallen, winter had suddenly arrived, and now the warmer weather had thawed the ground once more.","As a result, the earth had become somewhat muddy and difficult to manage.","Still, it was not so bad that my feet sank as though I were walking through a swamp or tidal flat. It was merely annoying.","’I should gather some gravel from the river later.’","When constructing a building, the most important thing was the ground.","Compacting and reinforcing the earth alone had taken more than half of the entire construction time.","Since I planned to build a furnace and an oven soon, I intended to compact the ground thoroughly.","I could gather gravel from the river, spread it over the ground, and press it down firmly.","\"Wonmo, come here.\"","\"Kkyu?\"","\"Uhehehe.\"","It was evening, and the sky was gradually growing dark.","I wrapped my arms around Wonmo and rolled around on the floor with him.","Winter was over and Wonmo had awakened, so we would finally be able to resume our activities in earnest.","Once I finished everything that needed to be done, I could explore the surrounding territory as well.","’As long as that damned yellow dust doesn’t come.’","It might even be a sandstorm rather than ordinary yellow dust.","Then again, unlike spring in Korea, this place might not get any at all.","I had finished laying all the groundwork necessary to prepare for spring.","’Still, I should put up the tent flap just in case.’","Once I covered the cave entrance with the tent flap, I was ready for bed.","I then tossed more firewood into the fireplace to keep the cave warm.","\"Achoo!\"","I sneezed while getting ready. My nose was incredibly itchy.","It was not a cold. My nose had quite literally begun itching all of a sudden.","’What is this? I have a bad feeling about it.’","Should I sleep while wearing my mask, just in case? It would be uncomfortable, but it would not prevent me from sleeping.","I told the speedy sloth staring blankly into the fire to take good care of things, then went to sleep.","Oh, and I did not forget to practice my internal energy cultivation method before falling asleep.","I had to train consistently if I wanted my abilities to improve even slightly.","And so, I spent the night in the cave while eagerly anticipating the arrival of spring.","The next morning—","Whoooooosh!","The moment I pulled aside the tent flap, a bright yellow world greeted me.","So the yellow dust really did come.","I had only just thought that when—","\"Achoo! Achoo! Aaaaachoo!\"","I began sneezing repeatedly. My nose was not merely itchy anymore; it was starting to sting.","I assumed it was because of the yellow dust, but it was strange that I was sneezing rather than coughing.","Even with my mask on, I felt as though something bright yellow was forcing its way through it.","Suspecting the worst, I barely managed to open my eyes.","’Wait. Don’t tell me this isn’t yellow dust, but...’","The pollen that had tormented me every spring.","\"Aaaaaachoo!!!\"","Pollen billowed through the air like yellow dust, dyeing the entire world yellow."]},{"title":"Chapter 148","paragraphs":["Spring (3)","My pollen allergy was not particularly severe.","It only made me sneeze and gave me a runny nose. Nothing more than that.","If I wore a mask, the symptoms practically disappeared altogether.","\"Achoo! Sniff!\"","Fortunately, the pollen in the Forest of Four Seasons affected me in much the same way.","Its concentration was simply incredibly high—comparable not to the yellow dust that reached Korea, but to the yellow dust in China itself. The symptoms were no different.","Once I put on the mask-like face covering that Praise the Sun had given me, I felt considerably better.","There was nothing I could do about the pollen I had already inhaled, though.","’How do the animals survive in an environment like this?’","I alternated my gaze between the speedy sloth and Wonmo.","The speedy sloth was tossing firewood into the fireplace, while Wonmo stared at me with his round eyes wide open.","I wondered how those two had adapted to this awful environment.","’Whatever else happens, having a home is essential.’","It was not optional. It was a necessity for survival.","If I had failed to claim this cave, I probably would have been swept up in one of the disasters and died.","While exploring, it would be wise to search for shelters where I could take refuge from disasters along the way.","’The pollen has... died down a little.’","The pollen storm had almost subsided.","It seemed all the flowers had bloomed simultaneously with the arrival of spring, causing an extreme amount of pollen to fill the air.","As far as I knew, pollen levels normally peaked around April or May, but the Forest of Four Seasons did not care about such things.","Spring had arrived, so all the flowers had apparently gone, Wow, it’s spring! and bloomed together. The end.","’The problem is that it all erupts at once.’","Still wearing my face covering, I headed outside.","My nose remained itchy, but not enough to make me sneeze. I could not do anything about the runny nose, though.","Thinking that I would have to wash the face covering thoroughly later, I armed myself. My first objective was to collect some gravel.","For the first time in a while, I brought the speedy sloth and Wonmo along with me. Neither of them seemed bothered by the pollen.","\"Pchoo!\"","Or maybe not. Perhaps they had merely been holding it in.","Judging by Wonmo’s sneeze, it seemed to vary from one individual to another.","It was a pollen allergy , after all. The difference between having it and not having it was significant.","When we eventually reached the river, I saw that its surface was still frozen.","The ice must have melted underneath, however, because the water was flowing swiftly.","’I should be able to start setting fish traps soon.’","From now on, I planned to set two traps instead of one.","Having experienced how abruptly winter could arrive, I needed to prepare more smoked food.","’Do frogs hibernate too?’","As I gathered gravel and placed it into a sack, I carefully examined my surroundings.","A frog or some other creature might suddenly leap out.","Fortunately, perhaps because spring had only just arrived, there were no animals in sight.","Once I had filled the sack with gravel, I returned to the cave. All I had to do now was spread it over the ground and compact it.","’Why is this mud so sticky?’","However, since the yard covered a fairly large area, I had no choice but to make several trips.","The ground had not been this bad when it first rained. Winter was responsible for its current state.","The earth freezing solid had contributed, but the snow was probably the decisive factor.","Even though I had scattered salt over the ground from time to time, I had still been unable to prevent it from freezing.","’That takes care of the ground. Shall I start building?’","It was time to rebuild the oven and furnace that the avalanche had swept away.","I planned to construct them sturdily enough to withstand any future disasters.","’If I want to anchor them firmly, I should dig into the ground a little.’","I dug out the ground and laid bricks at the bottom.","Then I stacked the bricks one by one, following the same design I had used before.","Between the bricks, I applied mortar made by mixing sand and cement.","Finally, I repeatedly slid the tray in and out to make sure that the dimensions were correct.","The preparations had taken a long time, but the construction itself went quickly since I had already built one before.","’Just in case, I should build a wall behind it.’","Having learned from the avalanche that had descended from behind the cave, I built the oven directly against the cave wall.","Even that did not seem sufficient, so I decided to erect a solid barrier behind the oven as well.","It would be better than having it collapse and rebuilding it every time a disaster struck.","’Hmm... Will this work?’","Somehow, however, I ended up constructing a barricade rather than a simple wall.","The wall surrounded the entire oven, and its thickness was no joke either.","I wondered whether I had invested too much into it, but it was already finished. There was nothing I could do about it now.","’All that’s left is the furnace.’","I built the furnace directly against the cave as well.","As with the oven, I did not forget to erect walls around it.","I had also applied the cement meticulously, so it should not collapse easily.","’Hmm. Perfect.’","With the cave in the middle, the oven and furnace now stood on either side of it.","I left the areas beside them empty to allow for future expansion work(?).","Wearing a satisfied expression, I photographed the front of the cave and uploaded the pictures to the Gallery.","Title: Rebuilt Everything","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the cave’s front)","(Photo of the gravel-covered ground)","(Photo of the forest radiating warmth)","As of today, winter has ended and spring has arrived in the Forest of Four Seasons.","As soon as spring arrived, I rebuilt everything the avalanche swept away.","Time to resume my industrious life.","└ Heavenly Demon: They resemble wings. It seems you possess considerable knowledge of architecture as well.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you, haha.","└ SwordMaster: Did you spread gravel over the ground because of the mud?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. Ordinary rain isn’t too bad, but after winter the ground becomes far too muddy.","└ SwordMaster: A good decision. Incidentally, did you learn to spread gravel like that in the military?","└ Wild Grylls: How did you know?","└ SwordMaster: I did the same thing.","└ The military really teaches you all kinds of things, doesn’t it?","└ That’s because it has all kinds of people. Sometimes you meet someone who makes you wonder, Why is this guy even in the army?","└ The only useful thing I learned was spear fighting. Having a spear makes an enormous difference.","└ Passing Dwarf: Right. Hey, don’t tell me my mold got swept away too.","└ Wild Grylls: I could move the mold, so I brought it inside.","└ Passing Dwarf: That’s a relief. That thing’s expensive, you punk.","└ Wild Grylls: No matter how expensive it is, it can’t cost more than mithril, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ve got nothing to say to that, damn it. Lolol.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh, can you give me two fish traps? I think I’ll be making a lot of smoked food from now on.","└ Passing Dwarf: I can, but don’t you have anything to give me in return?","└ Wild Grylls: If I find anything that can be made into alcohol, I’ll tell you immediately.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, lol.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: An impressive arrangement. Are those bricks truly that sturdy?","└ Wild Grylls: They’re meaningless before the power of nature, but they are sturdy. Besides, I used cement this time, so they should be even stronger.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: I see. That may prove useful later. Are you planning to stop after completing those?","└ Wild Grylls: Of course not. I still need to gather firewood and make charcoal.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: It must be difficult having to build and cultivate everything yourself.","└ Wild Grylls: It is, but completing something is extremely satisfying.","It was difficult to put into words how satisfying it felt to complete something I had designed.","I had built these things out of necessity, but I could not deny the sense of fulfillment they gave me.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: I see. In that case, are you also planning to farm?","└ Wild Grylls: I might try, but wouldn’t it be difficult?","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: Since this is the Forest of Four Seasons, it might not be as difficult as you think.","└ Wild Grylls: Perhaps you’re right.","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: You’re seriously underestimating farming;; Just plowing a field is exhausting, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Is it really that hard?","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: Honestly, the quality of the land matters most, but farming there will probably be even harder because the weather is insane. You said the season changes every week, right?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: Then ordinary farming knowledge might be useless. With the weather changing constantly, the plants won’t be able to grow properly.","└ Wild Grylls: Hmm... Understood. I’ll take that into consideration.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: So there was such a problem. I only just realized it myself.","They said pleasure came after hardship.","But after hearing the explanation from a registered user who appeared to be an actual farmer, I began to hesitate.","He added that if I was going to gamble in a casino, I would be better off farming instead.","Farming was labor every bit as unpredictable as gambling, and this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","’I’ll need fertilizer, and I’ll have to water everything... There certainly is a lot to consider.’","I already had plenty to do. Adding farming to the list would make things difficult in many ways.","The Forest of Four Seasons was also a region where disasters erupted whenever they felt like it.","I was already busy enough looking after myself. I had no spare capacity to devote to farming.","The only consolation—if it could be called one—was that I was not planning to operate an actual farm. It would be closer to maintaining a small vegetable garden.","’Should I ask the raccoon family to help?’","I immediately discarded that idea.","The father raccoon was busy searching for medicinal herbs.","The mother raccoon would have her hands full caring for the baby raccoons. I could not think of any suitable source of labor.","’Still, I should at least look for an appropriate plot, just in case.’","This was merely preparation for the possibility. I would only start farming if I genuinely had enough free time.","I spent the rest of the morning cleaning everything up. For lunch, I ate the fish that remained in the metal container.","It had been so long since I last ate fish that it tasted even more delicious.","[ Passing Dwarf: Here are the two fish traps. Be careful not to let them get destroyed again.]","[ Wild Grylls: I’ll try. I can anticipate the changing seasons, but I never know when it will rain. Oh, can you give me a barricade too?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Just build a thick wall out of bricks. That would be far better.]","[ Wild Grylls: You think so too?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Yep. No matter how exceptional wood might be, it can’t compare to stone. Unless it comes from the World Tree, I suppose.]","The World Tree.","Come to think of it, I had once seen an incredibly enormous tree.","It was when I experienced an out-of-body state after receiving the second mnemonic verse from the Heavenly Demon.","I could not be certain that it was the World Tree, but it might be worth investigating.","[ Wild Grylls: Is the World Tree really that tough?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Its branches perform better than steel. Need I say more?]","[ Wild Grylls: Damn. Then what about the gloves I received from that elf before? Are the leaves just ordinary leaves?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. But the silkworm wasn’t an ordinary silkworm either. I don’t know what was going through that knife-ear’s head, but they gave you something genuinely valuable.]","The gloves Planting Trees had given me.","I had been making excellent use of them.","I had given them the Guardian’s Core in exchange, but I had no idea what they were doing with it now.","They occasionally appeared in the Gallery, but as always, all they ever talked about was planting trees.","’World Tree or not, I hope there’s something useful there.’","The place was extremely far away to begin with, making a round trip difficult.","After thanking the dwarf, I examined the fish traps.","Normally, it would have been better to visit the river tomorrow, but food had to be gathered whenever the opportunity presented itself.","I could break the ice myself and install the traps today.","’There’s a grassland across the river this time.’","The region on the other side of the river changed at certain intervals.","I did not know how long those intervals were or what determined the next environment.","Perhaps I needed to uncover that pattern soon. Doing so would expand the range within which I could operate.","\"...Huh?\"","Wait. What was that?","I blinked.","Since it was a grassland, I could accept that it contained various animals.","Therefore, I could overlook the presence of a giraffe. I could even overlook that giraffe fighting back against a predator.","But I could not simply overlook the person riding on the giraffe’s back and swinging a sword.","It was not as though a giraffe were a horse.","Rub, rub—","The sight was so unbelievable that I rubbed my eyes and looked again.","Unfortunately, it seemed to be the exact moment when the region was changing. The grassland across the river blurred like a mirage.","A barren, rocky wasteland then replaced it.","The knight who had been riding the giraffe had vanished without a trace.","’Are there really people here?’","For a moment, faint hope arose within me.","’But he was riding a giraffe.’","He had even fought like a knight while doing so.","Confronted by such an utterly bizarre sight, I could not help feeling confused."]},{"title":"Chapter 149","paragraphs":["Countermeasures (1)","My confusion over the existence of a knight riding a giraffe lasted only briefly. He had already vanished, and there was nothing I could do about it, so I decided to focus on the task at hand.","First, I broke through the ice covering the river and plunged my hand into the water to provoke the golden frog.","Of course, it would be better if the golden frog was still hibernating and did not appear.","Then I would not have to waste any time dealing with it.","Splash—","\"Gaaah!\"","The moment I put my hand in, a strange cry escaped my lips. The water was far too cold.","I had gotten a rough idea of its temperature from the water coming through the hose, but feeling it directly against my skin made it seem even colder.","Still, it was something I had to endure to secure food.","Fortunately, the golden frog must have still been hibernating, because it did not appear.","\"Brrrrr. S-so cold.\"","There was nothing I could do about the cold, though. This was exactly why I had wanted to acquire cold resistance.","Shivering violently from the chill that surged through me the moment I stepped into the river, I installed the fish traps.","All the shoes I had traded for until now were waterproof, but the river was too deep.","That left me no choice but to enter it wearing sneakers.","’Just ten minutes. I only have to endure it for ten minutes...!’","There was a risk of frostbite, but I should be fine. I might not possess cold resistance, but I could wield cold energy.","That should provide a certain degree of protection, so I was not worried about frostbite.","The water was simply mind-numbingly cold.","After installing both traps, I hurried back to the cave.","The first thing I did upon returning was heat some water and soak my feet in it.","I probably would not suffer frostbite, but this was merely a precaution.","As I sat there with my feet submerged, I recalled the scene I had witnessed earlier.","’Was the person I saw across the river really there?’","Not only had he been riding a giraffe, but he had also been wielding a sword like a knight.","Even the predators surrounding him—lions, to be precise—had been unable been unable to approach him easily.","’Wait. Come to think of it, wasn’t his sword glowing?’","The sword the knight had been holding had definitely emitted a green light.","Although the glow had been rather faint, it was unmistakably green.","Only the mythricon I had given away should glow green.","’Then was that Ludwig?’","Ludwig—the holy knight renowned for his upright character.","And the man who posted exceptionally middle-aged-sounding messages in the Gallery.","It was entirely possible that he had been the one swinging a sword from a giraffe’s back.","’Seriously, the timing couldn’t have been worse.’","I thought about it while warming my feet in the heated water.","No matter how I looked at it, the timing was incredibly unfortunate. Why did the region have to change at that exact moment?","If I had been given one more minute—or even just thirty seconds—I could have examined him more closely.","’I really have the worst luck.’","The knight I suspected was Ludwig probably had not noticed me.","He had been locked in a fierce battle with a pride of lions. How could he possibly have spared any attention for the opposite side of the river?","’Come to think of it, didn’t they say giraffes don’t exist in this world?’","I was not completely certain, but that was how I remembered it.","Just in case, I searched the Gallery for \"giraffe.\"","Nothing appeared. There were posts containing the individual syllables, but there was no animal called a giraffe.","Unicorns and pegasi, by contrast, clearly existed. They were apparently regarded as ordinary knowledge.","Of course, giraffes might simply have been known by another name, so I even drew one to confirm.","Title: Does an Animal Like This Exist?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of my giraffe drawing)","Is there an animal with a long neck and legs like the one in this drawing? Where I came from, we called it a giraffe.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is not even a spirit beast. This is my first time seeing such a bizarre animal.","└ SwordMaster: Mine too. I’ve never seen or even heard of such an animal in my life.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Its long neck makes it look kind of sad.","└ Starlight Duchess: How does it eat with such a long neck?","└ Praise the Sun: There’s something... strangely fascinating about it. I want one.","└ Clever Demon: It’s seriously ugly as hell, lololol.","└ Do they use their necks like whips when they fight? Kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: How did you know? I heard they really do swing their necks to wreck their opponents. Otherwise, they kick with their hind legs.","└ What the hell kind of animal is that? You’ve got one hell of an imagination, lol.","└ What if it breaks its neck while attacking?;;","└ That body is the pinnacle of inefficiency, lol.","Since I was technically an animal as well, my existence probably served as another piece of evidence supporting the hypothesis.","However, while I knew the result, I still could not determine the cause.","’I suppose I’ll have to examine everything carefully.’","The conclusion was that I needed to learn more about this forest.","I had begun to suspect that my arrival here had not been a coincidence either.","Survival was important, but so was exploration. I needed to find clues if I wanted to improve my chances of escaping.","’I’ve been keeping a journal consistently, so only time will tell.’","Now that I had realized the seasons changed every week, I planned to devote more time to exploration.","Originally, I intended to remain in my shelter until I became stronger, but allowing that period to drag on for too long would not be wise.","Besides, winter would force me to rest anyway.","Of course, now that I had discovered evidence of another survivor, I first needed to devise countermeasures.","’I should provide them with something useful for survival.’","└ All-Father: Oh. What a fascinating animal. Something similar existed in the distant past.","└ Wild Grylls: Really?","└ All-Father: Yes. They were monsters called dinosaurs—the ancestors of dragons and drakes. Some dinosaurs had extremely long necks.","└ Did those dinosaurs fight with their necks too?","└ All-Father: According to one theory, they used their long tails like whips. Wyverns are also descendants of dinosaurs.","Was he talking about brachiosauruses?","It was fascinating that dinosaurs had existed in this world too.","No. Before that, it was even more fascinating that these people could not accept the existence of giraffes.","’Then what was the giraffe I saw?’","Had giraffes perhaps lost the struggle for survival and gone extinct?","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place where even herbivores were absurdly powerful, so perhaps they had survived here.","It was a reasonably convincing hypothesis.","If not, then—","’Could they be... connected to Earth?’","Just as I had suddenly fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons, animals from Earth might also have been brought here.","And was Ludwig, the knight riding the giraffe, truly the only person who had entered the Forest of Four Seasons?","I had heard that other people had been forcibly dragged in along with Ludwig.","If they were fortunate, they might still be alive somewhere in the forest, just like him.","However, from my own experience, the Forest of Four Seasons was an exceedingly difficult place to survive without a secure base.","Furthermore, without suitable tools, one’s chances of survival were practically nonexistent.","’Just as the Gallery helped me, I should help them.’","Unless they were me, anyone brought into the Forest of Four Seasons would be unable to access the Gallery.","There was no way to determine their locations either. Even asking the administrator would be useless.","The only thing I could do was throw survival supplies across the river.","Since I had no idea where they were, this was my best option.","’Food is the most important survival resource, but...’","Unfortunately, food was the one thing I could not spare.","Now that I knew winter would return, I needed to begin steadily building up my own reserves.","Conversely, that meant I could provide most things other than food.","’Weapons, for example.’","Weapons were extremely important in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Had I not survived countless crises after receiving the Heavenly Demon’s sword?","I did not know Ludwig’s exact circumstances, but he also seemed to have survived somehow with the mythricon sword.","’I’ll forge swords and throw them across the river. That should work.’","This was the best countermeasure I could devise. Nothing else came to mind.","Actually, there was one other possibility.","The signposts I had erected near the cave.","I could build an enormous sign visible from across the river.","It would be similar to the defector guidance signs installed along the front lines.","’I should have done this from the beginning...’","I had not installed any signposts near the river. That had been a major mistake.","For some reason, I had complacently assumed Ludwig would appear on my side.","Because of that, it had never occurred to me that the sign needed to be visible from across the river.","If I had erected one earlier, Ludwig might already have crossed over.","What a shame.","Learning from that mistake, I planned to write the message in multiple languages.","That way, it would be useful not only to Ludwig but to anyone who entered the forest, regardless of when or where they came from.","’I can ask the Gallery about each country’s language.’","Languages differed by race and nation, but I had the Gallery.","Since the registered users came from various backgrounds, I could simply ask them.","’The sign absolutely has to be large.’","I could construct it in much the same way as I had made the signposts.","However, its sheer size meant it would require a great deal of work. Joining all the pieces of timber together would be particularly difficult.","I constructed an enormous sign by fitting wooden boards one at a time onto long poles.","One might wonder whether that would make it difficult to write on, but there was no need to worry.","’I’ll attach a large sheet of paper to it.’","Attaching paper would make things easy. I would not have to write directly on the sign.","Smiling in satisfaction at the sign, which was clearly visible even from a distance, I accessed the Gallery.","I then purchased a sheet of paper to attach to it and asked the registered users for assistance.","[ Heavenly Demon: Shall I write exactly what you told me?]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes. Please do.]","[ Heavenly Demon: It is not difficult. Wait a moment.]","[ Wild Grylls: Understood.]","[ Heavenly Demon: (Photo of the notice written in the language of the Central Plains) Will this suffice?]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you! I think this every time I see it, but your handwriting is truly beautiful.]","[ Heavenly Demon: Thank you.]","First, I received the Central Plains version from the Heavenly Demon.","Then SwordMaster, who had briefly decided to play a prank, provided the Messiah Empire’s language.","[ SwordMaster: (Photo of an explanation written in the language of the Messiah Empire) Will this do?]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes! Thank you so much!]","[ SwordMaster: Wait. Let me send you another one...!]","[ Wild Grylls: Huh?]","[ SwordMaster: (Photo of the notice written in the language of the Messiah Empire) Here’s the new one, haha.]","[ Wild Grylls: What did you write the first time?]","[ SwordMaster: I wrote, \"Become stronger and marry me.\"]","[ Wild Grylls: ;;;]","[ Passing Dwarf: Good grief. I never imagined I’d do something like this in my entire life, lol.]","[ Wild Grylls: Try to understand how I feel. I’m desperate too.]","[ Passing Dwarf: Fine. Wait a moment.]","I received the dwarven language from the dwarf.","I also asked Cheonggu Princess, All-Father, Praise the Sun, Planting Trees, Suspiciously, and several others.","Through them, I obtained the languages of various countries and races.","Someone might wonder why I did not simply make a public Gallery post asking everyone at once. I went through the extra trouble because the replies would probably have become too chaotic.","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: (Photo of the notice written in El Dorado’s language) Will this work?!]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you. I sincerely hope Ludwig sees it.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Have you seen Mr. Ludwig?!]","[ Wild Grylls: I think I did, but I’m not certain. He was riding a giraffe and swinging the sword I gave him.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: A giraffe... Do you mean that bizarre animal from your post?!]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: I see! It may be strange, but I’m relieved to hear that he’s alive! Please contact me immediately if you confirm his survival!]","[ Wild Grylls: Understood.]","Finally, I received the El Dorado version from the administrator, who was originally from there.","I copied all the languages I had received from the various nations and races onto the paper.","I used black paint so that the words would contrast sharply against the white background.","’There are so many languages. This is exhausting.’","The paper itself was enormous, and copying foreign languages onto it was difficult work.","I had to use the available space efficiently, so maintaining my concentration was especially important.","Eventually, I finished writing the message in every language.","Smiling, I looked over the completed notice.","Its contents were roughly as follows:","[Gallery registered user Wild Grylls welcomes all survivors!]","[If you can read this, follow the signposts downhill! You will eventually see a cave!]","[We are stronger together than we are alone! Let’s overcome this together!]","How should I put it?","It did not exactly feel like a survival notice.","’It almost sounds like a government advertisement encouraging people to immigrate...’","Anyway, now that the notice was complete, all that remained was to produce the survival supplies.","’Let’s get moving.’","There was no point in constructing the sign if those who saw it could not survive long enough to reach me.","I gripped my pickaxe and began mining the mithril buried within the cave.","And as I did—","’Please survive.’","I desperately prayed that someone would survive long enough to reach me."]},{"title":"Chapter 150","paragraphs":["Countermeasures (2)","Title: Made a Notice","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the notice)","I’m planning to install this where it can be seen from across the river.","I originally wasn’t going to put one near the river, but I saw a person on the other side today;;","It happened too quickly for me to take a picture, but I think it was the person sent by the Holy Kingdom. Yeah.","└ Heavenly Demon: Did you truly see a person?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. He was riding a giraffe and fighting lions.","└ SwordMaster: A giraffe is the long-necked animal you mentioned earlier, correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ SwordMaster: It seems like the rider wouldn’t be able to see ahead very well because of its neck;;","└ Wild Grylls: I haven’t asked one myself, so I wouldn’t know.","└ What if the giraffe comes across with him?","└ Lol, then you’ll have another mouth to feed.","└ With a neck that long, would it even fit inside your shelter?","└ That’s one problem, but it might also have a nasty temperament;;","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: That’s a good idea! Other survivors should be able to see it too!","└ Are you sure you didn’t see things? Maybe the Forest of Four Seasons showed you a hallucination.","└ It sounds far too detailed to be a hallucination. We’ll just have to wait and see, lol.","└ What if that person kills Grylls?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: That would never happen! Mr. Ludwig is a good man!","└ Even a good man can turn evil when his survival is at stake, Admin;;","└ I’m worried about that too. Ludwig might be fine, but what if another survivor arrives and causes trouble?","At first, the responses were exactly what one would expect from the Gallery, but various concerns soon followed.","Suppose there truly were survivors in the Forest of Four Seasons. They might see the notice and cross the river.","But what happened after that? What if a survivor harbored malicious intentions and tried to hurt me?","’It’s not impossible.’","When survival was at stake, every animal was effectively a competitor.","It was no different even between members of the same species.","Moreover, I could not speak the languages of this world, so persuading them would not be easy.","’I’ll have to make full use of the Gallery.’","Even the absurdly powerful sloth struggled to obtain food in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Without the Gallery, I would have starved to death too.","In an isolated place like this, access to the Gallery was an advantage in itself.","I could show it to the survivors and perhaps use it to translate our conversations.","’Recruiting them is still the highest priority. Manpower is what ultimately matters.’","There were things people could do and things only the Gallery could do.","As if on cue, a flood of comments expressing thoughts similar to mine appeared.","Some included insults, but I did not particularly care.","’I should install the notice first.’","Its size was not a problem. I had my subspace backpack.","Before long, I had carefully positioned it so that it could be clearly seen from across the river.","I could inspect its condition whenever I came to collect the fish traps.","’Crossing the river is another problem.’","The river was wide, and the current was far too strong. Crossing it without a boat would be difficult.","I briefly wondered whether a survivor might be able to leap across, but assuming that someone at such a level had survived without suffering any injuries would be overly optimistic.","The more survivors there were, the greater the possibility that one of them had injured legs.","Had I not possessed the elixir, I myself would have been forced to live with a disability.","’I need to build a bridge.’","One might wonder how a bridge could work when the region across the river changed in real time.","However, only the region beyond the river changed. The river itself always remained the same.","That meant there was always land with similar conditions on the opposite bank.","’I should measure the distance first.’","I took a rope from my subspace backpack. I always carried simple tools like that with me.","I then tied a dagger to its end and threw it across the river.","I did not throw it into the changing region itself, only as far as the boundary.","’As expected, it’s quite wide.’","I marked the rope and pulled it back.","I was about to return when I paused and stared at the region beyond the river.","The Forest of Four Seasons displayed all kinds of environments. At the moment, the other side was filled with fog.","What was hidden within that mist?","Could survivors truly be living even in a place like that?","’No matter how I look at it, I was incredibly lucky.’","Gallery access aside, I was fortunate merely to have found myself somewhere that made survival possible.","If I had appeared in the misty region, a volcanic zone, a desert, or even a snowy mountain...","The thought alone was horrifying.","’Where was that person? Don’t giraffes live on grasslands?’","There had also been lions surrounding him. Those were animals native to grasslands.","But I could not be certain of that either. Kangaroos lived not far from here.","As with humans, wherever an animal adapted became its habitat.","’I’ll take my time with the bridge and forge the swords first.’","Even a temporary bridge would take a long time to build. Swords would not.","Besides, I needed to test the father raccoon’s abilities.","Of course, sharpening swords was the dwarf’s specialty, so I decided to ask him for assistance.","[ Passing Dwarf: I think this every time I see you, but you have a tendency to view the world far too optimistically.]","[ Wild Grylls: What are you talking about?]","[ Passing Dwarf: I understand that you’re happy to have seen another survivor, but you should never make decisions recklessly when you’re excited. Think things through at least two or three times.]","His response was painfully sound advice.","At first, I wondered what had gotten into him.","This was the same dwarf who usually traded jokes with me and laughed about everything.","For him to say something like this meant I was making a rash decision. He was giving me a much-needed warning.","’Um...’","I pressed my lips together and considered what the dwarf might be concerned about.","I had planned to throw supplies—specifically, weapons—across the river for the survivors.","I had judged weapons to be more practical than food.","After all, mithril and orichalcum were scattered everywhere around me.","’...Could something like that gorilla end up using them?’","The gorillas might have looked different from humans, but they were effectively comparable to primitive mankind.","Some individuals used crude weapons, and the leader could even manipulate mana.","Imagine if one of them obtained a mythricon sword.","Forget survival—the entire ecosystem would be thrown into chaos.","’Come to think of it, they said monsters exist too.’","Goblins, orcs, gnolls, ogres, and other creatures commonly found in fantasy stories.","Those creatures were even more dangerous because they knew how to use tools.","If even apes could use mana here, why wouldn’t they be able to?","If things went wrong, I would personally be creating an unimaginably dangerous threat.","’Damn.’","A bitter taste filled my mouth.","As the dwarf had suggested, discovering another survivor must have gotten me overly excited.","In the end, I abandoned the idea of throwing swords across the river. The risks were far too great.","Still, I should forge a sword specifically for Ludwig.","It could serve as a spare.","’Before that, I should build the bridge.’","I asked the dwarf about that as well, requesting a suitable method for constructing a temporary bridge.","Since the river might swell when it rained, I wanted to build an arched bridge.","If even the dwarf did not know how, I planned to lay down a simple structure first and gradually reinforce it.","[ Passing Dwarf: There is one method, but I don’t know whether you can manage it alone.]","[ Wild Grylls: What is it?]","[ Passing Dwarf: It’s called a Da Vinci bridge. It’s an old construction method that has been used for ages. The structure is fairly simple, so I believe it was commonly used during wars.]","Da Vinci?","Could it possibly be the same Da Vinci I knew?","The familiar name startled me slightly.","Cement was one thing, but Da Vinci was the name of a famous historical figure, which made it difficult to dismiss.","[ Wild Grylls: Da Vinci? Is that a person’s name?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Huh? All I know is that the method has existed since ancient times.]","It seemed I would be better off asking All-Father.","For now, however, the origin of the name was less important than the construction method.","[ Wild Grylls: Can you teach me?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Teaching you is easy, but building it will be rough. Do whatever you want. By the way, can’t that person just jump across?]","[ Wild Grylls: How could anyone cross a river that way? Besides, he might have injured his legs.]","[ Passing Dwarf: Lol. In that case, you might as well mass-produce elixirs and scatter them around. That would probably work better.]","It was not as though I had never considered that.","However...","A mature mandrake alone was not enough to produce an elixir.","If I asked Starlight Duchess, she would naturally agree to make one for me, but repeatedly asking for favors would be embarrassing.","More importantly, the mandrake population was visibly beginning to decline.","’Now that I’m considering every detail, aren’t I in danger too?’","After thinking things over two or three times, I realized the dwarf’s advice was completely correct.","This was no time for me to act as though I had resources to spare.","My happiness at seeing another survivor must have lowered my intelligence.","’They say not to make decisions when you’re happy. This is exactly what they meant.’","Only twenty-two days had passed.","That was all, yet I already missed human company so much that it was driving me insane.","Seeing another survivor in that state must have briefly short-circuited my brain.","’I can’t afford to be so optimistic.’","After reaching that conclusion, I learned how to construct a Da Vinci bridge from the dwarf.","Naturally, he conveyed the instructions through a Gallery post. The structure itself was not particularly complicated.","The dwarf had even uploaded a video in which he demonstrated the assembly using small sticks. That made it easy to understand.","Understanding it was one thing.","The thought of constructing it out of full-sized timber already seemed overwhelming.","└ Passing Dwarf: If it’s too much of a pain, should I just make it for you?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I need to account for the changing region across the river, so I want to build it myself.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then I’ll give you a hand plane. Use this.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ Passing Dwarf: By the way, what will you do if an animal crosses instead of a person? Have you considered that?","└ Wild Grylls: The bridge is necessary because of the golden frogs anyway. Those bastards are basically guarding the crossing.","└ Passing Dwarf: Ah. That’s true.","Now that I had also received a hand plane from the dwarf, I began constructing the bridge in earnest.","The first step was logging.","This time, I was not gathering firewood but materials for the bridge.","I did not use mana. The cold energy might cause me to ruin the timber.","Crack!","A large tree toppled over.","All I had to do was process it piece by piece.","I set the smaller branches aside for firewood and charcoal, then cut the massive trunk into appropriately sized sections.","’Doing all of this alone is seriously exhausting.’","When would the region across the river turn back into a grassland?","I hoped it would change soon.","’But a Da Vinci bridge? Could it really be the Da Vinci I know?’","Between that and the cement, there were several strange similarities.","Were they truly the same things I knew, or were the names merely coincidences?","It was worth thinking about, but I decided to set it aside for now.","’Who cares?’","Survival was ultimately what mattered.","***","While Grylls was busily cutting down trees to build a temporary bridge, Ludwig—the holy knight riding the giraffe—found himself in a difficult situation.","The giraffe had not betrayed him.","On the contrary, they had just emerged victorious from their battle with the pride of lions.","Thanks to the giraffe’s extraordinary height, the battle had effectively been a siege.","His reach had not been a problem either, as the mythricon sword Grylls had gifted him had performed splendidly.","The sword reacted strongly to even the faintest amount of mana.","The Forest of Four Seasons possessed an exceptionally high mana density, making mana extremely difficult to use.","However, it was only difficult, not impossible. With sufficient concentration, Ludwig could manipulate it to a limited degree.","The drawback was that it felt like forcing an elephant through the eye of a needle, leaving him unable to exert even five percent of his normal power.","Even so, the mythricon sword’s superior performance had provided Ludwig with tremendous assistance.","\"Urgh...\"","But it inevitably had its limits.","After the fierce battle, Ludwig rested beneath a massive tree.","He groaned as he examined the place where the lions had wounded him.","Fortunately, both arms were unharmed, but a lion had bitten his right foot.","A lion’s bite was already renowned for its terrifying power, and this was a lion native to the Forest of Four Seasons.","It had literally crunched through his steel boot, leaving him severely injured.","’This is bad. I don’t see any medicinal herbs I can use for treatment.’","He had given all his potions and other healing supplies to Reis.","Aside from the mythricon sword, he had effectively entered the Forest of Four Seasons with nothing.","At first, a combination of coincidence and good fortune had made survival relatively easy.","It seemed that luck had finally run out.","’Considering the risk of infection, amputation would be the correct decision, but...’","Contemplating the worst-case scenario, he looked around.","There was nothing but an endless grassland. He could not see anywhere suitable for hiding and resting.","A cave?","Every cave he had discovered thus far was occupied by either a three-headed lion or a monster of comparable strength.","’But was the person I saw earlier merely an illusion?’","Ludwig recalled what had happened.","Across the river, he had seen someone who appeared to be from the Central Plains.","The sight had left him so stunned that he had suffered this injury.","He was fortunate that only his foot had been wounded. Without the giraffe, his life would likely have been in danger.","’If it wasn’t an illusion...’","He turned his head toward the river.","The landscape was different from before.","Previously, he had seen a forest on the opposite bank. Now, there was nothing but desert.","His delight at discovering a source of water had lasted only briefly. Even the region beyond the river had completely changed.","’If the flesh begins to necrotize, I’ll have to amputate.’","Until then, he had no choice but to monitor the wound.","Frowning, Ludwig raised his head.","It seemed he would have to use this enormous tree as a temporary shelter.","In his current condition, traveling anywhere would be dangerous.","’I’ll endure until the forest across the river appears again.’","Having made his decision, Ludwig turned his head.","The giraffe was lying nearby with its body curled up.","’I’ll take that fellow with me too.’","Ludwig was becoming increasingly attached to the giraffe.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]}]);
